      "target_section": "alpn-extension-value",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the first ALPN value is only a single character, then that character is treated as both the first and last character.\n",
      "id": "544d53d53d7103d5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 34,
      "quote": "If the first ALPN value is only a single character, then that character is treated as both the first and last character.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4/alpn-extension-value.toml",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "alpn-extension-value",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the first or last byte of the first ALPN is non-alphanumeric (meaning not `0x30-0x39`, `0x41-0x5A`, or `0x61-0x7A`), then we print the first and last characters of the hex representation of the first ALPN instead.\n",
      "id": "19860a88c01cf828",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 40,
