      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A ServerKeyExchange MUST NOT be sent (the server's certificate\ncontains all the necessary keying information required by the client\nto arrive at the premaster secret).\n",
      "id": "6032354b4b35e320",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 29,
      "quote": "A ServerKeyExchange MUST NOT be sent (the server's certificate contains all the necessary keying information required by the client to arrive at the premaster secret).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In ECDHE_ECDSA, the server's certificate MUST contain an ECDSA-\ncapable public key and be signed with ECDSA.\n",
      "id": "0a38b384f88d4f62",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 20,
      "quote": "In ECDHE_ECDSA, the server's certificate MUST contain an ECDSA- capable public key and be signed with ECDSA.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "These\nparameters MUST be signed with ECDSA using the private key\ncorresponding to the public key in the server's Certificate.\n",
      "id": "df4d980b0ba65ea1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 27,
      "quote": "These parameters MUST be signed with ECDSA using the private key corresponding to the public key in the server's Certificate.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This key exchange algorithm is the same as ECDH_ECDSA except that the\nserver's certificate MUST be signed with RSA rather than ECDSA.\n",
      "id": "149885e5b39803ab",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 8,
      "quote": "This key exchange algorithm is the same as ECDH_ECDSA except that the server's certificate MUST be signed with RSA rather than ECDSA.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This key exchange algorithm is the same as ECDHE_ECDSA except that\nthe server's certificate MUST contain an RSA public key authorized\nfor signing, and that the signature in the ServerKeyExchange message\nmust be computed with the corresponding RSA private key.\n",
      "id": "e6da303577262660",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 11,
      "quote": "This key exchange algorithm is the same as ECDHE_ECDSA except that the server's certificate MUST contain an RSA public key authorized for signing, and that the signature in the ServerKeyExchange message must be computed with the corresponding RSA private key.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server\ncertificate MUST be signed with RSA.\n",
      "id": "14f952119ca8136c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 20,
      "quote": "The server certificate MUST be signed with RSA.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In ECDH_anon, the server's Certificate, the CertificateRequest, the\nclient's Certificate, and the CertificateVerify messages MUST NOT be\nsent.\n",
      "id": "fff0d93dca07e43f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 35,
      "quote": "In ECDH_anon, the server's Certificate, the CertificateRequest, the client's Certificate, and the CertificateVerify messages MUST NOT be sent.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-2.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server MUST send an ephemeral ECDH public key and a specification\nof the corresponding curve in the ServerKeyExchange message.\n",
      "id": "fdb019a6e582df28",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 43,
      "quote": "The server MUST send an ephemeral ECDH public key and a specification of the corresponding curve in the ServerKeyExchange message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-2.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "These\nparameters MUST NOT be signed.\n",
      "id": "92c4cd732990c87c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 50,
      "quote": "These parameters MUST NOT be signed.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-2.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations of this\nalgorithm SHOULD provide authentication by other means.\n",
      "id": "b15358244dea7f9d",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 100,
      "quote": "Implementations of this algorithm SHOULD provide authentication by other means.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To use this authentication mechanism, the client MUST possess a\ncertificate containing an ECDSA-capable public key and signed with\nECDSA.\n",
      "id": "b912fd782c5a21ce",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 13,
      "quote": "To use this authentication mechanism, the client MUST possess a certificate containing an ECDSA-capable public key and signed with ECDSA.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To use this authentication mechanism, the client MUST possess a\ncertificate containing an ECDH-capable public key, and that\ncertificate MUST be signed with ECDSA.\n",
      "id": "67b3a7702fab57fd",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 26,
      "quote": "To use this authentication mechanism, the client MUST possess a certificate containing an ECDH-capable public key, and that certificate MUST be signed with ECDSA.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To use this authentication mechanism, the client MUST possess a\ncertificate containing an ECDH-capable public key, and that\ncertificate MUST be signed with ECDSA.\n",
      "id": "b654e502c187f940",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 34,
      "quote": "To use this authentication mechanism, the client MUST possess a certificate containing an ECDH-capable public key, and that certificate MUST be signed with ECDSA.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Furthermore, the client's\nECDH key MUST be on the same elliptic curve as the server's long-term\n(certified) ECDH key.\n",
      "id": "c9434f02818bfc5b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "Furthermore, the client's ECDH key MUST be on the same elliptic curve as the server's long-term (certified) ECDH key.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When using this authentication mechanism, the client MUST send an\nempty ClientKeyExchange as described in Section 5.7 and MUST NOT send\nthe CertificateVerify message.\n",
      "id": "518dadaf92cb97d2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 50,
      "quote": "When using this authentication mechanism, the client MUST send an empty ClientKeyExchange as described in Section 5.7 and MUST NOT send the CertificateVerify message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When using this authentication mechanism, the client MUST send an\nempty ClientKeyExchange as described in Section 5.7 and MUST NOT send\nthe CertificateVerify message.\n",
      "id": "84a90b1c9e2209ea",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 58,
      "quote": "When using this authentication mechanism, the client MUST send an empty ClientKeyExchange as described in Section 5.7 and MUST NOT send the CertificateVerify message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This authentication mechanism is identical to ECDSA_fixed_ECDH except\nthat the client's certificate MUST be signed with RSA.\n",
      "id": "0680b462dd160dfe",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 20,
      "quote": "This authentication mechanism is identical to ECDSA_fixed_ECDH except that the client's certificate MUST be signed with RSA.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-3.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A TLS client that proposes ECC cipher suites in its ClientHello\nmessage SHOULD include these extensions.\n",
      "id": "8a8dba963ac94ca6",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "A TLS client that proposes ECC cipher suites in its ClientHello message SHOULD include these extensions.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers implementing ECC\ncipher suites MUST support these extensions, and when a client uses\nthese extensions, servers MUST NOT negotiate the use of an ECC cipher\nsuite unless they can complete the handshake while respecting the\nchoice of curves and compression techniques specified by the client.\n",
      "id": "901ba56db37397e4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "Servers implementing ECC cipher suites MUST support these extensions, and when a client uses these extensions, servers MUST NOT negotiate the use of an ECC cipher suite unless they can complete the handshake while respecting the choice of curves and compression techniques specified by the client.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers implementing ECC\ncipher suites MUST support these extensions, and when a client uses\nthese extensions, servers MUST NOT negotiate the use of an ECC cipher\nsuite unless they can complete the handshake while respecting the\nchoice of curves and compression techniques specified by the client.\n",
      "id": "b993dd3a3d1b0b49",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 61,
      "quote": "Servers implementing ECC cipher suites MUST support these extensions, and when a client uses these extensions, servers MUST NOT negotiate the use of an ECC cipher suite unless they can complete the handshake while respecting the choice of curves and compression techniques specified by the client.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The client MUST NOT include these extensions in the ClientHello\nmessage if it does not propose any ECC cipher suites.\n",
      "id": "f4760ac4c5bb037a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 71,
      "quote": "The client MUST NOT include these extensions in the ClientHello message if it does not propose any ECC cipher suites.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The uncompressed point format is the default format in that\nimplementations of this document MUST support it for all of their\nsupported curves.\n",
      "id": "b4262cc8e7979b9e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 46,
      "quote": "The uncompressed point format is the default format in that implementations of this document MUST support it for all of their supported curves.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations of this document MAY support the\nansiX962_compressed_prime and ansiX962_compressed_char2 formats,\nwhere the former applies only to prime curves and the latter applies\nonly to characteristic-2 curves.\n",
      "id": "75bbe01ca0564d0b",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "Implementations of this document MAY support the ansiX962_compressed_prime and ansiX962_compressed_char2 formats, where the former applies only to prime curves and the latter applies only to characteristic-2 curves.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The extensions SHOULD be sent along with any ClientHello message that\nproposes ECC cipher suites.\n",
      "id": "3123d3f8d4a9e58f",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 69,
      "quote": "The extensions SHOULD be sent along with any ClientHello message that proposes ECC cipher suites.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients\nSHOULD send both the Supported Elliptic Curves Extension and the\nSupported Point Formats Extension.\n",
      "id": "75051c4cd959c823",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 76,
      "quote": "Clients SHOULD send both the Supported Elliptic Curves Extension and the Supported Point Formats Extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the Supported Point Formats\nExtension is indeed sent, it MUST contain the value 0 (uncompressed)\nas one of the items in the list of point formats.\n",
      "id": "dad5d63eacf19f24",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 84,
      "quote": "If the Supported Point Formats Extension is indeed sent, it MUST contain the value 0 (uncompressed) as one of the items in the list of point formats.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server that receives a ClientHello containing one or both of these\nextensions MUST use the client's enumerated capabilities to guide its\nselection of an appropriate cipher suite.\n",
      "id": "cf9d38bdf687314d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 92,
      "quote": "A server that receives a ClientHello containing one or both of these extensions MUST use the client's enumerated capabilities to guide its selection of an appropriate cipher suite.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a server does not understand the Supported Elliptic Curves\nExtension, does not understand the Supported Point Formats Extension,\nor is unable to complete the ECC handshake while restricting itself\nto the enumerated curves and point formats, it MUST NOT negotiate the\nuse of an ECC cipher suite.\n",
      "id": "f7761338561ba75d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 100,
      "quote": "If a server does not understand the Supported Elliptic Curves Extension, does not understand the Supported Point Formats Extension, or is unable to complete the ECC handshake while restricting itself to the enumerated curves and point formats, it MUST NOT negotiate the use of an ECC cipher suite.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Note that this octet string (Z in IEEE 1363 terminology) as\noutput by FE2OSP, the Field Element to Octet String Conversion\nPrimitive, has constant length for any given field; leading zeros\nfound in this octet string MUST NOT be truncated.\n",
      "id": "243904e208eea2bd",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "Note that this octet string (Z in IEEE 1363 terminology) as output by FE2OSP, the Field Element to Octet String Conversion Primitive, has constant length for any given field; leading zeros found in this octet string MUST NOT be truncated.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "All ECDSA computations MUST be performed according to ANSI X9.62 [7]\nor its successors.\n",
      "id": "c1ab19b94a9561d7",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 50,
      "quote": "All ECDSA computations MUST be performed according to ANSI X9.62 [7] or its successors.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The Supported\nPoint Formats Extension, when used, MUST contain the value 0\n(uncompressed) as one of the items in the list of point formats.\n",
      "id": "a95648544ccf7ff4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "The Supported Point Formats Extension, when used, MUST contain the value 0 (uncompressed) as one of the items in the list of point formats.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client that receives a ServerHello message containing a Supported\nPoint Formats Extension MUST respect the server's choice of point\nformats during the handshake (cf.\n",
      "id": "b49ba66fd2462583",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 62,
      "quote": "A client that receives a ServerHello message containing a Supported Point Formats Extension MUST respect the server's choice of point formats during the handshake (cf.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "ECC\npublic keys MUST be encoded in certificates as described in\nSection 5.9.\n",
      "id": "c60a8ca99b64aef6",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 71,
      "quote": "ECC public keys MUST be encoded in certificates as described in Section 5.9.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "ECDH_ECDSA              Certificate MUST contain an\nECDH-capable public key.\n",
      "id": "e1e07f3ccfdb82ce",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 79,
      "quote": "ECDH_ECDSA              Certificate MUST contain an ECDH-capable public key.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It\nMUST be signed with ECDSA.\n",
      "id": "252caeed607f7d30",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 86,
      "quote": "It MUST be signed with ECDSA.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "ECDHE_ECDSA             Certificate MUST contain an\nECDSA-capable public key.\n",
      "id": "0cfdbda7bb007cda",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 93,
      "quote": "ECDHE_ECDSA             Certificate MUST contain an ECDSA-capable public key.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It\nMUST be signed with ECDSA.\n",
      "id": "5ac3f21017b5172b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 100,
      "quote": "It MUST be signed with ECDSA.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "ECDH_RSA                Certificate MUST contain an\nECDH-capable public key.\n",
      "id": "20d0080c4e9cd3d8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 107,
      "quote": "ECDH_RSA                Certificate MUST contain an ECDH-capable public key.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It\nMUST be signed with RSA.\n",
      "id": "1a59b27b66394644",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 114,
      "quote": "It MUST be signed with RSA.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "ECDHE_RSA               Certificate MUST contain an\nRSA public key authorized for\nuse in digital signatures.\n",
      "id": "9dd4095f9a9b529c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 121,
      "quote": "ECDHE_RSA               Certificate MUST contain an RSA public key authorized for use in digital signatures.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It\nMUST be signed with RSA.\n",
      "id": "7a82e402be2e4884",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 129,
      "quote": "It MUST be signed with RSA.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the client has used a\nSupported Elliptic Curves Extension, the public key in the server's\ncertificate MUST respect the client's choice of elliptic curves; in\nparticular, the public key MUST employ a named curve (not the same\ncurve as an explicit curve) unless the client has indicated support\nfor explicit curves of the appropriate type.\n",
      "id": "157308eb444662d0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 136,
      "quote": "If the client has used a Supported Elliptic Curves Extension, the public key in the server's certificate MUST respect the client's choice of elliptic curves; in particular, the public key MUST employ a named curve (not the same curve as an explicit curve) unless the client has indicated support for explicit curves of the appropriate type.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the client has used a\nSupported Elliptic Curves Extension, the public key in the server's\ncertificate MUST respect the client's choice of elliptic curves; in\nparticular, the public key MUST employ a named curve (not the same\ncurve as an explicit curve) unless the client has indicated support\nfor explicit curves of the appropriate type.\n",
      "id": "97184be452ceda7c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 147,
      "quote": "If the client has used a Supported Elliptic Curves Extension, the public key in the server's certificate MUST respect the client's choice of elliptic curves; in particular, the public key MUST employ a named curve (not the same curve as an explicit curve) unless the client has indicated support for explicit curves of the appropriate type.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the client has used\na Supported Point Formats Extension, both the server's public key\npoint and (in the case of an explicit curve) the curve's base point\nMUST respect the client's choice of point formats.\n",
      "id": "71140e180c20852c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 158,
      "quote": "If the client has used a Supported Point Formats Extension, both the server's public key point and (in the case of an explicit curve) the curve's base point MUST respect the client's choice of point formats.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "(A server that\ncannot satisfy these requirements MUST NOT choose an ECC cipher suite\nin its ServerHello message.)\n",
      "id": "5e052b4747a84922",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 167,
      "quote": "(A server that cannot satisfy these requirements MUST NOT choose an ECC cipher suite in its ServerHello message.)",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This option\nSHOULD be used when applicable.\n",
      "id": "e2e2ba4132d3280d",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 204,
      "quote": "This option SHOULD be used when applicable.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This byte string may represent an elliptic curve point\nin uncompressed or compressed format; it MUST conform to what the\nclient has requested through a Supported Point Formats Extension\nif this extension was used.\n",
      "id": "19c368432c5f9c2f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 211,
      "quote": "This byte string may represent an elliptic curve point in uncompressed or compressed format; it MUST conform to what the client has requested through a Supported Point Formats Extension if this extension was used.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "ECDSA_sign              Certificate MUST contain an\nECDSA-capable public key and\nbe signed with ECDSA.\n",
      "id": "a1667e23ae4c93fa",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 67,
      "quote": "ECDSA_sign              Certificate MUST contain an ECDSA-capable public key and be signed with ECDSA.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "ECDSA_fixed_ECDH        Certificate MUST contain an\nECDH-capable public key on the\nsame elliptic curve as the server's\nlong-term ECDH key.\n",
      "id": "3bd27230f5cdaac3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 75,
      "quote": "ECDSA_fixed_ECDH        Certificate MUST contain an ECDH-capable public key on the same elliptic curve as the server's long-term ECDH key.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This certificate\nMUST be signed with ECDSA.\n",
      "id": "1d76477d091e47af",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 84,
      "quote": "This certificate MUST be signed with ECDSA.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "RSA_fixed_ECDH          Certificate MUST contain an\nECDH-capable public key on the\nsame elliptic curve as the server's\nlong-term ECDH key.\n",
      "id": "879816bc707532b1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 91,
      "quote": "RSA_fixed_ECDH          Certificate MUST contain an ECDH-capable public key on the same elliptic curve as the server's long-term ECDH key.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This certificate\nMUST be signed with RSA.\n",
      "id": "73e6371fde16b55c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 100,
      "quote": "This certificate MUST be signed with RSA.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Here, the format MUST\nconform to what the server has requested through a Supported Point\nFormats Extension if this extension was used, and MUST be\nuncompressed if this extension was not used.\n",
      "id": "7e270f600f45ea85",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 65,
      "quote": "Here, the format MUST conform to what the server has requested through a Supported Point Formats Extension if this extension was used, and MUST be uncompressed if this extension was not used.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Here, the format MUST\nconform to what the server has requested through a Supported Point\nFormats Extension if this extension was used, and MUST be\nuncompressed if this extension was not used.\n",
      "id": "55800e31287459e7",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 74,
      "quote": "Here, the format MUST conform to what the server has requested through a Supported Point Formats Extension if this extension was used, and MUST be uncompressed if this extension was not used.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "X.509 certificates containing ECC public keys or signed using ECDSA\nMUST comply with [14] or another RFC that replaces or extends it.\n",
      "id": "2588e9006c79f32b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 10,
      "quote": "X.509 certificates containing ECC public keys or signed using ECDSA MUST comply with [14] or another RFC that replaces or extends it.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients SHOULD use the elliptic curve domain parameters recommended\nin ANSI X9.62 [7], FIPS 186-2 [11], and SEC 2 [13].\n",
      "id": "eb94fefca361afd8",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 17,
      "quote": "Clients SHOULD use the elliptic curve domain parameters recommended in ANSI X9.62 [7], FIPS 186-2 [11], and SEC 2 [13].",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-5.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-5.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Server implementations SHOULD support all of the following cipher\nsuites, and client implementations SHOULD support at least one of\nthem: TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA,\nTLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA,\nTLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA, and\nTLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA.\n",
      "id": "8045312868227995",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 52,
      "quote": "Server implementations SHOULD support all of the following cipher suites, and client implementations SHOULD support at least one of them: TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA, TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA, TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA, and TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Server implementations SHOULD support all of the following cipher\nsuites, and client implementations SHOULD support at least one of\nthem: TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA,\nTLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA,\nTLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA, and\nTLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA.\n",
      "id": "83abcb2de07c146d",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 63,
      "quote": "Server implementations SHOULD support all of the following cipher suites, and client implementations SHOULD support at least one of them: TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA, TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA, TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA, and TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492/section-6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS_NULL_WITH_NULL_NULL is specified and is the initial state of a\nTLS connection during the first handshake on that channel, but MUST\nNOT be negotiated, as it provides no more protection than an\nunsecured connection.\n",
      "id": "43eb6e76cee468c0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 103,
      "quote": "TLS_NULL_WITH_NULL_NULL is specified and is the initial state of a TLS connection during the first handshake on that channel, but MUST NOT be negotiated, as it provides no more protection than an unsecured connection.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-A.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Using this mode therefore is of limited use: These\ncipher suites MUST NOT be used by TLS 1.2 implementations unless the\napplication layer has specifically requested to allow anonymous key\nexchange.\n",
      "id": "6b5bc3058008c1fe",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 112,
      "quote": "Using this mode therefore is of limited use: These cipher suites MUST NOT be used by TLS 1.2 implementations unless the application layer has specifically requested to allow anonymous key exchange.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-A.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the version chosen by the server is not supported by the client\n(or not acceptable), the client MUST send a \"protocol_version\" alert\nmessage and close the connection.\n",
      "id": "700bdc784a79faa2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 71,
      "quote": "If the version chosen by the server is not supported by the client (or not acceptable), the client MUST send a \"protocol_version\" alert message and close the connection.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-E.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a TLS server receives a ClientHello containing a version number\ngreater than the highest version supported by the server, it MUST\nreply according to the highest version supported by the server.\n",
      "id": "2a81384655a2beda",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 79,
      "quote": "If a TLS server receives a ClientHello containing a version number greater than the highest version supported by the server, it MUST reply according to the highest version supported by the server.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-E.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If server supports (or is\nwilling to use) only versions greater than client_version, it MUST\nsend a \"protocol_version\" alert message and close the connection.\n",
      "id": "ae098181d88e51e5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 87,
      "quote": "If server supports (or is willing to use) only versions greater than client_version, it MUST send a \"protocol_version\" alert message and close the connection.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-E.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Whenever a client already knows the highest protocol version known to\na server (for example, when resuming a session), it SHOULD initiate\nthe connection in that native protocol.\n",
      "id": "e43e96edec60f88c",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 95,
      "quote": "Whenever a client already knows the highest protocol version known to a server (for example, when resuming a session), it SHOULD initiate the connection in that native protocol.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-E.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Thus, TLS servers\ncompliant with this specification MUST accept any value {03,XX} as\nthe record layer version number for ClientHello.\n",
      "id": "0d1db0d903edb840",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 103,
      "quote": "Thus, TLS servers compliant with this specification MUST accept any value {03,XX} as the record layer version number for ClientHello.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-E.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS clients that wish to negotiate with older servers MAY send any\nvalue {03,XX} as the record layer version number.\n",
      "id": "84a474ad5017e375",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 111,
      "quote": "TLS clients that wish to negotiate with older servers MAY send any value {03,XX} as the record layer version number.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-E.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS 1.2 clients that wish to support SSL 2.0 servers MUST send\nversion 2.0 CLIENT-HELLO messages defined in [SSL2].\n",
      "id": "34372a80eb54bcf0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 85,
      "quote": "TLS 1.2 clients that wish to support SSL 2.0 servers MUST send version 2.0 CLIENT-HELLO messages defined in [SSL2].",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-E.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The message\nMUST contain the same version number as would be used for ordinary\nClientHello, and MUST encode the supported TLS cipher suites in the\nCIPHER-SPECS-DATA field as described below.\n",
      "id": "5ef315394488d8b8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 92,
      "quote": "The message MUST contain the same version number as would be used for ordinary ClientHello, and MUST encode the supported TLS cipher suites in the CIPHER-SPECS-DATA field as described below.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-E.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The message\nMUST contain the same version number as would be used for ordinary\nClientHello, and MUST encode the supported TLS cipher suites in the\nCIPHER-SPECS-DATA field as described below.\n",
      "id": "59980e5392cfec97",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 101,
      "quote": "The message MUST contain the same version number as would be used for ordinary ClientHello, and MUST encode the supported TLS cipher suites in the CIPHER-SPECS-DATA field as described below.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-E.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS 1.2 clients SHOULD NOT support SSL 2.0.\n",
      "id": "ba89ff3ae5129d95",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 110,
      "quote": "TLS 1.2 clients SHOULD NOT support SSL 2.0.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-E.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "However, even TLS servers that do not support SSL 2.0 MAY accept\nversion 2.0 CLIENT-HELLO messages.\n",
      "id": "e3c53dc950e66467",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 116,
      "quote": "However, even TLS servers that do not support SSL 2.0 MAY accept version 2.0 CLIENT-HELLO messages.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-E.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Note that this message MUST be sent directly on the\nwire, not wrapped as a TLS record.\n",
      "id": "38f61913600cfb23",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 123,
      "quote": "Note that this message MUST be sent directly on the wire, not wrapped as a TLS record.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-E.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "msg_length\nThe highest bit MUST be 1; the remaining bits contain the length\nof the following data in bytes.\n",
      "id": "c3ec5e81b3f4ac73",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 130,
      "quote": "msg_length The highest bit MUST be 1; the remaining bits contain the length of the following data in bytes.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-E.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The value MUST be 1.\n",
      "id": "9fe107e243596aab",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 138,
      "quote": "The value MUST be 1.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-E.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It\ncannot be zero and MUST be a multiple of the V2CipherSpec length\n(3).\n",
      "id": "5eacd0f07bd6be9a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 144,
      "quote": "It cannot be zero and MUST be a multiple of the V2CipherSpec length (3).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-E.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "session_id_length\nThis field MUST have a value of zero for a client that claims to\nsupport TLS 1.2.\n",
      "id": "c31daa890e6cf1ff",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 152,
      "quote": "session_id_length This field MUST have a value of zero for a client that claims to support TLS 1.2.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-E.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When using the SSLv2 backward-\ncompatible handshake the client SHOULD use a 32-byte challenge.\n",
      "id": "218e076aa986934c",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 160,
      "quote": "When using the SSLv2 backward- compatible handshake the client SHOULD use a 32-byte challenge.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-E.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "session_id\nThis field MUST be empty.\n",
      "id": "bfec6a115803841b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 167,
      "quote": "session_id This field MUST be empty.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-E.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Note: Requests to resume a TLS session MUST use a TLS client hello.\n",
      "id": "b163a48027855aeb",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 174,
      "quote": "Note: Requests to resume a TLS session MUST use a TLS client hello.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-E.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When TLS clients fall back to Version 2.0 compatibility mode, they\nMUST use special PKCS#1 block formatting.\n",
      "id": "787cb2debed37c49",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 23,
      "quote": "When TLS clients fall back to Version 2.0 compatibility mode, they MUST use special PKCS#1 block formatting.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-E.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When a client negotiates SSL 2.0 but also supports TLS, it MUST set\nthe right-hand (least-significant) 8 random bytes of the PKCS padding\n(not including the terminal null of the padding) for the RSA\nencryption of the ENCRYPTED-KEY-DATA field of the CLIENT-MASTER-KEY\nto 0x03 (the other padding bytes are random).\n",
      "id": "8f6b47bc96b7fe4d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 30,
      "quote": "When a client negotiates SSL 2.0 but also supports TLS, it MUST set the right-hand (least-significant) 8 random bytes of the PKCS padding (not including the terminal null of the padding) for the RSA encryption of the ENCRYPTED-KEY-DATA field of the CLIENT-MASTER-KEY to 0x03 (the other padding bytes are random).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-E.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When a TLS-capable server negotiates SSL 2.0 it SHOULD, after\ndecrypting the ENCRYPTED-KEY-DATA field, check that these 8 padding\nbytes are 0x03.\n",
      "id": "d3949525a2c3c7e4",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 40,
      "quote": "When a TLS-capable server negotiates SSL 2.0 it SHOULD, after decrypting the ENCRYPTED-KEY-DATA field, check that these 8 padding bytes are 0x03.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-E.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If they are not, the server SHOULD generate a random\nvalue for SECRET-KEY-DATA, and continue the handshake (which will\neventually fail since the keys will not match).\n",
      "id": "a827e49a715af01c",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 48,
      "quote": "If they are not, the server SHOULD generate a random value for SECRET-KEY-DATA, and continue the handshake (which will eventually fail since the keys will not match).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-E.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations SHOULD follow the\nguidelines found in [SUBGROUP].\n",
      "id": "bb454a2ed5201187",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 53,
      "quote": "Implementations SHOULD follow the guidelines found in [SUBGROUP].",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-F.1.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-F.1.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations SHOULD generate a\nnew X for each handshake when using DHE cipher suites.\n",
      "id": "4f21bc8b0746d419",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 60,
      "quote": "Implementations SHOULD generate a new X for each handshake when using DHE cipher suites.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-F.1.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-F.1.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The client SHOULD also verify that the DH public\nexponent appears to be of adequate size.\n",
      "id": "c46cb973f6008076",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 67,
      "quote": "The client SHOULD also verify that the DH public exponent appears to be of adequate size.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-F.1.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-F.1.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server MAY choose\nto assist the client by providing a known group, such as those\ndefined in [IKEALG] or [MODP].\n",
      "id": "bc5dd7cbcb6e59da",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 74,
      "quote": "The server MAY choose to assist the client by providing a known group, such as those defined in [IKEALG] or [MODP].",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/appendix-F.1.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-F.1.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  Alerts MUST now be sent in many cases.\n",
      "id": "60042970de80a81c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 61,
      "quote": "-  Alerts MUST now be sent in many cases.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  After a certificate_request, if no certificates are available,\nclients now MUST send an empty certificate list.\n",
      "id": "83388348709803ce",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 67,
      "quote": "-  After a certificate_request, if no certificates are available, clients now MUST send an empty certificate list.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  Support for the SSLv2 backward-compatible hello is now a MAY, not\na SHOULD, with sending it a SHOULD NOT.\n",
      "id": "316e0cee9e946d52",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 74,
      "quote": "-  Support for the SSLv2 backward-compatible hello is now a MAY, not a SHOULD, with sending it a SHOULD NOT.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  Support for the SSLv2 backward-compatible hello is now a MAY, not\na SHOULD, with sending it a SHOULD NOT.\n",
      "id": "bb98fc5ca7054716",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 81,
      "quote": "-  Support for the SSLv2 backward-compatible hello is now a MAY, not a SHOULD, with sending it a SHOULD NOT.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Support will probably\nbecome a SHOULD NOT in the future.\n",
      "id": "beac1fa5707c376b",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 88,
      "quote": "Support will probably become a SHOULD NOT in the future.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "As\ndiscussed in [PKCS1], the DigestInfo MUST be DER-encoded [X680]\n[X690].\n",
      "id": "11b05fbff9ef35e9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 101,
      "quote": "As discussed in [PKCS1], the DigestInfo MUST be DER-encoded [X680] [X690].",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-4.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-4.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For hash algorithms without parameters (which includes\nSHA-1), the DigestInfo.AlgorithmIdentifier.parameters field MUST be\nNULL, but implementations MUST accept both without parameters and\nwith NULL parameters.\n",
      "id": "e0b488389fade6e1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 109,
      "quote": "For hash algorithms without parameters (which includes SHA-1), the DigestInfo.AlgorithmIdentifier.parameters field MUST be NULL, but implementations MUST accept both without parameters and with NULL parameters.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-4.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-4.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For hash algorithms without parameters (which includes\nSHA-1), the DigestInfo.AlgorithmIdentifier.parameters field MUST be\nNULL, but implementations MUST accept both without parameters and\nwith NULL parameters.\n",
      "id": "03a05b577e467097",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 118,
      "quote": "For hash algorithms without parameters (which includes SHA-1), the DigestInfo.AlgorithmIdentifier.parameters field MUST be NULL, but implementations MUST accept both without parameters and with NULL parameters.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-4.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-4.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Other cipher suites MAY define their\nown MAC constructions, if needed.\n",
      "id": "2768a736183bc486",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "Other cipher suites MAY define their own MAC constructions, if needed.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "New cipher suites MUST explicitly specify a\nPRF and, in general, SHOULD use the TLS PRF with SHA-256 or a\nstronger standard hash function.\n",
      "id": "4e02e41ac2dfcc1a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 63,
      "quote": "New cipher suites MUST explicitly specify a PRF and, in general, SHOULD use the TLS PRF with SHA-256 or a stronger standard hash function.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "These current states MUST be updated for each\nrecord processed.\n",
      "id": "ed7a6dcdb3af45ec",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 140,
      "quote": "These current states MUST be updated for each record processed.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The sequence\nnumber MUST be set to zero whenever a connection state is made the\nactive state.\n",
      "id": "39ef6bb37553493b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 147,
      "quote": "The sequence number MUST be set to zero whenever a connection state is made the active state.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A sequence number is incremented after each\nrecord: specifically, the first record transmitted under a\nparticular connection state MUST use sequence number 0.\n",
      "id": "15f578a14bba092e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 155,
      "quote": "A sequence number is incremented after each record: specifically, the first record transmitted under a particular connection state MUST use sequence number 0.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Client\nmessage boundaries are not preserved in the record layer (i.e.,\nmultiple client messages of the same ContentType MAY be coalesced\ninto a single TLSPlaintext record, or a single message MAY be\nfragmented across several records).\n",
      "id": "1285579fbe7e3e95",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "Client message boundaries are not preserved in the record layer (i.e., multiple client messages of the same ContentType MAY be coalesced into a single TLSPlaintext record, or a single message MAY be fragmented across several records).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Client\nmessage boundaries are not preserved in the record layer (i.e.,\nmultiple client messages of the same ContentType MAY be coalesced\ninto a single TLSPlaintext record, or a single message MAY be\nfragmented across several records).\n",
      "id": "0e0b13b8d68c9422",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 74,
      "quote": "Client message boundaries are not preserved in the record layer (i.e., multiple client messages of the same ContentType MAY be coalesced into a single TLSPlaintext record, or a single message MAY be fragmented across several records).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The\nlength MUST NOT exceed 2^14.\n",
      "id": "6f82f89485aa012f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 84,
      "quote": "The length MUST NOT exceed 2^14.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations MUST NOT send zero-length fragments of Handshake,\nAlert, or ChangeCipherSpec content types.\n",
      "id": "62b89863c56b012d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 91,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST NOT send zero-length fragments of Handshake, Alert, or ChangeCipherSpec content types.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Zero-length fragments of\nApplication data MAY be sent as they are potentially useful as a\ntraffic analysis countermeasure.\n",
      "id": "29a12ec1ef750300",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 98,
      "quote": "Zero-length fragments of Application data MAY be sent as they are potentially useful as a traffic analysis countermeasure.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Note: Data of different TLS record layer content types MAY be\ninterleaved.\n",
      "id": "cccbcd4c4bf50f22",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 106,
      "quote": "Note: Data of different TLS record layer content types MAY be interleaved.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "However, records MUST be\ndelivered to the network in the same order as they are protected by\nthe record layer.\n",
      "id": "17aa580891ce38a8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 113,
      "quote": "However, records MUST be delivered to the network in the same order as they are protected by the record layer.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Recipients MUST receive and process interleaved\napplication layer traffic during handshakes subsequent to the first\none on a connection.\n",
      "id": "cecdfd1704812b37",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 121,
      "quote": "Recipients MUST receive and process interleaved application layer traffic during handshakes subsequent to the first one on a connection.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the decompression function encounters a\nTLSCompressed.fragment that would decompress to a length in excess of\n2^14 bytes, it MUST report a fatal decompression failure error.\n",
      "id": "0c0d73c4645ecc70",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 39,
      "quote": "If the decompression function encounters a TLSCompressed.fragment that would decompress to a length in excess of 2^14 bytes, it MUST report a fatal decompression failure error.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The length MUST NOT exceed 2^14 + 1024.\n",
      "id": "792e06e5f5c2a1c3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "The length MUST NOT exceed 2^14 + 1024.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "IV\nThe Initialization Vector (IV) SHOULD be chosen at random, and\nMUST be unpredictable.\n",
      "id": "06569ab3d40b212c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 85,
      "quote": "IV The Initialization Vector (IV) SHOULD be chosen at random, and MUST be unpredictable.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.2.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The\npadding MAY be any length up to 255 bytes, as long as it results\nin the TLSCiphertext.length being an integral multiple of the\nblock length.\n",
      "id": "bd83bd895e44a8f1",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 93,
      "quote": "The padding MAY be any length up to 255 bytes, as long as it results in the TLSCiphertext.length being an integral multiple of the block length.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.2.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each uint8 in the padding data\nvector MUST be filled with the padding length value.\n",
      "id": "e576942de1fc8e78",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 102,
      "quote": "Each uint8 in the padding data vector MUST be filled with the padding length value.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.2.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The receiver\nMUST check this padding and MUST use the bad_record_mac alert to\nindicate padding errors.\n",
      "id": "6d319981ad2afa9b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 109,
      "quote": "The receiver MUST check this padding and MUST use the bad_record_mac alert to indicate padding errors.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.2.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The receiver\nMUST check this padding and MUST use the bad_record_mac alert to\nindicate padding errors.\n",
      "id": "e4bab8ef7d16eb3e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 117,
      "quote": "The receiver MUST check this padding and MUST use the bad_record_mac alert to indicate padding errors.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.2.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "padding_length\nThe padding length MUST be such that the total size of the\nGenericBlockCipher structure is a multiple of the cipher's block\nlength.\n",
      "id": "410205111e1420bd",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 125,
      "quote": "padding_length The padding length MUST be such that the total size of the GenericBlockCipher structure is a multiple of the cipher's block length.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.2.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In order to defend against this attack, implementations\nMUST ensure that record processing time is essentially the same\nwhether or not the padding is correct.\n",
      "id": "4d34f0e911fabe13",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 134,
      "quote": "In order to defend against this attack, implementations MUST ensure that record processing time is essentially the same whether or not the padding is correct.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.2.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each AEAD cipher suite MUST specify how the nonce supplied to the\nAEAD operation is constructed, and what is the length of the\nGenericAEADCipher.nonce_explicit part.\n",
      "id": "6e4c5b4a522f32d3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 65,
      "quote": "Each AEAD cipher suite MUST specify how the nonce supplied to the AEAD operation is constructed, and what is the length of the GenericAEADCipher.nonce_explicit part.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.2.3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In this case, the implicit part SHOULD be derived\nfrom key_block as client_write_iv and server_write_iv (as described\nin Section 6.3), and the explicit part is included in\nGenericAEAEDCipher.nonce_explicit.\n",
      "id": "5378930e4e0fb906",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 73,
      "quote": "In this case, the implicit part SHOULD be derived from key_block as client_write_iv and server_write_iv (as described in Section 6.3), and the explicit part is included in GenericAEAEDCipher.nonce_explicit.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.2.3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each\nAEAD cipher MUST NOT produce an expansion of greater than 1024 bytes.\n",
      "id": "877e3225484f72ea",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 82,
      "quote": "Each AEAD cipher MUST NOT produce an expansion of greater than 1024 bytes.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.2.3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the decryption fails, a fatal bad_record_mac alert MUST be\ngenerated.\n",
      "id": "6d73ac65ab70ac99",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 89,
      "quote": "If the decryption fails, a fatal bad_record_mac alert MUST be generated.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.2.3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The length MUST NOT exceed 2^14 + 2048.\n",
      "id": "226509c18311a7b5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 35,
      "quote": "The length MUST NOT exceed 2^14 + 2048.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations MUST NOT send record types not defined in this\ndocument unless negotiated by some extension.\n",
      "id": "a6a10c1d470ab4c2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 37,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST NOT send record types not defined in this document unless negotiated by some extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a TLS\nimplementation receives an unexpected record type, it MUST send an\nunexpected_message alert.\n",
      "id": "fa17c76c3f783bd8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "If a TLS implementation receives an unexpected record type, it MUST send an unexpected_message alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Immediately after sending this message, the sender MUST instruct the\nrecord layer to make the write pending state the write active state.\n",
      "id": "f5d4fbaf2fcac628",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 37,
      "quote": "Immediately after sending this message, the sender MUST instruct the record layer to make the write pending state the write active state.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "However, once the ChangeCipherSpec has been sent, the\nnew CipherSpec MUST be used.\n",
      "id": "b8ca8c391dcedff6",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "However, once the ChangeCipherSpec has been sent, the new CipherSpec MUST be used.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Thus, a small window of time,\nduring which the recipient must buffer the data, MAY exist.\n",
      "id": "47b3ad3a92ef9778",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "Thus, a small window of time, during which the recipient must buffer the data, MAY exist.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The other party MUST respond with a close_notify\nalert of its own and close down the connection immediately,\ndiscarding any pending writes.\n",
      "id": "0ffef60a003d571d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 43,
      "quote": "The other party MUST respond with a close_notify alert of its own and close down the connection immediately, discarding any pending writes.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the application protocol will not\ntransfer any additional data, but will only close the underlying\ntransport connection, then the implementation MAY choose to close the\ntransport without waiting for the responding close_notify.\n",
      "id": "c40beeccf0397ecc",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "If the application protocol will not transfer any additional data, but will only close the underlying transport connection, then the implementation MAY choose to close the transport without waiting for the responding close_notify.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers and clients MUST\nforget any session-identifiers, keys, and secrets associated with a\nfailed connection.\n",
      "id": "fd2f5fa3f7ee1a9a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 171,
      "quote": "Servers and clients MUST forget any session-identifiers, keys, and secrets associated with a failed connection.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Thus, any connection terminated with a fatal\nalert MUST NOT be resumed.\n",
      "id": "8fc87e957b240662",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 179,
      "quote": "Thus, any connection terminated with a fatal alert MUST NOT be resumed.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Whenever an implementation encounters a condition which is defined as\na fatal alert, it MUST send the appropriate alert prior to closing\nthe connection.\n",
      "id": "be3dd6c9a9735e88",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 186,
      "quote": "Whenever an implementation encounters a condition which is defined as a fatal alert, it MUST send the appropriate alert prior to closing the connection.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For all errors where an alert level is not\nexplicitly specified, the sending party MAY determine at its\ndiscretion whether to treat this as a fatal error or not.\n",
      "id": "458ee2817c1ed8c9",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 194,
      "quote": "For all errors where an alert level is not explicitly specified, the sending party MAY determine at its discretion whether to treat this as a fatal error or not.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the\nimplementation chooses to send an alert but intends to close the\nconnection immediately afterwards, it MUST send that alert at the\nfatal alert level.\n",
      "id": "d0474c7b374c603f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 202,
      "quote": "If the implementation chooses to send an alert but intends to close the connection immediately afterwards, it MUST send that alert at the fatal alert level.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the receiving party decides\nnot to proceed with the connection (e.g., after having received a\nno_renegotiation alert that it is not willing to accept), it SHOULD\nsend a fatal alert to terminate the connection.\n",
      "id": "6973705f113ac27b",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 211,
      "quote": "If the receiving party decides not to proceed with the connection (e.g., after having received a no_renegotiation alert that it is not willing to accept), it SHOULD send a fatal alert to terminate the connection.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This alert also MUST be returned if an alert is sent because\na TLSCiphertext decrypted in an invalid way: either it wasn't an\neven multiple of the block length, or its padding values, when\nchecked, weren't correct.\n",
      "id": "92cfd2d14eeb3e57",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 220,
      "quote": "This alert also MUST be returned if an alert is sent because a TLSCiphertext decrypted in an invalid way: either it wasn't an even multiple of the block length, or its padding values, when checked, weren't correct.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It MUST\nNOT be sent by compliant implementations.\n",
      "id": "8081cbefd2f8f292",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 229,
      "quote": "It MUST NOT be sent by compliant implementations.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It MUST\nNOT be sent by compliant implementations.\n",
      "id": "a7e12688f6c1ec3e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 236,
      "quote": "It MUST NOT be sent by compliant implementations.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It MUST NOT\nbe sent by compliant implementations.\n",
      "id": "09de6a10d5779ede",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 243,
      "quote": "It MUST NOT be sent by compliant implementations.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In this case, other connections corresponding to the\nsession may continue, but the session identifier MUST be invalidated,\npreventing the failed session from being used to establish new\nconnections.\n",
      "id": "f98bff015c5eb8c8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 52,
      "quote": "In this case, other connections corresponding to the session may continue, but the session identifier MUST be invalidated, preventing the failed session from being used to establish new connections.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This secret MUST be quite long; currently defined key\nexchange methods exchange secrets that range from 46 bytes upwards.\n",
      "id": "0c85eb492c7ca349",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 153,
      "quote": "This secret MUST be quite long; currently defined key exchange methods exchange secrets that range from 46 bytes upwards.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the server has sent\na CertificateRequest message, the client MUST send the Certificate\nmessage.\n",
      "id": "9bfa5afd6c13422b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 160,
      "quote": "If the server has sent a CertificateRequest message, the client MUST send the Certificate message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "(See\nflow chart below.)  Application data MUST NOT be sent prior to the\ncompletion of the first handshake (before a cipher suite other than\nTLS_NULL_WITH_NULL_NULL is established).\n",
      "id": "c005b19cdcae83f3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 168,
      "quote": "(See flow chart below.)  Application data MUST NOT be sent prior to the completion of the first handshake (before a cipher suite other than TLS_NULL_WITH_NULL_NULL is established).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "At this point, both\nclient and server MUST send ChangeCipherSpec messages and proceed\ndirectly to Finished messages.\n",
      "id": "6b85dca03ab54687",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 177,
      "quote": "At this point, both client and server MUST send ChangeCipherSpec messages and proceed directly to Finished messages.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once the re-establishment is\ncomplete, the client and server MAY begin to exchange application\nlayer data.\n",
      "id": "ee9523f15d8c7808",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 185,
      "quote": "Once the re-establishment is complete, the client and server MAY begin to exchange application layer data.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The HelloRequest message MAY be sent by the server at any time.\n",
      "id": "5f42051f23c00086",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "The HelloRequest message MAY be sent by the server at any time.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers SHOULD NOT send a\nHelloRequest immediately upon the client's initial connection.\n",
      "id": "37e7cebc4e1d2ad4",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "Servers SHOULD NOT send a HelloRequest immediately upon the client's initial connection.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This message MAY be ignored by\nthe client if it does not wish to renegotiate a session, or the\nclient may, if it wishes, respond with a no_renegotiation alert.\n",
      "id": "0b172f4662c85b44",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "This message MAY be ignored by the client if it does not wish to renegotiate a session, or the client may, if it wishes, respond with a no_renegotiation alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "After sending a HelloRequest, servers SHOULD NOT repeat the\nrequest until the subsequent handshake negotiation is complete.\n",
      "id": "d89315937a12a46b",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 62,
      "quote": "After sending a HelloRequest, servers SHOULD NOT repeat the request until the subsequent handshake negotiation is complete.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This message MUST NOT be included in the message hashes that are\nmaintained throughout the handshake and used in the Finished messages\nand the certificate verify message.\n",
      "id": "f2020bbb3b60ef48",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 69,
      "quote": "This message MUST NOT be included in the message hashes that are maintained throughout the handshake and used in the Finished messages and the certificate verify message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The session identifier MAY be from an earlier connection,\n",
      "id": "200a2e1855b51311",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 153,
      "quote": "The session identifier MAY be from an earlier connection,",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Warning: Because the SessionID is transmitted without encryption or\nimmediate MAC protection, servers MUST NOT place confidential\ninformation in session identifiers or let the contents of fake\nsession identifiers cause any breach of security.\n",
      "id": "a62743a6a9b8bc3f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 159,
      "quote": "Warning: Because the SessionID is transmitted without encryption or immediate MAC protection, servers MUST NOT place confidential information in session identifiers or let the contents of fake session identifiers cause any breach of security.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the list contains cipher\nsuites the server does not recognize, support, or wish to use, the\nserver MUST ignore those cipher suites, and process the remaining\nones as usual.\n",
      "id": "a151d280cddf618b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 168,
      "quote": "If the list contains cipher suites the server does not recognize, support, or wish to use, the server MUST ignore those cipher suites, and process the remaining ones as usual.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This SHOULD be the latest\n(highest valued) version supported by the client.\n",
      "id": "2d06e63409f3046f",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 177,
      "quote": "This SHOULD be the latest (highest valued) version supported by the client.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the\nsession_id field is not empty (implying a session resumption\nrequest), this vector MUST include at least the cipher_suite from\nthat session.\n",
      "id": "8b7e7e4e5230bd25",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 184,
      "quote": "If the session_id field is not empty (implying a session resumption request), this vector MUST include at least the cipher_suite from that session.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the session_id field is not empty\n(implying a session resumption request), it MUST include the\n",
      "id": "f847cc4faea1d20d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 193,
      "quote": "If the session_id field is not empty (implying a session resumption request), it MUST include the",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This vector MUST contain,\nand all implementations MUST support, CompressionMethod.null.\n",
      "id": "cbdc88a490502d3a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 200,
      "quote": "This vector MUST contain, and all implementations MUST support, CompressionMethod.null.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This vector MUST contain,\nand all implementations MUST support, CompressionMethod.null.\n",
      "id": "4820146a0f84a3b5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 207,
      "quote": "This vector MUST contain, and all implementations MUST support, CompressionMethod.null.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "extensions\nClients MAY request extended functionality from servers by sending\ndata in the extensions field.\n",
      "id": "a206783c19d6ff71",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 214,
      "quote": "extensions Clients MAY request extended functionality from servers by sending data in the extensions field.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MUST accept ClientHello\nmessages both with and without the extensions field, and (as for all\nother messages) it MUST check that the amount of data in the message\nprecisely matches one of these formats; if not, then it MUST send a\nfatal \"decode_error\" alert.\n",
      "id": "a1a6a0d9233d3d76",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 222,
      "quote": "A server MUST accept ClientHello messages both with and without the extensions field, and (as for all other messages) it MUST check that the amount of data in the message precisely matches one of these formats; if not, then it MUST send a fatal \"decode_error\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In the event that a client requests additional functionality using\nextensions, and this functionality is not supplied by the server, the\nclient MAY abort the handshake.\n",
      "id": "e9b693e4352a0c5d",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 232,
      "quote": "In the event that a client requests additional functionality using extensions, and this functionality is not supplied by the server, the client MAY abort the handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MUST accept ClientHello\nmessages both with and without the extensions field, and (as for all\nother messages) it MUST check that the amount of data in the message\nprecisely matches one of these formats; if not, then it MUST send a\nfatal \"decode_error\" alert.\n",
      "id": "d7aea9a036e5534e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 240,
      "quote": "A server MUST accept ClientHello messages both with and without the extensions field, and (as for all other messages) it MUST check that the amount of data in the message precisely matches one of these formats; if not, then it MUST send a fatal \"decode_error\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MUST accept ClientHello\nmessages both with and without the extensions field, and (as for all\nother messages) it MUST check that the amount of data in the message\nprecisely matches one of these formats; if not, then it MUST send a\nfatal \"decode_error\" alert.\n",
      "id": "397f403cf4242b49",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 250,
      "quote": "A server MUST accept ClientHello messages both with and without the extensions field, and (as for all other messages) it MUST check that the amount of data in the message precisely matches one of these formats; if not, then it MUST send a fatal \"decode_error\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "random\nThis structure is generated by the server and MUST be\nindependently generated from the ClientHello.random.\n",
      "id": "2cd8e55f2d375205",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 75,
      "quote": "random This structure is generated by the server and MUST be independently generated from the ClientHello.random.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MUST be prepared to do a full\nnegotiation -- including negotiating new cipher suites -- during\nany handshake.\n",
      "id": "daf192020cd1a6e6",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 83,
      "quote": "Clients MUST be prepared to do a full negotiation -- including negotiating new cipher suites -- during any handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It MUST NOT appear in this extension.\n",
      "id": "4b6c20a0f6e7611b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 91,
      "quote": "It MUST NOT appear in this extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the client supports only the default hash and signature algorithms\n(listed in this section), it MAY omit the signature_algorithms\nextension.\n",
      "id": "76dc13f454f8e761",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 97,
      "quote": "If the client supports only the default hash and signature algorithms (listed in this section), it MAY omit the signature_algorithms extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the client does not support the default algorithms, or\nsupports other hash and signature algorithms (and it is willing to\nuse them for verifying messages sent by the server, i.e., server\ncertificates and server key exchange), it MUST send the\n",
      "id": "de029ba58ae9eec3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 105,
      "quote": "If the client does not support the default algorithms, or supports other hash and signature algorithms (and it is willing to use them for verifying messages sent by the server, i.e., server certificates and server key exchange), it MUST send the",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the client does not send the signature_algorithms extension, the\nserver MUST do the following:\n",
      "id": "b2cccc271a88f299",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 114,
      "quote": "If the client does not send the signature_algorithms extension, the server MUST do the following:",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MUST NOT offer it if they are offering prior versions.\n",
      "id": "83415ed0f767acb5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 121,
      "quote": "Clients MUST NOT offer it if they are offering prior versions.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MUST NOT send this extension.\n",
      "id": "1ef059cae8623007",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 127,
      "quote": "Servers MUST NOT send this extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS servers MUST support\nreceiving this extension.\n",
      "id": "cc798472ea927b80",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 133,
      "quote": "TLS servers MUST support receiving this extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An extension type MUST NOT appear in the ServerHello unless the same\nextension type appeared in the corresponding ClientHello.\n",
      "id": "1fa0160f9b0c9799",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 94,
      "quote": "An extension type MUST NOT appear in the ServerHello unless the same extension type appeared in the corresponding ClientHello.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a\nclient receives an extension type in ServerHello that it did not\nrequest in the associated ClientHello, it MUST abort the handshake\nwith an unsupported_extension fatal alert.\n",
      "id": "3cc3c5427e233106",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 101,
      "quote": "If a client receives an extension type in ServerHello that it did not request in the associated ClientHello, it MUST abort the handshake with an unsupported_extension fatal alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When multiple extensions of different types are present in the\nClientHello or ServerHello messages, the extensions MAY appear in any\norder.\n",
      "id": "2a0a1b4b5834d868",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 110,
      "quote": "When multiple extensions of different types are present in the ClientHello or ServerHello messages, the extensions MAY appear in any order.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "There MUST NOT be more than one extension of the same type.\n",
      "id": "e5c5be871f36b2e0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 118,
      "quote": "There MUST NOT be more than one extension of the same type.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Indeed, a client\nthat requests session resumption does not in general know whether the\nserver will accept this request, and therefore it SHOULD send the\nsame extensions as it would send if it were not attempting\nresumption.\n",
      "id": "b4015df2ceba27b1",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 124,
      "quote": "Indeed, a client that requests session resumption does not in general know whether the server will accept this request, and therefore it SHOULD send the same extensions as it would send if it were not attempting resumption.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server MUST send a Certificate message whenever the agreed-\nupon key exchange method uses certificates for authentication\n(this includes all key exchange methods defined in this document\nexcept DH_anon).\n",
      "id": "cdd104c1b35523b4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 126,
      "quote": "The server MUST send a Certificate message whenever the agreed- upon key exchange method uses certificates for authentication (this includes all key exchange methods defined in this document except DH_anon).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The certificate MUST be appropriate for the negotiated cipher\nsuite's key exchange algorithm and any negotiated extensions.\n",
      "id": "911cba4bc0a933d0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 135,
      "quote": "The certificate MUST be appropriate for the negotiated cipher suite's key exchange algorithm and any negotiated extensions.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The sender's\ncertificate MUST come first in the list.\n",
      "id": "efea0ef35bdcf56e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 142,
      "quote": "The sender's certificate MUST come first in the list.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each following\ncertificate MUST directly certify the one preceding it.\n",
      "id": "68f2ad9dbd32e14d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 149,
      "quote": "Each following certificate MUST directly certify the one preceding it.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Because\ncertificate validation requires that root keys be distributed\nindependently, the self-signed certificate that specifies the root\ncertificate authority MAY be omitted from the chain, under the\nassumption that the remote end must already possess it in order to\nvalidate it in any case.\n",
      "id": "fc3f9304b2c81b61",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 156,
      "quote": "Because certificate validation requires that root keys be distributed independently, the self-signed certificate that specifies the root certificate authority MAY be omitted from the chain, under the assumption that the remote end must already possess it in order to validate it in any case.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Note that a client MAY\nsend no certificates if it does not have an appropriate certificate\nto send in response to the server's authentication request.\n",
      "id": "f707615ff8ae88ed",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 167,
      "quote": "Note that a client MAY send no certificates if it does not have an appropriate certificate to send in response to the server's authentication request.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  The certificate type MUST be X.509v3, unless explicitly negotiated\notherwise (e.g., [TLSPGP]).\n",
      "id": "1920e291b1777c34",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 175,
      "quote": "-  The certificate type MUST be X.509v3, unless explicitly negotiated otherwise (e.g., [TLSPGP]).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  The end entity certificate's public key (and associated\nrestrictions) MUST be compatible with the selected key exchange\nalgorithm.\n",
      "id": "0d5d501e9975fc4a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 182,
      "quote": "-  The end entity certificate's public key (and associated restrictions) MUST be compatible with the selected key exchange algorithm.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "RSA                RSA public key; the certificate MUST allow the\nRSA_PSK            key to be used for encryption (the\nkeyEncipherment bit MUST be set if the key\nusage extension is present).\n",
      "id": "406b21501d74f827",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 190,
      "quote": "RSA                RSA public key; the certificate MUST allow the RSA_PSK            key to be used for encryption (the keyEncipherment bit MUST be set if the key usage extension is present).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "RSA                RSA public key; the certificate MUST allow the\nRSA_PSK            key to be used for encryption (the\nkeyEncipherment bit MUST be set if the key\nusage extension is present).\n",
      "id": "61078045e267d5a2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 199,
      "quote": "RSA                RSA public key; the certificate MUST allow the RSA_PSK            key to be used for encryption (the keyEncipherment bit MUST be set if the key usage extension is present).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "DHE_RSA            RSA public key; the certificate MUST allow the\nECDHE_RSA          key to be used for signing (the\ndigitalSignature bit MUST be set if the key\nusage extension is present) with the signature\nscheme and hash algorithm that will be employed\nin the server key exchange message.\n",
      "id": "baa608dda63dd58f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 208,
      "quote": "DHE_RSA            RSA public key; the certificate MUST allow the ECDHE_RSA          key to be used for signing (the digitalSignature bit MUST be set if the key usage extension is present) with the signature scheme and hash algorithm that will be employed in the server key exchange message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "DHE_RSA            RSA public key; the certificate MUST allow the\nECDHE_RSA          key to be used for signing (the\ndigitalSignature bit MUST be set if the key\nusage extension is present) with the signature\nscheme and hash algorithm that will be employed\nin the server key exchange message.\n",
      "id": "ae61172484da7b59",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 219,
      "quote": "DHE_RSA            RSA public key; the certificate MUST allow the ECDHE_RSA          key to be used for signing (the digitalSignature bit MUST be set if the key usage extension is present) with the signature scheme and hash algorithm that will be employed in the server key exchange message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "DHE_DSS            DSA public key; the certificate MUST allow the\nkey to be used for signing with the hash\nalgorithm that will be employed in the server\nkey exchange message.\n",
      "id": "dfc8522e86baa24e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 230,
      "quote": "DHE_DSS            DSA public key; the certificate MUST allow the key to be used for signing with the hash algorithm that will be employed in the server key exchange message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "DH_DSS             Diffie-Hellman public key; the keyAgreement bit\nDH_RSA             MUST be set if the key usage extension is\npresent.\n",
      "id": "f518af1ef42b5af3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 239,
      "quote": "DH_DSS             Diffie-Hellman public key; the keyAgreement bit DH_RSA             MUST be set if the key usage extension is present.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "ECDH_ECDSA         ECDH-capable public key; the public key MUST\nECDH_RSA           use a curve and point format supported by the\nclient, as described in [TLSECC].\n",
      "id": "9bd4d19547eb6614",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 247,
      "quote": "ECDH_ECDSA         ECDH-capable public key; the public key MUST ECDH_RSA           use a curve and point format supported by the client, as described in [TLSECC].",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "ECDHE_ECDSA        ECDSA-capable public key; the certificate MUST\nallow the key to be used for signing with the\nhash algorithm that will be employed in the\nserver key exchange message.\n",
      "id": "34754c7e8458e019",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 255,
      "quote": "ECDHE_ECDSA        ECDSA-capable public key; the certificate MUST allow the key to be used for signing with the hash algorithm that will be employed in the server key exchange message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The public key\nMUST use a curve and point format supported by\nthe client, as described in  [TLSECC].\n",
      "id": "aa2020ca69ac4e71",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 264,
      "quote": "The public key MUST use a curve and point format supported by the client, as described in  [TLSECC].",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the client provided a \"signature_algorithms\" extension, then all\ncertificates provided by the server MUST be signed by a\nhash/signature algorithm pair that appears in that extension.\n",
      "id": "a6bea436dd60f80c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 272,
      "quote": "If the client provided a \"signature_algorithms\" extension, then all certificates provided by the server MUST be signed by a hash/signature algorithm pair that appears in that extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Note\nthat this implies that a certificate containing a key for one\nsignature algorithm MAY be signed using a different signature\nalgorithm (for instance, an RSA key signed with a DSA key).\n",
      "id": "6053b51cc3d814bf",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 280,
      "quote": "Note that this implies that a certificate containing a key for one signature algorithm MAY be signed using a different signature algorithm (for instance, an RSA key signed with a DSA key).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Fixed DH certificates MAY be\nsigned with any hash/signature algorithm pair appearing in the\nextension.\n",
      "id": "99cfb00e1f59feea",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 289,
      "quote": "Fixed DH certificates MAY be signed with any hash/signature algorithm pair appearing in the extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the server has a single certificate, it SHOULD attempt to\nvalidate that it meets these criteria.\n",
      "id": "aafaf9ccf2dc34c3",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 297,
      "quote": "If the server has a single certificate, it SHOULD attempt to validate that it meets these criteria.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Other key exchange algorithms, such as those defined in [TLSECC],\nMUST specify whether the ServerKeyExchange message is sent or not;\nand if the message is sent, its contents.\n",
      "id": "4dbb0ccae611dda9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 119,
      "quote": "Other key exchange algorithms, such as those defined in [TLSECC], MUST specify whether the ServerKeyExchange message is sent or not; and if the message is sent, its contents.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the client has offered the \"signature_algorithms\" extension, the\nsignature algorithm and hash algorithm MUST be a pair listed in that\nextension.\n",
      "id": "5b289bd5870e9176",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 127,
      "quote": "If the client has offered the \"signature_algorithms\" extension, the signature algorithm and hash algorithm MUST be a pair listed in that extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In\norder to negotiate correctly, the server MUST check any candidate\ncipher suites against the \"signature_algorithms\" extension before\nselecting them.\n",
      "id": "7807ff698c60c927",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 135,
      "quote": "In order to negotiate correctly, the server MUST check any candidate cipher suites against the \"signature_algorithms\" extension before selecting them.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In addition, the hash and signature algorithms MUST be compatible\nwith the key in the server's end-entity certificate.\n",
      "id": "7b867e75dbe3b4df",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 144,
      "quote": "In addition, the hash and signature algorithms MUST be compatible with the key in the server's end-entity certificate.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "RSA keys MAY be\nused with any permitted hash algorithm, subject to restrictions in\nthe certificate, if any.\n",
      "id": "a3388ee098fb605d",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 151,
      "quote": "RSA keys MAY be used with any permitted hash algorithm, subject to restrictions in the certificate, if any.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If\nthe certificate_authorities list is empty, then the client MAY\nsend any certificate of the appropriate ClientCertificateType,\nunless there is some external arrangement to the contrary.\n",
      "id": "ecda1ce9f797cc54",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 89,
      "quote": "If the certificate_authorities list is empty, then the client MAY send any certificate of the appropriate ClientCertificateType, unless there is some external arrangement to the contrary.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  Any certificates provided by the client MUST be signed using a\nhash/signature algorithm pair found in\nsupported_signature_algorithms.\n",
      "id": "0d0d652968ddf17e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 98,
      "quote": "-  Any certificates provided by the client MUST be signed using a hash/signature algorithm pair found in supported_signature_algorithms.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  The end-entity certificate provided by the client MUST contain a\nkey that is compatible with certificate_types.\n",
      "id": "d12ca71258aefc80",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 106,
      "quote": "-  The end-entity certificate provided by the client MUST contain a key that is compatible with certificate_types.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the key is a\nsignature key, it MUST be usable with some hash/signature\nalgorithm pair in supported_signature_algorithms.\n",
      "id": "8655b95a6a0b35de",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 113,
      "quote": "If the key is a signature key, it MUST be usable with some hash/signature algorithm pair in supported_signature_algorithms.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For\nexample, if the server sends dss_fixed_dh certificate type and\n{{sha1, dsa}, {sha1, rsa}} signature types, the client MAY reply\nwith a certificate containing a static DH key, signed with RSA-\nSHA1.\n",
      "id": "298b00ea8b29965d",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 121,
      "quote": "For example, if the server sends dss_fixed_dh certificate type and {{sha1, dsa}, {sha1, rsa}} signature types, the client MAY reply with a certificate containing a static DH key, signed with RSA- SHA1.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Upon receipt of the ServerHelloDone message, the client SHOULD\nverify that the server provided a valid certificate, if required,\nand check that the server hello parameters are acceptable.\n",
      "id": "636736bf8038d803",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "Upon receipt of the ServerHelloDone message, the client SHOULD verify that the server provided a valid certificate, if required, and check that the server hello parameters are acceptable.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If no suitable certificate is available,\nthe client MUST send a certificate message containing no\ncertificates.\n",
      "id": "151c21870f9a2296",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 81,
      "quote": "If no suitable certificate is available, the client MUST send a certificate message containing no certificates.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the client does not send any certificates, the\nserver MAY at its discretion either continue the handshake without\nclient authentication, or respond with a fatal handshake_failure\nalert.\n",
      "id": "f194fc2a32ff890e",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 89,
      "quote": "If the client does not send any certificates, the server MAY at its discretion either continue the handshake without client authentication, or respond with a fatal handshake_failure alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Also, if some aspect of the certificate chain was\nunacceptable (e.g., it was not signed by a known, trusted CA), the\nserver MAY at its discretion either continue the handshake\n(considering the client unauthenticated) or send a fatal alert.\n",
      "id": "0d8e45afbb613a70",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 98,
      "quote": "Also, if some aspect of the certificate chain was unacceptable (e.g., it was not signed by a known, trusted CA), the server MAY at its discretion either continue the handshake (considering the client unauthenticated) or send a fatal alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The certificate MUST be appropriate for the negotiated\ncipher suite's key exchange algorithm, and any negotiated\nextensions.\n",
      "id": "e4787b07b98a759f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 107,
      "quote": "The certificate MUST be appropriate for the negotiated cipher suite's key exchange algorithm, and any negotiated extensions.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  The certificate type MUST be X.509v3, unless explicitly negotiated\notherwise (e.g., [TLSPGP]).\n",
      "id": "15a5e8777e74e422",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 115,
      "quote": "-  The certificate type MUST be X.509v3, unless explicitly negotiated otherwise (e.g., [TLSPGP]).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "rsa_sign            RSA public key; the certificate MUST allow the\nkey to be used for signing with the signature\nscheme and hash algorithm that will be\nemployed in the certificate verify message.\n",
      "id": "8ac3c0b3a0f67d6c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 122,
      "quote": "rsa_sign            RSA public key; the certificate MUST allow the key to be used for signing with the signature scheme and hash algorithm that will be employed in the certificate verify message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "dss_sign            DSA public key; the certificate MUST allow the\nkey to be used for signing with the hash\nalgorithm that will be employed in the\ncertificate verify message.\n",
      "id": "d74a7613efdedae0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 131,
      "quote": "dss_sign            DSA public key; the certificate MUST allow the key to be used for signing with the hash algorithm that will be employed in the certificate verify message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "ecdsa_sign          ECDSA-capable public key; the certificate MUST\nallow the key to be used for signing with the\nhash algorithm that will be employed in the\ncertificate verify message; the public key\nMUST use a curve and point format supported by\nthe server.\n",
      "id": "3867ef0d021d325c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 140,
      "quote": "ecdsa_sign          ECDSA-capable public key; the certificate MUST allow the key to be used for signing with the hash algorithm that will be employed in the certificate verify message; the public key MUST use a curve and point format supported by the server.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "ecdsa_sign          ECDSA-capable public key; the certificate MUST\nallow the key to be used for signing with the\nhash algorithm that will be employed in the\ncertificate verify message; the public key\nMUST use a curve and point format supported by\nthe server.\n",
      "id": "be42fe13fd2aaf9a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 151,
      "quote": "ecdsa_sign          ECDSA-capable public key; the certificate MUST allow the key to be used for signing with the hash algorithm that will be employed in the certificate verify message; the public key MUST use a curve and point format supported by the server.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "rsa_fixed_dh        Diffie-Hellman public key; MUST use the same\ndss_fixed_dh        parameters as server's key.\n",
      "id": "8bfa9843f1bc8260",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 162,
      "quote": "rsa_fixed_dh        Diffie-Hellman public key; MUST use the same dss_fixed_dh        parameters as server's key.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "rsa_fixed_ecdh      ECDH-capable public key; MUST use the\necdsa_fixed_ecdh    same curve as the server's key, and MUST use a\npoint format supported by the server.\n",
      "id": "fdcc673b54c87a53",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 169,
      "quote": "rsa_fixed_ecdh      ECDH-capable public key; MUST use the ecdsa_fixed_ecdh    same curve as the server's key, and MUST use a point format supported by the server.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "rsa_fixed_ecdh      ECDH-capable public key; MUST use the\necdsa_fixed_ecdh    same curve as the server's key, and MUST use a\npoint format supported by the server.\n",
      "id": "e2f89eff50a90086",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 177,
      "quote": "rsa_fixed_ecdh      ECDH-capable public key; MUST use the ecdsa_fixed_ecdh    same curve as the server's key, and MUST use a point format supported by the server.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  If the certificate_authorities list in the certificate request\nmessage was non-empty, one of the certificates in the certificate\nchain SHOULD be issued by one of the listed CAs.\n",
      "id": "fbdd7c6d2ad169d1",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 185,
      "quote": "-  If the certificate_authorities list in the certificate request message was non-empty, one of the certificates in the certificate chain SHOULD be issued by one of the listed CAs.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  The certificates MUST be signed using an acceptable hash/\nsignature algorithm pair, as described in Section 7.4.4.\n",
      "id": "346ff941473f1330",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 193,
      "quote": "-  The certificates MUST be signed using an acceptable hash/ signature algorithm pair, as described in Section 7.4.4.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Client implementations MUST always send the correct version number in\nPreMasterSecret.\n",
      "id": "5d698d625255842a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 144,
      "quote": "Client implementations MUST always send the correct version number in PreMasterSecret.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.7.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.7.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If ClientHello.client_version is TLS 1.1 or higher,\nserver implementations MUST check the version number as described in\nthe note below.\n",
      "id": "67b9a1ad839ac2d4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 151,
      "quote": "If ClientHello.client_version is TLS 1.1 or higher, server implementations MUST check the version number as described in the note below.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.7.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.7.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the version number is TLS 1.0 or earlier, server\nimplementations SHOULD check the version number, but MAY have a\nconfiguration option to disable the check.\n",
      "id": "35f3dbfe28f07a0c",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 159,
      "quote": "If the version number is TLS 1.0 or earlier, server implementations SHOULD check the version number, but MAY have a configuration option to disable the check.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.7.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.7.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Note that if the check\nfails, the PreMasterSecret SHOULD be randomized as described below.\n",
      "id": "bd150ab4b16de3eb",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 167,
      "quote": "Note that if the check fails, the PreMasterSecret SHOULD be randomized as described below.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.7.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.7.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "[KPR03] describe some theoretical attacks, and therefore\nthe first construction described is RECOMMENDED.\n",
      "id": "380419da6d0cc03b",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 174,
      "quote": "[KPR03] describe some theoretical attacks, and therefore the first construction described is RECOMMENDED.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.7.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.7.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In any case, a TLS server MUST NOT generate an alert if processing an\nRSA-encrypted premaster secret message fails, or the version number\nis not as expected.\n",
      "id": "27336fb8be63be9f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 181,
      "quote": "In any case, a TLS server MUST NOT generate an alert if processing an RSA-encrypted premaster secret message fails, or the version number is not as expected.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.7.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.7.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Instead, it MUST continue the handshake with a\nrandomly generated premaster secret.\n",
      "id": "48b12eda234b25d7",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 189,
      "quote": "Instead, it MUST continue the handshake with a randomly generated premaster secret.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.7.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.7.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "upgrading from SSLv3 MUST modify their implementations to generate\nand accept the correct encoding.\n",
      "id": "05289fd4308df2af",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 196,
      "quote": "upgrading from SSLv3 MUST modify their implementations to generate and accept the correct encoding.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.7.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.7.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Accordingly, implementations that use static RSA keys MUST\nuse RSA blinding or some other anti-timing technique, as described in\n[TIMING].\n",
      "id": "e6cbc6ebcc6b7e32",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 203,
      "quote": "Accordingly, implementations that use static RSA keys MUST use RSA blinding or some other anti-timing technique, as described in [TIMING].",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.7.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.7.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In this\ncase, the client key exchange message will be sent, but it MUST\nbe empty.\n",
      "id": "f7e6d4f308e4be6c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 37,
      "quote": "In this case, the client key exchange message will be sent, but it MUST be empty.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.7.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.7.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It MUST immediately\nfollow the client certificate message, if it is sent.\n",
      "id": "cbe49ddb743460f2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "It MUST immediately follow the client certificate message, if it is sent.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Otherwise,\nit MUST be the first message sent by the client after it receives\nthe ServerHelloDone message.\n",
      "id": "d1cbfee5ebead73c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "Otherwise, it MUST be the first message sent by the client after it receives the ServerHelloDone message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the client is sending a certificate containing a static\nDH exponent (i.e., it is doing fixed_dh client authentication),\nthen this message MUST be sent but MUST be empty.\n",
      "id": "e221b2abc9d88304",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 59,
      "quote": "If the client is sending a certificate containing a static DH exponent (i.e., it is doing fixed_dh client authentication), then this message MUST be sent but MUST be empty.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the client is sending a certificate containing a static\nDH exponent (i.e., it is doing fixed_dh client authentication),\nthen this message MUST be sent but MUST be empty.\n",
      "id": "0d296b04ea2441b3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 67,
      "quote": "If the client is sending a certificate containing a static DH exponent (i.e., it is doing fixed_dh client authentication), then this message MUST be sent but MUST be empty.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When\nsent, it MUST immediately follow the client key exchange message.\n",
      "id": "b20b3827afda582b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "When sent, it MUST immediately follow the client key exchange message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The hash and signature algorithms used in the signature MUST be\none of those present in the supported_signature_algorithms field\nof the CertificateRequest message.\n",
      "id": "4104871af91bf6d6",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 58,
      "quote": "The hash and signature algorithms used in the signature MUST be one of those present in the supported_signature_algorithms field of the CertificateRequest message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In addition, the hash and\nsignature algorithms MUST be compatible with the key in the\nclient's end-entity certificate.\n",
      "id": "e5e7bed08d81d935",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 66,
      "quote": "In addition, the hash and signature algorithms MUST be compatible with the key in the client's end-entity certificate.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "RSA keys MAY be used with any\npermitted hash algorithm, subject to restrictions in the\ncertificate, if any.\n",
      "id": "3e8e9b65dce97ee0",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 74,
      "quote": "RSA keys MAY be used with any permitted hash algorithm, subject to restrictions in the certificate, if any.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Recipients of Finished\nmessages MUST verify that the contents are correct.\n",
      "id": "1e76783b96268a2c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 75,
      "quote": "Recipients of Finished messages MUST verify that the contents are correct.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For the PRF\ndefined in Section 5, the Hash MUST be the Hash used as the basis\nfor the PRF.\n",
      "id": "352cd25301d9c932",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 82,
      "quote": "For the PRF defined in Section 5, the Hash MUST be the Hash used as the basis for the PRF.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Any cipher suite which defines a different PRF MUST\nalso define the Hash to use in the Finished computation.\n",
      "id": "72993ef157b4ca4f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 90,
      "quote": "Any cipher suite which defines a different PRF MUST also define the Hash to use in the Finished computation.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Future cipher suites MAY specify other lengths but such length\nMUST be at least 12 bytes.\n",
      "id": "af7cc27f9d095ff8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 97,
      "quote": "Future cipher suites MAY specify other lengths but such length MUST be at least 12 bytes.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The handshake protocol messages are presented below in the order they\nMUST be sent; sending handshake messages in an unexpected order\nresults in a fatal error.\n",
      "id": "086514cc30e23849",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "The handshake protocol messages are presented below in the order they MUST be sent; sending handshake messages in an unexpected order results in a fatal error.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The one message that is not bound by these ordering rules\nis the HelloRequest message, which can be sent at any time, but which\nSHOULD be ignored by the client if it arrives in the middle of a\nhandshake.\n",
      "id": "4d26e703003bb4c1",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 59,
      "quote": "The one message that is not bound by these ordering rules is the HelloRequest message, which can be sent at any time, but which SHOULD be ignored by the client if it arrives in the middle of a handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-7.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In the absence of an application profile standard specifying\notherwise, a TLS-compliant application MUST implement the cipher\nsuite TLS_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA (see Appendix A.5 for the\ndefinition).\n",
      "id": "206c164e2bc534ec",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 10,
      "quote": "In the absence of an application profile standard specifying otherwise, a TLS-compliant application MUST implement the cipher suite TLS_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA (see Appendix A.5 for the definition).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246/section-9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "o  The client MUST include either an empty \"renegotiation_info\"\nextension, or the TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV signaling\ncipher suite value in the ClientHello.\n",
      "id": "64877ede6ba6b5cc",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 34,
      "quote": "o  The client MUST include either an empty \"renegotiation_info\" extension, or the TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV signaling cipher suite value in the ClientHello.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-3.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-3.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Including both is NOT\nRECOMMENDED.\n",
      "id": "700ce4717f4f5aab",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "Including both is NOT RECOMMENDED.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-3.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-3.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "o  When a ServerHello is received, the client MUST check if it\nincludes the \"renegotiation_info\" extension:\n",
      "id": "4dd8c3322c6b3dc8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 49,
      "quote": "o  When a ServerHello is received, the client MUST check if it includes the \"renegotiation_info\" extension:",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-3.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-3.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The client MUST then verify that the length of the\n\"renegotiated_connection\" field is zero, and if it is not, MUST\nabort the handshake (by sending a fatal handshake_failure\nalert).\n",
      "id": "0a50342c39ae0aa0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "The client MUST then verify that the length of the \"renegotiated_connection\" field is zero, and if it is not, MUST abort the handshake (by sending a fatal handshake_failure alert).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-3.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-3.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The client MUST then verify that the length of the\n\"renegotiated_connection\" field is zero, and if it is not, MUST\nabort the handshake (by sending a fatal handshake_failure\nalert).\n",
      "id": "f17781d662f646c2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 65,
      "quote": "The client MUST then verify that the length of the \"renegotiated_connection\" field is zero, and if it is not, MUST abort the handshake (by sending a fatal handshake_failure alert).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-3.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-3.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "o  The client MUST include the \"renegotiation_info\" extension in the\nClientHello, containing the saved client_verify_data.\n",
      "id": "7a8d2bea0effa94f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "o  The client MUST include the \"renegotiation_info\" extension in the ClientHello, containing the saved client_verify_data.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-3.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-3.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The SCSV\nMUST NOT be included.\n",
      "id": "e78902a4a524e817",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "The SCSV MUST NOT be included.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-3.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-3.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "o  When a ServerHello is received, the client MUST verify that the\n\"renegotiation_info\" extension is present; if it is not, the\nclient MUST abort the handshake.\n",
      "id": "ec8ea810ad3a6864",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 39,
      "quote": "o  When a ServerHello is received, the client MUST verify that the \"renegotiation_info\" extension is present; if it is not, the client MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-3.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-3.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "o  When a ServerHello is received, the client MUST verify that the\n\"renegotiation_info\" extension is present; if it is not, the\nclient MUST abort the handshake.\n",
      "id": "7876356e25610ca3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "o  When a ServerHello is received, the client MUST verify that the \"renegotiation_info\" extension is present; if it is not, the client MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-3.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-3.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "o  The client MUST then verify that the first half of the\n\"renegotiated_connection\" field is equal to the saved\nclient_verify_data value, and the second half is equal to the\nsaved server_verify_data value.\n",
      "id": "ca255fa8a9c831f2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 55,
      "quote": "o  The client MUST then verify that the first half of the \"renegotiated_connection\" field is equal to the saved client_verify_data value, and the second half is equal to the saved server_verify_data value.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-3.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-3.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If they are not, the client MUST\nabort the handshake.\n",
      "id": "53bc49e341d672aa",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "If they are not, the client MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-3.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-3.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "o  When a ClientHello is received, the server MUST check if it\nincludes the TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV SCSV.\n",
      "id": "42fee3f1bdf70fb9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 46,
      "quote": "o  When a ClientHello is received, the server MUST check if it includes the TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV SCSV.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-3.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-3.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "o  The server MUST check if the \"renegotiation_info\" extension is\nincluded in the ClientHello.\n",
      "id": "e07d94bf28bf737f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 53,
      "quote": "o  The server MUST check if the \"renegotiation_info\" extension is included in the ClientHello.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-3.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-3.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server MUST then verify\nthat the length of the \"renegotiated_connection\" field is zero,\nand if it is not, MUST abort the handshake.\n",
      "id": "cc866b584e8367e1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 60,
      "quote": "The server MUST then verify that the length of the \"renegotiated_connection\" field is zero, and if it is not, MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-3.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-3.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server MUST then verify\nthat the length of the \"renegotiated_connection\" field is zero,\nand if it is not, MUST abort the handshake.\n",
      "id": "c2610fae3743ec59",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 68,
      "quote": "The server MUST then verify that the length of the \"renegotiated_connection\" field is zero, and if it is not, MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-3.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-3.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "o  If the secure_renegotiation flag is set to TRUE, the server MUST\ninclude an empty \"renegotiation_info\" extension in the ServerHello\nmessage.\n",
      "id": "c9d7a35db68e80e0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 76,
      "quote": "o  If the secure_renegotiation flag is set to TRUE, the server MUST include an empty \"renegotiation_info\" extension in the ServerHello message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-3.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-3.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS servers implementing this specification MUST ignore any unknown\nextensions offered by the client and they MUST accept version numbers\nhigher than their highest version number and negotiate the highest\ncommon version.\n",
      "id": "f0c5b2de1baa568f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 84,
      "quote": "TLS servers implementing this specification MUST ignore any unknown extensions offered by the client and they MUST accept version numbers higher than their highest version number and negotiate the highest common version.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-3.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-3.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS servers implementing this specification MUST ignore any unknown\nextensions offered by the client and they MUST accept version numbers\nhigher than their highest version number and negotiate the highest\ncommon version.\n",
      "id": "04210638809eddd3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 93,
      "quote": "TLS servers implementing this specification MUST ignore any unknown extensions offered by the client and they MUST accept version numbers higher than their highest version number and negotiate the highest common version.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-3.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-3.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS implementations MUST\ncontinue to comply with Section 7.4.1.4 for all other extensions.\n",
      "id": "9b705028fa53a808",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 102,
      "quote": "TLS implementations MUST continue to comply with Section 7.4.1.4 for all other extensions.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-3.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-3.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "o  When a ClientHello is received, the server MUST verify that it\ndoes not contain the TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV SCSV.\n",
      "id": "bbce47850d1bdec3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 27,
      "quote": "o  When a ClientHello is received, the server MUST verify that it does not contain the TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV SCSV.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-3.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-3.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If\nthe SCSV is present, the server MUST abort the handshake.\n",
      "id": "5c5c1594f928cc33",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 34,
      "quote": "If the SCSV is present, the server MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-3.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-3.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "o  The server MUST verify that the \"renegotiation_info\" extension is\npresent; if it is not, the server MUST abort the handshake.\n",
      "id": "4544c93b33d908a3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "o  The server MUST verify that the \"renegotiation_info\" extension is present; if it is not, the server MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-3.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-3.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "o  The server MUST verify that the \"renegotiation_info\" extension is\npresent; if it is not, the server MUST abort the handshake.\n",
      "id": "e1e5e852bb08728a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 48,
      "quote": "o  The server MUST verify that the \"renegotiation_info\" extension is present; if it is not, the server MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-3.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-3.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "o  The server MUST verify that the value of the\n\"renegotiated_connection\" field is equal to the saved\nclient_verify_data value; if it is not, the server MUST abort the\nhandshake.\n",
      "id": "b874f2aad6f4ff30",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 55,
      "quote": "o  The server MUST verify that the value of the \"renegotiated_connection\" field is equal to the saved client_verify_data value; if it is not, the server MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-3.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-3.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "o  The server MUST verify that the value of the\n\"renegotiated_connection\" field is equal to the saved\nclient_verify_data value; if it is not, the server MUST abort the\nhandshake.\n",
      "id": "49417f5b2df1c39c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "o  The server MUST verify that the value of the \"renegotiated_connection\" field is equal to the saved client_verify_data value; if it is not, the server MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-3.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-3.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "o  The server MUST include a \"renegotiation_info\" extension\ncontaining the saved client_verify_data and server_verify_data in\nthe ServerHello.\n",
      "id": "597fb9df89ac7610",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 73,
      "quote": "o  The server MUST include a \"renegotiation_info\" extension containing the saved client_verify_data and server_verify_data in the ServerHello.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-3.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-3.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Such clients MUST\ngenerate a fatal \"handshake_failure\" alert prior to terminating the\nconnection.\n",
      "id": "44b42fc4b4e7ec86",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 30,
      "quote": "Such clients MUST generate a fatal \"handshake_failure\" alert prior to terminating the connection.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It is RECOMMENDED that clients refuse this\nrenegotiation request.\n",
      "id": "17a73310425663cd",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 45,
      "quote": "It is RECOMMENDED that clients refuse this renegotiation request.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients that do so MUST respond to such\nrequests with a \"no_renegotiation\" alert (RFC 5246 requires this\nalert to be at the \"warning\" level).\n",
      "id": "3b24b0cc29836241",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 52,
      "quote": "Clients that do so MUST respond to such requests with a \"no_renegotiation\" alert (RFC 5246 requires this alert to be at the \"warning\" level).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If clients nevertheless choose to renegotiate, they\nMUST behave as described below.\n",
      "id": "5aada95a636d7762",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 60,
      "quote": "If clients nevertheless choose to renegotiate, they MUST behave as described below.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients that choose to renegotiate MUST provide either the\nTLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV SCSV or \"renegotiation_info\" in\ntheir ClientHello.\n",
      "id": "ec8b8e8e881118d5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 67,
      "quote": "Clients that choose to renegotiate MUST provide either the TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV SCSV or \"renegotiation_info\" in their ClientHello.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Thus,\nit is permitted, though NOT RECOMMENDED, for the client to simply\nsend the SCSV.\n",
      "id": "34a17c9799c71750",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 75,
      "quote": "Thus, it is permitted, though NOT RECOMMENDED, for the client to simply send the SCSV.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When the ServerHello is received, the client MUST verify that it does\nnot contain the \"renegotiation_info\" extension.\n",
      "id": "411cb11348fe81d7",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 83,
      "quote": "When the ServerHello is received, the client MUST verify that it does not contain the \"renegotiation_info\" extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If it does, the\nclient MUST abort the handshake.\n",
      "id": "ae7b7b28ecfff407",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 90,
      "quote": "If it does, the client MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In order to enable clients to probe, even servers that do not support\nrenegotiation MUST implement the minimal version of the extension\ndescribed in this document for initial handshakes, thus signaling\nthat they have been upgraded.\n",
      "id": "7ff29782b4e960d4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 23,
      "quote": "In order to enable clients to probe, even servers that do not support renegotiation MUST implement the minimal version of the extension described in this document for initial handshakes, thus signaling that they have been upgraded.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-4.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It is RECOMMENDED that servers not permit legacy renegotiation.\n",
      "id": "8be4faa466a149c8",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 19,
      "quote": "It is RECOMMENDED that servers not permit legacy renegotiation.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If\nservers nevertheless do permit it, they MUST follow the requirements\nin this section.\n",
      "id": "4d26b66474218409",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "If servers nevertheless do permit it, they MUST follow the requirements in this section.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "o  When a ClientHello is received, the server MUST verify that it\ndoes not contain the TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV SCSV.\n",
      "id": "871d73ea7e796244",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 33,
      "quote": "o  When a ClientHello is received, the server MUST verify that it does not contain the TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV SCSV.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If\nthe SCSV is present, the server MUST abort the handshake.\n",
      "id": "5c8b9749322b41f2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 40,
      "quote": "If the SCSV is present, the server MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "o  The server MUST verify that the \"renegotiation_info\" extension is\nnot present; if it is, the server MUST abort the handshake.\n",
      "id": "fd600a44fb642b25",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "o  The server MUST verify that the \"renegotiation_info\" extension is not present; if it is, the server MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "o  The server MUST verify that the \"renegotiation_info\" extension is\nnot present; if it is, the server MUST abort the handshake.\n",
      "id": "60d93122d1afd831",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "o  The server MUST verify that the \"renegotiation_info\" extension is not present; if it is, the server MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients\nthat support SSLv3 and offer secure renegotiation (either via SCSV or\n\"renegotiation_info\") MUST accept the \"renegotiation_info\" extension\nfrom the server, even if the server version is {0x03, 0x00}, and\nbehave as described in this specification.\n",
      "id": "22a362ea5074be6b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 26,
      "quote": "Clients that support SSLv3 and offer secure renegotiation (either via SCSV or \"renegotiation_info\") MUST accept the \"renegotiation_info\" extension from the server, even if the server version is {0x03, 0x00}, and behave as described in this specification.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-4.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-4.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS servers that support\nsecure renegotiation and support SSLv3 MUST accept SCSV or the\n\"renegotiation_info\" extension and respond as described in this\nspecification even if the offered client version is {0x03, 0x00}.\n",
      "id": "f0e97622f6918264",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 36,
      "quote": "TLS servers that support secure renegotiation and support SSLv3 MUST accept SCSV or the \"renegotiation_info\" extension and respond as described in this specification even if the offered client version is {0x03, 0x00}.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-4.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-4.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "SSLv3 clients that refuse renegotiation SHOULD use a fatal\nhandshake_failure alert.\n",
      "id": "a5aec8a585e0ab32",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 45,
      "quote": "SSLv3 clients that refuse renegotiation SHOULD use a fatal handshake_failure alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-4.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-4.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers SHOULD NOT allow\nclients to renegotiate without using this extension.\n",
      "id": "85453d8fe15fd23b",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 55,
      "quote": "Servers SHOULD NOT allow clients to renegotiate without using this extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS implementations SHOULD provide a mechanism to disable and enable\nrenegotiation.\n",
      "id": "f86ef1534b322335",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 62,
      "quote": "TLS implementations SHOULD provide a mechanism to disable and enable renegotiation.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746/section-5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Note, however, that if\nthe IKM is a Diffie-Hellman value, as in the case of TLS with Diffie-\nHellman, then the extract part SHOULD NOT be skipped.\n",
      "id": "b339cb10907936ae",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 31,
      "quote": "Note, however, that if the IKM is a Diffie-Hellman value, as in the case of TLS with Diffie- Hellman, then the extract part SHOULD NOT be skipped.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5869/section-3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5869",
      "target_section": "section-3.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This, however, is\nNOT RECOMMENDED, especially because it would omit the use of 'info'\nas part of the derivation process (and adding 'info' as an input to\nthe extract step is not advisable -- see [HKDF-paper]).\n",
      "id": "d1d98dd5eaba5a06",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 39,
      "quote": "This, however, is NOT RECOMMENDED, especially because it would omit the use of 'info' as part of the derivation process (and adding 'info' as an input to the extract step is not advisable -- see [HKDF-paper]).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5869/section-3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5869",
      "target_section": "section-3.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients and servers SHOULD NOT accept handshakes that do not use the\nextended master secret, especially if they rely on features like\ncompound authentication that fall into the vulnerable cases described\nin Section 6.1.\n",
      "id": "c3c647e251417465",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 38,
      "quote": "Clients and servers SHOULD NOT accept handshakes that do not use the extended master secret, especially if they rely on features like compound authentication that fall into the vulnerable cases described in Section 6.1.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the client and server agree on this extension and a full handshake\ntakes place, both client and server MUST use the extended master\nsecret derivation algorithm, as defined in Section 4.\n",
      "id": "9977d968b8ff4c48",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 19,
      "quote": "If the client and server agree on this extension and a full handshake takes place, both client and server MUST use the extended master secret derivation algorithm, as defined in Section 4.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In all handshakes, a client implementing this document MUST send the\n\"extended_master_secret\" extension in its ClientHello.\n",
      "id": "dbf985da62544926",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 36,
      "quote": "In all handshakes, a client implementing this document MUST send the \"extended_master_secret\" extension in its ClientHello.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a server implementing this document receives the\n\"extended_master_secret\" extension, it MUST include the extension in\nits ServerHello message.\n",
      "id": "ef991ab678a4c4d2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 43,
      "quote": "If a server implementing this document receives the \"extended_master_secret\" extension, it MUST include the extension in its ServerHello message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the server receives a ClientHello without the extension, it SHOULD\nabort the handshake if it does not wish to interoperate with legacy\nclients.\n",
      "id": "8fb126ed850747bf",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "If the server receives a ClientHello without the extension, it SHOULD abort the handshake if it does not wish to interoperate with legacy clients.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If it chooses to continue the handshake, then it MUST NOT\ninclude the extension in the ServerHello.\n",
      "id": "95b4f9801bf451a7",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 59,
      "quote": "If it chooses to continue the handshake, then it MUST NOT include the extension in the ServerHello.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a client receives a ServerHello without the extension, it SHOULD\nabort the handshake if it does not wish to interoperate with legacy\nservers.\n",
      "id": "8c342e5f6d9ec0f1",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 66,
      "quote": "If a client receives a ServerHello without the extension, it SHOULD abort the handshake if it does not wish to interoperate with legacy servers.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the client and server choose to continue a full handshake without\nthe extension, they MUST use the standard master secret derivation\nfor the new session.\n",
      "id": "a02e40ea31cd8058",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 74,
      "quote": "If the client and server choose to continue a full handshake without the extension, they MUST use the standard master secret derivation for the new session.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The client SHOULD NOT offer an abbreviated handshake to resume a\nsession that does not use an extended master secret.\n",
      "id": "36694cc3759e09e6",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 60,
      "quote": "The client SHOULD NOT offer an abbreviated handshake to resume a session that does not use an extended master secret.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Instead, it\nSHOULD offer a full handshake.\n",
      "id": "20f91dbf1a107589",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 67,
      "quote": "Instead, it SHOULD offer a full handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When offering an abbreviated handshake, the client MUST send the\n\"extended_master_secret\" extension in its ClientHello.\n",
      "id": "0f29b23845fd5bad",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 74,
      "quote": "When offering an abbreviated handshake, the client MUST send the \"extended_master_secret\" extension in its ClientHello.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "o  If the original session did not use the \"extended_master_secret\"\nextension but the new ClientHello contains the extension, then the\nserver MUST NOT perform the abbreviated handshake.\n",
      "id": "19a7dd198c4fc2f1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 81,
      "quote": "o  If the original session did not use the \"extended_master_secret\" extension but the new ClientHello contains the extension, then the server MUST NOT perform the abbreviated handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Instead, it\nSHOULD continue with a full handshake (as described in\nSection 5.2) to negotiate a new session.\n",
      "id": "ae2c07d5e2dbe749",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 89,
      "quote": "Instead, it SHOULD continue with a full handshake (as described in Section 5.2) to negotiate a new session.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "o  If the original session used the \"extended_master_secret\"\nextension but the new ClientHello does not contain it, the server\nMUST abort the abbreviated handshake.\n",
      "id": "42931484da217874",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 97,
      "quote": "o  If the original session used the \"extended_master_secret\" extension but the new ClientHello does not contain it, the server MUST abort the abbreviated handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "o  If neither the original session nor the new ClientHello uses the\nextension, the server SHOULD abort the handshake.\n",
      "id": "e4d5b8e87fd7d20e",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 105,
      "quote": "o  If neither the original session nor the new ClientHello uses the extension, the server SHOULD abort the handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "o  If the new ClientHello contains the extension and the server\nchooses to continue the handshake, then the server MUST include\nthe \"extended_master_secret\" extension in its ServerHello message.\n",
      "id": "d80abdc470d0a602",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 112,
      "quote": "o  If the new ClientHello contains the extension and the server chooses to continue the handshake, then the server MUST include the \"extended_master_secret\" extension in its ServerHello message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "o  If the original session did not use the \"extended_master_secret\"\nextension but the new ServerHello contains the extension, the\nclient MUST abort the handshake.\n",
      "id": "f05f2583a53ceeb5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 120,
      "quote": "o  If the original session did not use the \"extended_master_secret\" extension but the new ServerHello contains the extension, the client MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "o  If the original session used the extension but the new ServerHello\ndoes not contain the extension, the client MUST abort the\nhandshake.\n",
      "id": "8b13e9b80e6faebd",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 128,
      "quote": "o  If the original session used the extension but the new ServerHello does not contain the extension, the client MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Hence, the client or server MUST NOT\nexport any key material based on the new master secret for any\nsubsequent application-level authentication.\n",
      "id": "37c21fc93a4faf7a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "Hence, the client or server MUST NOT export any key material based on the new master secret for any subsequent application-level authentication.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-5.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In particular, it MUST\ndisable [RFC5705] and any Extensible Authentication Protocol (EAP)\nrelying on compound authentication [COMPOUND-AUTH].\n",
      "id": "0c0ca85f6380a902",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 49,
      "quote": "In particular, it MUST disable [RFC5705] and any Extensible Authentication Protocol (EAP) relying on compound authentication [COMPOUND-AUTH].",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-5.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Hence, the client or server MUST NOT use the current handshake's\n\"verify_data\" for application-level authentication.\n",
      "id": "da5199ce2beb1c3f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 57,
      "quote": "Hence, the client or server MUST NOT use the current handshake's \"verify_data\" for application-level authentication.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-5.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In particular,\nthe client MUST disable renegotiation and any use of the \"tls-unique\"\nchannel binding [RFC5929] on the current connection.\n",
      "id": "76ac9a16555ef421",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "In particular, the client MUST disable renegotiation and any use of the \"tls-unique\" channel binding [RFC5929] on the current connection.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-5.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the original session uses an extended master secret but the\nClientHello or ServerHello in the abbreviated handshake does not\ninclude the extension, it MAY be safe to continue the abbreviated\nhandshake since it is protected by the extended master secret of the\noriginal session.\n",
      "id": "204a24bf4a455b08",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 72,
      "quote": "If the original session uses an extended master secret but the ClientHello or ServerHello in the abbreviated handshake does not include the extension, it MAY be safe to continue the abbreviated handshake since it is protected by the extended master secret of the original session.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-5.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Since such situations are unusual and likely\nto be the result of transient or inadvertent misconfigurations, this\ndocument recommends that the client and server MUST abort such\nhandshakes.\n",
      "id": "3a8bbf5a09afa555",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 82,
      "quote": "Since such situations are unusual and likely to be the result of transient or inadvertent misconfigurations, this document recommends that the client and server MUST abort such handshakes.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-5.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "As such, hash functions such as MD5 or\nSHA1 are NOT RECOMMENDED.\n",
      "id": "0ddfd81345d710fc",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 24,
      "quote": "As such, hash functions such as MD5 or SHA1 are NOT RECOMMENDED.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients and servers\nimplementing this document SHOULD refuse SSL 3.0 handshakes.\n",
      "id": "da0c012fb96f247b",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 18,
      "quote": "Clients and servers implementing this document SHOULD refuse SSL 3.0 handshakes.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-6.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-6.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If they\nchoose to support SSL 3.0, the resulting sessions MUST use the legacy\nmaster secret computation, and the interoperability considerations of\nSection 5.4 apply.\n",
      "id": "46f249fde0d40537",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "If they choose to support SSL 3.0, the resulting sessions MUST use the legacy master secret computation, and the interoperability considerations of Section 5.4 apply.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627/section-6.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-6.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In ECDHE_ECDSA, the server's certificate MUST contain an ECDSA- or\nEdDSA-capable public key.\n",
      "id": "2a39fde98f5ad75f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 20,
      "quote": "In ECDHE_ECDSA, the server's certificate MUST contain an ECDSA- or EdDSA-capable public key.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "These\nparameters MUST be signed with ECDSA or EdDSA using the private key\ncorresponding to the public key in the server's Certificate.\n",
      "id": "291a0985b859f944",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 27,
      "quote": "These parameters MUST be signed with ECDSA or EdDSA using the private key corresponding to the public key in the server's Certificate.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This key exchange algorithm is the same as ECDHE_ECDSA except that\nthe server's certificate MUST contain an RSA public key authorized\nfor signing and the signature in the ServerKeyExchange message must\nbe computed with the corresponding RSA private key.\n",
      "id": "348b1e4ab58dd765",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 10,
      "quote": "This key exchange algorithm is the same as ECDHE_ECDSA except that the server's certificate MUST contain an RSA public key authorized for signing and the signature in the ServerKeyExchange message must be computed with the corresponding RSA private key.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In ECDH_anon, the server's Certificate, the CertificateRequest, the\nclient's Certificate, and the CertificateVerify messages MUST NOT be\nsent.\n",
      "id": "c24d35577fc2423f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 26,
      "quote": "In ECDH_anon, the server's Certificate, the CertificateRequest, the client's Certificate, and the CertificateVerify messages MUST NOT be sent.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server MUST send an ephemeral ECDH public key and a specification\nof the corresponding curve in the ServerKeyExchange message.\n",
      "id": "58b960af0c6c94fe",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 34,
      "quote": "The server MUST send an ephemeral ECDH public key and a specification of the corresponding curve in the ServerKeyExchange message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "These\nparameters MUST NOT be signed.\n",
      "id": "66b172da28da7b2a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "These parameters MUST NOT be signed.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Applications using TLS\nwith this algorithm SHOULD provide authentication by other means.\n",
      "id": "9d17bdec0f9f0bd5",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 76,
      "quote": "Applications using TLS with this algorithm SHOULD provide authentication by other means.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To use this authentication mechanism, the client MUST possess a\ncertificate containing an ECDSA- or EdDSA-capable public key.\n",
      "id": "a5a1a856a4eb6d01",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 12,
      "quote": "To use this authentication mechanism, the client MUST possess a certificate containing an ECDSA- or EdDSA-capable public key.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If these conditions are not met, the client SHOULD send a client\nCertificate message containing no certificates.\n",
      "id": "216e77cad00466cc",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 36,
      "quote": "If these conditions are not met, the client SHOULD send a client Certificate message containing no certificates.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In this case, the\nClientKeyExchange MUST be sent as described in Section 2, and the\nCertificateVerify MUST NOT be sent.\n",
      "id": "32768c3b86a6c2f8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 43,
      "quote": "In this case, the ClientKeyExchange MUST be sent as described in Section 2, and the CertificateVerify MUST NOT be sent.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In this case, the\nClientKeyExchange MUST be sent as described in Section 2, and the\nCertificateVerify MUST NOT be sent.\n",
      "id": "c7b8c47f0e086c5d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "In this case, the ClientKeyExchange MUST be sent as described in Section 2, and the CertificateVerify MUST NOT be sent.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A TLS client that proposes ECC cipher suites in its ClientHello\nmessage SHOULD include these extensions.\n",
      "id": "ec7f3de658831d92",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "A TLS client that proposes ECC cipher suites in its ClientHello message SHOULD include these extensions.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers implementing ECC\ncipher suites MUST support these extensions, and when a client uses\nthese extensions, servers MUST NOT negotiate the use of an ECC cipher\nsuite unless they can complete the handshake while respecting the\nchoice of curves specified by the client.\n",
      "id": "686812fd76808cd5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 49,
      "quote": "Servers implementing ECC cipher suites MUST support these extensions, and when a client uses these extensions, servers MUST NOT negotiate the use of an ECC cipher suite unless they can complete the handshake while respecting the choice of curves specified by the client.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers implementing ECC\ncipher suites MUST support these extensions, and when a client uses\nthese extensions, servers MUST NOT negotiate the use of an ECC cipher\nsuite unless they can complete the handshake while respecting the\nchoice of curves specified by the client.\n",
      "id": "5d796f7bd9dceed6",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 59,
      "quote": "Servers implementing ECC cipher suites MUST support these extensions, and when a client uses these extensions, servers MUST NOT negotiate the use of an ECC cipher suite unless they can complete the handshake while respecting the choice of curves specified by the client.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The client MUST NOT include these extensions in the ClientHello\nmessage if it does not propose any ECC cipher suites.\n",
      "id": "e249d1573a9f0453",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 69,
      "quote": "The client MUST NOT include these extensions in the ClientHello message if it does not propose any ECC cipher suites.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations of this document MUST support the\nuncompressed format for all of their supported curves and MUST NOT\nsupport other formats for curves defined in this specification.\n",
      "id": "e6f28c6c0a9a0d4c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "Implementations of this document MUST support the uncompressed format for all of their supported curves and MUST NOT support other formats for curves defined in this specification.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations of this document MUST support the\nuncompressed format for all of their supported curves and MUST NOT\nsupport other formats for curves defined in this specification.\n",
      "id": "14bbf6a66073b36d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 50,
      "quote": "Implementations of this document MUST support the uncompressed format for all of their supported curves and MUST NOT support other formats for curves defined in this specification.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For\nbackwards compatibility purposes, the point format list extension MAY\nstill be included and contain exactly one value: the uncompressed\npoint format (0).\n",
      "id": "d7157eeecc781bb5",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 58,
      "quote": "For backwards compatibility purposes, the point format list extension MAY still be included and contain exactly one value: the uncompressed point format (0).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the client sends the extension and the extension does not contain\nthe uncompressed point format, and the client has used the Supported\nGroups extension to indicate support for any of the curves defined in\nthis specification, then the server MUST abort the handshake and\nreturn an illegal_parameter alert.\n",
      "id": "72a667ff0b59b57f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 67,
      "quote": "If the client sends the extension and the extension does not contain the uncompressed point format, and the client has used the Supported Groups extension to indicate support for any of the curves defined in this specification, then the server MUST abort the handshake and return an illegal_parameter alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client compliant with this specification that supports no other\ncurves MUST send the following octets; note that the first two octets\nindicate the extension type (Supported Point Formats Extension):\n",
      "id": "29a1afa6cbd4c01c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 77,
      "quote": "A client compliant with this specification that supports no other curves MUST send the following octets; note that the first two octets indicate the extension type (Supported Point Formats Extension):",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The extensions SHOULD be sent along with any ClientHello message that\nproposes ECC cipher suites.\n",
      "id": "cb0861754406459d",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 72,
      "quote": "The extensions SHOULD be sent along with any ClientHello message that proposes ECC cipher suites.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients\nSHOULD send both the Supported Elliptic Curves Extension and the\nSupported Point Formats Extension.\n",
      "id": "4b51dda061af512a",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 79,
      "quote": "Clients SHOULD send both the Supported Elliptic Curves Extension and the Supported Point Formats Extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the Supported Point Formats\nExtension is indeed sent, it MUST contain the value 0 (uncompressed)\nas one of the items in the list of point formats.\n",
      "id": "a55d0193c96cb4b9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 87,
      "quote": "If the Supported Point Formats Extension is indeed sent, it MUST contain the value 0 (uncompressed) as one of the items in the list of point formats.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server that receives a ClientHello containing one or both of these\nextensions MUST use the client's enumerated capabilities to guide its\nselection of an appropriate cipher suite.\n",
      "id": "d9e7419b6f7c2048",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 95,
      "quote": "A server that receives a ClientHello containing one or both of these extensions MUST use the client's enumerated capabilities to guide its selection of an appropriate cipher suite.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The\nserver MUST consider the extensions in both cases.\n",
      "id": "c69618dcdc626af2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 103,
      "quote": "The server MUST consider the extensions in both cases.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a server does not understand the Supported Elliptic Curves\nExtension, does not understand the Supported Point Formats Extension,\nor is unable to complete the ECC handshake while restricting itself\nto the enumerated curves and point formats, it MUST NOT negotiate the\nuse of an ECC cipher suite.\n",
      "id": "4e3b7164ae1cb002",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 110,
      "quote": "If a server does not understand the Supported Elliptic Curves Extension, does not understand the Supported Point Formats Extension, or is unable to complete the ECC handshake while restricting itself to the enumerated curves and point formats, it MUST NOT negotiate the use of an ECC cipher suite.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Element to Octet String Conversion Primitive), has constant length\nfor any given field; leading zeros found in this octet string MUST\nNOT be truncated.\n",
      "id": "13dd574aa96e188c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 62,
      "quote": "Element to Octet String Conversion Primitive), has constant length for any given field; leading zeros found in this octet string MUST NOT be truncated.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An ECDHE key exchange using X25519 (curve x25519) goes as follows:\n(1) each party picks a secret key d uniformly at random and computes\nthe corresponding public key x = X25519(d, G); (2) parties exchange\ntheir public keys and compute a shared secret as x_S = X25519(d,\nx_peer); and (3), if either party obtains all-zeroes x_S, it MUST\nabort the handshake (as required by definition of X25519 and X448).\n",
      "id": "8db52409c1e765ad",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 70,
      "quote": "An ECDHE key exchange using X25519 (curve x25519) goes as follows: (1) each party picks a secret key d uniformly at random and computes the corresponding public key x = X25519(d, G); (2) parties exchange their public keys and compute a shared secret as x_S = X25519(d, x_peer); and (3), if either party obtains all-zeroes x_S, it MUST abort the handshake (as required by definition of X25519 and X448).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "All ECDSA computations MUST be performed according to ANSI X9.62 or\nits successors.\n",
      "id": "7553d3a84c5a94a9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 81,
      "quote": "All ECDSA computations MUST be performed according to ANSI X9.62 or its successors.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A secure hash function such as SHA-256, SHA-384, or SHA-512 from\n[FIPS.180-4] MUST be used.\n",
      "id": "14d998f8d5008140",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 88,
      "quote": "A secure hash function such as SHA-256, SHA-384, or SHA-512 from [FIPS.180-4] MUST be used.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "All EdDSA computations MUST be performed according to [RFC8032] or\nits successors.\n",
      "id": "67a8aa8c014d73ae",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 95,
      "quote": "All EdDSA computations MUST be performed according to [RFC8032] or its successors.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The context parameter for Ed448 MUST be\nset to the empty string.\n",
      "id": "fdea0dad11553ec1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 102,
      "quote": "The context parameter for Ed448 MUST be set to the empty string.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "EdDSA signatures MUST have HashAlgorithm of 8\n(Intrinsic).\n",
      "id": "2d87dc8aaa556c5e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 109,
      "quote": "EdDSA signatures MUST have HashAlgorithm of 8 (Intrinsic).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "With the NIST curves, each party MUST validate the public key sent by\nits peer in the ClientKeyExchange and ServerKeyExchange messages.\n",
      "id": "df27364aeb636a56",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 21,
      "quote": "With the NIST curves, each party MUST validate the public key sent by its peer in the ClientKeyExchange and ServerKeyExchange messages.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A\nreceiving party MUST check that the x and y parameters from the\npeer's public value satisfy the curve equation, y^2 = x^3 + ax + b\nmod p.\n",
      "id": "ab4db91a42d6f42f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 28,
      "quote": "A receiving party MUST check that the x and y parameters from the peer's public value satisfy the curve equation, y^2 = x^3 + ax + b mod p.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "With X25519 and X448, a receiving party MUST check whether the\ncomputed premaster secret is the all-zero value and abort the\nhandshake if so, as described in Section 6 of [RFC7748].\n",
      "id": "cd4bafa9e69839ef",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 37,
      "quote": "With X25519 and X448, a receiving party MUST check whether the computed premaster secret is the all-zero value and abort the handshake if so, as described in Section 6 of [RFC7748].",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Note\nthat the server MAY include items that were not found in the client's\nlist.\n",
      "id": "0cefd0e155c9c60f",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "Note that the server MAY include items that were not found in the client's list.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The Supported\nPoint Formats Extension, when used, MUST contain the value 0\n(uncompressed) as one of the items in the list of point formats.\n",
      "id": "1c7695b832c1f827",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 59,
      "quote": "The Supported Point Formats Extension, when used, MUST contain the value 0 (uncompressed) as one of the items in the list of point formats.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client that receives a ServerHello message containing a Supported\nPoint Formats Extension MUST respect the server's choice of point\nformats during the handshake (cf.\n",
      "id": "c5d966f90f8a3810",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 67,
      "quote": "A client that receives a ServerHello message containing a Supported Point Formats Extension MUST respect the server's choice of point formats during the handshake (cf.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "ECC\npublic keys MUST be encoded in certificates as described in\nSection 5.9.\n",
      "id": "a964d776937be6b3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "ECC public keys MUST be encoded in certificates as described in Section 5.9.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "+-------------+-----------------------------------------------------+\n| Algorithm   | Server Certificate Type                             |\n+-------------+-----------------------------------------------------+\n| ECDHE_ECDSA | Certificate MUST contain an ECDSA- or EdDSA-capable |\n|             | public key.\n",
      "id": "a7bef5faf655b80c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 62,
      "quote": "+-------------+-----------------------------------------------------+ | Algorithm   | Server Certificate Type                             | +-------------+-----------------------------------------------------+ | ECDHE_ECDSA | Certificate MUST contain an ECDSA- or EdDSA-capable | |             | public key.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "|\n| ECDHE_RSA   | Certificate MUST contain an RSA public key.\n",
      "id": "ef9b7cfb6c6f3493",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 72,
      "quote": "| | ECDHE_RSA   | Certificate MUST contain an RSA public key.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "certificate MUST respect the client's choice of elliptic curves.\n",
      "id": "391ae3faf896ea44",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 79,
      "quote": "certificate MUST respect the client's choice of elliptic curves.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A\nserver that cannot satisfy this requirement MUST NOT choose an ECC\ncipher suite in its ServerHello message.)\n",
      "id": "bd57251d4ba0ec65",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 85,
      "quote": "A server that cannot satisfy this requirement MUST NOT choose an ECC cipher suite in its ServerHello message.)",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This structure MUST NOT be used with Ed25519 and\nEd448 public keys.\n",
      "id": "2e83ec188f74914f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 167,
      "quote": "This structure MUST NOT be used with Ed25519 and Ed448 public keys.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The certificate MUST\ncontain an ECDSA- or EdDSA-capable public key.\n",
      "id": "cff0ec5b0e04e84c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "The certificate MUST contain an ECDSA- or EdDSA-capable public key.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "X.509 certificates containing ECC public keys or signed using ECDSA\nMUST comply with [RFC3279] or another RFC that replaces or extends\nit.\n",
      "id": "ea849bc1685e263d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 18,
      "quote": "X.509 certificates containing ECC public keys or signed using ECDSA MUST comply with [RFC3279] or another RFC that replaces or extends it.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "X.509 certificates containing ECC public keys or signed using\nEdDSA MUST comply with [RFC8410].\n",
      "id": "cb4c3778b2da0906",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 26,
      "quote": "X.509 certificates containing ECC public keys or signed using EdDSA MUST comply with [RFC8410].",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients SHOULD use the elliptic\ncurve domain parameters recommended in ANSI X9.62, FIPS 186-4, and\nSEC 2 [SECG-SEC2], or in [RFC8032].\n",
      "id": "28b0ea7665fb5e48",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 33,
      "quote": "Clients SHOULD use the elliptic curve domain parameters recommended in ANSI X9.62, FIPS 186-4, and SEC 2 [SECG-SEC2], or in [RFC8032].",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "EdDSA keys using the Ed25519 algorithm MUST use the ed25519 signature\nalgorithm, and Ed448 keys MUST use the ed448 signature algorithm.\n",
      "id": "5ca49bc13a3f9e17",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "EdDSA keys using the Ed25519 algorithm MUST use the ed25519 signature algorithm, and Ed448 keys MUST use the ed448 signature algorithm.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "EdDSA keys using the Ed25519 algorithm MUST use the ed25519 signature\nalgorithm, and Ed448 keys MUST use the ed448 signature algorithm.\n",
      "id": "80b141be0eb30e2e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 48,
      "quote": "EdDSA keys using the Ed25519 algorithm MUST use the ed25519 signature algorithm, and Ed448 keys MUST use the ed448 signature algorithm.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Ed25519, Ed25519ph, Ed448, and Ed448ph keys MUST NOT be used\nwith ECDSA.\n",
      "id": "a6d1b922b7554e4c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 55,
      "quote": "Ed25519, Ed25519ph, Ed448, and Ed448ph keys MUST NOT be used with ECDSA.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-5.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Server implementations SHOULD support all of the following cipher\nsuites, and client implementations SHOULD support at least one of\nthem:\n",
      "id": "60ec3ea14ab6ede0",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "Server implementations SHOULD support all of the following cipher suites, and client implementations SHOULD support at least one of them:",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Server implementations SHOULD support all of the following cipher\nsuites, and client implementations SHOULD support at least one of\nthem:\n",
      "id": "f6e71499122c81a8",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 59,
      "quote": "Server implementations SHOULD support all of the following cipher suites, and client implementations SHOULD support at least one of them:",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422/section-6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If clients need to send such alerts, they\nSHOULD first rekey to the handshake keys if possible.\n",
      "id": "a2ee6f8a7733095b",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "If clients need to send such alerts, they SHOULD first rekey to the handshake keys if possible.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-A.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Values within \"obsolete_RESERVED\" ranges are used in previous\nversions of TLS and MUST NOT be offered or negotiated by TLS 1.3\nimplementations.\n",
      "id": "cc8e8ef842ef4a02",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 39,
      "quote": "Values within \"obsolete_RESERVED\" ranges are used in previous versions of TLS and MUST NOT be offered or negotiated by TLS 1.3 implementations.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-B.3.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-B.3.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS 1.3 implementations MUST NOT send them but might receive them\nfrom older TLS implementations.\n",
      "id": "2c920933bb19d4cc",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 11,
      "quote": "TLS 1.3 implementations MUST NOT send them but might receive them from older TLS implementations.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-B.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-B",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It is RECOMMENDED to use\nan existing CSPRNG implementation in preference to crafting a new\none.\n",
      "id": "0bbba21f0dfca88f",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "It is RECOMMENDED to use an existing CSPRNG implementation in preference to crafting a new one.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-C.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-C.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Applications SHOULD also enforce minimum and maximum key sizes.\n",
      "id": "7af41b1565bc5ed7",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 17,
      "quote": "Applications SHOULD also enforce minimum and maximum key sizes.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-C.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-C.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  Do you use a strong and, most importantly, properly seeded random\nnumber generator (see Appendix C.1) when generating Diffie-Hellman\nprivate values, the ECDSA \"k\" parameter, and other security-\ncritical values?  It is RECOMMENDED that implementations implement\n\"deterministic ECDSA\" as specified in [RFC6979].\n",
      "id": "4e5a754d37c84740",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 77,
      "quote": "-  Do you use a strong and, most importantly, properly seeded random number generator (see Appendix C.1) when generating Diffie-Hellman private values, the ECDSA \"k\" parameter, and other security- critical values?  It is RECOMMENDED that implementations implement \"deterministic ECDSA\" as specified in [RFC6979].",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-C.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-C.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients SHOULD NOT reuse a ticket for multiple connections.\n",
      "id": "bd5f13e873bac452",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 14,
      "quote": "Clients SHOULD NOT reuse a ticket for multiple connections.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-C.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-C.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers that issue tickets SHOULD offer at least as many tickets as\nthe number of connections that a client might use; for example, a web\nbrowser using HTTP/1.1 [RFC7230] might open six connections to a\nserver.\n",
      "id": "5151770057b1be2f",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 20,
      "quote": "Servers that issue tickets SHOULD offer at least as many tickets as the number of connections that a client might use; for example, a web browser using HTTP/1.1 [RFC7230] might open six connections to a server.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-C.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-C.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers SHOULD issue new tickets with every connection.\n",
      "id": "e86bd8f9684b019e",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 29,
      "quote": "Servers SHOULD issue new tickets with every connection.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-C.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-C.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If no such mechanism is used, then the connection has no\nprotection against active man-in-the-middle attack; applications\nMUST NOT use TLS in such a way absent explicit configuration or a\nspecific application profile.\n",
      "id": "3561e9a36182968d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 27,
      "quote": "If no such mechanism is used, then the connection has no protection against active man-in-the-middle attack; applications MUST NOT use TLS in such a way absent explicit configuration or a specific application profile.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-C.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-C.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client using a ticket for resumption SHOULD initiate the connection\nusing the version that was previously negotiated.\n",
      "id": "b97bdb9d2be7f8f3",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 31,
      "quote": "A client using a ticket for resumption SHOULD initiate the connection using the version that was previously negotiated.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Note that 0-RTT data is not compatible with older servers and\nSHOULD NOT be sent absent knowledge that the server supports TLS 1.3.\n",
      "id": "35068840e4eaee92",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 38,
      "quote": "Note that 0-RTT data is not compatible with older servers and SHOULD NOT be sent absent knowledge that the server supports TLS 1.3.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the version chosen by the server is not supported by the client\n(or is not acceptable), the client MUST abort the handshake with a\n\"protocol_version\" alert.\n",
      "id": "f066cdc4aefd277a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 45,
      "quote": "If the version chosen by the server is not supported by the client (or is not acceptable), the client MUST abort the handshake with a \"protocol_version\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Multiple connection attempts may be required\nin order to negotiate a backward-compatible connection; however, this\npractice is vulnerable to downgrade attacks and is NOT RECOMMENDED.\n",
      "id": "efa42305151d508f",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 53,
      "quote": "Multiple connection attempts may be required in order to negotiate a backward-compatible connection; however, this practice is vulnerable to downgrade attacks and is NOT RECOMMENDED.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the\n\"supported_versions\" extension is present, the server MUST negotiate\nusing that extension as described in Section 4.2.1.\n",
      "id": "3a6067026e99b485",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 23,
      "quote": "If the \"supported_versions\" extension is present, the server MUST negotiate using that extension as described in Section 4.2.1.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the\n\"supported_versions\" extension is not present, the server MUST\nnegotiate the minimum of ClientHello.legacy_version and TLS 1.2.\n",
      "id": "2315680880bc1220",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 31,
      "quote": "If the \"supported_versions\" extension is not present, the server MUST negotiate the minimum of ClientHello.legacy_version and TLS 1.2.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the \"supported_versions\" extension is absent and the\nserver only supports versions greater than\nClientHello.legacy_version, the server MUST abort the handshake with\na \"protocol_version\" alert.\n",
      "id": "9a1df01807262f78",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 39,
      "quote": "If the \"supported_versions\" extension is absent and the server only supports versions greater than ClientHello.legacy_version, the server MUST abort the handshake with a \"protocol_version\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers will receive various\nTLS 1.x versions in this field, but its value MUST always be ignored.\n",
      "id": "4ece12480903d6f8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 48,
      "quote": "Servers will receive various TLS 1.x versions in this field, but its value MUST always be ignored.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client that attempts to send 0-RTT data MUST fail a connection if\nit receives a ServerHello with TLS 1.2 or older.\n",
      "id": "028959579192d69c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 23,
      "quote": "A client that attempts to send 0-RTT data MUST fail a connection if it receives a ServerHello with TLS 1.2 or older.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To avoid a downgrade attack, the\nclient SHOULD NOT disable TLS 1.3, only 0-RTT.\n",
      "id": "4346047eb50a6dec",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 30,
      "quote": "To avoid a downgrade attack, the client SHOULD NOT disable TLS 1.3, only 0-RTT.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To avoid this error condition, multi-server deployments SHOULD ensure\na uniform and stable deployment of TLS 1.3 without 0-RTT prior to\nenabling 0-RTT.\n",
      "id": "00c048af65d0cb67",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 37,
      "quote": "To avoid this error condition, multi-server deployments SHOULD ensure a uniform and stable deployment of TLS 1.3 without 0-RTT prior to enabling 0-RTT.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "change_cipher_spec at any time during the handshake, as they must be\nignored by the peer, but if the client sends a non-empty session ID,\nthe server MUST send the change_cipher_spec as described in this\nappendix.\n",
      "id": "c8590e94e3cc2198",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 37,
      "quote": "change_cipher_spec at any time during the handshake, as they must be ignored by the peer, but if the client sends a non-empty session ID, the server MUST send the change_cipher_spec as described in this appendix.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations negotiating the use of older versions of TLS SHOULD\nprefer forward secret and AEAD cipher suites, when available.\n",
      "id": "74480234ccca040e",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 45,
      "quote": "Implementations negotiating the use of older versions of TLS SHOULD prefer forward secret and AEAD cipher suites, when available.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations MUST NOT offer or\nnegotiate RC4 cipher suites for any version of TLS for any reason.\n",
      "id": "7703f525bc4eeb62",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 52,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST NOT offer or negotiate RC4 cipher suites for any version of TLS for any reason.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Ciphers with a strength less than 112 bits MUST NOT be offered or\nnegotiated for any version of TLS for any reason.\n",
      "id": "82e9cb80ecee2e35",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 59,
      "quote": "Ciphers with a strength less than 112 bits MUST NOT be offered or negotiated for any version of TLS for any reason.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The security of SSL 3.0 [RFC6101] is considered insufficient for the\nreasons enumerated in [RFC7568], and it MUST NOT be negotiated for\nany reason.\n",
      "id": "3cf353e9f50ad543",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 66,
      "quote": "The security of SSL 3.0 [RFC6101] is considered insufficient for the reasons enumerated in [RFC7568], and it MUST NOT be negotiated for any reason.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The security of SSL 2.0 [SSL2] is considered insufficient for the\nreasons enumerated in [RFC6176], and it MUST NOT be negotiated for\nany reason.\n",
      "id": "2b681dce619f1b96",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 74,
      "quote": "The security of SSL 2.0 [SSL2] is considered insufficient for the reasons enumerated in [RFC6176], and it MUST NOT be negotiated for any reason.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations MUST NOT send an SSL version 2.0 compatible\nCLIENT-HELLO.\n",
      "id": "6e8dd4744ce39c19",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 82,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST NOT send an SSL version 2.0 compatible CLIENT-HELLO.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations MUST NOT negotiate TLS 1.3 or later\nusing an SSL version 2.0 compatible CLIENT-HELLO.\n",
      "id": "f10eed25cec55366",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 89,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST NOT negotiate TLS 1.3 or later using an SSL version 2.0 compatible CLIENT-HELLO.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations\nare NOT RECOMMENDED to accept an SSL version 2.0 compatible\nCLIENT-HELLO in order to negotiate older versions of TLS.\n",
      "id": "0985e2af6cada2d2",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 96,
      "quote": "Implementations are NOT RECOMMENDED to accept an SSL version 2.0 compatible CLIENT-HELLO in order to negotiate older versions of TLS.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations MUST NOT send a ClientHello.legacy_version or\nServerHello.legacy_version set to 0x0300 or less.\n",
      "id": "bfb9f71abc4a91c2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 104,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST NOT send a ClientHello.legacy_version or ServerHello.legacy_version set to 0x0300 or less.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Any endpoint\nreceiving a Hello message with ClientHello.legacy_version or\nServerHello.legacy_version set to 0x0300 MUST abort the handshake\nwith a \"protocol_version\" alert.\n",
      "id": "0e0ab1aba675f6c4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 111,
      "quote": "Any endpoint receiving a Hello message with ClientHello.legacy_version or ServerHello.legacy_version set to 0x0300 MUST abort the handshake with a \"protocol_version\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations MUST NOT send any records with a version less than\n0x0300.\n",
      "id": "d1b8e8ea942b08a0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 120,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST NOT send any records with a version less than 0x0300.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations SHOULD NOT accept any records with a version\nless than 0x0300 (but may inadvertently do so if the record version\nnumber is ignored completely).\n",
      "id": "67d6a696f79ab6c3",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 127,
      "quote": "Implementations SHOULD NOT accept any records with a version less than 0x0300 (but may inadvertently do so if the record version number is ignored completely).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations MUST NOT use the Truncated HMAC extension, defined in\nSection 7 of [RFC6066], as it is not applicable to AEAD algorithms\nand has been shown to be insecure in some scenarios.\n",
      "id": "4fee5afe842ed71a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 135,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST NOT use the Truncated HMAC extension, defined in Section 7 of [RFC6066], as it is not applicable to AEAD algorithms and has been shown to be insecure in some scenarios.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The value of\nTLSPlaintext.legacy_record_version MUST be ignored by all\nimplementations.\n",
      "id": "99b83b5962448de8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "The value of TLSPlaintext.legacy_record_version MUST be ignored by all implementations.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The value of TLSCiphertext.legacy_record_version is\nincluded in the additional data for deprotection but MAY otherwise be\nignored or MAY be validated to match the fixed constant value.\n",
      "id": "b98b4fb854b4236d",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 52,
      "quote": "The value of TLSCiphertext.legacy_record_version is included in the additional data for deprotection but MAY otherwise be ignored or MAY be validated to match the fixed constant value.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The value of TLSCiphertext.legacy_record_version is\nincluded in the additional data for deprotection but MAY otherwise be\nignored or MAY be validated to match the fixed constant value.\n",
      "id": "b34cc700de0737aa",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 60,
      "quote": "The value of TLSCiphertext.legacy_record_version is included in the additional data for deprotection but MAY otherwise be ignored or MAY be validated to match the fixed constant value.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In order to maximize\ninteroperability with older endpoints, implementations that negotiate\nthe use of TLS 1.0-1.2 SHOULD set the record layer version number to\nthe negotiated version for the ServerHello and all records\nthereafter.\n",
      "id": "e674a1714eca67e2",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 68,
      "quote": "In order to maximize interoperability with older endpoints, implementations that negotiate the use of TLS 1.0-1.2 SHOULD set the record layer version number to the negotiated version for the ServerHello and all records thereafter.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For maximum compatibility with previously non-standard behavior and\nmisconfigured deployments, all implementations SHOULD support\nvalidation of certification paths based on the expectations in this\ndocument, even when handling prior TLS versions' handshakes (see\nSection 4.4.2.2).\n",
      "id": "ab1f5ed888cf0ba9",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 78,
      "quote": "For maximum compatibility with previously non-standard behavior and misconfigured deployments, all implementations SHOULD support validation of certification paths based on the expectations in this document, even when handling prior TLS versions' handshakes (see Section 4.4.2.2).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Because TLS 1.3 always hashes in the transcript\nup to the server Finished, implementations which support both TLS 1.3\nand earlier versions SHOULD indicate the use of the Extended Master\nSecret extension in their APIs whenever TLS 1.3 is used.\n",
      "id": "fe86e7a8b5c83900",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 88,
      "quote": "Because TLS 1.3 always hashes in the transcript up to the server Finished, implementations which support both TLS 1.3 and earlier versions SHOULD indicate the use of the Extended Master Secret extension in their APIs whenever TLS 1.3 is used.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-D.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This ordering should always be followed\n(including in future revisions of this document); in particular, one\nSHOULD NOT use an output of HKDF-Extract as an input to another\napplication of HKDF-Extract without an HKDF-Expand in between.\n",
      "id": "009fd41556087e22",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 29,
      "quote": "This ordering should always be followed (including in future revisions of this document); in particular, one SHOULD NOT use an output of HKDF-Extract as an input to another application of HKDF-Extract without an HKDF-Expand in between.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-E.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "However, because these secrets can be used to compute any\nexporter value, they SHOULD be erased as soon as possible.\n",
      "id": "0a02875bb8c242ad",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 16,
      "quote": "However, because these secrets can be used to compute any exporter value, they SHOULD be erased as soon as possible.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-E.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the\ntotal set of exporter labels is known, then implementations SHOULD\npre-compute the inner Derive-Secret stage of the exporter computation\nfor all those labels, then erase the [early_]exporter_master_secret,\nfollowed by each inner value as soon as it is known that it will not\nbe needed again.\n",
      "id": "af74694f0ca7b101",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 23,
      "quote": "If the total set of exporter labels is known, then implementations SHOULD pre-compute the inner Derive-Secret stage of the exporter computation for all those labels, then erase the [early_]exporter_master_secret, followed by each inner value as soon as it is known that it will not be needed again.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-E.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations\nMUST NOT combine external PSKs with certificate-based authentication\nof either the client or the server unless negotiated by some\nextension.\n",
      "id": "1af1d337d9d83a9a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 158,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST NOT combine external PSKs with certificate-based authentication of either the client or the server unless negotiated by some extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-E.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Note: Exporters can produce arbitrary-length values; if exporters are\nto be used as channel bindings, the exported value MUST be large\nenough to provide collision resistance.\n",
      "id": "70f2af4c037cbd60",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 167,
      "quote": "Note: Exporters can produce arbitrary-length values; if exporters are to be used as channel bindings, the exported value MUST be large enough to provide collision resistance.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-E.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In addition, the early exporter SHOULD NOT be used to generate\nserver-to-client encryption keys because that would entail the reuse\nof those keys.\n",
      "id": "7c674ac475b32ec5",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 17,
      "quote": "In addition, the early exporter SHOULD NOT be used to generate server-to-client encryption keys because that would entail the reuse of those keys.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-E.5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Because clients\ndo not know the exact details of server behavior, they MUST NOT send\nmessages in early data which are not safe to have replayed and which\nthey would not be willing to retry across multiple 1-RTT connections.\n",
      "id": "665545eb9626a988",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 77,
      "quote": "Because clients do not know the exact details of server behavior, they MUST NOT send messages in early data which are not safe to have replayed and which they would not be willing to retry across multiple 1-RTT connections.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-E.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Application protocols MUST NOT use 0-RTT data without a profile that\ndefines its use.\n",
      "id": "42961b7486c365d4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 86,
      "quote": "Application protocols MUST NOT use 0-RTT data without a profile that defines its use.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-E.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In addition, to avoid accidental misuse, TLS implementations MUST NOT\nenable 0-RTT (either sending or accepting) unless specifically\nrequested by the application and MUST NOT automatically resend 0-RTT\ndata if it is rejected by the server unless instructed by the\napplication.\n",
      "id": "438f1a4e5a47e9c2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 93,
      "quote": "In addition, to avoid accidental misuse, TLS implementations MUST NOT enable 0-RTT (either sending or accepting) unless specifically requested by the application and MUST NOT automatically resend 0-RTT data if it is rejected by the server unless instructed by the application.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-E.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In addition, to avoid accidental misuse, TLS implementations MUST NOT\nenable 0-RTT (either sending or accepting) unless specifically\nrequested by the application and MUST NOT automatically resend 0-RTT\ndata if it is rejected by the server unless instructed by the\napplication.\n",
      "id": "864e66e7e2835036",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 103,
      "quote": "In addition, to avoid accidental misuse, TLS implementations MUST NOT enable 0-RTT (either sending or accepting) unless specifically requested by the application and MUST NOT automatically resend 0-RTT data if it is rejected by the server unless instructed by the application.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-E.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In order to allow applications to implement this kind of\nprocessing, TLS implementations MUST provide a way for the\napplication to determine if the handshake has completed.\n",
      "id": "e1cc5e24dfd13535",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 113,
      "quote": "In order to allow applications to implement this kind of processing, TLS implementations MUST provide a way for the application to determine if the handshake has completed.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/appendix-E.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "IESG Approval is REQUIRED for a Y->N transition.\n",
      "id": "2a949f7ea5bda2af",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 108,
      "quote": "IESG Approval is REQUIRED for a Y->N transition.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "IESG Approval is REQUIRED\nfor a Y->N transition.\n",
      "id": "92102a254396ddbc",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 114,
      "quote": "IESG Approval is REQUIRED for a Y->N transition.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If no\ncommon cryptographic parameters can be negotiated, the server MUST\nabort the handshake with an appropriate alert.\n",
      "id": "b10dfa8c5b12ee19",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "If no common cryptographic parameters can be negotiated, the server MUST abort the handshake with an appropriate alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When a client offers\nresumption via a PSK, it SHOULD also supply a \"key_share\" extension\nto the server to allow the server to decline resumption and fall back\nto a full handshake, if needed.\n",
      "id": "97f6e2d3dfd9cd33",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 85,
      "quote": "When a client offers resumption via a PSK, it SHOULD also supply a \"key_share\" extension to the server to allow the server to decline resumption and fall back to a full handshake, if needed.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When PSKs are provisioned out of band, the PSK identity and the KDF\nhash algorithm to be used with the PSK MUST also be provisioned.\n",
      "id": "cd50d0124ec4eee9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 94,
      "quote": "When PSKs are provisioned out of band, the PSK identity and the KDF hash algorithm to be used with the PSK MUST also be provisioned.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If (EC)DHE key establishment\nis in use, then the ServerHello contains a \"key_share\" extension with\nthe server's ephemeral Diffie-Hellman share; the server's share MUST\nbe in the same group as one of the client's shares.\n",
      "id": "75d473a313035a90",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 149,
      "quote": "If (EC)DHE key establishment is in use, then the ServerHello contains a \"key_share\" extension with the server's ephemeral Diffie-Hellman share; the server's share MUST be in the same group as one of the client's shares.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Application Data MUST NOT be sent prior to sending the Finished\nmessage, except as specified in Section 2.3.\n",
      "id": "38850007859c392a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 158,
      "quote": "Application Data MUST NOT be sent prior to sending the Finished message, except as specified in Section 2.3.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If there is no overlap between the received\n\"supported_groups\" and the groups supported by the server, then the\nserver MUST abort the handshake with a \"handshake_failure\" or an\n\"insufficient_security\" alert.\n",
      "id": "e068d06631fb6532",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 68,
      "quote": "If there is no overlap between the received \"supported_groups\" and the groups supported by the server, then the server MUST abort the handshake with a \"handshake_failure\" or an \"insufficient_security\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the server selects a PSK, then it MUST also select a key\nestablishment mode from the set indicated by the client's\n\"psk_key_exchange_modes\" extension (at present, PSK alone or with\n(EC)DHE).\n",
      "id": "dd1ae794904f99ea",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 77,
      "quote": "If the server selects a PSK, then it MUST also select a key establishment mode from the set indicated by the client's \"psk_key_exchange_modes\" extension (at present, PSK alone or with (EC)DHE).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the server selects an (EC)DHE group and the client did not offer a\ncompatible \"key_share\" extension in the initial ClientHello, the\nserver MUST respond with a HelloRetryRequest (Section 4.1.4) message.\n",
      "id": "9cef03a329d73ad2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 86,
      "quote": "If the server selects an (EC)DHE group and the client did not offer a compatible \"key_share\" extension in the initial ClientHello, the server MUST respond with a HelloRetryRequest (Section 4.1.4) message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the server is unable to negotiate a supported set of parameters\n(i.e., there is no overlap between the client and server parameters),\nit MUST abort the handshake with either a \"handshake_failure\" or\n\"insufficient_security\" fatal alert (see Section 6).\n",
      "id": "e7575817257f2d9b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 94,
      "quote": "If the server is unable to negotiate a supported set of parameters (i.e., there is no overlap between the client and server parameters), it MUST abort the handshake with either a \"handshake_failure\" or \"insufficient_security\" fatal alert (see Section 6).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When a client first connects to a server, it is REQUIRED to send the\nClientHello as its first TLS message.\n",
      "id": "005b19d69b5f0606",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 144,
      "quote": "When a client first connects to a server, it is REQUIRED to send the ClientHello as its first TLS message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In that case, the client MUST send the same\nClientHello without modification, except as follows:\n",
      "id": "872331e419b16210",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 151,
      "quote": "In that case, the client MUST send the same ClientHello without modification, except as follows:",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Because TLS 1.3 forbids renegotiation, if a server has negotiated\nTLS 1.3 and receives a ClientHello at any other time, it MUST\nterminate the connection with an \"unexpected_message\" alert.\n",
      "id": "41a65620371214a9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 158,
      "quote": "Because TLS 1.3 forbids renegotiation, if a server has negotiated TLS 1.3 and receives a ClientHello at any other time, it MUST terminate the connection with an \"unexpected_message\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a server established a TLS connection with a previous version of\nTLS and receives a TLS 1.3 ClientHello in a renegotiation, it MUST\nretain the previous protocol version.\n",
      "id": "d5176110f47f21ce",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 166,
      "quote": "If a server established a TLS connection with a previous version of TLS and receives a TLS 1.3 ClientHello in a renegotiation, it MUST retain the previous protocol version.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In particular, it MUST NOT\nnegotiate TLS 1.3.\n",
      "id": "c96714f548349547",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 174,
      "quote": "In particular, it MUST NOT negotiate TLS 1.3.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In\nTLS 1.3, the client indicates its version preferences in the\n\"supported_versions\" extension (Section 4.2.1) and the\nlegacy_version field MUST be set to 0x0303, which is the version\nnumber for TLS 1.2.\n",
      "id": "73c92d8a7f6bd05f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 181,
      "quote": "In TLS 1.3, the client indicates its version preferences in the \"supported_versions\" extension (Section 4.2.1) and the legacy_version field MUST be set to 0x0303, which is the version number for TLS 1.2.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client which has a\ncached session ID set by a pre-TLS 1.3 server SHOULD set this\nfield to that value.\n",
      "id": "4d1e858cb75ea39c",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 191,
      "quote": "A client which has a cached session ID set by a pre-TLS 1.3 server SHOULD set this field to that value.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In compatibility mode (see Appendix D.4),\nthis field MUST be non-empty, so a client not offering a\npre-TLS 1.3 session MUST generate a new 32-byte value.\n",
      "id": "afa3e54661eb83a4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 199,
      "quote": "In compatibility mode (see Appendix D.4), this field MUST be non-empty, so a client not offering a pre-TLS 1.3 session MUST generate a new 32-byte value.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In compatibility mode (see Appendix D.4),\nthis field MUST be non-empty, so a client not offering a\npre-TLS 1.3 session MUST generate a new 32-byte value.\n",
      "id": "d7a3d4bdf1ac6eea",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 207,
      "quote": "In compatibility mode (see Appendix D.4), this field MUST be non-empty, so a client not offering a pre-TLS 1.3 session MUST generate a new 32-byte value.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This value\nneed not be random but SHOULD be unpredictable to avoid\nimplementations fixating on a specific value (also known as\nossification).\n",
      "id": "923169c159396cbf",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 215,
      "quote": "This value need not be random but SHOULD be unpredictable to avoid implementations fixating on a specific value (also known as ossification).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Otherwise, it MUST be set as a zero-length vector\n(i.e., a zero-valued single byte length field).\n",
      "id": "ee1a31fbf30cf717",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 224,
      "quote": "Otherwise, it MUST be set as a zero-length vector (i.e., a zero-valued single byte length field).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the list contains cipher suites that the server\ndoes not recognize, support, or wish to use, the server MUST\nignore those cipher suites and process the remaining ones as\nusual.\n",
      "id": "d5e0951fab56264d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 231,
      "quote": "If the list contains cipher suites that the server does not recognize, support, or wish to use, the server MUST ignore those cipher suites and process the remaining ones as usual.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the client is attempting a PSK key establishment, it\nSHOULD advertise at least one cipher suite indicating a Hash\nassociated with the PSK.\n",
      "id": "00c2c5849fdcde05",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 240,
      "quote": "If the client is attempting a PSK key establishment, it SHOULD advertise at least one cipher suite indicating a Hash associated with the PSK.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For every TLS 1.3 ClientHello, this vector\nMUST contain exactly one byte, set to zero, which corresponds to\nthe \"null\" compression method in prior versions of TLS.\n",
      "id": "48f7675934f4aa5d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 248,
      "quote": "For every TLS 1.3 ClientHello, this vector MUST contain exactly one byte, set to zero, which corresponds to the \"null\" compression method in prior versions of TLS.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a\nTLS 1.3 ClientHello is received with any other value in this\nfield, the server MUST abort the handshake with an\n\"illegal_parameter\" alert.\n",
      "id": "3b18e0360f05118c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 256,
      "quote": "If a TLS 1.3 ClientHello is received with any other value in this field, the server MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Note that TLS 1.3 servers might\nreceive TLS 1.2 or prior ClientHellos which contain other\ncompression methods and (if negotiating such a prior version) MUST\nfollow the procedures for the appropriate prior version of TLS.\n",
      "id": "67ad389ea2030a1a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 265,
      "quote": "Note that TLS 1.3 servers might receive TLS 1.2 or prior ClientHellos which contain other compression methods and (if negotiating such a prior version) MUST follow the procedures for the appropriate prior version of TLS.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MUST ignore unrecognized extensions.\n",
      "id": "4ba5414f74ef5bf4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 274,
      "quote": "Servers MUST ignore unrecognized extensions.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If negotiating a version of TLS prior to 1.3,\na server MUST check that the message either contains no data after\nlegacy_compression_methods or that it contains a valid extensions\nblock with no data following.\n",
      "id": "60407c4a111ead29",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 280,
      "quote": "If negotiating a version of TLS prior to 1.3, a server MUST check that the message either contains no data after legacy_compression_methods or that it contains a valid extensions block with no data following.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If not, then it MUST abort the\nhandshake with a \"decode_error\" alert.\n",
      "id": "a5bd580df3bdfa90",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 289,
      "quote": "If not, then it MUST abort the handshake with a \"decode_error\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In the event that a client requests additional functionality using\nextensions and this functionality is not supplied by the server, the\nclient MAY abort the handshake.\n",
      "id": "a5b1e321d8c36bb8",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 296,
      "quote": "In the event that a client requests additional functionality using extensions and this functionality is not supplied by the server, the client MAY abort the handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In TLS 1.3, the TLS server indicates\nits version using the \"supported_versions\" extension\n(Section 4.2.1), and the legacy_version field MUST be set to\n0x0303, which is the version number for TLS 1.2.\n",
      "id": "45d3759c87b023f9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 113,
      "quote": "In TLS 1.3, the TLS server indicates its version using the \"supported_versions\" extension (Section 4.2.1), and the legacy_version field MUST be set to 0x0303, which is the version number for TLS 1.2.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The last 8 bytes MUST be\noverwritten as described below if negotiating TLS 1.2 or TLS 1.1,\nbut the remaining bytes MUST be random.\n",
      "id": "39bcef49b9ae72d1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 122,
      "quote": "The last 8 bytes MUST be overwritten as described below if negotiating TLS 1.2 or TLS 1.1, but the remaining bytes MUST be random.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The last 8 bytes MUST be\noverwritten as described below if negotiating TLS 1.2 or TLS 1.1,\nbut the remaining bytes MUST be random.\n",
      "id": "fd53c4afa6e8fd00",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 130,
      "quote": "The last 8 bytes MUST be overwritten as described below if negotiating TLS 1.2 or TLS 1.1, but the remaining bytes MUST be random.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This structure is\ngenerated by the server and MUST be generated independently of the\nClientHello.random.\n",
      "id": "af6ec61269ebb2d8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 138,
      "quote": "This structure is generated by the server and MUST be generated independently of the ClientHello.random.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client which\nreceives a legacy_session_id_echo field that does not match what\nit sent in the ClientHello MUST abort the handshake with an\n\"illegal_parameter\" alert.\n",
      "id": "d391da7ea2ed3323",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 146,
      "quote": "A client which receives a legacy_session_id_echo field that does not match what it sent in the ClientHello MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client which receives a\ncipher suite that was not offered MUST abort the handshake with an\n\"illegal_parameter\" alert.\n",
      "id": "72a82d1141e3171f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 155,
      "quote": "A client which receives a cipher suite that was not offered MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "legacy_compression_method:  A single byte which MUST have the\nvalue 0.\n",
      "id": "f72d30fe8f1f3d3c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 163,
      "quote": "legacy_compression_method:  A single byte which MUST have the value 0.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The ServerHello MUST only include\nextensions which are required to establish the cryptographic\ncontext and negotiate the protocol version.\n",
      "id": "eab010798f42628c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 170,
      "quote": "The ServerHello MUST only include extensions which are required to establish the cryptographic context and negotiate the protocol version.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "All TLS 1.3\nServerHello messages MUST contain the \"supported_versions\"\nextension.\n",
      "id": "1b957a008808a714",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 178,
      "quote": "All TLS 1.3 ServerHello messages MUST contain the \"supported_versions\" extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Upon receiving a message with type server_hello, implementations MUST\nfirst examine the Random value and, if it matches this value, process\nit as described in Section 4.1.4).\n",
      "id": "6182228959970007",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 186,
      "quote": "Upon receiving a message with type server_hello, implementations MUST first examine the Random value and, if it matches this value, process it as described in Section 4.1.4).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS 1.3 servers which negotiate TLS 1.2 or below in\nresponse to a ClientHello MUST set the last 8 bytes of their Random\nvalue specially in their ServerHello.\n",
      "id": "4417392a7fb8abca",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 194,
      "quote": "TLS 1.3 servers which negotiate TLS 1.2 or below in response to a ClientHello MUST set the last 8 bytes of their Random value specially in their ServerHello.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If negotiating TLS 1.2, TLS 1.3 servers MUST set the last 8 bytes of\ntheir Random value to the bytes:\n",
      "id": "dee73fa43fc5774c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 202,
      "quote": "If negotiating TLS 1.2, TLS 1.3 servers MUST set the last 8 bytes of their Random value to the bytes:",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If negotiating TLS 1.1 or below, TLS 1.3 servers MUST, and TLS 1.2\nservers SHOULD, set the last 8 bytes of their ServerHello.Random\nvalue to the bytes:\n",
      "id": "1e0a3de4ec540923",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 209,
      "quote": "If negotiating TLS 1.1 or below, TLS 1.3 servers MUST, and TLS 1.2 servers SHOULD, set the last 8 bytes of their ServerHello.Random value to the bytes:",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS 1.3 clients receiving a ServerHello indicating TLS 1.2 or below\nMUST check that the last 8 bytes are not equal to either of these\nvalues.\n",
      "id": "cd2e51dbcfe07872",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 217,
      "quote": "TLS 1.3 clients receiving a ServerHello indicating TLS 1.2 or below MUST check that the last 8 bytes are not equal to either of these values.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS 1.2 clients SHOULD also check that the last 8 bytes are\nnot equal to the second value if the ServerHello indicates TLS 1.1 or\nbelow.\n",
      "id": "76b8d4e5b54a6641",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 225,
      "quote": "TLS 1.2 clients SHOULD also check that the last 8 bytes are not equal to the second value if the ServerHello indicates TLS 1.1 or below.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a match is found, the client MUST abort the handshake with\nan \"illegal_parameter\" alert.\n",
      "id": "5d01154e70093464",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 233,
      "quote": "If a match is found, the client MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A legacy TLS client performing renegotiation with TLS 1.2 or prior\nand which receives a TLS 1.3 ServerHello during renegotiation MUST\nabort the handshake with a \"protocol_version\" alert.\n",
      "id": "a9c4d9de9bc869e6",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 240,
      "quote": "A legacy TLS client performing renegotiation with TLS 1.2 or prior and which receives a TLS 1.3 ServerHello during renegotiation MUST abort the handshake with a \"protocol_version\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server's extensions MUST contain \"supported_versions\".\n",
      "id": "29c848806cacb9e3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "The server's extensions MUST contain \"supported_versions\".",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Additionally, it SHOULD contain the minimal set of extensions\nnecessary for the client to generate a correct ClientHello pair.\n",
      "id": "dd15bfb69bcdd610",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 70,
      "quote": "Additionally, it SHOULD contain the minimal set of extensions necessary for the client to generate a correct ClientHello pair.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "As\nwith the ServerHello, a HelloRetryRequest MUST NOT contain any\nextensions that were not first offered by the client in its\nClientHello, with the exception of optionally the \"cookie\" (see\nSection 4.2.2) extension.\n",
      "id": "dbb8e4564a355733",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 77,
      "quote": "As with the ServerHello, a HelloRetryRequest MUST NOT contain any extensions that were not first offered by the client in its ClientHello, with the exception of optionally the \"cookie\" (see Section 4.2.2) extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Upon receipt of a HelloRetryRequest, the client MUST check the\nlegacy_version, legacy_session_id_echo, cipher_suite, and\nlegacy_compression_method as specified in Section 4.1.3 and then\nprocess the extensions, starting with determining the version using\n\"supported_versions\".\n",
      "id": "abf9a5b268de4302",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 87,
      "quote": "Upon receipt of a HelloRetryRequest, the client MUST check the legacy_version, legacy_session_id_echo, cipher_suite, and legacy_compression_method as specified in Section 4.1.3 and then process the extensions, starting with determining the version using \"supported_versions\".",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MUST abort the handshake with an\n\"illegal_parameter\" alert if the HelloRetryRequest would not result\nin any change in the ClientHello.\n",
      "id": "f3026b04b3878269",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 97,
      "quote": "Clients MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert if the HelloRetryRequest would not result in any change in the ClientHello.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a client receives a second\nHelloRetryRequest in the same connection (i.e., where the ClientHello\nwas itself in response to a HelloRetryRequest), it MUST abort the\nhandshake with an \"unexpected_message\" alert.\n",
      "id": "bdae2e12f7b1d4f9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 105,
      "quote": "If a client receives a second HelloRetryRequest in the same connection (i.e., where the ClientHello was itself in response to a HelloRetryRequest), it MUST abort the handshake with an \"unexpected_message\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Otherwise, the client MUST process all extensions in the\nHelloRetryRequest and send a second updated ClientHello.\n",
      "id": "1862fd868a428757",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 114,
      "quote": "Otherwise, the client MUST process all extensions in the HelloRetryRequest and send a second updated ClientHello.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client which receives a cipher suite that was not offered MUST\nabort the handshake.\n",
      "id": "6cb0ef45c8699ad3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 121,
      "quote": "A client which receives a cipher suite that was not offered MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MUST ensure that they negotiate the\nsame cipher suite when receiving a conformant updated ClientHello (if\nthe server selects the cipher suite as the first step in the\nnegotiation, then this will happen automatically).\n",
      "id": "fa90a6ebf67b5372",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 128,
      "quote": "Servers MUST ensure that they negotiate the same cipher suite when receiving a conformant updated ClientHello (if the server selects the cipher suite as the first step in the negotiation, then this will happen automatically).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Upon receiving\nthe ServerHello, clients MUST check that the cipher suite supplied in\nthe ServerHello is the same as that in the HelloRetryRequest and\notherwise abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.\n",
      "id": "75443a4e3d4c052a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 137,
      "quote": "Upon receiving the ServerHello, clients MUST check that the cipher suite supplied in the ServerHello is the same as that in the HelloRetryRequest and otherwise abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In addition, in its updated ClientHello, the client SHOULD NOT offer\nany pre-shared keys associated with a hash other than that of the\nselected cipher suite.\n",
      "id": "29f45c7e3f29acaa",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 146,
      "quote": "In addition, in its updated ClientHello, the client SHOULD NOT offer any pre-shared keys associated with a hash other than that of the selected cipher suite.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The value of selected_version in the HelloRetryRequest\n\"supported_versions\" extension MUST be retained in the ServerHello,\nand a client MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\"\nalert if the value changes.\n",
      "id": "65e6f4b97af84f33",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 154,
      "quote": "The value of selected_version in the HelloRetryRequest \"supported_versions\" extension MUST be retained in the ServerHello, and a client MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert if the value changes.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The value of selected_version in the HelloRetryRequest\n\"supported_versions\" extension MUST be retained in the ServerHello,\nand a client MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\"\nalert if the value changes.\n",
      "id": "c4928a980c0f9cd9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 163,
      "quote": "The value of selected_version in the HelloRetryRequest \"supported_versions\" extension MUST be retained in the ServerHello, and a client MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert if the value changes.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations of this specification MUST send this extension in the\nClientHello containing all versions of TLS which they are prepared to\nnegotiate (for this specification, that means minimally 0x0304, but\nif previous versions of TLS are allowed to be negotiated, they MUST\nbe present as well).\n",
      "id": "76ee01ab38ae49ec",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 61,
      "quote": "Implementations of this specification MUST send this extension in the ClientHello containing all versions of TLS which they are prepared to negotiate (for this specification, that means minimally 0x0304, but if previous versions of TLS are allowed to be negotiated, they MUST be present as well).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations of this specification MUST send this extension in the\nClientHello containing all versions of TLS which they are prepared to\nnegotiate (for this specification, that means minimally 0x0304, but\nif previous versions of TLS are allowed to be negotiated, they MUST\nbe present as well).\n",
      "id": "90297231957bd8ef",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 71,
      "quote": "Implementations of this specification MUST send this extension in the ClientHello containing all versions of TLS which they are prepared to negotiate (for this specification, that means minimally 0x0304, but if previous versions of TLS are allowed to be negotiated, they MUST be present as well).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If this extension is not present, servers which are compliant with\nthis specification and which also support TLS 1.2 MUST negotiate\nTLS 1.2 or prior as specified in [RFC5246], even if\nClientHello.legacy_version is 0x0304 or later.\n",
      "id": "6bd8bc474596d812",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 81,
      "quote": "If this extension is not present, servers which are compliant with this specification and which also support TLS 1.2 MUST negotiate TLS 1.2 or prior as specified in [RFC5246], even if ClientHello.legacy_version is 0x0304 or later.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MAY abort the\nhandshake upon receiving a ClientHello with legacy_version 0x0304 or\nlater.\n",
      "id": "2b9e23db3a8bf16c",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 90,
      "quote": "Servers MAY abort the handshake upon receiving a ClientHello with legacy_version 0x0304 or later.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If this extension is present in the ClientHello, servers MUST NOT use\nthe ClientHello.legacy_version value for version negotiation and MUST\nuse only the \"supported_versions\" extension to determine client\npreferences.\n",
      "id": "30b97efb1204a874",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 98,
      "quote": "If this extension is present in the ClientHello, servers MUST NOT use the ClientHello.legacy_version value for version negotiation and MUST use only the \"supported_versions\" extension to determine client preferences.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If this extension is present in the ClientHello, servers MUST NOT use\nthe ClientHello.legacy_version value for version negotiation and MUST\nuse only the \"supported_versions\" extension to determine client\npreferences.\n",
      "id": "117b8e4cf38485f1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 107,
      "quote": "If this extension is present in the ClientHello, servers MUST NOT use the ClientHello.legacy_version value for version negotiation and MUST use only the \"supported_versions\" extension to determine client preferences.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MUST only select a version of TLS present in\nthat extension and MUST ignore any unknown versions that are present\nin that extension.\n",
      "id": "9bb38757ec23daa3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 116,
      "quote": "Servers MUST only select a version of TLS present in that extension and MUST ignore any unknown versions that are present in that extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MUST only select a version of TLS present in\nthat extension and MUST ignore any unknown versions that are present\nin that extension.\n",
      "id": "8ba00072029cd718",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 124,
      "quote": "Servers MUST only select a version of TLS present in that extension and MUST ignore any unknown versions that are present in that extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MUST be prepared to\nreceive ClientHellos that include this extension but do not include\n0x0304 in the list of versions.\n",
      "id": "c0b04475fe68a2dd",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 132,
      "quote": "Servers MUST be prepared to receive ClientHellos that include this extension but do not include 0x0304 in the list of versions.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations of TLS 1.3 which choose to support prior\nversions of TLS SHOULD support TLS 1.2.\n",
      "id": "eeedb52a4b15ed1e",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 140,
      "quote": "Implementations of TLS 1.3 which choose to support prior versions of TLS SHOULD support TLS 1.2.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server which negotiates a version of TLS prior to TLS 1.3 MUST set\nServerHello.version and MUST NOT send the \"supported_versions\"\nextension.\n",
      "id": "688dd95fa5fc7d0d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 147,
      "quote": "A server which negotiates a version of TLS prior to TLS 1.3 MUST set ServerHello.version and MUST NOT send the \"supported_versions\" extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server which negotiates a version of TLS prior to TLS 1.3 MUST set\nServerHello.version and MUST NOT send the \"supported_versions\"\nextension.\n",
      "id": "b488c0e18b2fce50",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 155,
      "quote": "A server which negotiates a version of TLS prior to TLS 1.3 MUST set ServerHello.version and MUST NOT send the \"supported_versions\" extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server which negotiates TLS 1.3 MUST respond by sending\na \"supported_versions\" extension containing the selected version\nvalue (0x0304).\n",
      "id": "046ad44ca04a3e8f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 163,
      "quote": "A server which negotiates TLS 1.3 MUST respond by sending a \"supported_versions\" extension containing the selected version value (0x0304).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It MUST set the ServerHello.legacy_version field to\n0x0303 (TLS 1.2).\n",
      "id": "e90ff39c0d4d11d6",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 171,
      "quote": "It MUST set the ServerHello.legacy_version field to 0x0303 (TLS 1.2).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MUST check for this extension prior to\nprocessing the rest of the ServerHello (although they will have to\n",
      "id": "ea526891e6481a37",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 178,
      "quote": "Clients MUST check for this extension prior to processing the rest of the ServerHello (although they will have to",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If this\nextension is present, clients MUST ignore the\nServerHello.legacy_version value and MUST use only the\n\"supported_versions\" extension to determine the selected version.\n",
      "id": "74f3ad32a0f00007",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 185,
      "quote": "If this extension is present, clients MUST ignore the ServerHello.legacy_version value and MUST use only the \"supported_versions\" extension to determine the selected version.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If this\nextension is present, clients MUST ignore the\nServerHello.legacy_version value and MUST use only the\n\"supported_versions\" extension to determine the selected version.\n",
      "id": "57500015faad53dd",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 194,
      "quote": "If this extension is present, clients MUST ignore the ServerHello.legacy_version value and MUST use only the \"supported_versions\" extension to determine the selected version.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If\nthe \"supported_versions\" extension in the ServerHello contains a\nversion not offered by the client or contains a version prior to\nTLS 1.3, the client MUST abort the handshake with an\n\"illegal_parameter\" alert.\n",
      "id": "fbe002703a61e612",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 203,
      "quote": "If the \"supported_versions\" extension in the ServerHello contains a version not offered by the client or contains a version prior to TLS 1.3, the client MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the\nclient opts to do so, it MUST supply both the \"pre_shared_key\" and\n\"early_data\" extensions.\n",
      "id": "23025bbd378fa98e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 131,
      "quote": "If the client opts to do so, it MUST supply both the \"pre_shared_key\" and \"early_data\" extensions.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The PSK used to encrypt the\nearly data MUST be the first PSK listed in the client's\n\"pre_shared_key\" extension.\n",
      "id": "d6262dcc5a65eeb6",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 139,
      "quote": "The PSK used to encrypt the early data MUST be the first PSK listed in the client's \"pre_shared_key\" extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For PSKs provisioned via NewSessionTicket, a server MUST validate\nthat the ticket age for the selected PSK identity (computed by\nsubtracting ticket_age_add from PskIdentity.obfuscated_ticket_age\nmodulo 2^32) is within a small tolerance of the time since the ticket\nwas issued (see Section 8).\n",
      "id": "844f87075683da49",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 147,
      "quote": "For PSKs provisioned via NewSessionTicket, a server MUST validate that the ticket age for the selected PSK identity (computed by subtracting ticket_age_add from PskIdentity.obfuscated_ticket_age modulo 2^32) is within a small tolerance of the time since the ticket was issued (see Section 8).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If it is not, the server SHOULD proceed\nwith the handshake but reject 0-RTT, and SHOULD NOT take any other\naction that assumes that this ClientHello is fresh.\n",
      "id": "710e2c7e2536e962",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 157,
      "quote": "If it is not, the server SHOULD proceed with the handshake but reject 0-RTT, and SHOULD NOT take any other action that assumes that this ClientHello is fresh.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If it is not, the server SHOULD proceed\nwith the handshake but reject 0-RTT, and SHOULD NOT take any other\naction that assumes that this ClientHello is fresh.\n",
      "id": "77fe6b7805044ab1",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 165,
      "quote": "If it is not, the server SHOULD proceed with the handshake but reject 0-RTT, and SHOULD NOT take any other action that assumes that this ClientHello is fresh.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server which receives an \"early_data\" extension MUST behave in one\nof three ways:\n",
      "id": "d81672f8522ce714",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 173,
      "quote": "A server which receives an \"early_data\" extension MUST behave in one of three ways:",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST NOT include the\n\"early_data\" extension in its followup ClientHello.\n",
      "id": "d7b27ded396d510e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 180,
      "quote": "A client MUST NOT include the \"early_data\" extension in its followup ClientHello.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In order to accept early data, the server MUST have accepted a PSK\ncipher suite and selected the first key offered in the client's\n\"pre_shared_key\" extension.\n",
      "id": "ffe09bf4a6a1f7fd",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 187,
      "quote": "In order to accept early data, the server MUST have accepted a PSK cipher suite and selected the first key offered in the client's \"pre_shared_key\" extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In addition, it MUST verify that the\nfollowing values are the same as those associated with the\nselected PSK:\n",
      "id": "5a68da93877fb1c0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 195,
      "quote": "In addition, it MUST verify that the following values are the same as those associated with the selected PSK:",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Future extensions MUST define their interaction with 0-RTT.\n",
      "id": "d277b84bf1a7b06e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 203,
      "quote": "Future extensions MUST define their interaction with 0-RTT.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If any of these checks fail, the server MUST NOT respond with the\nextension and must discard all the first-flight data using one of the\nfirst two mechanisms listed above (thus falling back to 1-RTT or\n2-RTT).\n",
      "id": "f615fea14e863ff0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 209,
      "quote": "If any of these checks fail, the server MUST NOT respond with the extension and must discard all the first-flight data using one of the first two mechanisms listed above (thus falling back to 1-RTT or 2-RTT).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the server chooses to accept the \"early_data\" extension, then it\nMUST comply with the same error-handling requirements specified for\nall records when processing early data records.\n",
      "id": "605af3386085090a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 218,
      "quote": "If the server chooses to accept the \"early_data\" extension, then it MUST comply with the same error-handling requirements specified for all records when processing early data records.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Specifically, if the\nserver fails to decrypt a 0-RTT record following an accepted\n\"early_data\" extension, it MUST terminate the connection with a\n\"bad_record_mac\" alert as per Section 5.2.\n",
      "id": "6c9dc5834099cf71",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 226,
      "quote": "Specifically, if the server fails to decrypt a 0-RTT record following an accepted \"early_data\" extension, it MUST terminate the connection with a \"bad_record_mac\" alert as per Section 5.2.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the server rejects the \"early_data\" extension, the client\napplication MAY opt to retransmit the Application Data previously\nsent in early data once the handshake has been completed.\n",
      "id": "1b1fb0021ac37e01",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 235,
      "quote": "If the server rejects the \"early_data\" extension, the client application MAY opt to retransmit the Application Data previously sent in early data once the handshake has been completed.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A TLS implementation SHOULD NOT automatically resend early data;\napplications are in a better position to decide when retransmission\nis appropriate.\n",
      "id": "aa53e90df0a806c2",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 243,
      "quote": "A TLS implementation SHOULD NOT automatically resend early data; applications are in a better position to decide when retransmission is appropriate.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A TLS implementation MUST NOT automatically resend\nearly data unless the negotiated connection selects the same ALPN\nprotocol.\n",
      "id": "aadce952eb81e08f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 251,
      "quote": "A TLS implementation MUST NOT automatically resend early data unless the negotiated connection selects the same ALPN protocol.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MUST NOT attempt to\nuse tickets which have ages greater than the \"ticket_lifetime\" value\nwhich was provided with the ticket.\n",
      "id": "70a7626e603a4383",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 19,
      "quote": "Clients MUST NOT attempt to use tickets which have ages greater than the \"ticket_lifetime\" value which was provided with the ticket.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.11.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In order to avoid deadlocks,\nwhen accepting \"early_data\", servers MUST process the client's\nClientHello and then immediately send their flight of messages,\nrather than waiting for the client's EndOfEarlyData message before\nsending its ServerHello.\n",
      "id": "231a4f40282f02e3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 13,
      "quote": "In order to avoid deadlocks, when accepting \"early_data\", servers MUST process the client's ClientHello and then immediately send their flight of messages, rather than waiting for the client's EndOfEarlyData message before sending its ServerHello.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.11.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For identities\nestablished externally, an obfuscated_ticket_age of 0 SHOULD be\nused, and servers MUST ignore the value.\n",
      "id": "7429abf3835d4721",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 113,
      "quote": "For identities established externally, an obfuscated_ticket_age of 0 SHOULD be used, and servers MUST ignore the value.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For externally established PSKs, the Hash algorithm MUST be set when\n",
      "id": "6ea23c49a492d05e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 121,
      "quote": "For externally established PSKs, the Hash algorithm MUST be set when",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server MUST ensure that it selects a compatible PSK\n(if any) and cipher suite.\n",
      "id": "f3064356bb5fa9ac",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 127,
      "quote": "The server MUST ensure that it selects a compatible PSK (if any) and cipher suite.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients, however, SHOULD\nstore the SNI with the PSK to fulfill the requirements of\nSection 4.6.1.\n",
      "id": "8c132252468686fc",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 134,
      "quote": "Clients, however, SHOULD store the SNI with the PSK to fulfill the requirements of Section 4.6.1.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Any unknown PSKs (e.g., ones\nnot in the PSK database or encrypted with an unknown key) SHOULD\nsimply be ignored.\n",
      "id": "3b6b02db3d65bab7",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 142,
      "quote": "Any unknown PSKs (e.g., ones not in the PSK database or encrypted with an unknown key) SHOULD simply be ignored.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If no acceptable PSKs are found, the server\nSHOULD perform a non-PSK handshake if possible.\n",
      "id": "40e78921cdaf2102",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 150,
      "quote": "If no acceptable PSKs are found, the server SHOULD perform a non-PSK handshake if possible.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If backward\ncompatibility is important, client-provided, externally established\nPSKs SHOULD influence cipher suite selection.\n",
      "id": "65f219443c6233d9",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 157,
      "quote": "If backward compatibility is important, client-provided, externally established PSKs SHOULD influence cipher suite selection.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Prior to accepting PSK key establishment, the server MUST validate\nthe corresponding binder value (see Section 4.2.11.2 below).\n",
      "id": "aee3a4b91390d1b6",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 165,
      "quote": "Prior to accepting PSK key establishment, the server MUST validate the corresponding binder value (see Section 4.2.11.2 below).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If this\nvalue is not present or does not validate, the server MUST abort the\nhandshake.\n",
      "id": "cb53eb2a6f7c43aa",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 172,
      "quote": "If this value is not present or does not validate, the server MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers SHOULD NOT attempt to validate multiple binders;\nrather, they SHOULD select a single PSK and validate solely the\nbinder that corresponds to that PSK.\n",
      "id": "2c53ae685b9a4ba5",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 180,
      "quote": "Servers SHOULD NOT attempt to validate multiple binders; rather, they SHOULD select a single PSK and validate solely the binder that corresponds to that PSK.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers SHOULD NOT attempt to validate multiple binders;\nrather, they SHOULD select a single PSK and validate solely the\nbinder that corresponds to that PSK.\n",
      "id": "8d4e351161aa827d",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 188,
      "quote": "Servers SHOULD NOT attempt to validate multiple binders; rather, they SHOULD select a single PSK and validate solely the binder that corresponds to that PSK.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MUST verify that the server's selected_identity is within the\nrange supplied by the client, that the server selected a cipher suite\nindicating a Hash associated with the PSK, and that a server\n\"key_share\" extension is present if required by the ClientHello\n\"psk_key_exchange_modes\" extension.\n",
      "id": "a7b66586bd3d512c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 196,
      "quote": "Clients MUST verify that the server's selected_identity is within the range supplied by the client, that the server selected a cipher suite indicating a Hash associated with the PSK, and that a server \"key_share\" extension is present if required by the ClientHello \"psk_key_exchange_modes\" extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If these values are not\nconsistent, the client MUST abort the handshake with an\n\"illegal_parameter\" alert.\n",
      "id": "192b651a7ed0e300",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 206,
      "quote": "If these values are not consistent, the client MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the server supplies an \"early_data\" extension, the client MUST\nverify that the server's selected_identity is 0.\n",
      "id": "c0179567d3dbf745",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 214,
      "quote": "If the server supplies an \"early_data\" extension, the client MUST verify that the server's selected_identity is 0.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If any other value\nis returned, the client MUST abort the handshake with an\n\"illegal_parameter\" alert.\n",
      "id": "c9165a378ef788dd",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 221,
      "quote": "If any other value is returned, the client MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The \"pre_shared_key\" extension MUST be the last extension in the\nClientHello (this facilitates implementation as described below).\n",
      "id": "80e1b862f9dfbc85",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 229,
      "quote": "The \"pre_shared_key\" extension MUST be the last extension in the ClientHello (this facilitates implementation as described below).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MUST check that it is the last extension and otherwise fail\nthe handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.\n",
      "id": "165b38376175b179",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 236,
      "quote": "Servers MUST check that it is the last extension and otherwise fail the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When sending a HelloRetryRequest, the server MAY provide a \"cookie\"\nextension to the client (this is an exception to the usual rule that\nthe only extensions that may be sent are those that appear in the\nClientHello).\n",
      "id": "79824a7b4eb20072",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 37,
      "quote": "When sending a HelloRetryRequest, the server MAY provide a \"cookie\" extension to the client (this is an exception to the usual rule that the only extensions that may be sent are those that appear in the ClientHello).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When sending the new ClientHello, the client MUST copy\nthe contents of the extension received in the HelloRetryRequest into\na \"cookie\" extension in the new ClientHello.\n",
      "id": "2e326cab508fa7f2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 46,
      "quote": "When sending the new ClientHello, the client MUST copy the contents of the extension received in the HelloRetryRequest into a \"cookie\" extension in the new ClientHello.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MUST NOT use\ncookies in their initial ClientHello in subsequent connections.\n",
      "id": "bd0d6be60129293b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "Clients MUST NOT use cookies in their initial ClientHello in subsequent connections.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers operating statelessly MUST ignore these records.\n",
      "id": "cbcf7b78e9caf6cf",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 61,
      "quote": "Servers operating statelessly MUST ignore these records.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The keys found in certificates MUST also\nbe of appropriate type for the signature algorithms they are used\nwith.\n",
      "id": "f6840a998bc64b3b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 172,
      "quote": "The keys found in certificates MUST also be of appropriate type for the signature algorithms they are used with.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients which desire the\nserver to authenticate itself via a certificate MUST send the\n\"signature_algorithms\" extension.\n",
      "id": "0a0ef6ed6de0e1ac",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 180,
      "quote": "Clients which desire the server to authenticate itself via a certificate MUST send the \"signature_algorithms\" extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a server is authenticating via\na certificate and the client has not sent a \"signature_algorithms\"\nextension, then the server MUST abort the handshake with a\n\"missing_extension\" alert (see Section 9.2).\n",
      "id": "dadffba726b05db4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 188,
      "quote": "If a server is authenticating via a certificate and the client has not sent a \"signature_algorithms\" extension, then the server MUST abort the handshake with a \"missing_extension\" alert (see Section 9.2).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS 1.2 implementations SHOULD also process this extension.\n",
      "id": "4cabe718c48e4a28",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 197,
      "quote": "TLS 1.2 implementations SHOULD also process this extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations which have the same policy in both cases MAY omit the\n\"signature_algorithms_cert\" extension.\n",
      "id": "a1ead1d2188a0c2c",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 203,
      "quote": "Implementations which have the same policy in both cases MAY omit the \"signature_algorithms_cert\" extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "These values refer solely to signatures\nwhich appear in certificates (see Section 4.4.2.2) and are not\ndefined for use in signed TLS handshake messages, although they\nMAY appear in \"signature_algorithms\" and\n\"signature_algorithms_cert\" for backward compatibility with\nTLS 1.2.\n",
      "id": "3af7b0cda3b0e97c",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 210,
      "quote": "These values refer solely to signatures which appear in certificates (see Section 4.4.2.2) and are not defined for use in signed TLS handshake messages, although they MAY appear in \"signature_algorithms\" and \"signature_algorithms_cert\" for backward compatibility with TLS 1.2.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The length of the Salt MUST be equal to the length of the output\nof the digest algorithm.\n",
      "id": "80555d519c6f2370",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 221,
      "quote": "The length of the Salt MUST be equal to the length of the output of the digest algorithm.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the public key is carried in an X.509\ncertificate, it MUST use the rsaEncryption OID [RFC5280].\n",
      "id": "2152825c8167f789",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 228,
      "quote": "If the public key is carried in an X.509 certificate, it MUST use the rsaEncryption OID [RFC5280].",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The length of the Salt MUST be equal to the length of the digest\nalgorithm.\n",
      "id": "51d2174120eeeacf",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 235,
      "quote": "The length of the Salt MUST be equal to the length of the digest algorithm.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the public key is carried in an X.509 certificate,\nit MUST use the RSASSA-PSS OID [RFC5756].\n",
      "id": "5a0f30e26a8a0901",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 242,
      "quote": "If the public key is carried in an X.509 certificate, it MUST use the RSASSA-PSS OID [RFC5756].",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When used in\ncertificate signatures, the algorithm parameters MUST be DER\nencoded.\n",
      "id": "d44f4b10e6141a1e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 249,
      "quote": "When used in certificate signatures, the algorithm parameters MUST be DER encoded.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the corresponding public key's parameters are\npresent, then the parameters in the signature MUST be identical to\nthose in the public key.\n",
      "id": "8edde5af99d0f493",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 257,
      "quote": "If the corresponding public key's parameters are present, then the parameters in the signature MUST be identical to those in the public key.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "These values refer solely to\nsignatures which appear in certificates (see Section 4.4.2.2) and\nare not defined for use in signed TLS handshake messages, although\nthey MAY appear in \"signature_algorithms\" and\n\"signature_algorithms_cert\" for backward compatibility with\nTLS 1.2.\n",
      "id": "e20adffb9dd4f740",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 265,
      "quote": "These values refer solely to signatures which appear in certificates (see Section 4.4.2.2) and are not defined for use in signed TLS handshake messages, although they MAY appear in \"signature_algorithms\" and \"signature_algorithms_cert\" for backward compatibility with TLS 1.2.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints SHOULD NOT negotiate these algorithms but are\npermitted to do so solely for backward compatibility.\n",
      "id": "420ec11afd4d43dc",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 276,
      "quote": "Endpoints SHOULD NOT negotiate these algorithms but are permitted to do so solely for backward compatibility.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients\noffering these values MUST list them as the lowest priority\n(listed after all other algorithms in SignatureSchemeList).\n",
      "id": "5fb8786068822c94",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 283,
      "quote": "Clients offering these values MUST list them as the lowest priority (listed after all other algorithms in SignatureSchemeList).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS 1.3 servers MUST NOT offer a SHA-1 signed certificate unless\nno valid certificate chain can be produced without it (see\nSection 4.4.2.2).\n",
      "id": "bd27d653b32bb7a5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 291,
      "quote": "TLS 1.3 servers MUST NOT offer a SHA-1 signed certificate unless no valid certificate chain can be produced without it (see Section 4.4.2.2).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A certificate that\nbegins a certification path MAY use a signature algorithm that is not\nadvertised as being supported in the \"signature_algorithms\"\nextension.\n",
      "id": "1e225cfcb93bee7d",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 299,
      "quote": "A certificate that begins a certification path MAY use a signature algorithm that is not advertised as being supported in the \"signature_algorithms\" extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS 1.3\nimplementations willing to negotiate TLS 1.2 MUST behave in\naccordance with the requirements of [RFC5246] when negotiating that\nversion.\n",
      "id": "e1419856d5601312",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 308,
      "quote": "TLS 1.3 implementations willing to negotiate TLS 1.2 MUST behave in accordance with the requirements of [RFC5246] when negotiating that version.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  TLS 1.2 ClientHellos MAY omit this extension.\n",
      "id": "585d67023015314a",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 317,
      "quote": "-  TLS 1.2 ClientHellos MAY omit this extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "They MUST NOT be offered or negotiated by any\nimplementation.\n",
      "id": "a5bda35bb775d91b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 323,
      "quote": "They MUST NOT be offered or negotiated by any implementation.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In particular, MD5 [SLOTH], SHA-224, and DSA\nMUST NOT be used.\n",
      "id": "bcab6d6ee60587cb",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 330,
      "quote": "In particular, MD5 [SLOTH], SHA-224, and DSA MUST NOT be used.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If TLS 1.2 is negotiated, implementations MUST be prepared\nto accept a signature that uses any curve that they advertised in\nthe \"supported_groups\" extension.\n",
      "id": "54bc1a1342dc0c08",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 337,
      "quote": "If TLS 1.2 is negotiated, implementations MUST be prepared to accept a signature that uses any curve that they advertised in the \"supported_groups\" extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  Implementations that advertise support for RSASSA-PSS (which is\nmandatory in TLS 1.3) MUST be prepared to accept a signature using\nthat scheme even when TLS 1.2 is negotiated.\n",
      "id": "b61c99b381030efb",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 345,
      "quote": "-  Implementations that advertise support for RSASSA-PSS (which is mandatory in TLS 1.3) MUST be prepared to accept a signature using that scheme even when TLS 1.2 is negotiated.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The \"certificate_authorities\" extension is used to indicate the\ncertificate authorities (CAs) which an endpoint supports and which\nSHOULD be used by the receiving endpoint to guide certificate\nselection.\n",
      "id": "e648ff193a53d846",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 35,
      "quote": "The \"certificate_authorities\" extension is used to indicate the certificate authorities (CAs) which an endpoint supports and which SHOULD be used by the receiving endpoint to guide certificate selection.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The client MAY send the \"certificate_authorities\" extension in the\nClientHello message.\n",
      "id": "3cd98aedfa14d59a",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "The client MAY send the \"certificate_authorities\" extension in the ClientHello message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server MAY send it in the\nCertificateRequest message.\n",
      "id": "6ed0c296f2ca915c",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "The server MAY send it in the CertificateRequest message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This extension, if provided by the server, MUST only be sent\nin the CertificateRequest message.\n",
      "id": "7805c955ccca5cef",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 57,
      "quote": "This extension, if provided by the server, MUST only be sent in the CertificateRequest message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the server has included a non-empty\nfilters list, the client certificate included in the response MUST\ncontain all of the specified extension OIDs that the client\nrecognizes.\n",
      "id": "0a7645c1d5aae21d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "If the server has included a non-empty filters list, the client certificate included in the response MUST contain all of the specified extension OIDs that the client recognizes.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For each extension OID recognized by the client, all\nof the specified values MUST be present in the client certificate\n(but the certificate MAY have other values as well).\n",
      "id": "b7a12abb9462706d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 73,
      "quote": "For each extension OID recognized by the client, all of the specified values MUST be present in the client certificate (but the certificate MAY have other values as well).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "However, the\nclient MUST ignore and skip any unrecognized certificate extension\nOIDs.\n",
      "id": "6baf2ddd3b3f8316",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 81,
      "quote": "However, the client MUST ignore and skip any unrecognized certificate extension OIDs.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the client ignored some of the required certificate\nextension OIDs and supplied a certificate that does not satisfy\nthe request, the server MAY at its discretion either continue the\nconnection without client authentication or abort the handshake\nwith an \"unsupported_certificate\" alert.\n",
      "id": "b1f1a5ea963868ee",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 89,
      "quote": "If the client ignored some of the required certificate extension OIDs and supplied a certificate that does not satisfy the request, the server MAY at its discretion either continue the connection without client authentication or abort the handshake with an \"unsupported_certificate\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Any given OID MUST NOT\nappear more than once in the filters list.\n",
      "id": "aed4e48326840399",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 99,
      "quote": "Any given OID MUST NOT appear more than once in the filters list.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The\nspecial anyExtendedKeyUsage OID MUST NOT be used in the request.\n",
      "id": "b0ed093de5c6b444",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 106,
      "quote": "The special anyExtendedKeyUsage OID MUST NOT be used in the request.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MUST NOT send a post-handshake CertificateRequest to clients\nwhich do not offer this extension.\n",
      "id": "c6909abf7bf8febd",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 16,
      "quote": "Servers MUST NOT send a post-handshake CertificateRequest to clients which do not offer this extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MUST NOT send this\nextension.\n",
      "id": "25f3792191b278d1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 23,
      "quote": "Servers MUST NOT send this extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MUST NOT act upon any information\nfound in \"supported_groups\" prior to successful completion of the\nhandshake but MAY use the information learned from a successfully\ncompleted handshake to change what groups they use in their\n\"key_share\" extension in subsequent connections.\n",
      "id": "d4c70d2c2c9de825",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 62,
      "quote": "Clients MUST NOT act upon any information found in \"supported_groups\" prior to successful completion of the handshake but MAY use the information learned from a successfully completed handshake to change what groups they use in their \"key_share\" extension in subsequent connections.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the server has a\ngroup it prefers to the ones in the \"key_share\" extension but is\nstill willing to accept the ClientHello, it SHOULD send\n\"supported_groups\" to update the client's view of its preferences;\nthis extension SHOULD contain all groups the server supports,\nregardless of whether they are currently supported by the client.\n",
      "id": "dd278e4e443b2f2a",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 72,
      "quote": "If the server has a group it prefers to the ones in the \"key_share\" extension but is still willing to accept the ClientHello, it SHOULD send \"supported_groups\" to update the client's view of its preferences; this extension SHOULD contain all groups the server supports, regardless of whether they are currently supported by the client.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the server has a\ngroup it prefers to the ones in the \"key_share\" extension but is\nstill willing to accept the ClientHello, it SHOULD send\n\"supported_groups\" to update the client's view of its preferences;\nthis extension SHOULD contain all groups the server supports,\nregardless of whether they are currently supported by the client.\n",
      "id": "c1b493bba3b178da",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 83,
      "quote": "If the server has a group it prefers to the ones in the \"key_share\" extension but is still willing to accept the ClientHello, it SHOULD send \"supported_groups\" to update the client's view of its preferences; this extension SHOULD contain all groups the server supports, regardless of whether they are currently supported by the client.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Peers MUST validate each other's public key Y by ensuring that 1 < Y\n< p-1.\n",
      "id": "95b6307e3854a0ff",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 19,
      "quote": "Peers MUST validate each other's public key Y by ensuring that 1 < Y < p-1.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.8.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.8.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For the curves secp256r1, secp384r1, and secp521r1, peers MUST\nvalidate each other's public value Q by ensuring that the point is a\nvalid point on the elliptic curve.\n",
      "id": "863aeebe2d32fa79",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 43,
      "quote": "For the curves secp256r1, secp384r1, and secp521r1, peers MUST validate each other's public value Q by ensuring that the point is a valid point on the elliptic curve.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.8.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.8.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MAY send an empty client_shares vector in order to request\ngroup selection from the server, at the cost of an additional round\ntrip (see Section 4.1.4).\n",
      "id": "8ad40ad8bc81a988",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 101,
      "quote": "Clients MAY send an empty client_shares vector in order to request group selection from the server, at the cost of an additional round trip (see Section 4.1.4).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This vector MAY be empty if the client is requesting a\nHelloRetryRequest.\n",
      "id": "1d30392ee23c71f0",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 109,
      "quote": "This vector MAY be empty if the client is requesting a HelloRetryRequest.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each KeyShareEntry value MUST correspond to a\ngroup offered in the \"supported_groups\" extension and MUST appear in\nthe same order.\n",
      "id": "592c5005e18aab18",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 116,
      "quote": "Each KeyShareEntry value MUST correspond to a group offered in the \"supported_groups\" extension and MUST appear in the same order.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each KeyShareEntry value MUST correspond to a\ngroup offered in the \"supported_groups\" extension and MUST appear in\nthe same order.\n",
      "id": "bd064bae6be53a1f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 124,
      "quote": "Each KeyShareEntry value MUST correspond to a group offered in the \"supported_groups\" extension and MUST appear in the same order.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "However, the values MAY be a non-contiguous subset\nof the \"supported_groups\" extension and MAY omit the most preferred\ngroups.\n",
      "id": "d199239e9bebe2ea",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 132,
      "quote": "However, the values MAY be a non-contiguous subset of the \"supported_groups\" extension and MAY omit the most preferred groups.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "However, the values MAY be a non-contiguous subset\nof the \"supported_groups\" extension and MAY omit the most preferred\ngroups.\n",
      "id": "9cc8089c5a9441ad",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 140,
      "quote": "However, the values MAY be a non-contiguous subset of the \"supported_groups\" extension and MAY omit the most preferred groups.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The\nkey_exchange values for each KeyShareEntry MUST be generated\nindependently.\n",
      "id": "8d4143c57d9c0f95",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 148,
      "quote": "The key_exchange values for each KeyShareEntry MUST be generated independently.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MUST NOT offer multiple KeyShareEntry values\nfor the same group.\n",
      "id": "d07524c1b0d9b4d4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 156,
      "quote": "Clients MUST NOT offer multiple KeyShareEntry values for the same group.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MUST NOT offer any KeyShareEntry values\nfor groups not listed in the client's \"supported_groups\" extension.\n",
      "id": "5a759d7ae2a8ccf8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 163,
      "quote": "Clients MUST NOT offer any KeyShareEntry values for groups not listed in the client's \"supported_groups\" extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MAY check for violations of these rules and abort the\nhandshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert if one is violated.\n",
      "id": "3f842d08be5f5108",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 170,
      "quote": "Servers MAY check for violations of these rules and abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert if one is violated.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Upon receipt of this extension in a HelloRetryRequest, the client\nMUST verify that (1) the selected_group field corresponds to a group\nwhich was provided in the \"supported_groups\" extension in the\noriginal ClientHello and (2) the selected_group field does not\ncorrespond to a group which was provided in the \"key_share\" extension\nin the original ClientHello.\n",
      "id": "a77380646188cccb",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 177,
      "quote": "Upon receipt of this extension in a HelloRetryRequest, the client MUST verify that (1) the selected_group field corresponds to a group which was provided in the \"supported_groups\" extension in the original ClientHello and (2) the selected_group field does not correspond to a group which was provided in the \"key_share\" extension in the original ClientHello.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If either of these checks fails, then\nthe client MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\"\nalert.\n",
      "id": "9715f0bec6100ed9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 188,
      "quote": "If either of these checks fails, then the client MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Otherwise, when sending the new ClientHello, the client MUST\n",
      "id": "36c532a56bfb49d0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 196,
      "quote": "Otherwise, when sending the new ClientHello, the client MUST",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This value MUST be in the same\ngroup as the KeyShareEntry value offered by the client that the\nserver has selected for the negotiated key exchange.\n",
      "id": "6b1d704717f26870",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 202,
      "quote": "This value MUST be in the same group as the KeyShareEntry value offered by the client that the server has selected for the negotiated key exchange.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers\nMUST NOT send a KeyShareEntry for any group not indicated in the\nclient's \"supported_groups\" extension and MUST NOT send a\nKeyShareEntry when using the \"psk_ke\" PskKeyExchangeMode.\n",
      "id": "be143059001f489d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 210,
      "quote": "Servers MUST NOT send a KeyShareEntry for any group not indicated in the client's \"supported_groups\" extension and MUST NOT send a KeyShareEntry when using the \"psk_ke\" PskKeyExchangeMode.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers\nMUST NOT send a KeyShareEntry for any group not indicated in the\nclient's \"supported_groups\" extension and MUST NOT send a\nKeyShareEntry when using the \"psk_ke\" PskKeyExchangeMode.\n",
      "id": "e23bde55d4a98e04",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 219,
      "quote": "Servers MUST NOT send a KeyShareEntry for any group not indicated in the client's \"supported_groups\" extension and MUST NOT send a KeyShareEntry when using the \"psk_ke\" PskKeyExchangeMode.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If using\n(EC)DHE key establishment and a HelloRetryRequest containing a\n\"key_share\" extension was received by the client, the client MUST\nverify that the selected NamedGroup in the ServerHello is the same as\nthat in the HelloRetryRequest.\n",
      "id": "d4dc4fb9c6c474e0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 228,
      "quote": "If using (EC)DHE key establishment and a HelloRetryRequest containing a \"key_share\" extension was received by the client, the client MUST verify that the selected NamedGroup in the ServerHello is the same as that in the HelloRetryRequest.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If this check fails, the client MUST\nabort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.\n",
      "id": "f856403d3f06c9df",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 238,
      "quote": "If this check fails, the client MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In order to use PSKs, clients MUST also send a\n\"psk_key_exchange_modes\" extension.\n",
      "id": "e67a8d8ea44d5276",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "In order to use PSKs, clients MUST also send a \"psk_key_exchange_modes\" extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST provide a \"psk_key_exchange_modes\" extension if it\noffers a \"pre_shared_key\" extension.\n",
      "id": "cedafc4dba6de757",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 48,
      "quote": "A client MUST provide a \"psk_key_exchange_modes\" extension if it offers a \"pre_shared_key\" extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If clients offer\n\"pre_shared_key\" without a \"psk_key_exchange_modes\" extension,\nservers MUST abort the handshake.\n",
      "id": "c573d9ded17dea75",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 55,
      "quote": "If clients offer \"pre_shared_key\" without a \"psk_key_exchange_modes\" extension, servers MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MUST NOT select a key\nexchange mode that is not listed by the client.\n",
      "id": "af42cbb374401cba",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 63,
      "quote": "Servers MUST NOT select a key exchange mode that is not listed by the client.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers SHOULD NOT\nsend NewSessionTicket with tickets that are not compatible with the\nadvertised modes; however, if a server does so, the impact will just\nbe that the client's attempts at resumption fail.\n",
      "id": "80fd55e2e50f76be",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 70,
      "quote": "Servers SHOULD NOT send NewSessionTicket with tickets that are not compatible with the advertised modes; however, if a server does so, the impact will just be that the client's attempts at resumption fail.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server MUST NOT send a \"psk_key_exchange_modes\" extension.\n",
      "id": "8751adeedec4cecf",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 79,
      "quote": "The server MUST NOT send a \"psk_key_exchange_modes\" extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In this mode, the server\nMUST NOT supply a \"key_share\" value.\n",
      "id": "e293f13c9eb24316",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 85,
      "quote": "In this mode, the server MUST NOT supply a \"key_share\" value.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In this mode, the\nclient and server MUST supply \"key_share\" values as described in\nSection 4.2.8.\n",
      "id": "b6b9a4366888818a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 92,
      "quote": "In this mode, the client and server MUST supply \"key_share\" values as described in Section 4.2.8.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server sends extension requests in the\nCertificateRequest message which a client MAY respond to with a\nCertificate message.\n",
      "id": "a037a5758b71e9ad",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 159,
      "quote": "The server sends extension requests in the CertificateRequest message which a client MAY respond to with a Certificate message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server MAY also send unsolicited extensions\nin the NewSessionTicket, though the client does not respond directly\nto these.\n",
      "id": "498cfeb6682ed352",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 167,
      "quote": "The server MAY also send unsolicited extensions in the NewSessionTicket, though the client does not respond directly to these.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations MUST NOT send extension responses if the remote\nendpoint did not send the corresponding extension requests, with the\nexception of the \"cookie\" extension in the HelloRetryRequest.\n",
      "id": "10c68cc726525727",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 175,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST NOT send extension responses if the remote endpoint did not send the corresponding extension requests, with the exception of the \"cookie\" extension in the HelloRetryRequest.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Upon\nreceiving such an extension, an endpoint MUST abort the handshake\nwith an \"unsupported_extension\" alert.\n",
      "id": "a39513dea09440d0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 183,
      "quote": "Upon receiving such an extension, an endpoint MUST abort the handshake with an \"unsupported_extension\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an implementation receives an extension\nwhich it recognizes and which is not specified for the message in\nwhich it appears, it MUST abort the handshake with an\n\"illegal_parameter\" alert.\n",
      "id": "63b9edf8e4f04e81",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 191,
      "quote": "If an implementation receives an extension which it recognizes and which is not specified for the message in which it appears, it MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When multiple extensions of different types are present, the\nextensions MAY appear in any order, with the exception of\n\"pre_shared_key\" (Section 4.2.11) which MUST be the last extension in\nthe ClientHello (but can appear anywhere in the ServerHello\nextensions block).\n",
      "id": "197ed0bf4ed3ac80",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 200,
      "quote": "When multiple extensions of different types are present, the extensions MAY appear in any order, with the exception of \"pre_shared_key\" (Section 4.2.11) which MUST be the last extension in the ClientHello (but can appear anywhere in the ServerHello extensions block).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "There MUST NOT be more than one extension of the\nsame type in a given extension block.\n",
      "id": "4c0c81955d98f4ff",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 210,
      "quote": "There MUST NOT be more than one extension of the same type in a given extension block.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In all handshakes, the server MUST send the EncryptedExtensions\nmessage immediately after the ServerHello message.\n",
      "id": "88c30e1bfb734cce",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 26,
      "quote": "In all handshakes, the server MUST send the EncryptedExtensions message immediately after the ServerHello message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The client MUST check EncryptedExtensions for the\npresence of any forbidden extensions and if any are found MUST abort\nthe handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.\n",
      "id": "4934e7e9be30604c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 33,
      "quote": "The client MUST check EncryptedExtensions for the presence of any forbidden extensions and if any are found MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The client MUST check EncryptedExtensions for the\npresence of any forbidden extensions and if any are found MUST abort\nthe handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.\n",
      "id": "2246a53463058a37",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "The client MUST check EncryptedExtensions for the presence of any forbidden extensions and if any are found MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server which is authenticating with a certificate MAY optionally\nrequest a certificate from the client.\n",
      "id": "f2804bd9a42479aa",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "A server which is authenticating with a certificate MAY optionally request a certificate from the client.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This message, if sent, MUST\nfollow EncryptedExtensions.\n",
      "id": "6154ee949912e856",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "This message, if sent, MUST follow EncryptedExtensions.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The certificate_request_context MUST be\nunique within the scope of this connection (thus preventing replay\nof client CertificateVerify messages).\n",
      "id": "2b7278e0ff990212",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 61,
      "quote": "The certificate_request_context MUST be unique within the scope of this connection (thus preventing replay of client CertificateVerify messages).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This field SHALL be zero\nlength unless used for the post-handshake authentication exchanges\ndescribed in Section 4.6.2.\n",
      "id": "0c5b32e3f91a809a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 69,
      "quote": "This field SHALL be zero length unless used for the post-handshake authentication exchanges described in Section 4.6.2.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When requesting post-handshake\nauthentication, the server SHOULD make the context unpredictable\nto the client (e.g., by randomly generating it) in order to\nprevent an attacker who has temporary access to the client's\nprivate key from pre-computing valid CertificateVerify messages.\n",
      "id": "a8b224a5a55478e7",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 77,
      "quote": "When requesting post-handshake authentication, the server SHOULD make the context unpredictable to the client (e.g., by randomly generating it) in order to prevent an attacker who has temporary access to the client's private key from pre-computing valid CertificateVerify messages.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The \"signature_algorithms\" extension\nMUST be specified, and other extensions may optionally be included\nif defined for this message.\n",
      "id": "6732b022d6dbc39e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 87,
      "quote": "The \"signature_algorithms\" extension MUST be specified, and other extensions may optionally be included if defined for this message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MUST ignore unrecognized\nextensions.\n",
      "id": "7824b9464825dd83",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 95,
      "quote": "Clients MUST ignore unrecognized extensions.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers which are authenticating with a PSK MUST NOT send the\nCertificateRequest message in the main handshake, though they MAY\nsend it in post-handshake authentication (see Section 4.6.2) provided\nthat the client has sent the \"post_handshake_auth\" extension (see\nSection 4.2.6).\n",
      "id": "d59e29730d8701ee",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 102,
      "quote": "Servers which are authenticating with a PSK MUST NOT send the CertificateRequest message in the main handshake, though they MAY send it in post-handshake authentication (see Section 4.6.2) provided that the client has sent the \"post_handshake_auth\" extension (see Section 4.2.6).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Specifically, the body of the\n\"status_request\" extension from the server MUST be a\nCertificateStatus structure as defined in [RFC6066], which is\ninterpreted as defined in [RFC6960].\n",
      "id": "99e9813b5474e471",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 35,
      "quote": "Specifically, the body of the \"status_request\" extension from the server MUST be a CertificateStatus structure as defined in [RFC6066], which is interpreted as defined in [RFC6960].",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS 1.3 servers MUST NOT act upon its presence or information in it\nwhen processing ClientHello messages; in particular, they MUST NOT\nsend the status_request_v2 extension in the EncryptedExtensions,\nCertificateRequest, or Certificate messages.\n",
      "id": "790f01944937d089",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "TLS 1.3 servers MUST NOT act upon its presence or information in it when processing ClientHello messages; in particular, they MUST NOT send the status_request_v2 extension in the EncryptedExtensions, CertificateRequest, or Certificate messages.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS 1.3 servers MUST NOT act upon its presence or information in it\nwhen processing ClientHello messages; in particular, they MUST NOT\nsend the status_request_v2 extension in the EncryptedExtensions,\nCertificateRequest, or Certificate messages.\n",
      "id": "d59c6ce161f7d151",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 53,
      "quote": "TLS 1.3 servers MUST NOT act upon its presence or information in it when processing ClientHello messages; in particular, they MUST NOT send the status_request_v2 extension in the EncryptedExtensions, CertificateRequest, or Certificate messages.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS 1.3 servers MUST be\nable to process ClientHello messages that include it, as it MAY be\nsent by clients that wish to use it in earlier protocol versions.\n",
      "id": "bf45a719222b1e69",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 62,
      "quote": "TLS 1.3 servers MUST be able to process ClientHello messages that include it, as it MAY be sent by clients that wish to use it in earlier protocol versions.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MAY request that a client present an OCSP response with its\ncertificate by sending an empty \"status_request\" extension in its\nCertificateRequest message.\n",
      "id": "60a71ea562cdaff8",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 70,
      "quote": "A server MAY request that a client present an OCSP response with its certificate by sending an empty \"status_request\" extension in its CertificateRequest message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the client opts to send an OCSP\nresponse, the body of its \"status_request\" extension MUST be a\nCertificateStatus structure as defined in [RFC6066].\n",
      "id": "e99e9695dc6392a0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 78,
      "quote": "If the client opts to send an OCSP response, the body of its \"status_request\" extension MUST be a CertificateStatus structure as defined in [RFC6066].",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  The certificate type MUST be X.509v3 [RFC5280], unless explicitly\nnegotiated otherwise (e.g., [RFC7250]).\n",
      "id": "33a8ef11c32c54a1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 50,
      "quote": "-  The certificate type MUST be X.509v3 [RFC5280], unless explicitly negotiated otherwise (e.g., [RFC7250]).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  The server's end-entity certificate's public key (and associated\nrestrictions) MUST be compatible with the selected authentication\nalgorithm from the client's \"signature_algorithms\" extension\n(currently RSA, ECDSA, or EdDSA).\n",
      "id": "fb35068b9112978a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 57,
      "quote": "-  The server's end-entity certificate's public key (and associated restrictions) MUST be compatible with the selected authentication algorithm from the client's \"signature_algorithms\" extension (currently RSA, ECDSA, or EdDSA).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  The certificate MUST allow the key to be used for signing (i.e.,\nthe digitalSignature bit MUST be set if the Key Usage extension is\npresent) with a signature scheme indicated in the client's\n\"signature_algorithms\"/\"signature_algorithms_cert\" extensions (see\nSection 4.2.3).\n",
      "id": "c18374c7eda655fe",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 66,
      "quote": "-  The certificate MUST allow the key to be used for signing (i.e., the digitalSignature bit MUST be set if the Key Usage extension is present) with a signature scheme indicated in the client's \"signature_algorithms\"/\"signature_algorithms_cert\" extensions (see Section 4.2.3).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  The certificate MUST allow the key to be used for signing (i.e.,\nthe digitalSignature bit MUST be set if the Key Usage extension is\npresent) with a signature scheme indicated in the client's\n\"signature_algorithms\"/\"signature_algorithms_cert\" extensions (see\nSection 4.2.3).\n",
      "id": "85ec8572533919c9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 76,
      "quote": "-  The certificate MUST allow the key to be used for signing (i.e., the digitalSignature bit MUST be set if the Key Usage extension is present) with a signature scheme indicated in the client's \"signature_algorithms\"/\"signature_algorithms_cert\" extensions (see Section 4.2.3).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "As servers\nMAY require the presence of the \"server_name\" extension, clients\nSHOULD send this extension, when applicable.\n",
      "id": "70532d034b26d794",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 86,
      "quote": "As servers MAY require the presence of the \"server_name\" extension, clients SHOULD send this extension, when applicable.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "All certificates provided by the server MUST be signed by a signature\nalgorithm advertised by the client if it is able to provide such a\nchain (see Section 4.2.3).\n",
      "id": "25715c627c314159",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 94,
      "quote": "All certificates provided by the server MUST be signed by a signature algorithm advertised by the client if it is able to provide such a chain (see Section 4.2.3).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Certificates that are self-signed or\ncertificates that are expected to be trust anchors are not validated\nas part of the chain and therefore MAY be signed with any algorithm.\n",
      "id": "2c9c9fdc91b7b29f",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 102,
      "quote": "Certificates that are self-signed or certificates that are expected to be trust anchors are not validated as part of the chain and therefore MAY be signed with any algorithm.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the server cannot produce a certificate chain that is signed only\nvia the indicated supported algorithms, then it SHOULD continue the\nhandshake by sending the client a certificate chain of its choice\nthat may include algorithms that are not known to be supported by the\nclient.\n",
      "id": "412f77ccc1be5b6a",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 110,
      "quote": "If the server cannot produce a certificate chain that is signed only via the indicated supported algorithms, then it SHOULD continue the handshake by sending the client a certificate chain of its choice that may include algorithms that are not known to be supported by the client.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This fallback chain SHOULD NOT use the deprecated SHA-1 hash\nalgorithm in general, but MAY do so if the client's advertisement\npermits it, and MUST NOT do so otherwise.\n",
      "id": "001c0a7f58cb969b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 120,
      "quote": "This fallback chain SHOULD NOT use the deprecated SHA-1 hash algorithm in general, but MAY do so if the client's advertisement permits it, and MUST NOT do so otherwise.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the client cannot construct an acceptable chain using the provided\ncertificates and decides to abort the handshake, then it MUST abort\nthe handshake with an appropriate certificate-related alert (by\ndefault, \"unsupported_certificate\"; see Section 6.2 for more\ninformation).\n",
      "id": "c55bc846986a19e3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 128,
      "quote": "If the client cannot construct an acceptable chain using the provided certificates and decides to abort the handshake, then it MUST abort the handshake with an appropriate certificate-related alert (by default, \"unsupported_certificate\"; see Section 6.2 for more information).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  The certificate type MUST be X.509v3 [RFC5280], unless explicitly\nnegotiated otherwise (e.g., [RFC7250]).\n",
      "id": "f9dd2494d87fc7ac",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "-  The certificate type MUST be X.509v3 [RFC5280], unless explicitly negotiated otherwise (e.g., [RFC7250]).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  If the \"certificate_authorities\" extension in the\nCertificateRequest message was present, at least one of the\ncertificates in the certificate chain SHOULD be issued by one of\nthe listed CAs.\n",
      "id": "92ea039063a6a4fc",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "-  If the \"certificate_authorities\" extension in the CertificateRequest message was present, at least one of the certificates in the certificate chain SHOULD be issued by one of the listed CAs.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  The certificates MUST be signed using an acceptable signature\nalgorithm, as described in Section 4.3.2.\n",
      "id": "6bf6f8481195f98e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "-  The certificates MUST be signed using an acceptable signature algorithm, as described in Section 4.3.2.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  If the CertificateRequest message contained a non-empty\n\"oid_filters\" extension, the end-entity certificate MUST match the\nextension OIDs that are recognized by the client, as described in\nSection 4.2.5.\n",
      "id": "1a30a23a8556e7df",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 48,
      "quote": "-  If the CertificateRequest message contained a non-empty \"oid_filters\" extension, the end-entity certificate MUST match the extension OIDs that are recognized by the client, as described in Section 4.2.5.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the server supplies an empty Certificate message, the client MUST\nabort the handshake with a \"decode_error\" alert.\n",
      "id": "b813fbbef032d115",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 38,
      "quote": "If the server supplies an empty Certificate message, the client MUST abort the handshake with a \"decode_error\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the client does not send any certificates (i.e., it sends an empty\nCertificate message), the server MAY at its discretion either\ncontinue the handshake without client authentication or abort the\nhandshake with a \"certificate_required\" alert.\n",
      "id": "6d0ca28921107181",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 45,
      "quote": "If the client does not send any certificates (i.e., it sends an empty Certificate message), the server MAY at its discretion either continue the handshake without client authentication or abort the handshake with a \"certificate_required\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Also, if some aspect\nof the certificate chain was unacceptable (e.g., it was not signed by\na known, trusted CA), the server MAY at its discretion either\ncontinue the handshake (considering the client unauthenticated) or\nabort the handshake.\n",
      "id": "e7d903a7de7bfb9f",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "Also, if some aspect of the certificate chain was unacceptable (e.g., it was not signed by a known, trusted CA), the server MAY at its discretion either continue the handshake (considering the client unauthenticated) or abort the handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Any endpoint receiving any certificate which it would need to\nvalidate using any signature algorithm using an MD5 hash MUST abort\nthe handshake with a \"bad_certificate\" alert.\n",
      "id": "132b530bdf9da2be",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "Any endpoint receiving any certificate which it would need to validate using any signature algorithm using an MD5 hash MUST abort the handshake with a \"bad_certificate\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "SHA-1 is deprecated,\nand it is RECOMMENDED that any endpoint receiving any certificate\nwhich it would need to validate using any signature algorithm using a\nSHA-1 hash abort the handshake with a \"bad_certificate\" alert.\n",
      "id": "f151b59e45cf2d77",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 72,
      "quote": "SHA-1 is deprecated, and it is RECOMMENDED that any endpoint receiving any certificate which it would need to validate using any signature algorithm using a SHA-1 hash abort the handshake with a \"bad_certificate\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "All endpoints are RECOMMENDED to transition to SHA-256 or better as\nsoon as possible to maintain interoperability with implementations\ncurrently in the process of phasing out SHA-1 support.\n",
      "id": "19cbf074f6884de1",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 81,
      "quote": "All endpoints are RECOMMENDED to transition to SHA-256 or better as soon as possible to maintain interoperability with implementations currently in the process of phasing out SHA-1 support.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Note that a certificate containing a key for one signature algorithm\nMAY be signed using a different signature algorithm (for instance, an\nRSA key signed with an ECDSA key).\n",
      "id": "7698cae83a8477d9",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 89,
      "quote": "Note that a certificate containing a key for one signature algorithm MAY be signed using a different signature algorithm (for instance, an RSA key signed with an ECDSA key).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server MUST send a Certificate message whenever the agreed-upon\nkey exchange method uses certificates for authentication (this\nincludes all key exchange methods defined in this document\nexcept PSK).\n",
      "id": "4abd77d3223ab59d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 100,
      "quote": "The server MUST send a Certificate message whenever the agreed-upon key exchange method uses certificates for authentication (this includes all key exchange methods defined in this document except PSK).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The client MUST send a Certificate message if and only if the server\nhas requested client authentication via a CertificateRequest message\n(Section 4.3.2).\n",
      "id": "6ee525cff6c4fb04",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 109,
      "quote": "The client MUST send a Certificate message if and only if the server has requested client authentication via a CertificateRequest message (Section 4.3.2).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the server requests client authentication but no\nsuitable certificate is available, the client MUST send a Certificate\nmessage containing no certificates (i.e., with the \"certificate_list\"\nfield having length 0).\n",
      "id": "209e70c7a0100e05",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 117,
      "quote": "If the server requests client authentication but no suitable certificate is available, the client MUST send a Certificate message containing no certificates (i.e., with the \"certificate_list\" field having length 0).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A Finished message MUST be sent regardless\nof whether the Certificate message is empty.\n",
      "id": "fef3fbcc5a95ef7d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 126,
      "quote": "A Finished message MUST be sent regardless of whether the Certificate message is empty.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Otherwise (in the case of server authentication),\nthis field SHALL be zero length.\n",
      "id": "e7ed6e804d4612a7",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 133,
      "quote": "Otherwise (in the case of server authentication), this field SHALL be zero length.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Extensions in the Certificate message from the server MUST\ncorrespond to ones from the ClientHello message.\n",
      "id": "4d236a60cfe3e9b9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 140,
      "quote": "Extensions in the Certificate message from the server MUST correspond to ones from the ClientHello message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Extensions in\nthe Certificate message from the client MUST correspond to\nextensions in the CertificateRequest message from the server.\n",
      "id": "24d1ae85db088862",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 147,
      "quote": "Extensions in the Certificate message from the client MUST correspond to extensions in the CertificateRequest message from the server.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If\nan extension applies to the entire chain, it SHOULD be included in\nthe first CertificateEntry.\n",
      "id": "61c0ebc6382ecf37",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 155,
      "quote": "If an extension applies to the entire chain, it SHOULD be included in the first CertificateEntry.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The sender's certificate MUST come in the first\nCertificateEntry in the list.\n",
      "id": "8bd9f50007fe8614",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 163,
      "quote": "The sender's certificate MUST come in the first CertificateEntry in the list.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each following certificate SHOULD\ndirectly certify the one immediately preceding it.\n",
      "id": "06c90425c39d6264",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 170,
      "quote": "Each following certificate SHOULD directly certify the one immediately preceding it.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Because\ncertificate validation requires that trust anchors be distributed\nindependently, a certificate that specifies a trust anchor MAY be\nomitted from the chain, provided that supported peers are known to\npossess any omitted certificates.\n",
      "id": "d04f65875f448f5f",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 177,
      "quote": "Because certificate validation requires that trust anchors be distributed independently, a certificate that specifies a trust anchor MAY be omitted from the chain, provided that supported peers are known to possess any omitted certificates.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For maximum\ncompatibility, all implementations SHOULD be prepared to handle\npotentially extraneous certificates and arbitrary orderings from any\nTLS version, with the exception of the end-entity certificate which\nMUST be first.\n",
      "id": "bced0d15f317e6e6",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 187,
      "quote": "For maximum compatibility, all implementations SHOULD be prepared to handle potentially extraneous certificates and arbitrary orderings from any TLS version, with the exception of the end-entity certificate which MUST be first.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the RawPublicKey certificate type was negotiated, then the\ncertificate_list MUST contain no more than one CertificateEntry,\nwhich contains an ASN1_subjectPublicKeyInfo value as defined in\n[RFC7250], Section 3.\n",
      "id": "b3a41dfc5c7396fd",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 197,
      "quote": "If the RawPublicKey certificate type was negotiated, then the certificate_list MUST contain no more than one CertificateEntry, which contains an ASN1_subjectPublicKeyInfo value as defined in [RFC7250], Section 3.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The OpenPGP certificate type [RFC6091] MUST NOT be used with TLS 1.3.\n",
      "id": "06daca84ed05e630",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 206,
      "quote": "The OpenPGP certificate type [RFC6091] MUST NOT be used with TLS 1.3.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server's certificate_list MUST always be non-empty.\n",
      "id": "063a327f4f1026ef",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 212,
      "quote": "The server's certificate_list MUST always be non-empty.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MUST send this message when authenticating\nvia a certificate.\n",
      "id": "3c4506799a955fc3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 105,
      "quote": "Servers MUST send this message when authenticating via a certificate.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MUST send this message whenever\nauthenticating via a certificate (i.e., when the Certificate message\nis non-empty).\n",
      "id": "5755391d5adf153b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 112,
      "quote": "Clients MUST send this message whenever authenticating via a certificate (i.e., when the Certificate message is non-empty).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When sent, this message MUST appear immediately after\nthe Certificate message and immediately prior to the Finished\nmessage.\n",
      "id": "f8ccf36c91c96ca8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 120,
      "quote": "When sent, this message MUST appear immediately after the Certificate message and immediately prior to the Finished message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the CertificateVerify message is sent by a server, the signature\nalgorithm MUST be one offered in the client's \"signature_algorithms\"\nextension unless no valid certificate chain can be produced without\nunsupported algorithms (see Section 4.2.3).\n",
      "id": "807d40e07e7d6710",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 128,
      "quote": "If the CertificateVerify message is sent by a server, the signature algorithm MUST be one offered in the client's \"signature_algorithms\" extension unless no valid certificate chain can be produced without unsupported algorithms (see Section 4.2.3).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If sent by a client, the signature algorithm used in the signature\nMUST be one of those present in the supported_signature_algorithms\nfield of the \"signature_algorithms\" extension in the\nCertificateRequest message.\n",
      "id": "ac7884a896092f0c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 137,
      "quote": "If sent by a client, the signature algorithm used in the signature MUST be one of those present in the supported_signature_algorithms field of the \"signature_algorithms\" extension in the CertificateRequest message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In addition, the signature algorithm MUST be compatible with the key\nin the sender's end-entity certificate.\n",
      "id": "cbc1a9c461a530b8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 146,
      "quote": "In addition, the signature algorithm MUST be compatible with the key in the sender's end-entity certificate.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "RSA signatures MUST use an\nRSASSA-PSS algorithm, regardless of whether RSASSA-PKCS1-v1_5\nalgorithms appear in \"signature_algorithms\".\n",
      "id": "bee992947076e70e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 153,
      "quote": "RSA signatures MUST use an RSASSA-PSS algorithm, regardless of whether RSASSA-PKCS1-v1_5 algorithms appear in \"signature_algorithms\".",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The SHA-1 algorithm\nMUST NOT be used in any signatures of CertificateVerify messages.\n",
      "id": "4ffb772758831195",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 161,
      "quote": "The SHA-1 algorithm MUST NOT be used in any signatures of CertificateVerify messages.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The receiver of a CertificateVerify message MUST verify the signature\nfield.\n",
      "id": "f7c86278942b878c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 168,
      "quote": "The receiver of a CertificateVerify message MUST verify the signature field.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the verification fails, the receiver MUST terminate the handshake\nwith a \"decrypt_error\" alert.\n",
      "id": "2ab9d05e0729a616",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 175,
      "quote": "If the verification fails, the receiver MUST terminate the handshake with a \"decrypt_error\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Recipients of Finished messages MUST verify that the contents are\ncorrect and if incorrect MUST terminate the connection with a\n\"decrypt_error\" alert.\n",
      "id": "c4ccb40458fdb6ba",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "Recipients of Finished messages MUST verify that the contents are correct and if incorrect MUST terminate the connection with a \"decrypt_error\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Recipients of Finished messages MUST verify that the contents are\ncorrect and if incorrect MUST terminate the connection with a\n\"decrypt_error\" alert.\n",
      "id": "3a3f2cb092a5db0b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 72,
      "quote": "Recipients of Finished messages MUST verify that the contents are correct and if incorrect MUST terminate the connection with a \"decrypt_error\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MAY send data after sending their first flight, but\nbecause the handshake is not yet complete, they have no assurance\nof either the peer's identity or its liveness (i.e., the\nClientHello might have been replayed).\n",
      "id": "3ab151fc48220efc",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 80,
      "quote": "Servers MAY send data after sending their first flight, but because the handshake is not yet complete, they have no assurance of either the peer's identity or its liveness (i.e., the ClientHello might have been replayed).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Any records following a Finished message MUST be encrypted under the\nappropriate application traffic key as described in Section 7.2.\n",
      "id": "20c88df99fc188c5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 89,
      "quote": "Any records following a Finished message MUST be encrypted under the appropriate application traffic key as described in Section 7.2.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the server sent an \"early_data\" extension in EncryptedExtensions,\nthe client MUST send an EndOfEarlyData message after receiving the\nserver Finished.\n",
      "id": "8d86c83b6ba1e239",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 20,
      "quote": "If the server sent an \"early_data\" extension in EncryptedExtensions, the client MUST send an EndOfEarlyData message after receiving the server Finished.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the server does not send an \"early_data\"\nextension in EncryptedExtensions, then the client MUST NOT send an\nEndOfEarlyData message.\n",
      "id": "60e42197a49c8cc1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 28,
      "quote": "If the server does not send an \"early_data\" extension in EncryptedExtensions, then the client MUST NOT send an EndOfEarlyData message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MUST NOT send this message, and clients receiving it MUST\nterminate the connection with an \"unexpected_message\" alert.\n",
      "id": "33f9be56ce97aa48",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 36,
      "quote": "Servers MUST NOT send this message, and clients receiving it MUST terminate the connection with an \"unexpected_message\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MUST NOT send this message, and clients receiving it MUST\nterminate the connection with an \"unexpected_message\" alert.\n",
      "id": "9c5c7a47a8941f28",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 43,
      "quote": "Servers MUST NOT send this message, and clients receiving it MUST terminate the connection with an \"unexpected_message\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "At any time after the server has received the client Finished\nmessage, it MAY send a NewSessionTicket message.\n",
      "id": "b47112b06121bd19",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 121,
      "quote": "At any time after the server has received the client Finished message, it MAY send a NewSessionTicket message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The client MAY use this PSK for future handshakes by including the\nticket value in the \"pre_shared_key\" extension in its ClientHello\n(Section 4.2.11).\n",
      "id": "88317ae72d3cde40",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 128,
      "quote": "The client MAY use this PSK for future handshakes by including the ticket value in the \"pre_shared_key\" extension in its ClientHello (Section 4.2.11).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MAY send multiple tickets on a single\nconnection, either immediately after each other or after specific\nevents (see Appendix C.4).\n",
      "id": "4c38754828ceb6dd",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 136,
      "quote": "Servers MAY send multiple tickets on a single connection, either immediately after each other or after specific events (see Appendix C.4).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Any ticket MUST only be resumed with a cipher suite that has the same\nKDF hash algorithm as that used to establish the original connection.\n",
      "id": "50cafc10dd4cd60e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 144,
      "quote": "Any ticket MUST only be resumed with a cipher suite that has the same KDF hash algorithm as that used to establish the original connection.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MUST only resume if the new SNI value is valid for the server\ncertificate presented in the original session and SHOULD only resume\nif the SNI value matches the one used in the original session.\n",
      "id": "62780f142b254398",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 151,
      "quote": "Clients MUST only resume if the new SNI value is valid for the server certificate presented in the original session and SHOULD only resume if the SNI value matches the one used in the original session.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If such an indication\nis provided (externally or by any other means), clients MAY resume\nwith a different SNI value.\n",
      "id": "d38158b72b5f36c0",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 159,
      "quote": "If such an indication is provided (externally or by any other means), clients MAY resume with a different SNI value.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "On resumption, if reporting an SNI value to the calling application,\nimplementations MUST use the value sent in the resumption ClientHello\nrather than the value sent in the previous session.\n",
      "id": "957277b04d13793f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 167,
      "quote": "On resumption, if reporting an SNI value to the calling application, implementations MUST use the value sent in the resumption ClientHello rather than the value sent in the previous session.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Note: Although the resumption master secret depends on the client's\nsecond flight, a server which does not request client authentication\nMAY compute the remainder of the transcript independently and then\nsend a NewSessionTicket immediately upon sending its Finished rather\nthan waiting for the client Finished.\n",
      "id": "5fad9888d43e71c6",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 175,
      "quote": "Note: Although the resumption master secret depends on the client's second flight, a server which does not request client authentication MAY compute the remainder of the transcript independently and then send a NewSessionTicket immediately upon sending its Finished rather than waiting for the client Finished.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MUST NOT use any value greater than\n604800 seconds (7 days).\n",
      "id": "656f61a2ad010ccb",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 185,
      "quote": "Servers MUST NOT use any value greater than 604800 seconds (7 days).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MUST NOT cache\ntickets for longer than 7 days, regardless of the ticket_lifetime,\nand MAY delete tickets earlier based on local policy.\n",
      "id": "3786b4560b269dc3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 192,
      "quote": "Clients MUST NOT cache tickets for longer than 7 days, regardless of the ticket_lifetime, and MAY delete tickets earlier based on local policy.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server\nMAY treat a ticket as valid for a shorter period of time than what\nis stated in the ticket_lifetime.\n",
      "id": "e0fa0b26c5ad6c69",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 200,
      "quote": "A server MAY treat a ticket as valid for a shorter period of time than what is stated in the ticket_lifetime.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server MUST generate a fresh value\nfor each ticket it sends.\n",
      "id": "704e0778f9d4d9f1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 208,
      "quote": "The server MUST generate a fresh value for each ticket it sends.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It MAY be either a database\nlookup key or a self-encrypted and self-authenticated value.\n",
      "id": "25df5e791c23a767",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 215,
      "quote": "It MAY be either a database lookup key or a self-encrypted and self-authenticated value.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MUST ignore\nunrecognized extensions.\n",
      "id": "1683f8d2499d6545",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 222,
      "quote": "Clients MUST ignore unrecognized extensions.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server receiving more than\nmax_early_data_size bytes of 0-RTT data SHOULD terminate the\nconnection with an \"unexpected_message\" alert.\n",
      "id": "a9aa147ad6009df2",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 229,
      "quote": "A server receiving more than max_early_data_size bytes of 0-RTT data SHOULD terminate the connection with an \"unexpected_message\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Note that servers\nthat reject early data due to lack of cryptographic material will\nbe unable to differentiate padding from content, so clients\nSHOULD NOT depend on being able to send large quantities of\npadding in early data records.\n",
      "id": "ae8d2b48a4bceb0f",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 237,
      "quote": "Note that servers that reject early data due to lack of cryptographic material will be unable to differentiate padding from content, so clients SHOULD NOT depend on being able to send large quantities of padding in early data records.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It is RECOMMENDED that\nimplementations place limits on the total lifetime of such keying\nmaterial; these limits should take into account the lifetime of the\npeer's certificate, the likelihood of intervening revocation, and the\ntime since the peer's online CertificateVerify signature.\n",
      "id": "4dc02e565166411e",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 247,
      "quote": "It is RECOMMENDED that implementations place limits on the total lifetime of such keying material; these limits should take into account the lifetime of the peer's certificate, the likelihood of intervening revocation, and the time since the peer's online CertificateVerify signature.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When the client has sent the \"post_handshake_auth\" extension (see\nSection 4.2.6), a server MAY request client authentication at any\ntime after the handshake has completed by sending a\nCertificateRequest message.\n",
      "id": "438dbd2bea4b8abd",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 30,
      "quote": "When the client has sent the \"post_handshake_auth\" extension (see Section 4.2.6), a server MAY request client authentication at any time after the handshake has completed by sending a CertificateRequest message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The client MUST respond with the\nappropriate Authentication messages (see Section 4.4).\n",
      "id": "35cd9979ecfd7824",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 39,
      "quote": "The client MUST respond with the appropriate Authentication messages (see Section 4.4).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the client\nchooses to authenticate, it MUST send Certificate, CertificateVerify,\n",
      "id": "8a21f3070a6cfc56",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 46,
      "quote": "If the client chooses to authenticate, it MUST send Certificate, CertificateVerify,",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If it declines, it MUST send a Certificate message\ncontaining no certificates followed by Finished.\n",
      "id": "5f208b021853c834",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 53,
      "quote": "If it declines, it MUST send a Certificate message containing no certificates followed by Finished.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "All of the client's\nmessages for a given response MUST appear consecutively on the wire\nwith no intervening messages of other types.\n",
      "id": "9f8f5b236f156e92",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 60,
      "quote": "All of the client's messages for a given response MUST appear consecutively on the wire with no intervening messages of other types.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client that receives a CertificateRequest message without having\nsent the \"post_handshake_auth\" extension MUST send an\n\"unexpected_message\" fatal alert.\n",
      "id": "807815266896ed1a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 68,
      "quote": "A client that receives a CertificateRequest message without having sent the \"post_handshake_auth\" extension MUST send an \"unexpected_message\" fatal alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Note: Because client authentication could involve prompting the user,\nservers MUST be prepared for some delay, including receiving an\narbitrary number of other messages between sending the\nCertificateRequest and receiving a response.\n",
      "id": "9e5880b87c69bb5b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 76,
      "quote": "Note: Because client authentication could involve prompting the user, servers MUST be prepared for some delay, including receiving an arbitrary number of other messages between sending the CertificateRequest and receiving a response.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In addition, clients\nwhich receive multiple CertificateRequests in close succession MAY\nrespond to them in a different order than they were received (the\ncertificate_request_context value allows the server to disambiguate\nthe responses).\n",
      "id": "7c4d138a019c95a5",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 85,
      "quote": "In addition, clients which receive multiple CertificateRequests in close succession MAY respond to them in a different order than they were received (the certificate_request_context value allows the server to disambiguate the responses).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations\nthat receive a KeyUpdate message prior to receiving a Finished\nmessage MUST terminate the connection with an \"unexpected_message\"\nalert.\n",
      "id": "92e3477eaaadd25e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "Implementations that receive a KeyUpdate message prior to receiving a Finished message MUST terminate the connection with an \"unexpected_message\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "After sending a KeyUpdate message, the sender SHALL send all\nits traffic using the next generation of keys, computed as described\nin Section 7.2.\n",
      "id": "f8407f08d1aceec4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 63,
      "quote": "After sending a KeyUpdate message, the sender SHALL send all its traffic using the next generation of keys, computed as described in Section 7.2.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Upon receiving a KeyUpdate, the receiver MUST update\nits receiving keys.\n",
      "id": "65c2e4a1e0bf6095",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 71,
      "quote": "Upon receiving a KeyUpdate, the receiver MUST update its receiving keys.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an implementation\nreceives any other value, it MUST terminate the connection with an\n\"illegal_parameter\" alert.\n",
      "id": "0d8fcff31c67d68c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 78,
      "quote": "If an implementation receives any other value, it MUST terminate the connection with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the request_update field is set to \"update_requested\", then the\nreceiver MUST send a KeyUpdate of its own with request_update set to\n\"update_not_requested\" prior to sending its next Application Data\nrecord.\n",
      "id": "82b8c00e6c35283f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 86,
      "quote": "If the request_update field is set to \"update_requested\", then the receiver MUST send a KeyUpdate of its own with request_update set to \"update_not_requested\" prior to sending its next Application Data record.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Both sender and receiver MUST encrypt their KeyUpdate messages with\nthe old keys.\n",
      "id": "d2679b8d99d7be1b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 95,
      "quote": "Both sender and receiver MUST encrypt their KeyUpdate messages with the old keys.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Additionally, both sides MUST enforce that a KeyUpdate\nwith the old key is received before accepting any messages encrypted\nwith the new key.\n",
      "id": "b4f728e261adcfc6",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 102,
      "quote": "Additionally, both sides MUST enforce that a KeyUpdate with the old key is received before accepting any messages encrypted with the new key.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.6.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Protocol messages MUST be sent in the order defined in Section 4.4.1\nand shown in the diagrams in Section 2.\n",
      "id": "51cc0ba4bb43053e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "Protocol messages MUST be sent in the order defined in Section 4.4.1 and shown in the diagrams in Section 2.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A peer which receives a\nhandshake message in an unexpected order MUST abort the handshake\nwith an \"unexpected_message\" alert.\n",
      "id": "582063b0b4f85d4f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 58,
      "quote": "A peer which receives a handshake message in an unexpected order MUST abort the handshake with an \"unexpected_message\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Any future content types MUST specify appropriate\nrules.\n",
      "id": "afece72bbf74f839",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 94,
      "quote": "Any future content types MUST specify appropriate rules.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Handshake messages MAY be coalesced into a single TLSPlaintext record\nor fragmented across several records, provided that:\n",
      "id": "5b47fcbfb934d2b0",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 101,
      "quote": "Handshake messages MAY be coalesced into a single TLSPlaintext record or fragmented across several records, provided that:",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  Handshake messages MUST NOT be interleaved with other record\ntypes.\n",
      "id": "8f1d9492101803c9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 108,
      "quote": "-  Handshake messages MUST NOT be interleaved with other record types.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "That is, if a handshake message is split over two or more\nrecords, there MUST NOT be any other records between them.\n",
      "id": "d2e3e303f5f37e0f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 115,
      "quote": "That is, if a handshake message is split over two or more records, there MUST NOT be any other records between them.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  Handshake messages MUST NOT span key changes.\n",
      "id": "ebb70a46fd83640d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 122,
      "quote": "-  Handshake messages MUST NOT span key changes.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations\nMUST verify that all messages immediately preceding a key change\nalign with a record boundary; if not, then they MUST terminate the\nconnection with an \"unexpected_message\" alert.\n",
      "id": "7a77923b3669c943",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 128,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST verify that all messages immediately preceding a key change align with a record boundary; if not, then they MUST terminate the connection with an \"unexpected_message\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations\nMUST verify that all messages immediately preceding a key change\nalign with a record boundary; if not, then they MUST terminate the\nconnection with an \"unexpected_message\" alert.\n",
      "id": "7c1bdef84bd17ef7",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 137,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST verify that all messages immediately preceding a key change align with a record boundary; if not, then they MUST terminate the connection with an \"unexpected_message\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Because the\nClientHello, EndOfEarlyData, ServerHello, Finished, and KeyUpdate\nmessages can immediately precede a key change, implementations\nMUST send these messages in alignment with a record boundary.\n",
      "id": "87940533f7d1258f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 146,
      "quote": "Because the ClientHello, EndOfEarlyData, ServerHello, Finished, and KeyUpdate messages can immediately precede a key change, implementations MUST send these messages in alignment with a record boundary.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations MUST NOT send zero-length fragments of Handshake\ntypes, even if those fragments contain padding.\n",
      "id": "5ab1d4af34771a2b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 155,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST NOT send zero-length fragments of Handshake types, even if those fragments contain padding.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Alert messages (Section 6) MUST NOT be fragmented across records, and\nmultiple alert messages MUST NOT be coalesced into a single\nTLSPlaintext record.\n",
      "id": "2c3b71700e7ec641",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 162,
      "quote": "Alert messages (Section 6) MUST NOT be fragmented across records, and multiple alert messages MUST NOT be coalesced into a single TLSPlaintext record.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Alert messages (Section 6) MUST NOT be fragmented across records, and\nmultiple alert messages MUST NOT be coalesced into a single\nTLSPlaintext record.\n",
      "id": "0ff81eefbb127a30",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 170,
      "quote": "Alert messages (Section 6) MUST NOT be fragmented across records, and multiple alert messages MUST NOT be coalesced into a single TLSPlaintext record.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In other words, a record with an Alert type\nMUST contain exactly one message.\n",
      "id": "ff510e2f3879e3c8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 178,
      "quote": "In other words, a record with an Alert type MUST contain exactly one message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Zero-length\nfragments of Application Data MAY be sent, as they are potentially\nuseful as a traffic analysis countermeasure.\n",
      "id": "d80bafd3bab6356c",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 185,
      "quote": "Zero-length fragments of Application Data MAY be sent, as they are potentially useful as a traffic analysis countermeasure.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Application Data\nfragments MAY be split across multiple records or coalesced into a\nsingle record.\n",
      "id": "da7930fd52343add",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 193,
      "quote": "Application Data fragments MAY be split across multiple records or coalesced into a single record.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "legacy_record_version:  MUST be set to 0x0303 for all records\ngenerated by a TLS 1.3 implementation other than an initial\nClientHello (i.e., one not generated after a HelloRetryRequest),\nwhere it MAY also be 0x0301 for compatibility purposes.\n",
      "id": "af6a599231e82c87",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 201,
      "quote": "legacy_record_version:  MUST be set to 0x0303 for all records generated by a TLS 1.3 implementation other than an initial ClientHello (i.e., one not generated after a HelloRetryRequest), where it MAY also be 0x0301 for compatibility purposes.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This\nfield is deprecated and MUST be ignored for all purposes.\n",
      "id": "49920aa0f68db405",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 210,
      "quote": "This field is deprecated and MUST be ignored for all purposes.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The length MUST NOT exceed 2^14 bytes.\n",
      "id": "b6d99337d8b40616",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 217,
      "quote": "The length MUST NOT exceed 2^14 bytes.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An\nendpoint that receives a record that exceeds this length MUST\nterminate the connection with a \"record_overflow\" alert.\n",
      "id": "28e9bb30c7b9872f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 223,
      "quote": "An endpoint that receives a record that exceeds this length MUST terminate the connection with a \"record_overflow\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In order to maximize backward\ncompatibility, a record containing an initial ClientHello SHOULD have\nversion 0x0301 (reflecting TLS 1.0) and a record containing a second\nClientHello or a ServerHello MUST have version 0x0303 (reflecting\nTLS 1.2).\n",
      "id": "515feb29da93c676",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 231,
      "quote": "In order to maximize backward compatibility, a record containing an initial ClientHello SHOULD have version 0x0301 (reflecting TLS 1.0) and a record containing a second ClientHello or a ServerHello MUST have version 0x0303 (reflecting TLS 1.2).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Note that Application Data\nrecords MUST NOT be written to the wire unprotected (see Section 2\nfor details).\n",
      "id": "c5e295988a31fd93",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 241,
      "quote": "Note that Application Data records MUST NOT be written to the wire unprotected (see Section 2 for details).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The length\nMUST NOT exceed 2^14 + 256 bytes.\n",
      "id": "454d9fb43b281160",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 117,
      "quote": "The length MUST NOT exceed 2^14 + 256 bytes.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint that receives a\nrecord that exceeds this length MUST terminate the connection with\na \"record_overflow\" alert.\n",
      "id": "60b57f5e24c268ce",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 124,
      "quote": "An endpoint that receives a record that exceeds this length MUST terminate the connection with a \"record_overflow\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the decryption fails, the receiver MUST terminate the connection\nwith a \"bad_record_mac\" alert.\n",
      "id": "550533427877dc47",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 132,
      "quote": "If the decryption fails, the receiver MUST terminate the connection with a \"bad_record_mac\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An AEAD algorithm used in TLS 1.3 MUST NOT produce an expansion\ngreater than 255 octets.\n",
      "id": "d55c1f6d962c3080",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 139,
      "quote": "An AEAD algorithm used in TLS 1.3 MUST NOT produce an expansion greater than 255 octets.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint that receives a record from its\npeer with TLSCiphertext.length larger than 2^14 + 256 octets MUST\nterminate the connection with a \"record_overflow\" alert.\n",
      "id": "b465beed1e7bb402",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 146,
      "quote": "An endpoint that receives a record from its peer with TLSCiphertext.length larger than 2^14 + 256 octets MUST terminate the connection with a \"record_overflow\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each sequence number is\nset to zero at the beginning of a connection and whenever the key is\nchanged; the first record transmitted under a particular traffic key\nMUST use sequence number 0.\n",
      "id": "717d6a17974a6dfb",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 36,
      "quote": "Each sequence number is set to zero at the beginning of a connection and whenever the key is changed; the first record transmitted under a particular traffic key MUST use sequence number 0.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a TLS implementation would need to wrap a sequence number, it MUST\neither rekey (Section 4.6.3) or terminate the connection.\n",
      "id": "70132ac22369ba0d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 45,
      "quote": "If a TLS implementation would need to wrap a sequence number, it MUST either rekey (Section 4.6.3) or terminate the connection.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An AEAD algorithm where N_MAX is less than 8 bytes\nMUST NOT be used with TLS.\n",
      "id": "3e5d058d3ea7fce9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 52,
      "quote": "An AEAD algorithm where N_MAX is less than 8 bytes MUST NOT be used with TLS.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When generating a TLSCiphertext record, implementations MAY choose to\npad.\n",
      "id": "0cfbe485b0eddf36",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "When generating a TLSCiphertext record, implementations MAY choose to pad.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations MUST set the\npadding octets to all zeros before encrypting.\n",
      "id": "180a59e64012365e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 63,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST set the padding octets to all zeros before encrypting.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations\nMUST NOT send Handshake and Alert records that have a zero-length\nTLSInnerPlaintext.content; if such a message is received, the\nreceiving implementation MUST terminate the connection with an\n\"unexpected_message\" alert.\n",
      "id": "aeb89794c6089f72",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 70,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST NOT send Handshake and Alert records that have a zero-length TLSInnerPlaintext.content; if such a message is received, the receiving implementation MUST terminate the connection with an \"unexpected_message\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations\nMUST NOT send Handshake and Alert records that have a zero-length\nTLSInnerPlaintext.content; if such a message is received, the\nreceiving implementation MUST terminate the connection with an\n\"unexpected_message\" alert.\n",
      "id": "a118bc99178b292f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 80,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST NOT send Handshake and Alert records that have a zero-length TLSInnerPlaintext.content; if such a message is received, the receiving implementation MUST terminate the connection with an \"unexpected_message\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations MUST limit their scanning to the cleartext returned\nfrom the AEAD decryption.\n",
      "id": "98e95302e05d1d70",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 90,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST limit their scanning to the cleartext returned from the AEAD decryption.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a receiving implementation does not\nfind a non-zero octet in the cleartext, it MUST terminate the\nconnection with an \"unexpected_message\" alert.\n",
      "id": "f2c1b930dbe14713",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 97,
      "quote": "If a receiving implementation does not find a non-zero octet in the cleartext, it MUST terminate the connection with an \"unexpected_message\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The presence of padding does not change the overall record size\nlimitations: the full encoded TLSInnerPlaintext MUST NOT exceed 2^14\n+ 1 octets.\n",
      "id": "1c4206b295549383",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 105,
      "quote": "The presence of padding does not change the overall record size limitations: the full encoded TLSInnerPlaintext MUST NOT exceed 2^14 + 1 octets.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations SHOULD do a key update as described in Section 4.6.3\nprior to reaching these limits.\n",
      "id": "7890db0808608291",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 18,
      "quote": "Implementations SHOULD do a key update as described in Section 4.6.3 prior to reaching these limits.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An implementation may receive an unencrypted record of type\nchange_cipher_spec consisting of the single byte value 0x01 at any\ntime after the first ClientHello message has been sent or received\nand before the peer's Finished message has been received and MUST\nsimply drop it without further processing.\n",
      "id": "4fc3eb763e6c43cd",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 39,
      "quote": "An implementation may receive an unencrypted record of type change_cipher_spec consisting of the single byte value 0x01 at any time after the first ClientHello message has been sent or received and before the peer's Finished message has been received and MUST simply drop it without further processing.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An\nimplementation which receives any other change_cipher_spec value or\nwhich receives a protected change_cipher_spec record MUST abort the\nhandshake with an \"unexpected_message\" alert.\n",
      "id": "890f25a5b8932ad4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 49,
      "quote": "An implementation which receives any other change_cipher_spec value or which receives a protected change_cipher_spec record MUST abort the handshake with an \"unexpected_message\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an implementation\ndetects a change_cipher_spec record received before the first\nClientHello message or after the peer's Finished message, it MUST be\ntreated as an unexpected record type (though stateless servers may\nnot be able to distinguish these cases from allowed cases).\n",
      "id": "1cf6c4b857bb323e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 58,
      "quote": "If an implementation detects a change_cipher_spec record received before the first ClientHello message or after the peer's Finished message, it MUST be treated as an unexpected record type (though stateless servers may not be able to distinguish these cases from allowed cases).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations MUST NOT send record types not defined in this\ndocument unless negotiated by some extension.\n",
      "id": "1254a67aac3d1def",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 68,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST NOT send record types not defined in this document unless negotiated by some extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a TLS\nimplementation receives an unexpected record type, it MUST terminate\nthe connection with an \"unexpected_message\" alert.\n",
      "id": "a4c522e6b51da31d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 75,
      "quote": "If a TLS implementation receives an unexpected record type, it MUST terminate the connection with an \"unexpected_message\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Any data received\nafter a closure alert has been received MUST be ignored.\n",
      "id": "427c0622337c3cf1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 48,
      "quote": "Any data received after a closure alert has been received MUST be ignored.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This alert SHOULD be followed by a\n\"close_notify\".\n",
      "id": "f80d5d2255cb0a67",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 55,
      "quote": "This alert SHOULD be followed by a \"close_notify\".",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Either party MAY initiate a close of its write side of the connection\nby sending a \"close_notify\" alert.\n",
      "id": "e8b1f77b8344c845",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 62,
      "quote": "Either party MAY initiate a close of its write side of the connection by sending a \"close_notify\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Any data received after a closure\nalert has been received MUST be ignored.\n",
      "id": "7bd813240fa800f2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 69,
      "quote": "Any data received after a closure alert has been received MUST be ignored.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each party MUST send a \"close_notify\" alert before closing its write\nside of the connection, unless it has already sent some error alert.\n",
      "id": "d6c260c7e5198c26",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 76,
      "quote": "Each party MUST send a \"close_notify\" alert before closing its write side of the connection, unless it has already sent some error alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the application protocol using TLS provides that any data may be\ncarried over the underlying transport after the TLS connection is\nclosed, the TLS implementation MUST receive a \"close_notify\" alert\nbefore indicating end-of-data to the application layer.\n",
      "id": "eade19117bff73fa",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 83,
      "quote": "If the application protocol using TLS provides that any data may be carried over the underlying transport after the TLS connection is closed, the TLS implementation MUST receive a \"close_notify\" alert before indicating end-of-data to the application layer.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Upon transmission or\nreceipt of a fatal alert message, both parties MUST immediately close\nthe connection.\n",
      "id": "73707b6f47c2cb1c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 134,
      "quote": "Upon transmission or receipt of a fatal alert message, both parties MUST immediately close the connection.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Whenever an implementation encounters a fatal error condition, it\nSHOULD send an appropriate fatal alert and MUST close the connection\nwithout sending or receiving any additional data.\n",
      "id": "a9e4330365e99b57",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 142,
      "quote": "Whenever an implementation encounters a fatal error condition, it SHOULD send an appropriate fatal alert and MUST close the connection without sending or receiving any additional data.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In the rest of\nthis specification, when the phrases \"terminate the connection\" and\n\"abort the handshake\" are used without a specific alert it means that\nthe implementation SHOULD send the alert indicated by the\ndescriptions below.\n",
      "id": "af4c3f2cf7fa98a2",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 150,
      "quote": "In the rest of this specification, when the phrases \"terminate the connection\" and \"abort the handshake\" are used without a specific alert it means that the implementation SHOULD send the alert indicated by the descriptions below.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The phrases \"terminate the connection with an X\nalert\" and \"abort the handshake with an X alert\" mean that the\nimplementation MUST send alert X if it sends any alert.\n",
      "id": "b2e246f2a5ee5653",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 160,
      "quote": "The phrases \"terminate the connection with an X alert\" and \"abort the handshake with an X alert\" mean that the implementation MUST send alert X if it sends any alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The\nimplementation SHOULD provide a way to facilitate logging the sending\nand receiving of alerts.\n",
      "id": "7bc2a3d73c5ed00b",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 168,
      "quote": "The implementation SHOULD provide a way to facilitate logging the sending and receiving of alerts.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Sending this alert is OPTIONAL; servers MAY instead choose to send\na \"decrypt_error\" alert to merely indicate an invalid PSK\nidentity.\n",
      "id": "9bac4c3ca9719a26",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 176,
      "quote": "Sending this alert is OPTIONAL; servers MAY instead choose to send a \"decrypt_error\" alert to merely indicate an invalid PSK identity.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Sending this alert is OPTIONAL; servers MAY instead choose to send\na \"decrypt_error\" alert to merely indicate an invalid PSK\nidentity.\n",
      "id": "ac79219d091286d1",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 184,
      "quote": "Sending this alert is OPTIONAL; servers MAY instead choose to send a \"decrypt_error\" alert to merely indicate an invalid PSK identity.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Upon receiving such an alert, the TLS\nimplementation SHOULD indicate end-of-data to the application.\n",
      "id": "eb061ccb4fda51e3",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 78,
      "quote": "Upon receiving such an alert, the TLS implementation SHOULD indicate end-of-data to the application.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Upon receiving an error alert, the TLS implementation\nSHOULD indicate an error to the application and MUST NOT allow any\nfurther data to be sent or received on the connection.\n",
      "id": "310f852b73456b73",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 85,
      "quote": "Upon receiving an error alert, the TLS implementation SHOULD indicate an error to the application and MUST NOT allow any further data to be sent or received on the connection.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers and\nclients MUST forget the secret values and keys established in failed\nconnections, with the exception of the PSKs associated with session\ntickets, which SHOULD be discarded if possible.\n",
      "id": "26ade86012b63452",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 93,
      "quote": "Servers and clients MUST forget the secret values and keys established in failed connections, with the exception of the PSKs associated with session tickets, which SHOULD be discarded if possible.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "All the alerts listed in Section 6.2 MUST be sent with\nAlertLevel=fatal and MUST be treated as error alerts when received\nregardless of the AlertLevel in the message.\n",
      "id": "a73ea16e71e6132f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 102,
      "quote": "All the alerts listed in Section 6.2 MUST be sent with AlertLevel=fatal and MUST be treated as error alerts when received regardless of the AlertLevel in the message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "All the alerts listed in Section 6.2 MUST be sent with\nAlertLevel=fatal and MUST be treated as error alerts when received\nregardless of the AlertLevel in the message.\n",
      "id": "987d0f8c54b31cba",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 110,
      "quote": "All the alerts listed in Section 6.2 MUST be sent with AlertLevel=fatal and MUST be treated as error alerts when received regardless of the AlertLevel in the message.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Unknown Alert types\nMUST be treated as error alerts.\n",
      "id": "56c60b19961343b2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 118,
      "quote": "Unknown Alert types MUST be treated as error alerts.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Peers which receive a message which\ncannot be parsed according to the syntax (e.g., have a length\nextending beyond the message boundary or contain an out-of-range\nlength) MUST terminate the connection with a \"decode_error\" alert.\n",
      "id": "7e0e5ddbee0b7a8e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 125,
      "quote": "Peers which receive a message which cannot be parsed according to the syntax (e.g., have a length extending beyond the message boundary or contain an out-of-range length) MUST terminate the connection with a \"decode_error\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Peers which receive a message which is syntactically correct but\nsemantically invalid (e.g., a DHE share of p - 1, or an invalid enum)\nMUST terminate the connection with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.\n",
      "id": "8ae6750bdf39c438",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 134,
      "quote": "Peers which receive a message which is syntactically correct but semantically invalid (e.g., a DHE share of p - 1, or an invalid enum) MUST terminate the connection with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once all the values which are to be derived from a given secret have\nbeen computed, that secret SHOULD be erased.\n",
      "id": "6bc759f7b9849141",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 137,
      "quote": "Once all the values which are to be derived from a given secret have been computed, that secret SHOULD be erased.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-7.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-7.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once client_/server_application_traffic_secret_N+1 and its associated\ntraffic keys have been computed, implementations SHOULD delete\nclient_/server_application_traffic_secret_N and its associated\ntraffic keys.\n",
      "id": "cfe8bdaea826337d",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 24,
      "quote": "Once client_/server_application_traffic_secret_N+1 and its associated traffic keys have been computed, implementations SHOULD delete client_/server_application_traffic_secret_N and its associated traffic keys.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-7.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-7.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Note that this octet string (\"Z\" in IEEE 1363 terminology) as output\nby FE2OSP (the Field Element to Octet String Conversion Primitive)\nhas constant length for any given field; leading zeros found in this\noctet string MUST NOT be truncated.\n",
      "id": "cae85e0066ec3ebf",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "Note that this octet string (\"Z\" in IEEE 1363 terminology) as output by FE2OSP (the Field Element to Octet String Conversion Primitive) has constant length for any given field; leading zeros found in this octet string MUST NOT be truncated.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-7.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For these curves, implementations SHOULD use the approach specified\nin [RFC7748] to calculate the Diffie-Hellman shared secret.\n",
      "id": "dfd6f746d42d57e3",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "For these curves, implementations SHOULD use the approach specified in [RFC7748] to calculate the Diffie-Hellman shared secret.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-7.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations MUST check whether the computed Diffie-Hellman shared\nsecret is the all-zero value and abort if so, as described in\nSection 6 of [RFC7748].\n",
      "id": "5b7fa6c9e5f3ef42",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 58,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST check whether the computed Diffie-Hellman shared secret is the all-zero value and abort if so, as described in Section 6 of [RFC7748].",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-7.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If implementors use an alternative\nimplementation of these elliptic curves, they SHOULD perform the\nadditional checks specified in Section 7 of [RFC7748].\n",
      "id": "65feb35cdd638bb9",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 66,
      "quote": "If implementors use an alternative implementation of these elliptic curves, they SHOULD perform the additional checks specified in Section 7 of [RFC7748].",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-7.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations MUST use the\nexporter_master_secret unless explicitly specified by the\napplication.\n",
      "id": "c2c215862a5cc104",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 39,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST use the exporter_master_secret unless explicitly specified by the application.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-7.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-7.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A separate\ninterface for the early exporter is RECOMMENDED; this avoids the\nexporter user accidentally using an early exporter when a regular one\nis desired or vice versa.\n",
      "id": "242c553d92dc555f",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "A separate interface for the early exporter is RECOMMENDED; this avoids the exporter user accidentally using an early exporter when a regular one is desired or vice versa.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-7.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-7.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Future\nspecifications MUST NOT define a use of exporters that permit both an\nempty context and no context with the same label.\n",
      "id": "ee5c8494b1be21a1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "Future specifications MUST NOT define a use of exporters that permit both an empty context and no context with the same label.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-7.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-7.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "New uses of\nexporters SHOULD provide a context in all exporter computations,\nthough the value could be empty.\n",
      "id": "76d395f5924fdcae",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "New uses of exporters SHOULD provide a context in all exporter computations, though the value could be empty.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-7.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-7.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MAY\nalso implement data stores with false positives, such as Bloom\nfilters, in which case they MUST respond to apparent replay by\nrejecting 0-RTT but MUST NOT abort the handshake.\n",
      "id": "badf6aa73ca08365",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 70,
      "quote": "Servers MAY also implement data stores with false positives, such as Bloom filters, in which case they MUST respond to apparent replay by rejecting 0-RTT but MUST NOT abort the handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-8.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-8.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MAY\nalso implement data stores with false positives, such as Bloom\nfilters, in which case they MUST respond to apparent replay by\nrejecting 0-RTT but MUST NOT abort the handshake.\n",
      "id": "b709fb3e5bc7e49c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 79,
      "quote": "Servers MAY also implement data stores with false positives, such as Bloom filters, in which case they MUST respond to apparent replay by rejecting 0-RTT but MUST NOT abort the handshake.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-8.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-8.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server MUST derive the storage key only from validated sections\nof the ClientHello.\n",
      "id": "8e6662057b842cec",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 88,
      "quote": "The server MUST derive the storage key only from validated sections of the ClientHello.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-8.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-8.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When implementations are freshly started, they SHOULD reject 0-RTT as\nlong as any portion of their recording window overlaps the startup\ntime.\n",
      "id": "506d21e361f07876",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 95,
      "quote": "When implementations are freshly started, they SHOULD reject 0-RTT as long as any portion of their recording window overlaps the startup time.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-8.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-8.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers\nSHOULD provide that level of replay safety by implementing one of the\nmethods described in this section or by equivalent means.\n",
      "id": "198216a05282200a",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 60,
      "quote": "Servers SHOULD provide that level of replay safety by implementing one of the methods described in this section or by equivalent means.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Therefore, in normal\noperation, clients will not know which, if any, of these mechanisms\nservers actually implement and hence MUST only send early data which\nthey deem safe to be replayed.\n",
      "id": "aecaea45e0c77642",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 68,
      "quote": "Therefore, in normal operation, clients will not know which, if any, of these mechanisms servers actually implement and hence MUST only send early data which they deem safe to be replayed.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server MUST ensure that any\ninstance of it (be it a machine, a thread, or any other entity within\nthe relevant serving infrastructure) would accept 0-RTT for the same\n0-RTT handshake at most once; this limits the number of replays to\nthe number of server instances in the deployment.\n",
      "id": "a8aaf9bd5a7e6c3a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 77,
      "quote": "The server MUST ensure that any instance of it (be it a machine, a thread, or any other entity within the relevant serving infrastructure) would accept 0-RTT for the same 0-RTT handshake at most once; this limits the number of replays to the number of server instances in the deployment.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The \"at most once per\nserver instance\" guarantee is a minimum requirement; servers SHOULD\nlimit 0-RTT replays further when feasible.\n",
      "id": "bd47aa35da83a93b",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 87,
      "quote": "The \"at most once per server instance\" guarantee is a minimum requirement; servers SHOULD limit 0-RTT replays further when feasible.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The second class of attack cannot be prevented at the TLS layer and\nMUST be dealt with by any application.\n",
      "id": "237a288793ba68d2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 95,
      "quote": "The second class of attack cannot be prevented at the TLS layer and MUST be dealt with by any application.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A TLS-compliant application MUST implement the TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256\n[GCM] cipher suite and SHOULD implement the TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384\n[GCM] and TLS_CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256 [RFC8439] cipher suites (see\nAppendix B.4).\n",
      "id": "c7fcc6080fa679b0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 19,
      "quote": "A TLS-compliant application MUST implement the TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 [GCM] cipher suite and SHOULD implement the TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 [GCM] and TLS_CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256 [RFC8439] cipher suites (see Appendix B.4).",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A TLS-compliant application MUST support digital signatures with\nrsa_pkcs1_sha256 (for certificates), rsa_pss_rsae_sha256 (for\nCertificateVerify and certificates), and ecdsa_secp256r1_sha256.\n",
      "id": "286b5edd0e7f482c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 28,
      "quote": "A TLS-compliant application MUST support digital signatures with rsa_pkcs1_sha256 (for certificates), rsa_pss_rsae_sha256 (for CertificateVerify and certificates), and ecdsa_secp256r1_sha256.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A\nTLS-compliant application MUST support key exchange with secp256r1\n(NIST P-256) and SHOULD support key exchange with X25519 [RFC7748].\n",
      "id": "ef81424b150a1b31",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 36,
      "quote": "A TLS-compliant application MUST support key exchange with secp256r1 (NIST P-256) and SHOULD support key exchange with X25519 [RFC7748].",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In the absence of an application profile standard specifying\notherwise, a TLS-compliant application MUST implement the following\nTLS extensions:\n",
      "id": "9c4532a440392a66",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 65,
      "quote": "In the absence of an application profile standard specifying otherwise, a TLS-compliant application MUST implement the following TLS extensions:",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "All implementations MUST send and use these extensions when offering\napplicable features:\n",
      "id": "7654d63ef6f08d33",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 73,
      "quote": "All implementations MUST send and use these extensions when offering applicable features:",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  \"supported_versions\" is REQUIRED for all ClientHello, ServerHello,\nand HelloRetryRequest messages.\n",
      "id": "65404e762827ad15",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 80,
      "quote": "-  \"supported_versions\" is REQUIRED for all ClientHello, ServerHello, and HelloRetryRequest messages.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  \"signature_algorithms\" is REQUIRED for certificate authentication.\n",
      "id": "05a5770443f47966",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 87,
      "quote": "-  \"signature_algorithms\" is REQUIRED for certificate authentication.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  \"supported_groups\" is REQUIRED for ClientHello messages using DHE\nor ECDHE key exchange.\n",
      "id": "9b951a3b69a50da9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 93,
      "quote": "-  \"supported_groups\" is REQUIRED for ClientHello messages using DHE or ECDHE key exchange.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  \"key_share\" is REQUIRED for DHE or ECDHE key exchange.\n",
      "id": "2b877a7ae2c027b0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 100,
      "quote": "-  \"key_share\" is REQUIRED for DHE or ECDHE key exchange.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  \"pre_shared_key\" is REQUIRED for PSK key agreement.\n",
      "id": "a3e60b7eb95ea9fa",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 106,
      "quote": "-  \"pre_shared_key\" is REQUIRED for PSK key agreement.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  \"psk_key_exchange_modes\" is REQUIRED for PSK key agreement.\n",
      "id": "47caccfb362c73c1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 112,
      "quote": "-  \"psk_key_exchange_modes\" is REQUIRED for PSK key agreement.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Such a ClientHello\nmessage MUST meet the following requirements:\n",
      "id": "5a87558e78b64aa7",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 118,
      "quote": "Such a ClientHello message MUST meet the following requirements:",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  If not containing a \"pre_shared_key\" extension, it MUST contain\nboth a \"signature_algorithms\" extension and a \"supported_groups\"\nextension.\n",
      "id": "7641303a5c24c7ab",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 125,
      "quote": "-  If not containing a \"pre_shared_key\" extension, it MUST contain both a \"signature_algorithms\" extension and a \"supported_groups\" extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  If containing a \"supported_groups\" extension, it MUST also contain\na \"key_share\" extension, and vice versa.\n",
      "id": "1451b6d64bdf36ca",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 133,
      "quote": "-  If containing a \"supported_groups\" extension, it MUST also contain a \"key_share\" extension, and vice versa.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers receiving a ClientHello which does not conform to these\nrequirements MUST abort the handshake with a \"missing_extension\"\nalert.\n",
      "id": "5e076a4a578a793c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 140,
      "quote": "Servers receiving a ClientHello which does not conform to these requirements MUST abort the handshake with a \"missing_extension\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Additionally, all implementations MUST support the use of the\n\"server_name\" extension with applications capable of using it.\n",
      "id": "3c3af8db0cf2b6c4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 148,
      "quote": "Additionally, all implementations MUST support the use of the \"server_name\" extension with applications capable of using it.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MAY require clients to send a valid \"server_name\" extension.\n",
      "id": "8da6419cca4a819e",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 155,
      "quote": "Servers MAY require clients to send a valid \"server_name\" extension.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers requiring this extension SHOULD respond to a ClientHello\nlacking a \"server_name\" extension by terminating the connection with\na \"missing_extension\" alert.\n",
      "id": "3a6c13ca6b586f23",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 161,
      "quote": "Servers requiring this extension SHOULD respond to a ClientHello lacking a \"server_name\" extension by terminating the connection with a \"missing_extension\" alert.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This section describes invariants that TLS endpoints and middleboxes\nMUST follow.\n",
      "id": "ea1aaa22ae38e4cd",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 63,
      "quote": "This section describes invariants that TLS endpoints and middleboxes MUST follow.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "At the same\ntime, deployments update at different rates, so a newer client or\nserver MAY continue to support older parameters, which would allow it\nto interoperate with older endpoints.\n",
      "id": "dddad5ad17bcbaa9",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 70,
      "quote": "At the same time, deployments update at different rates, so a newer client or server MAY continue to support older parameters, which would allow it to interoperate with older endpoints.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For this to work, implementations MUST correctly handle extensible\nfields:\n",
      "id": "2357b170fa5c0810",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 79,
      "quote": "For this to work, implementations MUST correctly handle extensible fields:",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  A client sending a ClientHello MUST support all parameters\nadvertised in it.\n",
      "id": "09ee5050fa2823ea",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 86,
      "quote": "-  A client sending a ClientHello MUST support all parameters advertised in it.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  A server receiving a ClientHello MUST correctly ignore all\nunrecognized cipher suites, extensions, and other parameters.\n",
      "id": "ba6a3d27c859e350",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 93,
      "quote": "-  A server receiving a ClientHello MUST correctly ignore all unrecognized cipher suites, extensions, and other parameters.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In\nTLS 1.3, a client receiving a CertificateRequest or\nNewSessionTicket MUST also ignore all unrecognized extensions.\n",
      "id": "bae9452a96487f27",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 100,
      "quote": "In TLS 1.3, a client receiving a CertificateRequest or NewSessionTicket MUST also ignore all unrecognized extensions.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  A middlebox which terminates a TLS connection MUST behave as a\ncompliant TLS server (to the original client), including having a\ncertificate which the client is willing to accept, and also as a\ncompliant TLS client (to the original server), including verifying\nthe original server's certificate.\n",
      "id": "8b48d211625c9cef",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 108,
      "quote": "-  A middlebox which terminates a TLS connection MUST behave as a compliant TLS server (to the original client), including having a certificate which the client is willing to accept, and also as a compliant TLS client (to the original server), including verifying the original server's certificate.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In particular, it MUST\ngenerate its own ClientHello containing only parameters it\nunderstands, and it MUST generate a fresh ServerHello random\nvalue, rather than forwarding the endpoint's value.\n",
      "id": "8be96a1700525c30",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 118,
      "quote": "In particular, it MUST generate its own ClientHello containing only parameters it understands, and it MUST generate a fresh ServerHello random value, rather than forwarding the endpoint's value.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In particular, it MUST\ngenerate its own ClientHello containing only parameters it\nunderstands, and it MUST generate a fresh ServerHello random\nvalue, rather than forwarding the endpoint's value.\n",
      "id": "fb55f13ef1a2c97e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 127,
      "quote": "In particular, it MUST generate its own ClientHello containing only parameters it understands, and it MUST generate a fresh ServerHello random value, rather than forwarding the endpoint's value.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "-  A middlebox which forwards ClientHello parameters it does not\nunderstand MUST NOT process any messages beyond that ClientHello.\n",
      "id": "5ed5cbaa5100f294",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 136,
      "quote": "-  A middlebox which forwards ClientHello parameters it does not understand MUST NOT process any messages beyond that ClientHello.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It MUST forward all subsequent traffic unmodified.\n",
      "id": "d9c4dad00c9fcee4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 143,
      "quote": "It MUST forward all subsequent traffic unmodified.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "These additions MAY\nchange any message beyond the ClientHello arbitrarily.\n",
      "id": "3eff94e9d64753d2",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 149,
      "quote": "These additions MAY change any message beyond the ClientHello arbitrarily.",
      "source": "compliance/specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446/section-9.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-9.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "id": "baf971f52ae287f7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 199,
      "quote": "For the curves secp256r1, secp384r1, and secp521r1, peers MUST validate each other's public value Q by ensuring that the point is a valid point on the elliptic curve.",
      "source": "crypto/s2n_ecc_evp.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.8.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ed2e60c02847225c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 204,
      "quote": "With the NIST curves, each party MUST validate the public key sent by its peer in the ClientKeyExchange and ServerKeyExchange messages.  A receiving party MUST check that the x and y parameters from the peer's public value satisfy the curve equation, y^2 = x^3 + ax + b mod p.",
      "source": "crypto/s2n_ecc_evp.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.11",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5995f7198499383f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 20,
      "quote": "PRK  = 0x077709362c2e32df0ddc3f0dc47bba63 90b6c73bb50f9c3122ec844ad7c2b3e5 (32 octets)",
      "source": "tests/testlib/s2n_resumption_testlib.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5869",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "58d05f40520fc508",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "Unknown Alert types MUST be treated as error alerts.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_alerts_protocol_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "9e7179294667d054",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 63,
      "quote": "All the alerts listed in Section 6.2 MUST be sent with AlertLevel=fatal and MUST be treated as error alerts when received regardless of the AlertLevel in the message.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_alerts_protocol_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "0e56140e79982039",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 156,
      "quote": "Upon receiving an error alert, the TLS implementation SHOULD indicate an error to the application and MUST NOT allow any further data to be sent or received on the connection.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_alerts_protocol_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "733fbeb20320d33f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 172,
      "quote": "Upon transmission or receipt of a fatal alert message, both parties MUST immediately close the connection.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_alerts_protocol_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "59a5f1de77ba78b9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 181,
      "quote": "The implementation SHOULD provide a way to facilitate logging the sending and receiving of alerts.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_alerts_protocol_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "ae3b93c9d925c720",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 302,
      "quote": "Upon transmission or receipt of a fatal alert message, both parties MUST immediately close the connection.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_alerts_protocol_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "be444e3ddd1c19ac",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 311,
      "quote": "Whenever an implementation encounters a fatal error condition, it SHOULD send an appropriate fatal alert",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_alerts_protocol_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "5e683d86c1df515c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 324,
      "quote": "and MUST close the connection without sending or receiving any additional data.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_alerts_protocol_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "b48ccfa53809448c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 337,
      "quote": "Either party MAY initiate a close of its write side of the connection by sending a \"close_notify\" alert.  Any data received after a closure alert has been received MUST be ignored.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_alerts_protocol_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "d78bd80ce93c474f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 389,
      "quote": "Any data received after a closure alert has been received MUST be ignored.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_alerts_protocol_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "a3947f5dd9df4f38",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 405,
      "quote": "Each party MUST send a \"close_notify\" alert before closing its write side of the connection, unless it has already sent some error alert. This does not have any effect on its read side of the connection.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_alerts_protocol_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "0a3a6405540804fd",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 444,
      "quote": "The \"close_notify\" alert is used to indicate orderly closure of one direction of the connection.  Upon receiving such an alert, the TLS implementation SHOULD indicate end-of-data to the application.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_alerts_protocol_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "4bd07f69034e4314",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 470,
      "quote": "Note that this is a change from versions of TLS prior to TLS 1.3 in which implementations were required to react to a \"close_notify\" by discarding pending writes and sending an immediate \"close_notify\" alert of their own.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_alerts_protocol_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "633de2c619a2b13a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 528,
      "quote": "If a transport-level close is received prior to a \"close_notify\", the receiver cannot know that all the data that was sent has been received.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_alerts_protocol_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "6.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "82b9fad6a2557b0d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 534,
      "quote": "If the application protocol using TLS provides that any data may be carried over the underlying transport after the TLS connection is closed, the TLS implementation MUST receive a \"close_notify\" alert before indicating end-of-data to the application layer.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_alerts_protocol_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "6.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "02a16cec81965f7d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 189,
      "quote": "The client MAY send the \"certificate_authorities\" extension in the ClientHello message.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_cert_authorities_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "d5d81ff4d4d50258",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 250,
      "quote": "The server MAY send it in the CertificateRequest message.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_cert_authorities_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "519fb8bbdc7af9ca",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 104,
      "quote": "that the server selected a cipher suite indicating a Hash associated with the PSK",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_cipher_suite_match_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "bf34ce56e5aa5018",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 300,
      "quote": "o  When a ClientHello is received, the server MUST check if it includes the TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV SCSV.  If it does, set the secure_renegotiation flag to TRUE.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_cipher_suite_match_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.6",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "de51bb753f5ff8ed",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 792,
      "quote": "The server MUST ensure that it selects a compatible PSK (if any) and cipher suite.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_cipher_suite_match_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "09909db927a4fc04",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 79,
      "quote": "When a PSK is used and early data is allowed for that PSK, the client can send Application Data in its first flight of messages.  If the client opts to do so, it MUST supply both the \"pre_shared_key\" and \"early_data\" extensions.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_early_data_indication_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "93c25423c0e152f2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 101,
      "quote": "A client MUST NOT include the \"early_data\" extension in its followup ClientHello.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_early_data_indication_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "54df1c7fa9c225c9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 106,
      "quote": "-  Removing the \"early_data\" extension (Section 4.2.10) if one was present.  Early data is not permitted after a HelloRetryRequest.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_early_data_indication_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "320102222914a9b7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 276,
      "quote": "A client MUST NOT include the \"early_data\" extension in its followup ClientHello.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_early_data_indication_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "401896ecbaa7202a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 404,
      "quote": "A server which receives an \"early_data\" extension MUST behave in one of three ways:",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_early_data_indication_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "81ac0f279bca3327",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 409,
      "quote": "-  Request that the client send another ClientHello by responding with a HelloRetryRequest.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_early_data_indication_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "ec9fbda41a8ca396",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 465,
      "quote": "A client that proposes ECC cipher suites may choose not to include these extensions. In this case, the server is free to choose any one of the elliptic curves or point formats listed in Section 5.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_hello_recv_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "30d9ec71280b9f0b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 212,
      "quote": "This message MAY be ignored by the client if it does not wish to renegotiate a session, or the client may, if it wishes, respond with a no_renegotiation alert.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_hello_request_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "0616745bf9b58291",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 253,
      "quote": "TLS implementations SHOULD provide a mechanism to disable and enable renegotiation.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_hello_request_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "5",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "4878ab2c305b29a1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 258,
      "quote": "This message MAY be ignored by the client if it does not wish to renegotiate a session, or the client may, if it wishes, respond with a no_renegotiation alert.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_hello_request_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "97cbaa711dbdaafb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 303,
      "quote": "TLS implementations SHOULD provide a mechanism to disable and enable renegotiation.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_hello_request_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "5",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "0a1b2dc21da92584",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 384,
      "quote": "This text applies if the connection's \"secure_renegotiation\" flag is set to FALSE. It is possible that un-upgraded servers will request that the client renegotiate.  It is RECOMMENDED that clients refuse this renegotiation request.  Clients that do so MUST respond to such requests with a \"no_renegotiation\" alert (RFC 5246 requires this alert to be at the \"warning\" level).  It is possible that the apparently un-upgraded server is in fact an attacker who is then allowing the client to renegotiate with a different, legitimate, upgraded server.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_hello_request_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "5bcfdae8c4bdeada",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 478,
      "quote": "SSLv3 does not define the \"no_renegotiation\" alert (and does not offer a way to indicate a refusal to renegotiate at a \"warning\" level).  SSLv3 clients that refuse renegotiation SHOULD use a fatal handshake_failure alert.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_hello_request_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "4.5",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "860b63c0f64f096c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 408,
      "quote": "Otherwise, the client MUST process all extensions in the HelloRetryRequest and send a second updated ClientHello.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_hello_retry_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "8ac20731e36fb61b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 472,
      "quote": "If the server selects an (EC)DHE group and the client did not offer a compatible \"key_share\" extension in the initial ClientHello, the server MUST respond with a HelloRetryRequest (Section 4.1.4) message.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_hello_retry_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "a0d055b6d9c39627",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 542,
      "quote": "If a client receives a second HelloRetryRequest in the same connection (i.e., where the ClientHello was itself in response to a HelloRetryRequest), it MUST abort the handshake with an \"unexpected_message\" alert.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_hello_retry_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "baf742f8356dfdfb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 623,
      "quote": "Upon receiving a message with type server_hello, implementations MUST first examine the Random value and, if it matches this value, process it as described in Section 4.1.4).",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_hello_retry_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "9995896098fcf65b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 645,
      "quote": "Upon receiving the ServerHello, clients MUST check that the cipher suite supplied in the ServerHello is the same as that in the HelloRetryRequest and otherwise abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_hello_retry_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "21dc78dd610dc39e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 684,
      "quote": "The client will also send a ClientHello when the server has responded to its ClientHello with a HelloRetryRequest.  In that case, the client MUST send the same ClientHello without modification",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_hello_retry_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "3508fa55b70932fd",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 931,
      "quote": "Servers MUST ensure that they negotiate the same cipher suite when receiving a conformant updated ClientHello (if the server selects the cipher suite as the first step in the negotiation, then this will happen automatically).",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_hello_retry_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1e7a7d4ba07d3c0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1452,
      "quote": "As with the ServerHello, a HelloRetryRequest MUST NOT contain any extensions that were not first offered by the client in its ClientHello, with the exception of optionally the \"cookie\" (see Section 4.2.2) extension.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_hello_retry_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "4c4b46a80075d521",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1480,
      "quote": "Upon receipt of a HelloRetryRequest, the client MUST check the legacy_version, legacy_session_id_echo, cipher_suite, and legacy_compression_method as specified in Section 4.1.3 and then process the extensions, starting with determining the version using \"supported_versions\".",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_hello_retry_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "18ff6491d4079e1e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1591,
      "quote": "A client which receives a cipher suite that was not offered MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_hello_retry_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "fb204cec65cb67e5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1686,
      "quote": "The server's extensions MUST contain \"supported_versions\".",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_hello_retry_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "d06c6c5bd8f548f9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1750,
      "quote": "Servers MUST ensure that they negotiate the same cipher suite when receiving a conformant updated ClientHello (if the server selects the cipher suite as the first step in the negotiation, then this will happen automatically).",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_hello_retry_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "acc35cc6c3c008d6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1821,
      "quote": "The value of selected_version in the HelloRetryRequest \"supported_versions\" extension MUST be retained in the ServerHello, and a client MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert if the value changes.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_hello_retry_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "ec9c4b08ed2ea019",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1875,
      "quote": "Upon receipt of this extension in a HelloRetryRequest, the client MUST verify that (1) the selected_group field corresponds to a group which was provided in the \"supported_groups\" extension in the original ClientHello",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_hello_retry_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.2.8",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "b17f4f0602661715",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1956,
      "quote": "If using (EC)DHE key establishment and a HelloRetryRequest containing a \"key_share\" extension was received by the client, the client MUST verify that the selected NamedGroup in the ServerHello is the same as that in the HelloRetryRequest. If this check fails, the client MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_hello_retry_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.2.8",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "fa341e598dda598a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 564,
      "quote": "o  The client MUST include either an empty \"renegotiation_info\" extension, or the TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV signaling cipher suite value in the ClientHello.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_hello_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "b3712d1dcf1c9a8a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 187,
      "quote": "-   If a \"key_share\" extension was supplied in the HelloRetryRequest, replacing the list of shares with a list containing a single KeyShareEntry from the indicated group.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_key_share_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "3aaed3b8d5b80d25",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 193,
      "quote": "Otherwise, when sending the new ClientHello, the client MUST replace the original \"key_share\" extension with one containing only a new KeyShareEntry for the group indicated in the selected_group field of the triggering HelloRetryRequest.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_key_share_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.2.8",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "87021aa76c42de81",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 98,
      "quote": "If a server receives a maximum fragment length negotiation request for a value other than the allowed values, it MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_max_frag_len_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6066",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "f40d8d82aae98cec",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 140,
      "quote": "When a PSK is used and early data is allowed for that PSK, the client can send Application Data in its first flight of messages.  If the client opts to do so, it MUST supply both the \"pre_shared_key\" and \"early_data\" extensions.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_psk_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "9f8ff17762c81a2b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 402,
      "quote": "In addition, in its updated ClientHello, the client SHOULD NOT offer any pre-shared keys associated with a hash other than that of the selected cipher suite.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_psk_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "1535c7a286df59d1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 475,
      "quote": "In addition, in its updated ClientHello, the client SHOULD NOT offer any pre-shared keys associated with a hash other than that of the selected cipher suite.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_psk_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "71e35d08520feac5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1511,
      "quote": "-   Updating the \"pre_shared_key\" extension if present by recomputing the \"obfuscated_ticket_age\" and binder values and (optionally) removing any PSKs which are incompatible with the server's indicated cipher suite.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_psk_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "f4ebf968d4e47f24",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 59,
      "quote": "The server MUST then verify that the length of the \"renegotiated_connection\" field is zero, and if it is not, MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_renegotiation_info_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.6",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "ef174da8123ec9bc",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 101,
      "quote": "TLS servers that support secure renegotiation and support SSLv3 MUST accept SCSV or the \"renegotiation_info\" extension and respond as described in this specification even if the offered client version is {0x03, 0x00}.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_renegotiation_info_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "4.5",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "9b81f2954b40d1a0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 123,
      "quote": "o  The client MUST include either an empty \"renegotiation_info\" extension, or the TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV signaling cipher suite value in the ClientHello.  Including both is NOT RECOMMENDED.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_renegotiation_info_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "f7a87cc2f2377a62",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 165,
      "quote": "o  The server MUST check if the \"renegotiation_info\" extension is included in the ClientHello.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_renegotiation_info_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.6",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "71c85741b81eea01",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 225,
      "quote": "o  The client MUST include the \"renegotiation_info\" extension in the ClientHello",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_renegotiation_info_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.5",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "2c04bb940d7e7b57",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 245,
      "quote": "o  The client MUST include the \"renegotiation_info\" extension in the ClientHello, containing the saved client_verify_data.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_renegotiation_info_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.5",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "87ee908ab8941660",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 291,
      "quote": "The SCSV MUST NOT be included.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_renegotiation_info_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.5",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "9a74350847b41a25",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 324,
      "quote": "o  The server MUST verify that the value of the \"renegotiated_connection\" field is equal to the saved client_verify_data value; if it is not, the server MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_renegotiation_info_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.7",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "4743f154c3462b94",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 390,
      "quote": "o  The server MUST verify that the \"renegotiation_info\" extension is present; if it is not, the server MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_renegotiation_info_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.7",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "8468a20e82adc4cb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 421,
      "quote": "o  When a ClientHello is received, the server MUST verify that it does not contain the TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV SCSV.  If the SCSV is present, the server MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_renegotiation_info_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.7",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "ab94dc59dd45e77d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 394,
      "quote": "A TLS server can also receive a ClientHello indicating a version number smaller than its highest supported version. If the \"supported_versions\" extension is present, the server MUST negotiate using that extension as described in Section 4.2.1.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_client_supported_versions_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "5d114ca55e650c05",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 46,
      "quote": "-   Including a \"cookie\" extension if one was provided in the HelloRetryRequest.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_cookie_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "ae4597c12cf9dcdf",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 255,
      "quote": "When sending a HelloRetryRequest, the server MAY provide a \"cookie\" extension to the client (this is an exception to the usual rule that the only extensions that may be sent are those that appear in the ClientHello).  When sending the new ClientHello, the client MUST copy the contents of the extension received in the HelloRetryRequest into a \"cookie\" extension in the new ClientHello.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_cookie_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
