    {
      "id": "45da849a09c80518",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 427,
      "quote": "In order to accept early data, the server MUST have accepted a PSK cipher suite and selected the first key offered in the client's \"pre_shared_key\" extension.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_early_data_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "bea55874a7756c8f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 460,
      "quote": "In addition, it MUST verify that the following values are the same as those associated with the selected PSK:",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_early_data_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "ff590985d9967e47",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 468,
      "quote": "-  The TLS version number",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_early_data_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "b6ad4ee0bff0ce97",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 495,
      "quote": "-  The selected cipher suite",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_early_data_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "dd3f7e9e8182050f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 518,
      "quote": "-  The selected ALPN [RFC7301] protocol, if any",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_early_data_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "62655efaa879ccad",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 421,
      "quote": "For the curves secp256r1, secp384r1, and secp521r1, peers MUST validate each other's public value Q by ensuring that the point is a valid point on the elliptic curve.  The appropriate validation procedures are defined in Section 4.3.7 of [ECDSA] and alternatively in Section 5.6.2.3 of [KEYAGREEMENT].  This process consists of three steps: (1) verify that Q is not the point at infinity (O), (2) verify that for Q = (x, y) both integers x and y are in the correct interval, and (3) ensure that (x, y) is a correct solution to the elliptic curve equation.  For these curves, implementors do not need to verify membership in the correct subgroup.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_ecc_evp_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.8.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "dcb8f8870e12f1ba",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 75,
      "quote": "If the original session used the extension but the new ServerHello does not contain the extension, the client MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_ems_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "b842e2984c27809e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 31,
      "quote": "If the original session used the \"extended_master_secret\" extension but the new ClientHello does not contain it, the server MUST abort the abbreviated handshake.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_extended_master_secret_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "1b8bf376a2d23dd8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 68,
      "quote": "If the original session did not use the \"extended_master_secret\" extension but the new ClientHello contains the extension, then the server MUST NOT perform the abbreviated handshake.  Instead, it SHOULD continue with a full handshake (as described in Section 5.2) to negotiate a new session.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_extended_master_secret_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "508500918dae4f3b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 174,
      "quote": "Upon receiving such an extension, an endpoint MUST abort the handshake with an \"unsupported_extension\" alert.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_extension_type_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "69c9857fe87d1786",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 179,
      "quote": "If the original session did not use the \"extended_master_secret\" extension but the new ServerHello contains the extension, the client MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_extension_type_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "1b03262b18e4b6df",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 185,
      "quote": "As with the ServerHello, a HelloRetryRequest MUST NOT contain any extensions that were not first offered by the client in its ClientHello, with the exception of optionally the \"cookie\" (see Section 4.2.2) extension.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_extension_type_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "2a7b9dc49a99108c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 270,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST NOT send extension responses if the remote endpoint did not send the corresponding extension requests, with the exception of the \"cookie\" extension in the HelloRetryRequest.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_extension_type_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "92762bf0503913be",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 276,
      "quote": "As with the ServerHello, a HelloRetryRequest MUST NOT contain any extensions that were not first offered by the client in its ClientHello, with the exception of optionally the \"cookie\" (see Section 4.2.2) extension.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_extension_type_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "2aaafe4b264b7d82",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 245,
      "quote": "If the protocol is QUIC then the first character of the fingerprint is “q”, if DTLS it is \"d\", else it is “t”.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_fingerprint_ja4_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "quic-and-dtls",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "87ea60c160466652",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 281,
      "quote": "If the SNI extension (0x0000) exists, then the destination of the connection is a domain, or “d” in the fingerprint. If the SNI does not exist, then the destination is an IP address, or “i”.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_fingerprint_ja4_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "sni",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "c59090b7e6e86700",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 324,
      "quote": "0x0304 = TLS 1.3 = “13” 0x0303 = TLS 1.2 = “12” 0x0302 = TLS 1.1 = “11” 0x0301 = TLS 1.0 = “10”",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_fingerprint_ja4_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "tls-and-dtls-version",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "e5dd8707b6aa7a31",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 336,
      "quote": "0x0300 = SSL 3.0 = “s3” 0x0002 = SSL 2.0 = “s2”",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_fingerprint_ja4_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "tls-and-dtls-version",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "49129c994c69c69a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 353,
      "quote": "Handshake version (located at the top of the packet) should be ignored.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_fingerprint_ja4_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "tls-and-dtls-version",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "63c6a069fdf5e3c3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 381,
      "quote": "If extension 0x002b exists (supported_versions), then the version is the highest value in the extension.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_fingerprint_ja4_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "tls-and-dtls-version",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "224ded51e84738ab",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 411,
      "quote": "If the extension doesn’t exist, then the TLS version is the value of the Protocol Version.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_fingerprint_ja4_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "tls-and-dtls-version",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "1f8301318b2b388d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 439,
      "quote": "Remember to ignore GREASE values.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_fingerprint_ja4_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "tls-and-dtls-version",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "00f617f75d7ec467",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 482,
      "quote": "if there’s 6 cipher suites in the hello packet, then the value should be “06”.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_fingerprint_ja4_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "number-of-ciphers",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "d587646dec0001e4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 492,
      "quote": "If there’s > 99, which there should never be, then output “99”.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_fingerprint_ja4_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "number-of-ciphers",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "329422cf4a93e95c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 504,
      "quote": "2 character number of cipher suites, so if there’s 6 cipher suites in the hello packet, then the value should be “06”.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_fingerprint_ja4_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "number-of-ciphers",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "678d7883dae5b8a0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 522,
      "quote": "Remember, ignore GREASE values. They don’t count.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_fingerprint_ja4_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
