    },
    {
      "id": "8198ddedb9907ffb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 640,
      "quote": "The first and last alphanumeric characters of the ALPN (Application-Layer Protocol Negotiation) first value.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_fingerprint_ja4_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "alpn-extension-value",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "f5b967592b74dab3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 648,
      "quote": "In the above example, the first ALPN value is h2 so the first and last characters to use in the fingerprint are “h2”.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_fingerprint_ja4_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "alpn-extension-value",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "70d682250bb13007",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 680,
      "quote": "If the first ALPN listed was http/1.1 then the first and last characters to use in the fingerprint would be “h1”.",
