      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "alpn-extension-value",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "41988efe904967b2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 713,
      "quote": "If the first ALPN value is only a single character, then that character is treated as both the first and last character.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_fingerprint_ja4_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "alpn-extension-value",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "ce9e323ab7f12d06",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 744,
      "quote": "If the first or last byte of the first ALPN is non-alphanumeric (meaning not `0x30-0x39`, `0x41-0x5A`, or `0x61-0x7A`), then we print the first and last characters of the hex representation of the first ALPN instead.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_fingerprint_ja4_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "alpn-extension-value",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "62a342d349a0b621",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 758,
      "quote": "For example: * `0xAB` would be printed as \"ab\" * `0xAB 0xCD` would be printed as \"ad\" * `0x30 0xAB` would be printed as \"3b\" * `0x30 0x31 0xAB 0xCD` would be printed as \"3d\"",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_fingerprint_ja4_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "alpn-extension-value",
