    {
      "id": "c3a6f61e6e2a72af",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1232,
      "quote": "The extension list is created using the 4 character hex values of the extensions, lower case, comma delimited, sorted (not in the order they appear).",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_fingerprint_ja4_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "extension-hash",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "9fd9d917d34136fb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1254,
      "quote": "The signature algorithm hex values are then added to the end of the list in the order that they appear (not sorted) with an underscore delimiting the two lists.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_fingerprint_ja4_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "extension-hash",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "19f6ad686e5ecbb1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1263,
      "quote": "Are added to the end of the previous string to create: ``` 0005,000a,000b,000d,0012,0015,0017,001b,0023,002b,002d,0033,4469,ff01_0403,0804,0401,0503,0805,0501,0806,0601 ```",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_fingerprint_ja4_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "extension-hash",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "93ee4d52bd569614",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1288,
      "quote": "A 12 character truncated sha256 hash of the list of extensions, sorted by hex value, followed by the list of signature algorithms, in the order that they appear (not sorted).",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_fingerprint_ja4_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "extension-hash",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "f42286d0170cc108",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1297,
      "quote": "Hashed to: ``` e5627efa2ab19723084c1033a96c694a45826ab5a460d2d3fd5ffcfe97161c95 ``` Truncated to first 12 characters: ``` e5627efa2ab1 ```",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_fingerprint_ja4_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "extension-hash",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "82db14eb402b0413",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1324,
      "quote": "If there are no signature algorithms in the hello packet, then the string ends without an underscore and is hashed.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_fingerprint_ja4_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "extension-hash",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "b217df82158c7c60",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1385,
      "quote": "If there are no extensions in the sorted extensions list, then the value of JA4_c is set to `000000000000`",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_fingerprint_ja4_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "extension-hash",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "d45aaa763fb57017",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 43,
      "quote": "If the client attempts a 0-RTT handshake but the server rejects it, the server will generally not have the 0-RTT record protection keys and must instead use trial decryption (either with the 1-RTT handshake keys or by looking for a cleartext ClientHello in the case of a HelloRetryRequest) to find the first non-0-RTT message. If the server chooses to accept the \"early_data\" extension, then it MUST comply with the same error-handling requirements specified for all records when processing early data records.  Specifically, if the server fails to decrypt a 0-RTT record following an accepted \"early_data\" extension, it MUST terminate the connection with a \"bad_record_mac\" alert as per Section 5.2.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_handshake_io_early_data_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "bffd0e285cb526c2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 103,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST treat the receipt of a TLS KeyUpdate message as a connection error of type 0x010a, equivalent to a fatal TLS alert of unexpected_message",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_key_update_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "6",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "abd259e242aa52f6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 197,
      "quote": "The length of \"padding\" SHOULD be 32 - ((len(selected_protocol) + 2) % 32).",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_next_protocol_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/id/draft-agl-tls-nextprotoneg-03",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "765b60ccf44c3524",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 69,
      "quote": "For the same reasons, after a handshake has been performed for a given connection, renegotiations on the same connection MUST NOT include the \"next_protocol_negotiation\" extension.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_npn_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/id/draft-agl-tls-nextprotoneg-03",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "410462a9a6438026",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 203,
      "quote": "In the event that the client doesn't support any of server's protocols, or the server doesn't advertise any, it SHOULD select the first protocol that it supports.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_npn_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/id/draft-agl-tls-nextprotoneg-03",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "f1a46ea441f42264",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 227,
      "quote": "In the event that the client doesn't support any of server's protocols, or the server doesn't advertise any, it SHOULD select the first protocol that it supports.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_npn_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/id/draft-agl-tls-nextprotoneg-03",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "4d4ddad783843ba7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 483,
      "quote": "-  Handshake messages MUST NOT be interleaved with other record types.  That is, if a handshake message is split over two or more records, there MUST NOT be any other records between them.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_post_handshake_recv_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "bc663f02394e394e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 138,
      "quote": "A client MAY select one or more GREASE PskKeyExchangeMode values and advertise them in the \"psk_key_exchange_modes\" extension, if sent.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_psk_key_exchange_modes_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8701",
      "target_section": "section-3.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "957b96e4b604632f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 144,
      "quote": "When processing a ClientHello, servers MUST NOT treat GREASE values differently from any unknown value.  Servers MUST NOT negotiate any GREASE value when offered in a ClientHello.  Servers MUST correctly ignore unknown values in a ClientHello and attempt to negotiate with one of the remaining parameters.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_psk_key_exchange_modes_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8701",
      "target_section": "section-3.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "21105a6c77b39b09",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 160,
      "quote": "The following values are reserved as GREASE values for PskKeyExchangeModes: 0x0B 0x2A 0x49 0x68 0x87 0xA6 0xC5 0xE4",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_psk_key_exchange_modes_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8701",
      "target_section": "section-2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "52a57bf8d8863393",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 196,
      "quote": "For identities established externally, an obfuscated_ticket_age of 0 SHOULD be used, and servers MUST ignore the value.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_psk_offered_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "2a8a9692cd54325c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 379,
      "quote": "In addition, in its updated ClientHello, the client SHOULD NOT offer any pre-shared keys associated with a hash other than that of the selected cipher suite.  This allows the client to avoid having to compute partial hash transcripts for multiple hashes in the second ClientHello.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_psk_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "2d51fd94f8c17b64",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 73,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST send the quic_transport_parameters extension; endpoints that receive ClientHello or EncryptedExtensions messages without the quic_transport_parameters extension MUST close the connection with an error of type 0x016d (equivalent to a fatal TLS missing_extension alert",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_quic_transport_params_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "8.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "31360b2a87a99170",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 833,
      "quote": "If the original session used the \"extended_master_secret\" extension but the new ClientHello does not contain it, the server MUST abort the abbreviated handshake.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_resume_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "5fd67c025699cb20",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 846,
      "quote": "If the original session did not use the \"extended_master_secret\" extension but the new ClientHello contains the extension, then the server MUST NOT perform the abbreviated handshake.  Instead, it SHOULD continue with a full handshake (as described in Section 5.2) to negotiate a new session.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_resume_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "1b74529887b5d528",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1274,
      "quote": "Clients MUST NOT cache tickets for longer than 7 days, regardless of the ticket_lifetime, and MAY delete tickets earlier based on local policy.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_resume_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "582a5283db5e954a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 531,
      "quote": "If the original session used the \"extended_master_secret\" extension but the new ClientHello does not contain it, the server MUST abort the abbreviated handshake.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_self_talk_session_id_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "f8722ffd14543c06",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 584,
      "quote": "If the original session did not use the \"extended_master_secret\" extension but the new ClientHello contains the extension, then the server MUST NOT perform the abbreviated handshake.  Instead, it SHOULD continue with a full handshake (as described in Section 5.2) to negotiate a new session.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_self_talk_session_id_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "5cc49a157e83595c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 172,
      "quote": "A server which receives an \"early_data\" extension MUST behave in one of three ways:",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_early_data_indication_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "41710ca7fa823729",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 177,
      "quote": "-  Return its own \"early_data\" extension in EncryptedExtensions, indicating that it intends to process the early data.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_early_data_indication_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "98be7f7531d73cc1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 212,
      "quote": "A server which receives an \"early_data\" extension MUST behave in one of three ways: -  Ignore the extension and return a regular 1-RTT response.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_early_data_indication_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e89eecfd6f29f577",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 247,
      "quote": "A server which receives an \"early_data\" extension MUST behave in one of three ways:",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_early_data_indication_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "583a184c20dbda8d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 252,
      "quote": "-  Request that the client send another ClientHello by responding with a HelloRetryRequest.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_early_data_indication_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "17eee8a6df166de2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 554,
      "quote": "Clients MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert if the HelloRetryRequest would not result in any change in the ClientHello.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_hello_retry_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "c745ab8ce13d2b6e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 569,
      "quote": "and (2) the selected_group field does not correspond to a group which was provided in the \"key_share\" extension in the original ClientHello.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_hello_retry_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.2.8",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "cecdd217958e1a03",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 608,
      "quote": "A client that attempts to send 0-RTT data MUST fail a connection if it receives a ServerHello with TLS 1.2 or older.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_hello_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "055d27e3d4e260d6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 75,
      "quote": "Similarly, if a client receives a maximum fragment length negotiation response that differs from the length it requested, it MUST also abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_max_frag_len_extension_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6066",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "1e57bd19f7174cc7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "PRK (32 octets):  7d f2 35 f2 03 1d 2a 05 12 87 d0 2b 02 41 b0 bf da f8 6c c8 56 23 1f 2d 5a ba 46 c4 34 ec 19 6c",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_new_session_ticket_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8448",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7ee7a9f11dec1428",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 186,
      "quote": "The server MUST generate a fresh value for each ticket it sends.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_new_session_ticket_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "ef70f7add62f3037",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 325,
      "quote": "Servers MUST NOT use any value greater than 604800 seconds (7 days).",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_new_session_ticket_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "0a0450435f7b9587",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 402,
      "quote": "expanded (32 octets):  4e cd 0e b6 ec 3b 4d 87 f5 d6 02 8f 92 2c a4 c5 85 1a 27 7f d4 13 11 c9 e6 2d 2c 94 92 e1 c4 f3",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_new_session_ticket_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8448",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "03c7072fde6e7aa3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 569,
      "quote": "NewSessionTicket (205 octets):  04 00 00 c9 00 00 00 1e fa d6 aa c5 02 00 00 00 b2 2c 03 5d 82 93 59 ee 5f f7 af 4e c9 00 00 00 00 26 2a 64 94 dc 48 6d 2c 8a 34 cb 33 fa 90 bf 1b 00 70 ad 3c 49 88 83 c9 36 7c 09 a2 be 78 5a bc 55 cd 22 60 97 a3 a9 82 11 72 83 f8 2a 03 a1 43 ef d3 ff 5d d3 6d 64 e8 61 be 7f d6 1d 28 27 db 27 9c ce 14 50 77 d4 54 a3 66 4d 4e 6d a4 d2 9e e0 37 25 a6 a4 da fc d0 fc 67 d2 ae a7 05 29 51 3e 3d a2 67 7f a5 90 6c 5b 3f 7d 8f 92 f2 28 bd a4 0d da 72 14 70 f9 fb f2 97 b5 ae a6 17 64 6f ac 5c 03 27 2e 97 07 27 c6 21 a7 91 41 ef 5f 7d e6 50 5e 5b fb c3 88 e9 33 43 69 40 93 93 4a e4 d3 57 00 08 00 2a 00 04 00 00 04 00",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_new_session_ticket_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8448",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f1ca51e161bfa844",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 748,
      "quote": "The value of zero indicates that the ticket should be discarded immediately.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_new_session_ticket_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "0bf9651f174e9745",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 774,
      "quote": "Servers MUST NOT use any value greater than 604800 seconds (7 days).",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_new_session_ticket_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "8d74fd2afd944bd7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 834,
      "quote": "If the server determines that it does not want to include a ticket after it has included the SessionTicket extension in the ServerHello, then it sends a zero-length ticket in the NewSessionTicket handshake message.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_new_session_ticket_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5077",
      "target_section": "section-3.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "aeae97bfaa9c8913",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1021,
      "quote": "Note that in principle it is possible to continue issuing new tickets which indefinitely extend the lifetime of the keying material originally derived from an initial non-PSK handshake (which was most likely tied to the peer's certificate). It is RECOMMENDED that implementations place limits on the total lifetime of such keying material; these limits should take into account the lifetime of the peer's certificate, the likelihood of intervening revocation, and the time since the peer's online CertificateVerify signature.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_new_session_ticket_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "b359b4efd9578506",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "o  If the secure_renegotiation flag is set to TRUE, the server MUST include an empty \"renegotiation_info\" extension in the ServerHello message.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_renegotiation_info_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.6",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "3c6e004713d93f76",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 99,
      "quote": "In order to enable clients to probe, even servers that do not support renegotiation MUST implement the minimal version of the extension described in this document for initial handshakes, thus signaling that they have been upgraded.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_renegotiation_info_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "4.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "dd572bdb15f4c247",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 131,
      "quote": "Clients that support SSLv3 and offer secure renegotiation (either via SCSV or \"renegotiation_info\") MUST accept the \"renegotiation_info\" extension from the server, even if the server version is {0x03, 0x00}, and behave as described in this specification.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_renegotiation_info_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "4.5",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "96680edb95e16b70",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 187,
      "quote": "*  The client MUST then verify that the length of the \"renegotiated_connection\" field is zero, and if it is not, MUST abort the handshake (by sending a fatal handshake_failure alert).",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_renegotiation_info_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "3d1b9fc35fcb6e1d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 212,
      "quote": "*  If the extension is not present, the server does not support secure renegotiation; set secure_renegotiation flag to FALSE.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_renegotiation_info_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "e379e0ee9f032739",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 227,
      "quote": "o  When a ServerHello is received, the client MUST verify that the \"renegotiation_info\" extension is present; if it is not, the client MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_renegotiation_info_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.5",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "2adeae113bede334",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 244,
      "quote": "o  The client MUST then verify that the first half of the \"renegotiated_connection\" field is equal to the saved client_verify_data value, and the second half is equal to the saved server_verify_data value.  If they are not, the client MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_renegotiation_info_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.5",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "c2003520e2fb07a7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 359,
      "quote": "o  The server MUST include a \"renegotiation_info\" extension containing the saved client_verify_data and server_verify_data in the ServerHello.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_renegotiation_info_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.7",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "4ffd49d04997c13d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 407,
      "quote": "o  When a ServerHello is received, the client MUST check if it includes the \"renegotiation_info\" extension:",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_renegotiation_info_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "9fe0370090e91461",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 458,
      "quote": "Clients that support SSLv3 and offer secure renegotiation (either via SCSV or \"renegotiation_info\") MUST accept the \"renegotiation_info\" extension from the server, even if the server version is {0x03, 0x00}, and behave as described in this specification.  TLS servers that support secure renegotiation and support SSLv3 MUST accept SCSV or the \"renegotiation_info\" extension and respond as described in this specification even if the offered client version is {0x03, 0x00}.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_server_renegotiation_info_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "4.5",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
