    {
      "id": "7b52476f1ffcab9d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 649,
      "quote": "Field measurements [Ben17a] [Ben17b] [Res17a] [Res17b] have found that a significant number of middleboxes misbehave when a TLS client/server pair negotiates TLS 1.3.  Implementations can increase the chance of making connections through those middleboxes by making the TLS 1.3 handshake look more like a TLS 1.2 handshake:",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_tls13_handshake_state_machine_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "0a16a051daa825e2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 659,
      "quote": "If not offering early data, the client sends a dummy change_cipher_spec record (see the third paragraph of Section 5) immediately before its second flight.  This may either be before its second ClientHello or before its encrypted handshake flight.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_tls13_handshake_state_machine_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "d51bf5e4dec57307",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 698,
      "quote": "If offering early data, the record is placed immediately after the first ClientHello.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_tls13_handshake_state_machine_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "3937ff190bb4e94b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 720,
      "quote": "The server sends a dummy change_cipher_spec record immediately after its first handshake message.  This may either be after a ServerHello or a HelloRetryRequest.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_tls13_handshake_state_machine_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
