    {
      "id": "d2cbf58231865483",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 152,
      "quote": "When a full TLS handshake takes place, we define session_hash = Hash(handshake_messages) where \"handshake_messages\" refers to all handshake messages sent or received, starting at the ClientHello up to and including the ClientKeyExchange message, including the type and length fields of the handshake messages.",
      "source": "tests/unit/s2n_tls_prf_test.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Extension ignored when received - No customer use case",
      "id": "5cfe1b95c33ab976",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 112,
      "quote": "The \"certificate_authorities\" extension is used to indicate the certificate authorities (CAs) which an endpoint supports and which SHOULD be used by the receiving endpoint to guide certificate selection.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_cert_authorities.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "111c977248e6ff4d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 66,
      "quote": "struct { CertificateStatusType status_type; select (status_type) { case ocsp: OCSPResponse; } response; } CertificateStatus; opaque OCSPResponse<1..2^24-1>; An \"ocsp_response\" contains a complete, DER-encoded OCSP response (using the ASN.1 type OCSPResponse defined in [RFC2560]).  Only one OCSP response may be sent.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_cert_status.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6066",
      "target_section": "section-8",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5db26ee75711b9d1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 21,
      "quote": "When sending the new ClientHello, the client MUST copy the contents of the extension received in the HelloRetryRequest into a \"cookie\" extension in the new ClientHello.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_cookie.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "1063b342126a4e03",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 34,
      "quote": "struct { opaque cookie<1..2^16-1>; } Cookie;",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_cookie.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9ae84888c3932d79",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 28,
      "quote": "-  If not offering early data, the client sends a dummy change_cipher_spec record (see the third paragraph of Section 5) immediately before its second flight.  This may either be before its second ClientHello or before its encrypted handshake flight. If offering early data, the record is placed immediately after the first ClientHello.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_early_data_indication.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ee57a6f60560d9fb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 101,
      "quote": "A client MUST NOT include the \"early_data\" extension in its followup ClientHello.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_early_data_indication.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "dda48e86ba8cccf9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 107,
      "quote": "When a PSK is used and early data is allowed for that PSK, the client can send Application Data in its first flight of messages.  If the client opts to do so, it MUST supply both the \"pre_shared_key\" and \"early_data\" extensions.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_early_data_indication.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d41a405d89f0400f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 127,
      "quote": "The \"extension_data\" field of this extension contains an \"EarlyDataIndication\" value. struct {} Empty; struct { select (Handshake.msg_type) {",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_early_data_indication.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d18e0833ec8b1bd1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 136,
      "quote": "case client_hello:         Empty;",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_early_data_indication.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cf37298fbb33f2f2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 139,
      "quote": "}; } EarlyDataIndication;",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_early_data_indication.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "01e5a6662ef6af1c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 164,
      "quote": "A client MUST NOT include the \"early_data\" extension in its followup ClientHello.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_early_data_indication.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "54142eccdb97e136",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 27,
      "quote": "This document defines a new TLS extension, \"extended_master_secret\" (with extension type 0x0017), which is used to signal both client and server to use the extended master secret computation.  The \"extension_data\" field of this extension is empty.  Thus, the entire encoding of the extension is 00 17 00 00 (in hexadecimal.)",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_ems.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f3b3b908115e54ce",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "When offering an abbreviated handshake, the client MUST send the \"extended_master_secret\" extension in its ClientHello.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_ems.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b2e8aaad57056ae3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 88,
      "quote": "Otherwise, when sending the new ClientHello, the client MUST replace the original \"key_share\" extension with one containing only a new KeyShareEntry for the group indicated in the selected_group field of the triggering HelloRetryRequest.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_key_share.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.2.8",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "666d61c9917d37c1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 172,
      "quote": "Otherwise, when sending the new ClientHello, the client MUST replace the original \"key_share\" extension with one containing only a new KeyShareEntry for the group indicated in the selected_group field of the triggering HelloRetryRequest.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_key_share.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.2.8",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f0f918fba3b61161",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 446,
      "quote": "If the server selects an (EC)DHE group and the client did not offer a compatible \"key_share\" extension in the initial ClientHello, the server MUST respond with a HelloRetryRequest (Section 4.1.4) message.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_key_share.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For compatibility, we choose to ignore malformed extensions if they are optional",
      "id": "7078e9c71a305094",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 58,
      "quote": "If a server receives a maximum fragment length negotiation request for a value other than the allowed values, it MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_max_frag_len.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6066",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8248f030feae8562",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 70,
      "quote": "Once a maximum fragment length other than 2^14 has been successfully negotiated, the client and server MUST immediately begin fragmenting messages (including handshake messages) to ensure that no fragment larger than the negotiated length is sent.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_max_frag_len.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6066",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "003ce408b054b0aa",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 57,
      "quote": "When a PSK is used and early data is allowed for that PSK, the client can send Application Data in its first flight of messages.  If the client opts to do so, it MUST supply both the \"pre_shared_key\" and \"early_data\" extensions.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_psk.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5e3abede99d35ef8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 95,
      "quote": "The \"obfuscated_ticket_age\" field of each PskIdentity contains an obfuscated version of the ticket age formed by taking the age in milliseconds and adding the \"ticket_age_add\" value that was included with the ticket (see Section 4.6.1), modulo 2^32.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_psk.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6fd463dd3b01d109",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 108,
      "quote": "For identities established externally, an obfuscated_ticket_age of 0 SHOULD be used,",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_psk.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "753d152e32e5fb29",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 153,
      "quote": "In addition, in its updated ClientHello, the client SHOULD NOT offer any pre-shared keys associated with a hash other than that of the selected cipher suite.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_psk.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7daab9e552dd6150",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 361,
      "quote": "The \"pre_shared_key\" extension MUST be the last extension in the ClientHello (this facilitates implementation as described below). Servers MUST check that it is the last extension and otherwise fail the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_psk.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "20f54c35022a3caf",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 375,
      "quote": "If clients offer \"pre_shared_key\" without a \"psk_key_exchange_modes\" extension, servers MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_psk.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.9",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "1dc5526115a9d6f2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 402,
      "quote": "If no acceptable PSKs are found, the server SHOULD perform a non-PSK handshake if possible.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_psk.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cba0c033cd3db8e2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 411,
      "quote": "Prior to accepting PSK key establishment, the server MUST validate the corresponding binder value (see Section 4.2.11.2 below).  If this value is not present or does not validate, the server MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_psk.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "98e12e73d09e38ab",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 39,
      "quote": "o  The client MUST include the \"renegotiation_info\" extension in the ClientHello",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3370faddc4c7ddb6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 49,
      "quote": "o  The client MUST include the \"renegotiation_info\" extension in the ClientHello, containing the saved client_verify_data.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "85adbeb5e08f996c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 58,
      "quote": "This text applies if the connection's \"secure_renegotiation\" flag is set to TRUE (if it is set to FALSE, see Section 4.2).",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a46ce4748acb0c9d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 73,
      "quote": "o  The server MUST check if the \"renegotiation_info\" extension is included in the ClientHello.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "03b67ddd687b28be",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 78,
      "quote": "TLS servers that support secure renegotiation and support SSLv3 MUST accept SCSV or the \"renegotiation_info\" extension and respond as described in this specification even if the offered client version is {0x03, 0x00}.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "4.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "4c0f334c5aa1a8c5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 86,
      "quote": "The server MUST then verify that the length of the \"renegotiated_connection\" field is zero, and if it is not, MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ad4216bc2993b40f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 97,
      "quote": "If the extension is present, set secure_renegotiation flag to TRUE.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8b19c17ca36ab8c0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 115,
      "quote": "This text applies if the connection's \"secure_renegotiation\" flag is set to TRUE (if it is set to FALSE, see Section 4.4).",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.7",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "088d7f20abb21fca",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 122,
      "quote": "o  The server MUST verify that the value of the \"renegotiated_connection\" field is equal to the saved client_verify_data value; if it is not, the server MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.7",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8e3066315172e7a9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 165,
      "quote": "This text applies if the connection's \"secure_renegotiation\" flag is set to TRUE (if it is set to FALSE, see Section 4.4).",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.7",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "115c98a0b6be9555",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 172,
      "quote": "o  The server MUST verify that the \"renegotiation_info\" extension is present; if it is not, the server MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.7",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "61f896de291e5026",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 179,
      "quote": "o  If neither the TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV SCSV nor the \"renegotiation_info\" extension was included, set the secure_renegotiation flag to FALSE.  In this case, some servers may want to terminate the handshake instead of continuing",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The client hello legacy version is used for version selection on TLS 1.2 servers for backwards compatibility",
      "id": "942990c83d4c8342",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 147,
      "quote": "If this extension is present in the ClientHello, servers MUST NOT use the ClientHello.legacy_version value for version negotiation and MUST use only the \"supported_versions\" extension to determine client preferences.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_client_supported_versions.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Incorrect implementations exist in the wild. Skipping validation.",
      "id": "253b4914e685b146",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 70,
      "quote": "If the client sends the extension and the extension does not contain the uncompressed point format, and the client has used the Supported Groups extension to indicate support for any of the curves defined in this specification, then the server MUST abort the handshake and return an illegal_parameter alert.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_ec_point_format.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8422",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Incorrect implementations exist in the wild. Ignoring instead.",
      "id": "375c6eb7390322b7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 106,
      "quote": "If an implementation receives an extension which it recognizes and which is not specified for the message in which it appears, it MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_extension_list.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5532cacbe0753ea4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 138,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST NOT send extension responses if the remote endpoint did not send the corresponding extension requests, with the exception of the \"cookie\" extension in the HelloRetryRequest.  Upon receiving such an extension, an endpoint MUST abort the handshake with an \"unsupported_extension\" alert.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_extension_type.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8e36c618cf156bfc",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 145,
      "quote": "If the original session did not use the \"extended_master_secret\" extension but the new ServerHello contains the extension, the client MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_extension_type.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "20af75f7ff46ba2e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 150,
      "quote": "As with the ServerHello, a HelloRetryRequest MUST NOT contain any extensions that were not first offered by the client in its ClientHello, with the exception of optionally the \"cookie\" (see Section 4.2.2) extension.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_extension_type.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a351680ab895ce91",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 102,
      "quote": "The HelloRetryRequest extensions defined in this specification are: -  supported_versions (see Section 4.2.1) -  cookie (see Section 4.2.2) -  key_share (see Section 4.2.8)",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_extension_type_lists.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Currently only supported for servers -- no client use case",
      "id": "a1942acdd494e9ac",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 136,
      "quote": "The client MAY send the \"certificate_authorities\" extension in the ClientHello message.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_extension_type_lists.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d2f5765f40a6e11d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 142,
      "quote": "The server MAY send it in the CertificateRequest message.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_extension_type_lists.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "035ef14d103ff4a6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 28,
      "quote": "For the same reasons, after a handshake has been performed for a given connection, renegotiations on the same connection MUST NOT include the \"next_protocol_negotiation\" extension.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_npn.c",
      "target_path": "https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/id/draft-agl-tls-nextprotoneg-03",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "86243021998911af",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 85,
      "quote": "The \"extension_data\" field of a \"next_protocol_negotiation\" extension in a \"ServerHello\" contains an optional list of protocols advertised by the server.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_npn.c",
      "target_path": "https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/id/draft-agl-tls-nextprotoneg-03",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b3ee68b39358c442",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 95,
      "quote": "In the event that the client doesn't support any of server's protocols, or the server doesn't advertise any, it SHOULD select the first protocol that it supports.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_npn.c",
      "target_path": "https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/id/draft-agl-tls-nextprotoneg-03",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f1f9c78beb600deb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 33,
      "quote": "The \"extension_data\" field of this extension contains an \"EarlyDataIndication\" value. struct {} Empty; struct { select (Handshake.msg_type) { case new_session_ticket:   uint32 max_early_data_size;",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_nst_early_data_indication.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "18b3600491b5f0ea",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 43,
      "quote": "}; } EarlyDataIndication;",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_nst_early_data_indication.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e19b9a842772ba17",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "Servers MUST NOT select a key exchange mode that is not listed by the client.  This extension also restricts the modes for use with PSK resumption.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_psk_key_exchange_modes.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.9",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8c30e83563ff74ff",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 35,
      "quote": "A server MAY request that a client present an OCSP response with its certificate by sending an empty \"status_request\" extension in its CertificateRequest message.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_cert_status_request.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.4.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9650e4559b097dfd",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 21,
      "quote": "Cookies serve two primary purposes: -  Allowing the server to force the client to demonstrate reachability at their apparent network address (thus providing a measure of DoS protection).  This is primarily useful for non-connection-oriented transports (see [RFC6347] for an example of this). -  Allowing the server to offload state to the client, thus allowing it to send a HelloRetryRequest without storing any state.  The server can do this by storing the hash of the ClientHello in the HelloRetryRequest cookie (protected with some suitable integrity protection algorithm). When sending a HelloRetryRequest, the server MAY provide a \"cookie\" extension to the client (this is an exception to the usual rule that the only extensions that may be sent are those that appear in the ClientHello).",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_cookie.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "eb7e3a3357f34fc3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 52,
      "quote": "When sending the new ClientHello, the client MUST copy the contents of the extension received in the HelloRetryRequest into a \"cookie\" extension in the new ClientHello.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_cookie.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "479d5159a6f2c6fc",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 29,
      "quote": "A server which receives an \"early_data\" extension MUST behave in one of three ways: -  Ignore the extension and return a regular 1-RTT response.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_early_data_indication.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6d498e8a5425d9e8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "The \"extension_data\" field of this extension contains an \"EarlyDataIndication\" value. struct {} Empty; struct { select (Handshake.msg_type) {",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_early_data_indication.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b040a0ab047d751e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "case encrypted_extensions: Empty; }; } EarlyDataIndication;",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_early_data_indication.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3d6575bfdefd4906",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 63,
      "quote": "A server which receives an \"early_data\" extension MUST behave in one of three ways:",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_early_data_indication.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "86de1a31cfe883aa",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 67,
      "quote": "-  Return its own \"early_data\" extension in EncryptedExtensions, indicating that it intends to process the early data.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_early_data_indication.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "51c14eae89f530c7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 80,
      "quote": "If any of these checks fail, the server MUST NOT respond with the extension",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_early_data_indication.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "feccffbe05d89bad",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 28,
      "quote": "This document defines a new TLS extension, \"extended_master_secret\" (with extension type 0x0017), which is used to signal both client and server to use the extended master secret computation.  The \"extension_data\" field of this extension is empty.  Thus, the entire encoding of the extension is 00 17 00 00 (in hexadecimal.)",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_ems.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d0066b72b8d36def",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 66,
      "quote": "If the original session used the extension but the new ServerHello does not contain the extension, the client MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_ems.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "38b766fc7ea56fde",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 261,
      "quote": "If using (EC)DHE key establishment and a HelloRetryRequest containing a \"key_share\" extension was received by the client, the client MUST verify that the selected NamedGroup in the ServerHello is the same as that in the HelloRetryRequest. If this check fails, the client MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_key_share.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.2.8",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "fc9f7e433457259f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 61,
      "quote": "Similarly, if a client receives a maximum fragment length negotiation response that differs from the length it requested, it MUST also abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_max_fragment_length.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6066",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "265ee75d16fda59d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 70,
      "quote": "Once a maximum fragment length other than 2^14 has been successfully negotiated, the client and server MUST immediately begin fragmenting messages (including handshake messages) to ensure that no fragment larger than the negotiated length is sent.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_max_fragment_length.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6066",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "82db7560ff84ec18",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 29,
      "quote": "In order to enable clients to probe, even servers that do not support renegotiation MUST implement the minimal version of the extension described in this document for initial handshakes, thus signaling that they have been upgraded.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "4.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "15c6e5901c6a6062",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 49,
      "quote": "Note that sending a \"renegotiation_info\" extension in response to a ClientHello containing only the SCSV is an explicit exception to the prohibition in RFC 5246, Section 7.4.1.4, on the server sending unsolicited extensions and is only allowed because the client is signaling its willingness to receive the extension via the TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV SCSV.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "85f041e24eb46530",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 65,
      "quote": "o  If the secure_renegotiation flag is set to TRUE, the server MUST include an empty \"renegotiation_info\" extension in the ServerHello message.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8f011f4e7c4db444",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 76,
      "quote": "o  If the secure_renegotiation flag is set to TRUE, the server MUST include an empty \"renegotiation_info\" extension in the ServerHello message.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "55fb0dc70059d8cb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 97,
      "quote": "This text applies if the connection's \"secure_renegotiation\" flag is set to TRUE (if it is set to FALSE, see Section 4.4).",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.7",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3e54c106c9ef3a32",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 104,
      "quote": "o  The server MUST include a \"renegotiation_info\" extension containing the saved client_verify_data and server_verify_data in the ServerHello.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.7",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0a84dfbaa0314b15",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 129,
      "quote": "o  When a ServerHello is received, the client MUST check if it includes the \"renegotiation_info\" extension:",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "262cb940284de6ff",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 138,
      "quote": "*  The client MUST then verify that the length of the \"renegotiated_connection\" field is zero, and if it is not, MUST abort the handshake (by sending a fatal handshake_failure alert).",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "4a7c3d702b68da63",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 149,
      "quote": "*  If the extension is present, set the secure_renegotiation flag to TRUE.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f560be8b8fc4dac3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 163,
      "quote": "This text applies if the connection's \"secure_renegotiation\" flag is set to TRUE (if it is set to FALSE, see Section 4.2).",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "95ee8c9b7bd1c833",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 170,
      "quote": "o  The client MUST then verify that the first half of the \"renegotiated_connection\" field is equal to the saved client_verify_data value, and the second half is equal to the saved server_verify_data value.  If they are not, the client MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b0de584713655056",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 197,
      "quote": "Clients that support SSLv3 and offer secure renegotiation (either via SCSV or \"renegotiation_info\") MUST accept the \"renegotiation_info\" extension from the server, even if the server version is {0x03, 0x00}, and behave as described in this specification.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "4.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "52ee1c6edfb7cbba",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 218,
      "quote": "o  When a ServerHello is received, the client MUST verify that the \"renegotiation_info\" extension is present; if it is not, the client MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "30c887659afbac0d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 226,
      "quote": "*  If the extension is not present, the server does not support secure renegotiation; set secure_renegotiation flag to FALSE. In this case, some clients may want to terminate the handshake instead of continuing; see Section 4.1 for discussion.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Avoid interoperability problems",
      "id": "dc406c5f5841a5dd",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 235,
      "quote": "If clients wish to ensure that such attacks are impossible, they need to terminate the connection immediately upon failure to receive the extension without completing the handshake.  Such clients MUST generate a fatal \"handshake_failure\" alert prior to terminating the connection.  However, it is expected that many TLS servers that do not support renegotiation (and thus are not vulnerable) will not support this extension either, so in general, clients that implement this behavior will encounter interoperability problems.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_renegotiation_info.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "4.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "170136f2148e6adf",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 74,
      "quote": "The value of selected_version in the HelloRetryRequest \"supported_versions\" extension MUST be retained in the ServerHello, and a client MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert if the value changes.",
      "source": "tls/extensions/s2n_server_supported_versions.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "aa184e06e785fb4f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 63,
      "quote": "opaque_type:  The outer opaque_type field of a TLSCiphertext record is always set to the value 23 (application_data) for outward compatibility with middleboxes accustomed to parsing previous versions of TLS.  The actual content type of the record is found in TLSInnerPlaintext.type after decryption.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_aead.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d89b9417630633f0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 73,
      "quote": "legacy_record_version:  The legacy_record_version field is always 0x0303.  TLS 1.3 TLSCiphertexts are not generated until after TLS 1.3 has been negotiated, so there are no historical compatibility concerns where other values might be received.  Note that the handshake protocol, including the ClientHello and ServerHello messages, authenticates the protocol version, so this value is redundant.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_aead.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "66738e162a461ed8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 86,
      "quote": "length:  The length (in bytes) of the following TLSCiphertext.encrypted_record, which is the sum of the lengths of the content and the padding, plus one for the inner content type, plus any expansion added by the AEAD algorithm.  The length MUST NOT exceed 2^14 + 256 bytes.  An endpoint that receives a record that exceeds this length MUST terminate the connection with a \"record_overflow\" alert.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_aead.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a6bcf259c2ab4444",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 59,
      "quote": "Note: later in Section 3, \"abort the handshake\" is used as shorthand for \"send a fatal handshake_failure alert and terminate the connection\".",
      "source": "tls/s2n_alerts.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "89238f15801c4117",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 155,
      "quote": "MUST be treated as error alerts when received regardless of the AlertLevel in the message.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_alerts.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "12c3305363cb9cde",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 240,
      "quote": "Unknown Alert types MUST be treated as error alerts.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_alerts.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2a8ac6ecb268c005",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 276,
      "quote": "SSLv3 does not define the \"no_renegotiation\" alert (and does not offer a way to indicate a refusal to renegotiate at a \"warning\" level).  SSLv3 clients that refuse renegotiation SHOULD use a fatal handshake_failure alert.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_alerts.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "4.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Specific alerts could expose a side-channel attack vector.",
      "id": "167f228069a4e37b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 300,
      "quote": "The phrases \"terminate the connection with an X alert\" and \"abort the handshake with an X alert\" mean that the implementation MUST send alert X if it sends any alert.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_alerts.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9165055a648ca402",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 27,
      "quote": "enum { close_notify(0), unexpected_message(10), bad_record_mac(20), record_overflow(22), handshake_failure(40),",
      "source": "tls/s2n_alerts.h",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "01ce5bbcfcaa2cae",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "bad_certificate(42), unsupported_certificate(43), certificate_revoked(44), certificate_expired(45), certificate_unknown(46),",
      "source": "tls/s2n_alerts.h",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6786e3f9314bbb4c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "illegal_parameter(47), unknown_ca(48), access_denied(49), decode_error(50), decrypt_error(51),",
      "source": "tls/s2n_alerts.h",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a7150a2b6e8ea7ce",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 67,
      "quote": "protocol_version(70), insufficient_security(71), internal_error(80), inappropriate_fallback(86), user_canceled(90),",
      "source": "tls/s2n_alerts.h",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f0d2124756417608",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 80,
      "quote": "no_renegotiation(100),",
      "source": "tls/s2n_alerts.h",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0731d012469272fe",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 85,
      "quote": "missing_extension(109), unsupported_extension(110), unrecognized_name(112), bad_certificate_status_response(113), unknown_psk_identity(115),",
      "source": "tls/s2n_alerts.h",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "eb01d2c0dfb658a4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 98,
      "quote": "certificate_required(116), no_application_protocol(120), (255) } AlertDescription;",
      "source": "tls/s2n_alerts.h",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "67ee36b9a8dcf180",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 90,
      "quote": "CNSA (D)TLS connections MUST use secp384r1",
      "source": "tls/s2n_certificate_keys.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9151",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2a98b9560754241a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 96,
      "quote": "CNSA specifies a minimum modulus size of 3072 bits; however, only two modulus sizes (3072 bits and 4096 bits) are supported by this profile.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_certificate_keys.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9151",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6dfce7eafbecaf5d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1138,
      "quote": "A client which receives a cipher suite that was not offered MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_cipher_suites.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0afb153c9ad2fcbb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1143,
      "quote": "A client which receives a cipher suite that was not offered MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_cipher_suites.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3867219f122d4027",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1147,
      "quote": "Upon receipt of a HelloRetryRequest, the client MUST check the legacy_version, legacy_session_id_echo, cipher_suite",
      "source": "tls/s2n_cipher_suites.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "de5fac7d471d8d96",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1164,
      "quote": "that the server selected a cipher suite indicating a Hash associated with the PSK",
      "source": "tls/s2n_cipher_suites.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "57df50bf762de5f5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1174,
      "quote": "Upon receiving the ServerHello, clients MUST check that the cipher suite supplied in the ServerHello is the same as that in the HelloRetryRequest and otherwise abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_cipher_suites.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e3cbe3d6b92d0f23",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1257,
      "quote": "o  When a ClientHello is received, the server MUST verify that it does not contain the TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV SCSV.  If the SCSV is present, the server MUST abort the handshake.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_cipher_suites.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.7",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3bdcc57a5b805b7c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1265,
      "quote": "o  When a ClientHello is received, the server MUST check if it includes the TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV SCSV.  If it does, set the secure_renegotiation flag to TRUE.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_cipher_suites.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "1d6d6c925f4b3a77",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1330,
      "quote": "The server MUST ensure that it selects a compatible PSK (if any) and cipher suite.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_cipher_suites.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a4090da2657a18fd",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 88,
      "quote": "A server SHOULD treat the receipt of a TLS ClientHello with a non-empty legacy_session_id field as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_client_hello.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cf0b8179ef45bead",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 228,
      "quote": "The client will also send a ClientHello when the server has responded to its ClientHello with a HelloRetryRequest.  In that case, the client MUST send the same ClientHello without modification, except as follows:",
      "source": "tls/s2n_client_hello.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "4d693aade8696fcd",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 295,
      "quote": "-  If a \"key_share\" extension was supplied in the HelloRetryRequest, replacing the list of shares with a list containing a single KeyShareEntry from the indicated group.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_client_hello.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d4a4b19c354f7d22",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 304,
      "quote": "-  Removing the \"early_data\" extension (Section 4.2.10) if one was present.  Early data is not permitted after a HelloRetryRequest.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_client_hello.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e985629df8b99073",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 312,
      "quote": "-  Including a \"cookie\" extension if one was provided in the HelloRetryRequest.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_client_hello.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2c0825122fe6a680",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 320,
      "quote": "-  Updating the \"pre_shared_key\" extension if present by recomputing the \"obfuscated_ticket_age\" and binder values and (optionally) removing any PSKs which are incompatible with the server's indicated cipher suite.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_client_hello.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "95204dbcf3ee49d6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 550,
      "quote": "A client that proposes ECC cipher suites may choose not to include these extensions. In this case, the server is free to choose any one of the elliptic curves or point formats listed in Section 5.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_client_hello.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "683f6972634e6954",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 603,
      "quote": "Servers MUST ensure that they negotiate the same cipher suite when receiving a conformant updated ClientHello (if the server selects the cipher suite as the first step in the negotiation, then this will happen automatically).",
      "source": "tls/s2n_client_hello.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b67637c330398b96",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 766,
      "quote": "o  The client MUST include either an empty \"renegotiation_info\" extension, or the TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV signaling cipher suite value in the ClientHello.  Including both is NOT RECOMMENDED.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_client_hello.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6451a595e7cd6d86",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 775,
      "quote": "The SCSV MUST NOT be included.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_client_hello.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "3.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "db2d1c8eef4e200f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 29,
      "quote": "The HelloRequest message MAY be sent by the server at any time.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_client_hello_request.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "42b600441d3af609",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "This text applies if the connection's \"secure_renegotiation\" flag is set to FALSE. It is possible that un-upgraded servers will request that the client renegotiate.  It is RECOMMENDED that clients refuse this renegotiation request.  Clients that do so MUST respond to such requests with a \"no_renegotiation\" alert (RFC 5246 requires this alert to be at the \"warning\" level).  It is possible that the apparently un-upgraded server is in fact an attacker who is then allowing the client to renegotiate with a different, legitimate, upgraded server.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_client_hello_request.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "696c112d6f38c83d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 74,
      "quote": "This message MAY be ignored by the client if it does not wish to renegotiate a session, or the client may, if it wishes, respond with a no_renegotiation alert.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_client_hello_request.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c4c1c0b2af8a140d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1153,
      "quote": "TLS implementations SHOULD provide a mechanism to disable and enable renegotiation.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_config.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5746",
      "target_section": "5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "64999a6af667a906",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1718,
      "quote": "Note that this is a change from versions of TLS prior to TLS 1.3 in which implementations were required to react to a \"close_notify\" by discarding pending writes and sending an immediate \"close_notify\" alert of their own.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_connection.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "eb63de8a0b50e570",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 67,
      "quote": "In order to accept early data, the server MUST have accepted a PSK cipher suite and selected the first key offered in the client's \"pre_shared_key\" extension.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_early_data.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b64b8bc781cb0dad",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 79,
      "quote": "In addition, it MUST verify that the following values are the same as those associated with the selected PSK: -  The TLS version number",
      "source": "tls/s2n_early_data.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c5d07dc50a26395d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 88,
      "quote": "-  The selected cipher suite",
      "source": "tls/s2n_early_data.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2e091b2d42793f99",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 93,
      "quote": "-  The selected ALPN [RFC7301] protocol, if any",
      "source": "tls/s2n_early_data.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "41702b44e5aea298",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 122,
      "quote": "If any of these checks fail, the server MUST NOT respond with the extension",
      "source": "tls/s2n_early_data.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "61a7188690056ad4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "If the client attempts a 0-RTT handshake but the server rejects it, the server will generally not have the 0-RTT record protection keys and must instead use trial decryption (either with the 1-RTT handshake keys or by looking for a cleartext ClientHello in the case of a HelloRetryRequest) to find the first non-0-RTT message.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_early_data_io.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "60732fbc1e3c1231",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 187,
      "quote": "The program needs to ignore GREASE values anywhere it sees them",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "details",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5385bb10184826b8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "2 character number of cipher suites",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "number-of-ciphers",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8c36e80d673257bb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 35,
      "quote": "Same as counting ciphers.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "number-of-extensions",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "032627b4f20f0a0e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "0x0304 = TLS 1.3 = “13” 0x0303 = TLS 1.2 = “12” 0x0302 = TLS 1.1 = “11” 0x0301 = TLS 1.0 = “10”",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "tls-and-dtls-version",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d396db7402aafcd2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 67,
      "quote": "0x0300 = SSL 3.0 = “s3” 0x0002 = SSL 2.0 = “s2”",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "tls-and-dtls-version",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "164922c7935d0830",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 76,
      "quote": "Unknown = “00”",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "tls-and-dtls-version",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a75401a5d03af1a4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 106,
      "quote": "If there are no ciphers in the sorted cipher list, then the value of JA4_b is set to `000000000000`",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "cipher-hash",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ceefb6ef08c828d5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 110,
      "quote": "If there are no extensions in the sorted extensions list, then the value of JA4_c is set to `000000000000`",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "extension-hash",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "466b5201bd75eeeb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 134,
      "quote": "2 character number of cipher suites, so if there’s 6 cipher suites in the hello packet, then the value should be “06”.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "number-of-ciphers",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a145d6da167dcaff",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 138,
      "quote": "Same as counting ciphers.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "number-of-extensions",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "efb70f2d1076feb8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 146,
      "quote": "If there’s > 99, which there should never be, then output “99”.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "number-of-ciphers",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e6173f283bb42973",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 149,
      "quote": "Same as counting ciphers.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "number-of-extensions",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d6508b4aa062b542",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 179,
      "quote": "Remember to ignore GREASE values.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "tls-and-dtls-version",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "802383dd889850fc",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 186,
      "quote": "If extension 0x002b exists (supported_versions), then the version is the highest value in the extension.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "tls-and-dtls-version",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "046a524e7751a648",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 201,
      "quote": "If the extension doesn’t exist, then the TLS version is the value of the Protocol Version.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "tls-and-dtls-version",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5bc02644018eaec0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 209,
      "quote": "Handshake version (located at the top of the packet) should be ignored.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "tls-and-dtls-version",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3fbe92df374e82d8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 245,
      "quote": "The first and last alphanumeric characters of the ALPN (Application-Layer Protocol Negotiation) first value.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "alpn-extension-value",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e8acdc2a10430706",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 258,
      "quote": "If there is no ALPN extension, no ALPN values, or the first ALPN value is empty, then we print \"00\" as the value in the fingerprint.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "alpn-extension-value",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e6268f51f579ed91",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 262,
      "quote": "If the first ALPN value is only a single character, then that character is treated as both the first and last character.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "alpn-extension-value",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "65b7519aac2a45bf",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 273,
      "quote": "If the first or last byte of the first ALPN is non-alphanumeric (meaning not `0x30-0x39`, `0x41-0x5A`, or `0x61-0x7A`), then we print the first and last characters of the hex representation of the first ALPN instead.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "alpn-extension-value",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "63e259757e8c82b4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 304,
      "quote": "If the protocol is QUIC then the first character of the fingerprint is “q”, if DTLS it is \"d\", else it is “t”.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "quic-and-dtls",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "1caee42acc35fd6e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 319,
      "quote": "If the SNI extension (0x0000) exists, then the destination of the connection is a domain, or “d” in the fingerprint. If the SNI does not exist, then the destination is an IP address, or “i”.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "sni",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3aec7426df9e3a9b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 350,
      "quote": "The list is created using the 4 character hex values of the ciphers, lower case, comma delimited, ignoring GREASE.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "cipher-hash",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5a230fd674f88a3b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 369,
      "quote": "Remember, ignore GREASE values. They don’t count.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "number-of-ciphers",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "70d1338120f79d4b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 394,
      "quote": "A 12 character truncated sha256 hash of the list of ciphers sorted in hex order, first 12 characters.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "cipher-hash",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "49ee677dee628fa8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 414,
      "quote": "The extension list is created using the 4 character hex values of the extensions, lower case, comma delimited, sorted (not in the order they appear).",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "extension-hash",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d73ef6bd3f6ba556",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 434,
      "quote": "Ignore GREASE.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "number-of-extensions",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "951b3edb09ad2840",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 443,
      "quote": "Ignore the SNI extension (0000) and the ALPN extension (0010) as we’ve already captured them in the _a_ section of the fingerprint.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "extension-hash",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "814b439c5af3e0a4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 447,
      "quote": "Include SNI and ALPN.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "number-of-extensions",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5ba08e50269a6b8b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 516,
      "quote": "A 12 character truncated sha256 hash of the list of extensions, sorted by hex value, followed by the list of signature algorithms, in the order that they appear (not sorted).",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "extension-hash",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d41b8ab1fbf40eed",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 532,
      "quote": "The signature algorithm hex values are then added to the end of the list in the order that they appear (not sorted) with an underscore delimiting the two lists.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "extension-hash",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "43462d4f498ed268",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 537,
      "quote": "If there are no signature algorithms in the hello packet, then the string ends without an underscore and is hashed.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "extension-hash",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "eb7c93e39417b472",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 553,
      "quote": "(QUIC=”q”, DTLS=\"d\", or Normal TLS=”t”) (2 character TLS version) (SNI=”d” or no SNI=”i”) (2 character count of ciphers) (2 character count of extensions) (first and last characters of first ALPN extension value) _ (sha256 hash of the list of cipher hex codes sorted in hex order, truncated to 12 characters) _ (sha256 hash of (the list of extension hex codes sorted in hex order)_(the list of signature algorithms), truncated to 12 characters) The end result is a fingerprint that looks like: t13d1516h2_8daaf6152771_b186095e22b6",
      "source": "tls/s2n_fingerprint_ja4.c",
      "target_path": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md",
      "target_section": "ja4-algorithm",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d4328fc5f9e64fe9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 921,
      "quote": "A server which receives an \"early_data\" extension MUST behave in one of three ways:",
      "source": "tls/s2n_handshake_io.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8b26772c23f988bd",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 925,
      "quote": "-  Request that the client send another ClientHello by responding with a HelloRetryRequest.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_handshake_io.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "06bd06a271587156",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 997,
      "quote": "If the original session used the \"extended_master_secret\" extension but the new ClientHello does not contain it, the server MUST abort the abbreviated handshake.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_handshake_io.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e656d577ace20d4b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1410,
      "quote": "If the client attempts a 0-RTT handshake but the server rejects it, the server will generally not have the 0-RTT record protection keys and must instead use trial decryption (either with the 1-RTT handshake keys or by looking for a cleartext ClientHello in the case of a HelloRetryRequest) to find the first non-0-RTT message. If the server chooses to accept the \"early_data\" extension, then it MUST comply with the same error-handling requirements specified for all records when processing early data records.  Specifically, if the server fails to decrypt a 0-RTT record following an accepted \"early_data\" extension, it MUST terminate the connection with a \"bad_record_mac\" alert as per Section 5.2.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_handshake_io.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c98799ffc6c9c911",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1521,
      "quote": "The one message that is not bound by these ordering rules is the HelloRequest message, which can be sent at any time, but which SHOULD be ignored by the client if it arrives in the middle of a handshake.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_handshake_io.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a5f6cf539d47a153",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 26,
      "quote": "The length of \"padding\" SHOULD be 32 - ((len(selected_protocol) + 2) % 32).",
      "source": "tls/s2n_next_protocol.c",
      "target_path": "https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/id/draft-agl-tls-nextprotoneg-03",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e0d5be612f4055ef",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "A client that receives a CertificateRequest message without having sent the \"post_handshake_auth\" extension MUST send an \"unexpected_message\" fatal alert.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_post_handshake.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "33d8ff0ca81341c6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 733,
      "quote": "When the extended master secret extension is negotiated in a full handshake, the \"master_secret\" is computed as master_secret = PRF(pre_master_secret, \"extended master secret\", session_hash) [0..47];",
      "source": "tls/s2n_prf.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "66990f61301b46c0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 65,
      "quote": "Empty strings MUST NOT be included and byte strings MUST NOT be truncated.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_protocol_preferences.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7301",
      "target_section": "section-3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "be81006627be1304",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 117,
      "quote": "Empty strings MUST NOT be included and byte strings MUST NOT be truncated.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_protocol_preferences.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7301",
      "target_section": "section-3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7256e0586fd2c0b5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 219,
      "quote": "For identities established externally, an obfuscated_ticket_age of 0 SHOULD be used, and servers MUST ignore the value.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_psk.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.11",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a598f3de17ec2f4b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 288,
      "quote": "For PSKs provisioned via NewSessionTicket, a server MUST validate that the ticket age for the selected PSK identity (computed by subtracting ticket_age_add from PskIdentity.obfuscated_ticket_age modulo 2^32) is within a small tolerance of the time since the ticket was issued (see Section 8).",
      "source": "tls/s2n_psk.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7f987f8f24219b7b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 499,
      "quote": "In addition, in its updated ClientHello, the client SHOULD NOT offer any pre-shared keys associated with a hash other than that of the selected cipher suite.  This allows the client to avoid having to compute partial hash transcripts for multiple hashes in the second ClientHello.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_psk.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "40583e452d13c9a5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 36,
      "quote": "The record layer fragments information blocks into TLSPlaintext records carrying data in chunks of 2^14 bytes or less.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_record.h",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "25b6a89a97799601",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 40,
      "quote": "The record layer fragments information blocks into TLSPlaintext records carrying data in chunks of 2^14 bytes or less.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_record.h",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "00acf739cb3c57f0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "An AEAD algorithm used in TLS 1.3 MUST NOT produce an expansion greater than 255 octets.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_record.h",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7f0c9d42671d332f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "msg_length The highest bit MUST be 1; the remaining bits contain the length of the following data in bytes.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_record_read.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "appendix-E.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Incorrect implementations exist in the wild. Ignoring instead.",
      "id": "ebda44f328ee9120",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 135,
      "quote": "The length MUST NOT exceed 2^14 bytes.  An endpoint that receives a record that exceeds this length MUST terminate the connection with a \"record_overflow\" alert.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_record_read.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "dd57429528687d75",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 168,
      "quote": "This version value is historical, deriving from the use of 0x0301 for TLS 1.0 and 0x0300 for SSL 3.0.  In order to maximize backward compatibility, a record containing an initial ClientHello SHOULD have version 0x0301 (reflecting TLS 1.0)",
      "source": "tls/s2n_record_write.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "122aab061b35a69a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 189,
      "quote": "legacy_record_version:  MUST be set to 0x0303 for all records generated by a TLS 1.3 implementation other than an initial ClientHello (i.e., one not generated after a HelloRetryRequest), where it MAY also be 0x0301 for compatibility purposes.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_record_write.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "fa5ba97e0fb6e195",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 291,
      "quote": "The MAC is generated as: MAC(MAC_write_key, seq_num +",
      "source": "tls/s2n_record_write.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5f64b7b876639c80",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 302,
      "quote": "TLSCompressed.type +",
      "source": "tls/s2n_record_write.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "52db9bb965faadc9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 310,
      "quote": "TLSCompressed.version +",
      "source": "tls/s2n_record_write.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "481697350f70a9d1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 321,
      "quote": "TLSCompressed.length +",
      "source": "tls/s2n_record_write.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "80a914092bde5330",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 337,
      "quote": "TLSCompressed.fragment); where \"+\" denotes concatenation.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_record_write.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "10c7a804f11b2ae4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 180,
      "quote": "If a transport-level close is received prior to a \"close_notify\", the receiver cannot know that all the data that was sent has been received.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_recv.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "6.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "35c0915ee853b231",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 185,
      "quote": "If the application protocol using TLS provides that any data may be carried over the underlying transport after the TLS connection is closed, the TLS implementation MUST receive a \"close_notify\" alert before indicating end-of-data to the application layer.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_recv.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "6.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "72c90e53d7970bd8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 221,
      "quote": "-  Handshake messages MUST NOT be interleaved with other record types.  That is, if a handshake message is split over two or more records, there MUST NOT be any other records between them.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_recv.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c29888c48d2f4018",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 185,
      "quote": "o  If the original session did not use the \"extended_master_secret\" extension but the new ClientHello contains the extension, then the server MUST NOT perform the abbreviated handshake.  Instead, it SHOULD continue with a full handshake (as described in Section 5.2) to negotiate a new session. o  If the original session used the \"extended_master_secret\" extension but the new ClientHello does not contain it, the server MUST abort the abbreviated handshake.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_resume.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7627",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "deadbcc98c57841c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 329,
      "quote": "Clients MUST NOT cache tickets for longer than 7 days, regardless of the ticket_lifetime, and MAY delete tickets earlier based on local policy.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_resume.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7c5b0042523d5214",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 70,
      "quote": "Otherwise, the client MUST process all extensions in the HelloRetryRequest",
      "source": "tls/s2n_server_extensions.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9b5a8e3a9d05f14c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 113,
      "quote": "Upon receiving a message with type server_hello, implementations MUST first examine the Random value and, if it matches this value, process it as described in Section 4.1.4).",
      "source": "tls/s2n_server_hello.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "4fa511a47213fcaa",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 120,
      "quote": "If a client receives a second HelloRetryRequest in the same connection (i.e., where the ClientHello was itself in response to a HelloRetryRequest), it MUST abort the handshake with an \"unexpected_message\" alert.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_server_hello.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "63cc7d7cdbdccc3b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 129,
      "quote": "Upon receipt of a HelloRetryRequest, the client MUST check the legacy_version",
      "source": "tls/s2n_server_hello.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b9f459fc14a4cb28",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 148,
      "quote": "legacy_compression_method:  A single byte which MUST have the value 0.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_server_hello.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ad2af49d87d2a7a1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 152,
      "quote": "Upon receipt of a HelloRetryRequest, the client MUST check the legacy_version, legacy_session_id_echo, cipher_suite, and legacy_compression_method",
      "source": "tls/s2n_server_hello.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7329d68f68e012d6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 168,
      "quote": "The server's extensions MUST contain \"supported_versions\".",
      "source": "tls/s2n_server_hello.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "25e71d9f9201c77a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 182,
      "quote": "A client which receives a legacy_session_id_echo field that does not match what it sent in the ClientHello MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_server_hello.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a704046c4562f0fc",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 188,
      "quote": "Upon receipt of a HelloRetryRequest, the client MUST check the legacy_version, legacy_session_id_echo",
      "source": "tls/s2n_server_hello.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.1.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ab8b813285199d02",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 209,
      "quote": "A client that attempts to send 0-RTT data MUST fail a connection if it receives a ServerHello with TLS 1.2 or older.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_server_hello.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-D.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5207bb55282eb45b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 227,
      "quote": "If the server accepts the ticket and the Session ID is not empty, then it MUST respond with the same Session ID present in the ClientHello.  This allows the client to easily differentiate when the server is resuming a session from when it is falling back to a full handshake.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_server_hello.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5077",
      "target_section": "section-3.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c70971b044228b08",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 79,
      "quote": "Upon receipt of this extension in a HelloRetryRequest, the client MUST verify that (1) the selected_group field corresponds to a group which was provided in the \"supported_groups\" extension in the original ClientHello",
      "source": "tls/s2n_server_hello_retry.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.2.8",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "abe2c1e18887c5fd",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 96,
      "quote": "and (2) the selected_group field does not correspond to a group which was provided in the \"key_share\" extension in the original ClientHello.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_server_hello_retry.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.2.8",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "736e583531dbd4f5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 115,
      "quote": "If either of these checks fails, then the client MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_server_hello_retry.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "4.2.8",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8ca72b5c20a52a85",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 120,
      "quote": "Clients MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert if the HelloRetryRequest would not result in any change in the ClientHello.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_server_hello_retry.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7377202ed91006bc",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 88,
      "quote": "If the server determines that it does not want to include a ticket after it has included the SessionTicket extension in the ServerHello, then it sends a zero-length ticket in the NewSessionTicket handshake message.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_server_new_session_ticket.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5077",
      "target_section": "section-3.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "068721ca1344d595",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 152,
      "quote": "Note that in principle it is possible to continue issuing new tickets which indefinitely extend the lifetime of the keying material originally derived from an initial non-PSK handshake (which was most likely tied to the peer's certificate). It is RECOMMENDED that implementations place limits on the total lifetime of such keying material; these limits should take into account the lifetime of the peer's certificate, the likelihood of intervening revocation, and the time since the peer's online CertificateVerify signature.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_server_new_session_ticket.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "222a4f6d57c36608",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 188,
      "quote": "Indicates the lifetime in seconds as a 32-bit unsigned integer in network byte order from the time of ticket issuance.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_server_new_session_ticket.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "4c6258a8282758f0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 203,
      "quote": "Servers MUST NOT use any value greater than 604800 seconds (7 days).",
      "source": "tls/s2n_server_new_session_ticket.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "1ddf1297aca7204f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 213,
      "quote": "A per-ticket value that is unique across all tickets issued on this connection.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_server_new_session_ticket.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "596b9a418727d1dc",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 229,
      "quote": "A securely generated, random 32-bit value that is used to obscure the age of the ticket that the client includes in the \"pre_shared_key\" extension.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_server_new_session_ticket.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3db229f3e37c7153",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 248,
      "quote": "The PSK associated with the ticket is computed as: HKDF-Expand-Label(resumption_master_secret, \"resumption\", ticket_nonce, Hash.length)",
      "source": "tls/s2n_server_new_session_ticket.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d7fe87c5f8915549",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 291,
      "quote": "The server MUST generate a fresh value for each ticket it sends.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_server_new_session_ticket.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "31c3e709a81552f3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 327,
      "quote": "struct { uint32 ticket_lifetime; uint32 ticket_age_add; opaque ticket_nonce<0..255>; opaque ticket<1..2^16-1>; Extension extensions<0..2^16-2>; } NewSessionTicket;",
      "source": "tls/s2n_server_new_session_ticket.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7b7c9d531190c1e5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 354,
      "quote": "Servers MUST NOT use any value greater than 604800 seconds (7 days).",
      "source": "tls/s2n_server_new_session_ticket.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0b7e63295171db5c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 360,
      "quote": "The value of zero indicates that the ticket should be discarded immediately.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_server_new_session_ticket.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "385fa6d7f4ba5549",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 99,
      "quote": "Each party MUST send a \"close_notify\" alert before closing its write side of the connection, unless it has already sent some error alert.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_shutdown.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "96ac80c6102e48c0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 231,
      "quote": "If the CertificateVerify message is sent by a server, the signature algorithm MUST be one offered in the client's \"signature_algorithms\" extension unless no valid certificate chain can be produced without unsupported algorithms",
      "source": "tls/s2n_signature_algorithms.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Compatibility with hypothetical faulty peers",
      "id": "c2ec188f44132799",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 238,
      "quote": "If sent by a client, the signature algorithm used in the signature MUST be one of those present in the supported_signature_algorithms field of the \"signature_algorithms\" extension in the CertificateRequest message.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_signature_algorithms.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-4.4.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Compatibility with known faulty peers",
      "id": "4b8e90c9fa9f3640",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 247,
      "quote": "If the client has offered the \"signature_algorithms\" extension, the signature algorithm and hash algorithm MUST be a pair listed in that extension.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_signature_algorithms.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Compatibility with hypothetical faulty peers",
      "id": "c315549e46c96175",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 255,
      "quote": "The hash and signature algorithms used in the signature MUST be one of those present in the supported_signature_algorithms field of the CertificateRequest message.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_signature_algorithms.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.8",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3d5d47845fce009e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 270,
      "quote": "If the client does not send the signature_algorithms extension, the server MUST do the following: -  If the negotiated key exchange algorithm is one of (RSA, DHE_RSA, DH_RSA, RSA_PSK, ECDH_RSA, ECDHE_RSA), behave as if client had sent the value {sha1,rsa}. -  If the negotiated key exchange algorithm is one of (DHE_DSS, DH_DSS), behave as if the client had sent the value {sha1,dsa}. -  If the negotiated key exchange algorithm is one of (ECDH_ECDSA, ECDHE_ECDSA), behave as if the client had sent value {sha1,ecdsa}.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_signature_algorithms.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5246",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1.4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8348245b7e388976",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 26,
      "quote": "The notation \"K_{send,recv} = foo\" means \"set the send/recv key to the given key\".",
      "source": "tls/s2n_tls13_key_schedule.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-A",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a69c788b7dd5351e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 62,
      "quote": "The traffic keying material is generated from the following input values: -  A secret value",
      "source": "tls/s2n_tls13_key_schedule.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-7.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8f3767290faf7b2b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 74,
      "quote": "-  A purpose value indicating the specific value being generated",
      "source": "tls/s2n_tls13_key_schedule.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-7.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ba97988f04ab28d4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 82,
      "quote": "-  The length of the key being generated",
      "source": "tls/s2n_tls13_key_schedule.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-7.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "33d6a0a913b244c8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 99,
      "quote": "The traffic keying material is generated from an input traffic secret value using: [sender]_write_key = HKDF-Expand-Label(Secret, \"key\", \"\", key_length)",
      "source": "tls/s2n_tls13_key_schedule.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-7.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f31aee0f8d57612f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 111,
      "quote": "[sender]_write_iv  = HKDF-Expand-Label(Secret, \"iv\", \"\", iv_length)",
      "source": "tls/s2n_tls13_key_schedule.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-7.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "1f23306a2c3fe383",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 159,
      "quote": "Each sequence number is set to zero at the beginning of a connection and whenever the key is changed; the first record transmitted under a particular traffic key MUST use sequence number 0.",
      "source": "tls/s2n_tls13_key_schedule.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b5d331b6cca37dad",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 179,
      "quote": "Actions which are taken only in certain circumstances are indicated in [].",
      "source": "tls/s2n_tls13_key_schedule.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-A",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "544bc8d959e4a470",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 185,
      "quote": "START <----+ Send ClientHello |        | Recv HelloRetryRequest [K_send = early data] |        |",
      "source": "tls/s2n_tls13_key_schedule.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "12f123cba8c3a91b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 195,
      "quote": "v        | /                 WAIT_SH ----+ |                    | Recv ServerHello |                    | K_recv = handshake",
      "source": "tls/s2n_tls13_key_schedule.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d8277fc5598b706f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 205,
      "quote": "Can |                    V send |                 WAIT_EE early |                    | Recv EncryptedExtensions data |           +--------+--------+ |     Using |                 | Using certificate |       PSK |                 v |           |            WAIT_CERT_CR |           |        Recv |       | Recv CertificateRequest |           | Certificate |       v |           |             |    WAIT_CERT |           |             |       | Recv Certificate |           |             v       v |           |              WAIT_CV |           |                 | Recv CertificateVerify |           +> WAIT_FINISHED <+ |                  | Recv Finished \\                  | [Send EndOfEarlyData] | K_send = handshake",
      "source": "tls/s2n_tls13_key_schedule.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "fdefcd40151d14db",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 230,
      "quote": "| [Send Certificate [+ CertificateVerify]] Can send                  | Send Finished app data   -->            | K_send = K_recv = application",
      "source": "tls/s2n_tls13_key_schedule.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ac316efda2a4a5ae",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 240,
      "quote": "after here                v CONNECTED",
      "source": "tls/s2n_tls13_key_schedule.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a9bb8c7b4ccb2341",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 254,
      "quote": "START <-----+ Recv ClientHello |         | Send HelloRetryRequest v         | RECVD_CH ----+ | Select parameters v NEGOTIATED | Send ServerHello | K_send = handshake",
      "source": "tls/s2n_tls13_key_schedule.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "72b734ab58f9bb29",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 269,
      "quote": "| Send EncryptedExtensions | [Send CertificateRequest] Can send                       | [Send Certificate + CertificateVerify] app data                       | Send Finished after   -->                    | K_send = application",
      "source": "tls/s2n_tls13_key_schedule.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "95c6634b040d7912",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 280,
      "quote": "here                  +--------+--------+ No 0-RTT |                 | 0-RTT |                 | K_recv = handshake  |                 | K_recv = early data",
      "source": "tls/s2n_tls13_key_schedule.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6312befb1f45dc6d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 294,
      "quote": "[Skip decrypt errors] |    +------> WAIT_EOED -+ |    |       Recv |      | Recv EndOfEarlyData |    | early data |      | K_recv = handshake |    +------------+      |",
      "source": "tls/s2n_tls13_key_schedule.c",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.2",
