            "   Provisions Relating to IETF Documents",
            "   (http://trustee.ietf.org/license-info) in effect on the date of",
            "   publication of this document.  Please review these documents",
            "   carefully, as they describe your rights and restrictions with respect",
            "   to this document.  Code Components extracted from this document must",
            "   include Simplified BSD License text as described in Section 4.e of",
            "   the Trust Legal Provisions and are provided without warranty as",
            "   described in the Simplified BSD License."
          ],
          "title": "Copyright Notice"
        },
        {
          "id": "name-table-of-contents",
          "lines": [
            "   1.  Introduction . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .  3",
            "   2.  Requirements Notation  . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .  4",
            "   3.  Next Protocol Negotiation Extension  . . . . . . . . . . . . .  5",
            "   4.  Protocol selection . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .  8",
            "   5.  Design discussion  . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .  9",
            "   6.  Security considerations  . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 10",
            "   7.  IANA Considerations  . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 11",
            "   8.  Acknowledgments  . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 12",
            "   9.  References . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 13",
            "     9.1.  Normative References . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 13",
            "     9.2.  Informative References . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 13",
            "   Author's Address . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 14"
          ],
          "title": "Table of Contents"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-1",
          "lines": [
            "   The Next Protocol Negotiation extension (NPN) is currently used to",
            "   negotiate the use of SPDY [spdy] as an application level protocol on",
            "   port 443, and to perform SPDY version negotiation.  However, it is",
            "   not SPDY specific in any way.",
            "",
            "   Designers of new application level protocols are faced with a",
            "   problem: there are no good options for establishing a clean transport",
            "   for a new protocol and negotiating its use.  Negotiations on port 80",
            "   will run afoul of intercepting proxies.  Ports other than 80 and 443",
            "   are likely to be firewalled without any fast method of detection, and",
            "   are also unlikely to traverse HTTP proxies with CONNECT.  Negotiating",
            "   on port 443 is possible, but may run afoul of MITM proxies and also",
            "   uses a round trip for negotiation on top of the round trips for",
            "   establishing the TLS connection.  Negotiation at that level is also",
            "   dependent on the application level protocol, i.e. the real world",
            "   tolerance of servers to HTTP Upgrade requests.",
            "",
            "   Next Protocol Negotiation allows application level protocols to be",
            "   negotiated without additional round trips and with clean fallback in",
            "   the case of an unsupportive MITM proxy."
          ],
          "title": "Introduction"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2",
          "lines": [
            "   The key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\",",
            "   \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and \"OPTIONAL\" in this",
            "   document are to be interpreted as described in RFC 2119 [RFC2119]."
          ],
          "title": "Requirements Notation"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3",
          "lines": [
            "   A new extension type (\"next_protocol_negotiation(13172)\") is defined",
            "   and MAY be included by the client in its \"ClientHello\" message.  If,",
            "   and only if, the server sees this extension in the \"ClientHello\", it",
            "   MAY choose to echo the extension in its \"ServerHello\".",
            "",
            "   enum {",
            "     next_protocol_negotiation(13172), (65535)",
            "   } ExtensionType;",
            "",
            "   The \"extension_data\" field of a \"next_protocol_negotiation\" extension",
            "   in a \"ClientHello\" MUST be empty.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "86243021998911af"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The \"extension_data\" field of a \"next_protocol_negotiation\" extension"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "86243021998911af"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "in a \"ServerHello\" contains an optional list of protocols advertised"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "86243021998911af"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "by the server."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Protocols are named by opaque, non-empty byte strings"
              }
            ],
            "   and the list of protocols is serialized as a concatenation of 8-bit,",
            "   length prefixed byte strings.  Implementations MUST ensure that the",
            "   empty string is not included and that no byte strings are truncated.",
            "",
            "   A new handshake message type (\"next_protocol(67)\") is defined.  If,",
            "   and only if, the server included a \"next_protocol_negotiation\"",
            "   extension in its \"ServerHello\" message, the client MUST send a",
            "   \"NextProtocol\" message after its \"ChangeCipherSpec\" and before its",
            "   \"Finished\" message.",
            "",
            "   enum {",
            "     next_protocol(67), (65535)",
            "   } HandshakeType;",
            "",
            "   Therefore a full handshake with \"NextProtocol\" has the following flow",
            "   (contrast with section 7.3 of RFC 5246 [RFC5246]):",
            "",
            "   Client                                               Server",
            "",
            "   ClientHello (NPN extension)   -------->",
            "                                                   ServerHello",
            "                                                     (NPN extension &",
            "                                                      list of protocols)",
            "                                                  Certificate*",
            "                                            ServerKeyExchange*",
            "                                           CertificateRequest*",
            "                                <--------      ServerHelloDone",
            "   Certificate*",
            "   ClientKeyExchange",
            "   CertificateVerify*",
            "   [ChangeCipherSpec]",
            "   NextProtocol",
            "   Finished                     -------->",
            "                                            [ChangeCipherSpec]",
            "                                <--------             Finished",
            "   Application Data             <------->     Application Data",
            "",
            "   An abbreviated handshake with \"NextProtocol\" has the following flow:",
            "",
            "   Client                                                Server",
            "",
            "   ClientHello (NPN extension)    -------->",
            "                                                   ServerHello",
            "                                                     (NPN extension &",
            "                                                      list of protocols)",
            "                                            [ChangeCipherSpec]",
            "                                 <--------            Finished",
            "   [ChangeCipherSpec]",
            "   NextProtocol",
            "   Finished                      -------->",
            "   Application Data              <------->    Application Data",
            "",
            "   The \"NextProtocol\" message has the following format:",
            "",
            "   struct {",
            "     opaque selected_protocol<0..255>;",
            "     opaque padding<0..255>;",
            "   } NextProtocol;",
            "",
            "   The contents of \"selected_protocol\" are an opaque protocol string,",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   but need not have been advertised by the server.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "abd259e242aa52f6",
                  "a5f6cf539d47a153"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "The length of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "abd259e242aa52f6",
                  "a5f6cf539d47a153"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "\"padding\" SHOULD be 32 - ((len(selected_protocol) + 2) % 32)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Note"
              }
            ],
            "   that len(selected_protocol) does not include its length prefix.",
            "",
            "   Unlike many other TLS extensions, this extension does not establish",
            "",
            "   properties of the session, only of the connection.  When session",
            "   resumption or session tickets [RFC5077] are used, the previous",
            "   contents of this extension are irrelevant and only the values in the",
            "   new handshake messages are considered.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "765b60ccf44c3524",
                  "035ef14d103ff4a6"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "For the same reasons, after a handshake has been performed for a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "765b60ccf44c3524",
                  "035ef14d103ff4a6"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "given connection, renegotiations on the same connection MUST NOT"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "765b60ccf44c3524",
                  "035ef14d103ff4a6"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "include the \"next_protocol_negotiation\" extension."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "title": "Next Protocol Negotiation Extension"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4",
          "lines": [
            "   It's expected that a client will have a list of protocols that it",
            "   supports, in preference order, and will only select a protocol if the",
            "   server supports it.  In that case, the client SHOULD select the first",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   protocol advertised by the server that it also supports.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "410462a9a6438026",
                  "f1a46ea441f42264",
                  "b3ee68b39358c442"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "In the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "410462a9a6438026",
                  "f1a46ea441f42264",
                  "b3ee68b39358c442"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "event that the client doesn't support any of server's protocols, or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "410462a9a6438026",
                  "f1a46ea441f42264",
                  "b3ee68b39358c442"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "the server doesn't advertise any, it SHOULD select the first protocol"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "410462a9a6438026",
                  "f1a46ea441f42264",
                  "b3ee68b39358c442"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "that it supports."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   There may be cases where the client knows, via other means, that a",
            "   server supports an unadvertised protocol.  In these cases the client",
            "   can simply select that protocol."
          ],
          "title": "Protocol selection"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5",
          "lines": [
            "   NPN is an outlier from TLS in several respects: firstly that it",
            "   introduces a handshake message between the \"ChangeCipherSpec\" and",
            "   \"Finished\" message, that the handshake message is padded, and that",
            "   the negotiation isn't done purely with the hello messages.  All these",
            "   aspects of the protocol are intended to prevent middle-ware",
            "   discrimination based on the negotiated protocol and follow the",
            "   general principle that anything that can be encrypted, should be",
            "   encrypted.  The server's list of advertised protocols is in the clear",
            "   as a compromise between performance and robustness."
          ],
          "title": "Design discussion"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6",
          "lines": [
            "   The server's list of supported protocols is still advertised in the",
            "   clear with this extension.  This may be undesirable for certain",
            "   protocols (such as Tor [tor]) where one could imagine that hostile",
            "   networks would terminate any TLS connection with a server that",
            "   advertised such a capability.  In this case, clients may wish to",
            "   opportunistically select a protocol that wasn't advertised by the",
            "   server.  However, the workings of such a scheme are outside the scope",
            "   of this document."
          ],
          "title": "Security considerations"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7",
          "lines": [
            "   This document requires IANA to update its registry of TLS extensions",
            "   to assign entry 13172 as \"next_protocol_negotiation\".",
            "",
            "   This document also requires IANA to update its registry of TLS",
            "   handshake types to assign entry 67 as \"next_protocol\".",
            "",
            "   This document also requires IANA to create a registry of TLS Next",
            "   Protocol Negotiation protocol strings on a first come, first served",
            "   basis, initially containing the following entries:",
            "",
            "   o  \"http/1.1\": HTTP/1.1 [RFC2616]",
            "",
            "   o  \"spdy/1\": (obsolete) SPDY version 1",
            "",
            "   o  \"spdy/2\": SPDY version 2",
            "",
            "   o  \"spdy/3\": SPDY version 3"
          ],
          "title": "IANA Considerations"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-8",
          "lines": [
            "   This document benefited specifically from discussions with Wan-Teh",
            "   Chang and Nagendra Modadugu."
          ],
          "title": "Acknowledgments"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-9",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "References"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-9.1",
          "lines": [
            "   [RFC2119]  Bradner, S., \"Key words for use in RFCs to Indicate",
            "              Requirement Levels\", BCP 14, RFC 2119, March 1997.",
            "",
            "   [RFC5246]  Dierks, T. and E. Rescorla, \"The Transport Layer Security",
            "              (TLS) Protocol Version 1.2\", RFC 5246, August 2008."
          ],
          "title": "Normative References"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-9.2",
          "lines": [
            "   [RFC2616]  Fielding, R., Gettys, J., Mogul, J., Frystyk, H.,",
            "              Masinter, L., Leach, P., and T. Berners-Lee, \"Hypertext",
            "              Transfer Protocol -- HTTP/1.1\", RFC 2616, June 1999.",
            "",
            "   [RFC5077]  Salowey, J., Zhou, H., Eronen, P., and H. Tschofenig,",
            "              \"Transport Layer Security (TLS) Session Resumption without",
            "              Server-Side State\", RFC 5077, January 2008.",
            "",
            "   [tor]      Dingledine, R., Matthewson, N., and P. Syverson, \"Tor: The",
            "              Second-Generation Onion Router\", August 2004.",
            "",
            "   [spdy]     Belshe, M. and R. Peon, \"SPDY Protocol (Internet Draft)\",",
            "              Feb 2012."
          ],
          "title": "Informative References"
        },
        {
          "id": "name-author-s-address",
          "lines": [
            "   Adam Langley",
            "   Google Inc",
            "",
            "   Email: agl@google.com"
          ],
          "title": "Author's Address"
        }
      ]
    },
    "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/df3c067/technical_details/JA4.md": {
      "format": "markdown",
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "ja4-tls-client-fingerprinting",
          "lines": [
            "![JA4](https://github.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/blob/main/technical_details/JA4.png)",
            "",
            "JA4 looks at the TLS Client Hello packet and builds a fingerprint of the client based on attributes within the packet."
          ],
          "title": "JA4: TLS Client Fingerprinting"
        },
        {
          "id": "ja4-algorithm",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb7c93e39417b472"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "(QUIC=”q”, DTLS=\"d\", or Normal TLS=”t”)"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb7c93e39417b472"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "(2 character TLS version)"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb7c93e39417b472"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "(SNI=”d” or no SNI=”i”)"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb7c93e39417b472"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "(2 character count of ciphers)"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb7c93e39417b472"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "(2 character count of extensions)"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb7c93e39417b472"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "(first and last characters of first ALPN extension value)"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "_  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb7c93e39417b472"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "(sha256 hash of the list of cipher hex codes sorted in hex order, truncated to 12 characters)"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "_  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb7c93e39417b472"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "(sha256 hash of (the list of extension hex codes sorted in hex order)_(the list of signature algorithms), truncated to 12 characters)"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              }
            ],
            "  ",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb7c93e39417b472"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The end result is a fingerprint that looks like:"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb7c93e39417b472"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "t13d1516h2_8daaf6152771_b186095e22b6"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              }
            ]
          ],
          "title": "JA4 Algorithm:"
        },
        {
          "id": "details",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9e028d62c7dff9db",
                  "60732fbc1e3c1231"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The program needs to ignore GREASE values anywhere it sees them"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": ": (https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-davidben-tls-grease-01#page-5)"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "9e028d62c7dff9db"
          ],
          "title": "Details:"
        },
        {
          "id": "quic-and-dtls",
          "lines": [
            "“q”, \"d\" or “t”, denotes whether the hello packet is for QUIC, DTLS, or normal TLS.",
            "",
            "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/QUIC  ",
            "QUIC is the protocol which the new HTTP/3 standard utilizes, encapsulating TLS 1.3 into UDP packets. As QUIC was developed by Google, if an organization heavily utilizes Google products, QUIC could make up half of their network traffic, so this is important to capture.  ",
            "",
            "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Datagram_Transport_Layer_Security",
            "DTLS is a version of TLS that can operate over UDP or SCTP.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6bf28498a8020def",
                  "2aaafe4b264b7d82",
                  "63e259757e8c82b4"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "If the protocol is QUIC then the first character of the fingerprint is “q”, if DTLS it is \"d\", else it is “t”."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "6bf28498a8020def"
          ],
          "title": "QUIC and DTLS:"
        },
        {
          "id": "tls-and-dtls-version",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "The TLS version is shown in 3 different places. "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1428c0017187db27",
                  "63c6a069fdf5e3c3",
                  "802383dd889850fc"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "If extension 0x002b exists (supported_versions), then the version is the highest value in the extension."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "539b2b62e2955642",
                  "1f8301318b2b388d",
                  "d6508b4aa062b542"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Remember to ignore GREASE values."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb0d8cea6da41f19",
                  "224ded51e84738ab",
                  "046a524e7751a648"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "If the extension doesn’t exist, then the TLS version is the value of the Protocol Version."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bd9a4fcfe12555db",
                  "49129c994c69c69a",
                  "5bc02644018eaec0"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Handshake version (located at the top of the packet) should be ignored."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c59090b7e6e86700",
                  "032627b4f20f0a0e"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "0x0304 = TLS 1.3 = “13”"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c59090b7e6e86700",
                  "032627b4f20f0a0e"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "0x0303 = TLS 1.2 = “12”"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c59090b7e6e86700",
                  "032627b4f20f0a0e"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "0x0302 = TLS 1.1 = “11”"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c59090b7e6e86700",
                  "032627b4f20f0a0e"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "0x0301 = TLS 1.0 = “10”"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e5dd8707b6aa7a31",
                  "d396db7402aafcd2"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "0x0300 = SSL 3.0 = “s3”"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e5dd8707b6aa7a31",
                  "d396db7402aafcd2"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "0x0002 = SSL 2.0 = “s2”"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              }
            ],
            "0xfeff = DTLS 1.0 = \"d1\"  ",
            "0xfefd = DTLS 1.2 = \"d2\"  ",
            "0xfefc = DTLS 1.3 = \"d3\"  ",
            "  ",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "164922c7935d0830"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Unknown = “00”"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "1428c0017187db27",
            "539b2b62e2955642",
            "eb0d8cea6da41f19",
            "bd9a4fcfe12555db"
          ],
          "title": "TLS and DTLS Version:"
        },
        {
          "id": "sni",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bfbeadd251144071",
                  "87ea60c160466652",
                  "1caee42acc35fd6e"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "If the SNI extension (0x0000) exists, then the destination of the connection is a domain, or “d” in the fingerprint."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "87ea60c160466652",
                  "1caee42acc35fd6e"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a40df3676c0f12b2",
                  "87ea60c160466652",
                  "1caee42acc35fd6e"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "If the SNI does not exist, then the destination is an IP address, or “i”."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "bfbeadd251144071",
            "a40df3676c0f12b2"
          ],
          "title": "SNI:"
        },
        {
          "id": "number-of-ciphers",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e02ba26ad815ab89",
                  "329422cf4a93e95c",
                  "5385bb10184826b8",
                  "466b5201bd75eeeb"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "2 character number of cipher suites"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e02ba26ad815ab89",
                  "329422cf4a93e95c",
                  "466b5201bd75eeeb"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": ", so "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e02ba26ad815ab89",
                  "00f617f75d7ec467",
                  "329422cf4a93e95c",
                  "466b5201bd75eeeb"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "if there’s 6 cipher suites in the hello packet, then the value should be “06”."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f3c6c30c34319aca",
                  "d587646dec0001e4",
                  "efb70f2d1076feb8"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "If there’s > 99, which there should never be, then output “99”."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ef4a2e5f02700d37",
                  "678d7883dae5b8a0",
                  "5a230fd674f88a3b"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Remember, ignore GREASE values. They don’t count."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "e02ba26ad815ab89",
            "f3c6c30c34319aca",
            "ef4a2e5f02700d37"
          ],
          "title": "Number of Ciphers:"
        },
        {
          "id": "number-of-extensions",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b2dea909fbf024e7",
                  "23cbdacfe60d15e1",
                  "8c36e80d673257bb",
                  "a145d6da167dcaff",
                  "e6173f283bb42973"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Same as counting ciphers."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4d71fd63674c5b6c",
                  "66c1d9bcd8f47a04",
                  "d73ef6bd3f6ba556"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Ignore GREASE."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "92db7e943a995345",
                  "f8e0cd5e3e006627",
                  "814b439c5af3e0a4"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Include SNI and ALPN."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "b2dea909fbf024e7",
            "4d71fd63674c5b6c",
            "92db7e943a995345"
          ],
          "title": "Number of Extensions:"
        },
        {
          "id": "alpn-extension-value",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "25c4fc8ec33273ec",
                  "8198ddedb9907ffb",
                  "3fbe92df374e82d8"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "The first and last alphanumeric characters of the ALPN (Application-Layer Protocol Negotiation) first value."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              }
            ],
            "List of possible ALPN Values (scroll down): https://www.iana.org/assignments/tls-extensiontype-values/tls-extensiontype-values.xhtml",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f5b967592b74dab3"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "In the above example, the first ALPN value is h2 so the first and last characters to use in the fingerprint are “h2”."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "70d682250bb13007"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If the first ALPN listed was http/1.1 then the first and last characters to use in the fingerprint would be “h1”."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "In Wireshark this field is located under tls.handshake.extensions_alpn_str",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5fb8e6edc6235d5a",
                  "944174641ce86ad1",
                  "e8acdc2a10430706"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "If there is no ALPN extension, no ALPN values, or the first ALPN value is empty, then we print \"00\" as the value in the fingerprint."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "544d53d53d7103d5",
                  "41988efe904967b2",
                  "e6268f51f579ed91"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "If the first ALPN value is only a single character, then that character is treated as both the first and last character."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "19860a88c01cf828",
                  "ce9e323ab7f12d06",
                  "65b7519aac2a45bf"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "If the first or last byte of the first ALPN is non-alphanumeric (meaning not `0x30-0x39`, `0x41-0x5A`, or `0x61-0x7A`), then we print the first and last characters of the hex representation of the first ALPN instead."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "62a342d349a0b621"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "For example:"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "62a342d349a0b621"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "* `0xAB` would be printed as \"ab\""
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "62a342d349a0b621"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "* `0xAB 0xCD` would be printed as \"ad\""
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "62a342d349a0b621"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "* `0x30 0xAB` would be printed as \"3b\""
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "62a342d349a0b621"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "* `0x30 0x31 0xAB 0xCD` would be printed as \"3d\""
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "05aa24dc6286fd02"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "* `0x30 0xAB 0xCD 0x31` would be printed as \"01\""
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "25c4fc8ec33273ec",
            "5fb8e6edc6235d5a",
            "544d53d53d7103d5",
            "19860a88c01cf828"
          ],
          "title": "ALPN Extension Value:"
        },
        {
          "id": "cipher-hash",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f7fdffdd60c79348",
                  "dde6434e5f7d62d6",
                  "70d1338120f79d4b"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "A 12 character truncated sha256 hash of the "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f7fdffdd60c79348",
                  "dde6434e5f7d62d6",
                  "60d18e169b0207b7",
                  "70d1338120f79d4b"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "list of ciphers sorted in hex order"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f7fdffdd60c79348",
                  "dde6434e5f7d62d6",
                  "70d1338120f79d4b"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": ", first 12 characters."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2d161cffd935b4f9",
                  "01f7ac5ef5dfa811",
                  "3aec7426df9e3a9b"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "The list is created using the 4 character hex values of the ciphers, lower case, comma delimited, ignoring GREASE."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "afd81c7ce88405c3"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "Example:"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "afd81c7ce88405c3"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "```"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "afd81c7ce88405c3"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "1301,1302,1303,c02b,c02f,"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5a568b55b4e29e2a"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "c02c,c030,cca9,cca8,c013,"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1be2563251464b50"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "c014,009c,009d,002f,0035"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1be2563251464b50"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "```"
              }
            ],
            "Is sorted to:",
            "```",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "60701111f1fbae39"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "002f,0035,009c,009d,1301,1302,1303,c013,c014,c02b,c02c,c02f,c030,cca8,cca9"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "84e1c5c7963ddb75"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "= 8daaf6152771"
              }
            ],
            "```",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a3552f884a7981ee",
                  "db8e702ffa96cb7a",
                  "a75401a5d03af1a4"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "If there are no ciphers in the sorted cipher list, then the value of JA4_b is set to `000000000000`"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              }
            ],
            "We do this rather than running a sha256 hash of nothing as this makes it clear to the user when a field has no values."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "f7fdffdd60c79348",
            "2d161cffd935b4f9",
            "a3552f884a7981ee"
          ],
          "title": "Cipher hash:"
        },
        {
          "id": "extension-hash",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ee53628e0a654ca6",
                  "93ee4d52bd569614",
                  "5ba08e50269a6b8b"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "A 12 character truncated sha256 hash of the list of extensions, sorted by hex value, followed by the list of signature algorithms, in the order that they appear (not sorted)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d8b146b49ac7b0f1",
                  "c3a6f61e6e2a72af",
                  "49ee677dee628fa8"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "The extension list is created using the 4 character hex values of the extensions, lower case, comma delimited, sorted (not in the order they appear)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf5059a561f5caf7",
                  "6c4a35db6e8d8bdf",
                  "951b3edb09ad2840"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Ignore the SNI extension (0000) and the ALPN extension (0010) as we’ve already captured them in the _a_ section of the fingerprint."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " These values are omitted so that the same application would have the same _c_ section of the fingerprint regardless of if it were going to a domain, IP, or changing ALPNs."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dade8513c2762ccb",
                  "95c6d7eefd475ccc"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "For example:"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dade8513c2762ccb",
                  "95c6d7eefd475ccc"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "```"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dade8513c2762ccb",
                  "95c6d7eefd475ccc"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "001b,0000,0033,0010,4469,0017,002d,000d,"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4e5b400781f5919e",
                  "95c6d7eefd475ccc"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "0005,0023,0012,002b,ff01,000b,000a,0015"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4e5b400781f5919e",
                  "95c6d7eefd475ccc"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "```"
              }
            ],
            "Is sorted to:",
            "```",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a687fdf4d4228e96",
                  "0b4e725bd268cdac"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "0005,000a,000b,000d,0012,0015,0017,001b,0023,002b,002d,0033,4469,ff01"
              }
            ],
            "```",
            "(notice 0000 and 0010 is removed)",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b11bc78bc342ccd2",
                  "9fd9d917d34136fb",
                  "d41b8ab1fbf40eed"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "The signature algorithm hex values are then added to the end of the list in the order that they appear (not sorted) with an underscore delimiting the two lists."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5dd2f5c3a6eaa07a"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "For example the signature algorithms:"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5dd2f5c3a6eaa07a"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "```"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5dd2f5c3a6eaa07a"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "0403,0804,0401,0503,0805,0501,0806,0601"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5dd2f5c3a6eaa07a"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "```"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "19f6ad686e5ecbb1"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "Are added to the end of the previous string to create:"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "19f6ad686e5ecbb1"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "```"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "19f6ad686e5ecbb1"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "0005,000a,000b,000d,0012,0015,0017,001b,0023,002b,002d,0033,4469,ff01_0403,0804,0401,0503,0805,0501,0806,0601"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "19f6ad686e5ecbb1"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "```"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f42286d0170cc108"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "Hashed to:"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f42286d0170cc108"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "```"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f42286d0170cc108"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "e5627efa2ab19723084c1033a96c694a45826ab5a460d2d3fd5ffcfe97161c95"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f42286d0170cc108"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "```"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f42286d0170cc108"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "Truncated to first 12 characters:"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f42286d0170cc108"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "```"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f42286d0170cc108"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "e5627efa2ab1"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f42286d0170cc108"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "```"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "08d3c060c9df7fa9",
                  "82db14eb402b0413",
                  "43462d4f498ed268"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "If there are no signature algorithms in the hello packet, then the string ends without an underscore and is hashed."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              }
            ],
            "For example:",
            "```",
            "0005,000a,000b,000d,0012,0015,0017,001b,0023,002b,002d,0033,4469,ff01 = 6d807ffa2a79",
            "```",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "638da1e15e146a6b",
                  "b217df82158c7c60",
                  "ceefb6ef08c828d5"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "If there are no extensions in the sorted extensions list, then the value of JA4_c is set to `000000000000`"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              }
            ],
            "We do this rather than running a sha256 hash of nothing as this makes it clear to the user when a field has no values."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "ee53628e0a654ca6",
            "d8b146b49ac7b0f1",
            "bf5059a561f5caf7",
            "b11bc78bc342ccd2",
            "08d3c060c9df7fa9",
            "638da1e15e146a6b"
          ],
          "title": "Extension hash:"
        },
        {
          "id": "example",
          "lines": [
            "JA4 fingerprint:  ",
            "t (TLS over TCP)  ",
            "13 (TLS version 1.3)  ",
            "d (SNI exists so it’s going to a domain)  ",
            "15 (15 cipher suites ignoring grease)  ",
            "16 (16 extensions ignoring grease)  ",
            "h2 (first and last characters of the first ALPN extension value)  ",
            "_  ",
            "8daaf6152771 (truncated sha256 hash of the list of ciphers sorted)",
            "_  ",
            "e5627efa2ab1 (truncated sha256 hash of the list of extensions sorted, SNI and ALPN removed, followed by the list of signature algorithms)",
            "```",
            "JA4 = t13d1516h2_8daaf6152771_e5627efa2ab1  ",
            "```"
          ],
          "title": "Example"
        },
        {
          "id": "raw-output",
          "lines": [
            "The program should allow for raw outputs either sorted or original.  ",
            "-r (raw fingerprint) -o (original) ",
            "",
            "The raw fingerprint for JA4 would look like this:",
            "```",
            "JA4_r = t13d1516h2_002f,0035,009c,009d,1301,1302,1303,c013,c014,c02b,c02c,c02f,c030,cca8,cca9_0005,000a,000b,000d,0012,0015,0017,001b,0023,002b,002d,0033,4469,ff01_0403,0804,0401,0503,0805,0501,0806,0601",
            "```",
            "",
            "The \"o\" option includes the original values in the original order, less GREASE values. This means SNI (0000) and ALPN (0010) are included. ",
            "",
            "The raw fingerprint with the original ordering (-o) would look like this:",
            "```",
            "JA4_ro = t13d1516h2_1301,1302,1303,c02b,c02f,c02c,c030,cca9,cca8,c013,c014,009c,009d,002f,0035_001b,0000,0033,0010,4469,0017,002d,000d,0005,0023,0012,002b,ff01,000b,000a,0015_0403,0804,0401,0503,0805,0501,0806,0601",
            "```",
            "When ‘-o’ flag is specified, ‘ja4’ field must be renamed to ‘ja4_o’:",
            "```",
            "JA4_o = t13d1516h2_acb858a92679_18f69afefd3d",
            "```"
          ],
          "title": "Raw Output"
        }
      ],
      "title": "JA4: TLS Client Fingerprinting"
    },
    "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4492": {
      "format": "ietf",
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "name-status-of-this-memo",
          "lines": [
            "   This memo provides information for the Internet community.  It does",
            "   not specify an Internet standard of any kind.  Distribution of this",
            "   memo is unlimited."
          ],
          "title": "Status of This Memo"
        },
        {
          "id": "name-copyright-notice",
          "lines": [
            "   Copyright (C) The Internet Society (2006)."
          ],
          "title": "Copyright Notice"
        },
        {
          "id": "name-abstract",
          "lines": [
            "   This document describes new key exchange algorithms based on Elliptic",
            "   Curve Cryptography (ECC) for the Transport Layer Security (TLS)",
            "   protocol.  In particular, it specifies the use of Elliptic Curve",
            "   Diffie-Hellman (ECDH) key agreement in a TLS handshake and the use of",
            "   Elliptic Curve Digital Signature Algorithm (ECDSA) as a new",
            "   authentication mechanism."
          ],
          "title": "Abstract"
        },
        {
          "id": "name-table-of-contents",
          "lines": [
            "   1. Introduction ....................................................3",
            "   2. Key Exchange Algorithms .........................................4",
            "      2.1. ECDH_ECDSA .................................................6",
            "      2.2. ECDHE_ECDSA ................................................6",
            "      2.3. ECDH_RSA ...................................................7",
            "      2.4. ECDHE_RSA ..................................................7",
            "      2.5. ECDH_anon ..................................................7",
            "   3. Client Authentication ...........................................8",
            "      3.1. ECDSA_sign .................................................8",
            "      3.2. ECDSA_fixed_ECDH ...........................................9",
            "      3.3. RSA_fixed_ECDH .............................................9",
            "   4. TLS Extensions for ECC ..........................................9",
            "   5. Data Structures and Computations ...............................10",
            "      5.1. Client Hello Extensions ...................................10",
            "           5.1.1. Supported Elliptic Curves Extension ................12",
            "           5.1.2. Supported Point Formats Extension ..................13",
            "      5.2. Server Hello Extension ....................................14",
            "      5.3. Server Certificate ........................................15",
            "      5.4. Server Key Exchange .......................................17",
            "      5.5. Certificate Request .......................................21",
            "      5.6. Client Certificate ........................................22",
            "      5.7. Client Key Exchange .......................................23",
            "      5.8. Certificate Verify ........................................25",
            "      5.9. Elliptic Curve Certificates ...............................26",
            "      5.10. ECDH, ECDSA, and RSA Computations ........................26",
            "   6. Cipher Suites ..................................................27",
            "   7. Security Considerations ........................................28",
            "   8. IANA Considerations ............................................29",
            "   9. Acknowledgements ...............................................29",
            "   10. References ....................................................30",
            "      10.1. Normative References .....................................30",
            "      10.2. Informative References ...................................31",
            "   Appendix A.  Equivalent Curves (Informative) ......................32"
          ],
          "title": "Table of Contents"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-1",
          "lines": [
            "   Elliptic Curve Cryptography (ECC) is emerging as an attractive",
            "   public-key cryptosystem, in particular for mobile (i.e., wireless)",
            "   environments.  Compared to currently prevalent cryptosystems such as",
            "   RSA, ECC offers equivalent security with smaller key sizes.  This is",
            "   illustrated in the following table, based on [18], which gives",
            "   approximate comparable key sizes for symmetric- and asymmetric-key",
            "   cryptosystems based on the best-known algorithms for attacking them.",
            "",
            "                    Symmetric  |   ECC   |  DH/DSA/RSA",
            "                   ------------+---------+-------------",
            "                        80     |   163   |     1024",
            "                       112     |   233   |     2048",
            "                       128     |   283   |     3072",
            "                       192     |   409   |     7680",
            "                       256     |   571   |    15360",
            "",
            "                  Table 1: Comparable Key Sizes (in bits)",
            "",
            "   Smaller key sizes result in savings for power, memory, bandwidth, and",
            "   computational cost that make ECC especially attractive for",
            "   constrained environments.",
            "",
            "   This document describes additions to TLS to support ECC, applicable",
            "   both to TLS Version 1.0 [2] and to TLS Version 1.1 [3].  In",
            "   particular, it defines",
            "",
            "   o  the use of the Elliptic Curve Diffie-Hellman (ECDH) key agreement",
            "      scheme with long-term or ephemeral keys to establish the TLS",
            "      premaster secret, and",
            "",
            "   o  the use of fixed-ECDH certificates and ECDSA for authentication of",
            "      TLS peers.",
            "",
            "   The remainder of this document is organized as follows.  Section 2",
            "   provides an overview of ECC-based key exchange algorithms for TLS.",
            "   Section 3 describes the use of ECC certificates for client",
            "   authentication.  TLS extensions that allow a client to negotiate the",
            "   use of specific curves and point formats are presented in Section 4.",
            "   Section 5 specifies various data structures needed for an ECC-based",
            "   handshake, their encoding in TLS messages, and the processing of",
            "   those messages.  Section 6 defines new ECC-based cipher suites and",
            "   identifies a small subset of these as recommended for all",
            "   implementations of this specification.  Section 7 discusses security",
            "   considerations.  Section 8 describes IANA considerations for the name",
            "   spaces created by this document.  Section 9 gives acknowledgements.",
            "",
            "   This is followed by the lists of normative and informative references",
            "   cited in this document, the authors' contact information, and",
            "   statements on intellectual property rights and copyrights.",
            "",
            "   Implementation of this specification requires familiarity with TLS",
            "   [2][3], TLS extensions [4], and ECC [5][6][7][11][17].",
            "",
            "   The key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\",",
            "   \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and \"OPTIONAL\" in this",
            "   document are to be interpreted as described in RFC 2119 [1]."
          ],
          "title": "Introduction"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2",
          "lines": [
            "   This document introduces five new ECC-based key exchange algorithms",
            "   for TLS.  All of them use ECDH to compute the TLS premaster secret,",
            "   and they differ only in the lifetime of ECDH keys (long-term or",
            "   ephemeral) and the mechanism (if any) used to authenticate them.  The",
            "   derivation of the TLS master secret from the premaster secret and the",
            "   subsequent generation of bulk encryption/MAC keys and initialization",
            "   vectors is independent of the key exchange algorithm and not impacted",
            "   by the introduction of ECC.",
            "",
            "   The table below summarizes the new key exchange algorithms, which",
            "   mimic DH_DSS, DHE_DSS, DH_RSA, DHE_RSA, and DH_anon (see [2] and",
            "   [3]), respectively.",
            "",
            "          Key",
            "          Exchange",
            "          Algorithm           Description",
            "          ---------           -----------",
            "",
            "          ECDH_ECDSA          Fixed ECDH with ECDSA-signed certificates.",
            "",
            "          ECDHE_ECDSA         Ephemeral ECDH with ECDSA signatures.",
            "",
            "          ECDH_RSA            Fixed ECDH with RSA-signed certificates.",
            "",
            "          ECDHE_RSA           Ephemeral ECDH with RSA signatures.",
            "",
            "          ECDH_anon           Anonymous ECDH, no signatures.",
            "",
            "                     Table 2: ECC Key Exchange Algorithms",
            "",
            "   The ECDHE_ECDSA and ECDHE_RSA key exchange mechanisms provide forward",
            "   secrecy.  With ECDHE_RSA, a server can reuse its existing RSA",
            "   certificate and easily comply with a constrained client's elliptic",
            "   curve preferences (see Section 4).  However, the computational cost",
            "",
            "   incurred by a server is higher for ECDHE_RSA than for the traditional",
            "   RSA key exchange, which does not provide forward secrecy.",
            "",
            "   The ECDH_RSA mechanism requires a server to acquire an ECC",
            "   certificate, but the certificate issuer can still use an existing RSA",
            "   key for signing.  This eliminates the need to update the keys of",
            "   trusted certification authorities accepted by TLS clients.  The",
            "   ECDH_ECDSA mechanism requires ECC keys for the server as well as the",
            "   certification authority and is best suited for constrained devices",
            "   unable to support RSA.",
            "",
            "   The anonymous key exchange algorithm does not provide authentication",
            "   of the server or the client.  Like other anonymous TLS key exchanges,",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   it is subject to man-in-the-middle attacks.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b15358244dea7f9d"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "Implementations of this"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b15358244dea7f9d"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "algorithm SHOULD provide authentication by other means."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Note that there is no structural difference between ECDH and ECDSA",
            "   keys.  A certificate issuer may use X.509 v3 keyUsage and",
            "   extendedKeyUsage extensions to restrict the use of an ECC public key",
            "   to certain computations [15].  This document refers to an ECC key as",
            "   ECDH-capable if its use in ECDH is permitted.  ECDSA-capable is",
            "   defined similarly.",
            "",
            "              Client                                        Server",
            "              ------                                        ------",
            "",
            "              ClientHello          -------->",
            "                                                       ServerHello",
            "                                                      Certificate*",
            "                                                ServerKeyExchange*",
            "                                              CertificateRequest*+",
            "                                   <--------       ServerHelloDone",
            "              Certificate*+",
            "              ClientKeyExchange",
            "              CertificateVerify*+",
            "              [ChangeCipherSpec]",
            "              Finished             -------->",
            "                                                [ChangeCipherSpec]",
            "                                   <--------              Finished",
            "",
            "              Application Data     <------->      Application Data",
            "",
            "                   * message is not sent under some conditions",
            "                   + message is not sent unless client authentication",
            "                     is desired",
            "",
            "                 Figure 1: Message flow in a full TLS handshake",
            "",
            "   Figure 1 shows all messages involved in the TLS key establishment",
            "   protocol (aka full handshake).  The addition of ECC has direct impact",
            "   only on the ClientHello, the ServerHello, the server's Certificate",
            "   message, the ServerKeyExchange, the ClientKeyExchange, the",
            "   CertificateRequest, the client's Certificate message, and the",
            "   CertificateVerify.  Next, we describe each ECC key exchange algorithm",
            "   in greater detail in terms of the content and processing of these",
            "   messages.  For ease of exposition, we defer discussion of client",
            "   authentication and associated messages (identified with a + in",
            "   Figure 1) until Section 3 and of the optional ECC-specific extensions",
            "   (which impact the Hello messages) until Section 4."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "b15358244dea7f9d",
            "b15358244dea7f9d"
          ],
          "title": "Key Exchange Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.1",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a59b4d730cc8968f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "In ECDH_ECDSA, the server's certificate MUST contain an ECDH-capable"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a59b4d730cc8968f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "public key and be signed with ECDSA."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6032354b4b35e320"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "A ServerKeyExchange MUST NOT be sent (the server's certificate"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6032354b4b35e320"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "contains all the necessary keying information required by the client"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6032354b4b35e320"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "to arrive at the premaster secret)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The client generates an ECDH key pair on the same curve as the",
            "   server's long-term public key and sends its public key in the",
            "   ClientKeyExchange message (except when using client authentication",
            "   algorithm ECDSA_fixed_ECDH or RSA_fixed_ECDH, in which case the",
            "   modifications from Section 3.2 or Section 3.3 apply).",
            "",
            "   Both client and server perform an ECDH operation and use the",
            "   resultant shared secret as the premaster secret.  All ECDH",
            "   calculations are performed as specified in Section 5.10."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "a59b4d730cc8968f",
            "a59b4d730cc8968f",
            "6032354b4b35e320",
            "6032354b4b35e320",
            "6032354b4b35e320"
          ],
          "title": "ECDH_ECDSA"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.2",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a38b384f88d4f62"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "In ECDHE_ECDSA, the server's certificate MUST contain an ECDSA-"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a38b384f88d4f62"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "capable public key and be signed with ECDSA."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The server sends its ephemeral ECDH public key and a specification of",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   the corresponding curve in the ServerKeyExchange message.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "df4d980b0ba65ea1"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "These"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "df4d980b0ba65ea1"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "parameters MUST be signed with ECDSA using the private key"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "df4d980b0ba65ea1"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "corresponding to the public key in the server's Certificate."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The client generates an ECDH key pair on the same curve as the",
            "   server's ephemeral ECDH key and sends its public key in the",
            "   ClientKeyExchange message.",
            "",
            "   Both client and server perform an ECDH operation (Section 5.10) and",
            "   use the resultant shared secret as the premaster secret."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "0a38b384f88d4f62",
            "0a38b384f88d4f62",
            "df4d980b0ba65ea1",
            "df4d980b0ba65ea1",
            "df4d980b0ba65ea1"
          ],
          "title": "ECDHE_ECDSA"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.3",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "149885e5b39803ab"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "This key exchange algorithm is the same as ECDH_ECDSA except that the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "149885e5b39803ab"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "server's certificate MUST be signed with RSA rather than ECDSA."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "149885e5b39803ab",
            "149885e5b39803ab"
          ],
          "title": "ECDH_RSA"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.4",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e6da303577262660"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "This key exchange algorithm is the same as ECDHE_ECDSA except that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e6da303577262660"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "the server's certificate MUST contain an RSA public key authorized"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e6da303577262660"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "for signing, and that the signature in the ServerKeyExchange message"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e6da303577262660"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "must be computed with the corresponding RSA private key."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "14f952119ca8136c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The server"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "14f952119ca8136c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "certificate MUST be signed with RSA."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "e6da303577262660",
            "e6da303577262660",
            "e6da303577262660",
            "e6da303577262660",
            "14f952119ca8136c",
            "14f952119ca8136c"
          ],
          "title": "ECDHE_RSA"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.5",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fff0d93dca07e43f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "In ECDH_anon, the server's Certificate, the CertificateRequest, the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fff0d93dca07e43f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "client's Certificate, and the CertificateVerify messages MUST NOT be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fff0d93dca07e43f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "sent."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fdb019a6e582df28"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The server MUST send an ephemeral ECDH public key and a specification"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fdb019a6e582df28"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "of the corresponding curve in the ServerKeyExchange message."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "92c4cd732990c87c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "These"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "92c4cd732990c87c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "parameters MUST NOT be signed."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The client generates an ECDH key pair on the same curve as the",
            "   server's ephemeral ECDH key and sends its public key in the",
            "   ClientKeyExchange message.",
            "",
            "   Both client and server perform an ECDH operation and use the",
            "   resultant shared secret as the premaster secret.  All ECDH",
            "   calculations are performed as specified in Section 5.10.",
            "",
            "   Note that while the ECDH_ECDSA, ECDHE_ECDSA, ECDH_RSA, and ECDHE_RSA",
            "   key exchange algorithms require the server's certificate to be signed",
            "   with a particular signature scheme, this specification (following the",
            "   similar cases of DH_DSS, DHE_DSS, DH_RSA, and DHE_RSA in [2] and [3])",
            "   does not impose restrictions on signature schemes used elsewhere in",
            "   the certificate chain.  (Often such restrictions will be useful, and",
            "   it is expected that this will be taken into account in certification",
            "   authorities' signing practices.  However, such restrictions are not",
            "   strictly required in general: Even if it is beyond the capabilities",
            "   of a client to completely validate a given chain, the client may be",
            "   able to validate the server's certificate by relying on a trusted",
            "   certification authority whose certificate appears as one of the",
            "   intermediate certificates in the chain.)"
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "fff0d93dca07e43f",
            "fff0d93dca07e43f",
            "fff0d93dca07e43f",
            "fdb019a6e582df28",
            "fdb019a6e582df28",
            "92c4cd732990c87c",
            "92c4cd732990c87c"
          ],
          "title": "ECDH_anon"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3",
          "lines": [
            "   This document defines three new client authentication mechanisms,",
            "   each named after the type of client certificate involved: ECDSA_sign,",
            "   ECDSA_fixed_ECDH, and RSA_fixed_ECDH.  The ECDSA_sign mechanism is",
            "   usable with any of the non-anonymous ECC key exchange algorithms",
            "   described in Section 2 as well as other non-anonymous (non-ECC) key",
            "   exchange algorithms defined in TLS [2][3].  The ECDSA_fixed_ECDH and",
            "   RSA_fixed_ECDH mechanisms are usable with ECDH_ECDSA and ECDH_RSA.",
            "   Their use with ECDHE_ECDSA and ECDHE_RSA is prohibited because the",
            "   use of a long-term ECDH client key would jeopardize the forward",
            "   secrecy property of these algorithms.",
            "",
            "   The server can request ECC-based client authentication by including",
            "   one or more of these certificate types in its CertificateRequest",
            "   message.  The server must not include any certificate types that are",
            "   prohibited for the negotiated key exchange algorithm.  The client",
            "   must check if it possesses a certificate appropriate for any of the",
            "   methods suggested by the server and is willing to use it for",
            "   authentication.",
            "",
            "   If these conditions are not met, the client should send a client",
            "   Certificate message containing no certificates.  In this case, the",
            "   ClientKeyExchange should be sent as described in Section 2, and the",
            "   CertificateVerify should not be sent.  If the server requires client",
            "   authentication, it may respond with a fatal handshake failure alert.",
            "",
            "   If the client has an appropriate certificate and is willing to use it",
            "   for authentication, it must send that certificate in the client's",
            "   Certificate message (as per Section 5.6) and prove possession of the",
            "   private key corresponding to the certified key.  The process of",
            "   determining an appropriate certificate and proving possession is",
            "   different for each authentication mechanism and described below.",
            "",
            "   NOTE: It is permissible for a server to request (and the client to",
            "   send) a client certificate of a different type than the server",
            "   certificate."
          ],
          "title": "Client Authentication"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.1",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b912fd782c5a21ce"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "To use this authentication mechanism, the client MUST possess a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b912fd782c5a21ce"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "certificate containing an ECDSA-capable public key and signed with"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b912fd782c5a21ce"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "ECDSA."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The client proves possession of the private key corresponding to the",
            "   certified key by including a signature in the CertificateVerify",
            "   message as described in Section 5.8."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "b912fd782c5a21ce",
            "b912fd782c5a21ce",
            "b912fd782c5a21ce"
          ],
          "title": "ECDSA_sign"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.2",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "67b3a7702fab57fd",
                  "b654e502c187f940"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "To use this authentication mechanism, the client MUST possess a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "67b3a7702fab57fd",
                  "b654e502c187f940"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "certificate containing an ECDH-capable public key, and that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "67b3a7702fab57fd",
                  "b654e502c187f940"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "certificate MUST be signed with ECDSA."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c9434f02818bfc5b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Furthermore, the client's"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c9434f02818bfc5b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "ECDH key MUST be on the same elliptic curve as the server's long-term"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c9434f02818bfc5b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "(certified) ECDH key."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This might limit use of this mechanism to"
              }
            ],
            "   closed environments.  In situations where the client has an ECC key",
            "   on a different curve, it would have to authenticate using either",
            "   ECDSA_sign or a non-ECC mechanism (e.g., RSA).  Using fixed ECDH for",
            "   both servers and clients is computationally more efficient than",
            "   mechanisms providing forward secrecy.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "518dadaf92cb97d2",
                  "84a90b1c9e2209ea"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "When using this authentication mechanism, the client MUST send an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "518dadaf92cb97d2",
                  "84a90b1c9e2209ea"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "empty ClientKeyExchange as described in Section 5.7 and MUST NOT send"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "518dadaf92cb97d2",
                  "84a90b1c9e2209ea"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "the CertificateVerify message."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  The ClientKeyExchange is empty since"
              }
            ],
            "   the client's ECDH public key required by the server to compute the",
            "   premaster secret is available inside the client's certificate.  The",
            "   client's ability to arrive at the same premaster secret as the server",
            "   (demonstrated by a successful exchange of Finished messages) proves",
            "   possession of the private key corresponding to the certified public",
            "   key, and the CertificateVerify message is unnecessary."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "67b3a7702fab57fd",
            "67b3a7702fab57fd",
            "67b3a7702fab57fd",
            "b654e502c187f940",
            "b654e502c187f940",
            "b654e502c187f940",
            "c9434f02818bfc5b",
            "c9434f02818bfc5b",
            "c9434f02818bfc5b",
            "518dadaf92cb97d2",
            "518dadaf92cb97d2",
            "518dadaf92cb97d2",
            "84a90b1c9e2209ea",
            "84a90b1c9e2209ea",
            "84a90b1c9e2209ea"
          ],
          "title": "ECDSA_fixed_ECDH"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.3",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0680b462dd160dfe"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "This authentication mechanism is identical to ECDSA_fixed_ECDH except"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0680b462dd160dfe"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "that the client's certificate MUST be signed with RSA."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Note that while the ECDSA_sign, ECDSA_fixed_ECDH, and RSA_fixed_ECDH",
            "   client authentication mechanisms require the client's certificate to",
            "   be signed with a particular signature scheme, this specification does",
            "   not impose restrictions on signature schemes used elsewhere in the",
            "   certificate chain.  (Often such restrictions will be useful, and it",
            "   is expected that this will be taken into account in certification",
            "   authorities' signing practices.  However, such restrictions are not",
            "   strictly required in general: Even if it is beyond the capabilities",
            "   of a server to completely validate a given chain, the server may be",
            "   able to validate the clients certificate by relying on a trust anchor",
            "   that appears as one of the intermediate certificates in the chain.)"
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "0680b462dd160dfe",
            "0680b462dd160dfe"
          ],
          "title": "RSA_fixed_ECDH"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4",
          "lines": [
            "   Two new TLS extensions are defined in this specification: (i) the",
            "   Supported Elliptic Curves Extension, and (ii) the Supported Point",
            "   Formats Extension.  These allow negotiating the use of specific",
            "   curves and point formats (e.g., compressed vs. uncompressed,",
            "   respectively) during a handshake starting a new session.  These",
            "   extensions are especially relevant for constrained clients that may",
            "",
            "   only support a limited number of curves or point formats.  They",
            "   follow the general approach outlined in [4]; message details are",
            "   specified in Section 5.  The client enumerates the curves it supports",
            "   and the point formats it can parse by including the appropriate",
            "   extensions in its ClientHello message.  The server similarly",
            "   enumerates the point formats it can parse by including an extension",
            "   in its ServerHello message.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8a8dba963ac94ca6"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "A TLS client that proposes ECC cipher suites in its ClientHello"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8a8dba963ac94ca6"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "message SHOULD include these extensions."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "901ba56db37397e4",
                  "b993dd3a3d1b0b49"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Servers implementing ECC"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "901ba56db37397e4",
                  "b993dd3a3d1b0b49"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "cipher suites MUST support these extensions, and when a client uses"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "901ba56db37397e4",
                  "b993dd3a3d1b0b49"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "these extensions, servers MUST NOT negotiate the use of an ECC cipher"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "901ba56db37397e4",
                  "b993dd3a3d1b0b49"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "suite unless they can complete the handshake while respecting the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "901ba56db37397e4",
                  "b993dd3a3d1b0b49"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "choice of curves and compression techniques specified by the client."
              }
            ],
            "   This eliminates the possibility that a negotiated ECC handshake will",
            "   be subsequently aborted due to a client's inability to deal with the",
            "   server's EC key.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f4760ac4c5bb037a"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The client MUST NOT include these extensions in the ClientHello"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f4760ac4c5bb037a"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "message if it does not propose any ECC cipher suites."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ec9fbda41a8ca396",
                  "95204dbcf3ee49d6"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "A client that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ec9fbda41a8ca396",
                  "95204dbcf3ee49d6"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "proposes ECC cipher suites may choose not to include these"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ec9fbda41a8ca396",
                  "95204dbcf3ee49d6"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "extensions.  In this case, the server is free to choose any one of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ec9fbda41a8ca396",
                  "95204dbcf3ee49d6"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "the elliptic curves or point formats listed in Section 5."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  That"
              }
            ],
            "   section also describes the structure and processing of these",
            "   extensions in greater detail.",
            "",
            "   In the case of session resumption, the server simply ignores the",
            "   Supported Elliptic Curves Extension and the Supported Point Formats",
            "   Extension appearing in the current ClientHello message.  These",
            "   extensions only play a role during handshakes negotiating a new",
            "   session."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "8a8dba963ac94ca6",
            "8a8dba963ac94ca6",
            "901ba56db37397e4",
            "901ba56db37397e4",
            "901ba56db37397e4",
            "901ba56db37397e4",
            "901ba56db37397e4",
            "b993dd3a3d1b0b49",
            "b993dd3a3d1b0b49",
            "b993dd3a3d1b0b49",
            "b993dd3a3d1b0b49",
            "b993dd3a3d1b0b49",
            "f4760ac4c5bb037a",
            "f4760ac4c5bb037a"
          ],
          "title": "TLS Extensions for ECC"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5",
          "lines": [
            "   This section specifies the data structures and computations used by",
            "   ECC-based key mechanisms specified in Sections 2, 3, and 4.  The",
            "   presentation language used here is the same as that used in TLS",
            "   [2][3].  Since this specification extends TLS, these descriptions",
            "   should be merged with those in the TLS specification and any others",
            "   that extend TLS.  This means that enum types may not specify all",
            "   possible values, and structures with multiple formats chosen with a",
            "   select() clause may not indicate all possible cases."
          ],
          "title": "Data Structures and Computations"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.1",
          "lines": [
            "   This section specifies two TLS extensions that can be included with",
            "   the ClientHello message as described in [4], the Supported Elliptic",
            "   Curves Extension and the Supported Point Formats Extension.",
            "",
            "   When these extensions are sent:",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3123d3f8d4a9e58f"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "The extensions SHOULD be sent along with any ClientHello message that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3123d3f8d4a9e58f"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "proposes ECC cipher suites."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Meaning of these extensions:",
            "",
            "   These extensions allow a client to enumerate the elliptic curves it",
            "   supports and/or the point formats it can parse.",
            "",
            "   Structure of these extensions:",
            "",
            "   The general structure of TLS extensions is described in [4], and this",
            "   specification adds two new types to ExtensionType.",
            "",
            "       enum { elliptic_curves(10), ec_point_formats(11) } ExtensionType;",
            "",
            "   elliptic_curves (Supported Elliptic Curves Extension):   Indicates",
            "      the set of elliptic curves supported by the client.  For this",
            "      extension, the opaque extension_data field contains",
            "      EllipticCurveList.  See Section 5.1.1 for details.",
            "",
            "   ec_point_formats (Supported Point Formats Extension):   Indicates the",
            "      set of point formats that the client can parse.  For this",
            "      extension, the opaque extension_data field contains",
            "      ECPointFormatList.  See Section 5.1.2 for details.",
            "",
            "   Actions of the sender:",
            "",
            "   A client that proposes ECC cipher suites in its ClientHello message",
            "   appends these extensions (along with any others), enumerating the",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   curves it supports and the point formats it can parse.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "75051c4cd959c823"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "Clients"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "75051c4cd959c823"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "SHOULD send both the Supported Elliptic Curves Extension and the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "75051c4cd959c823"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "Supported Point Formats Extension."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dad5d63eacf19f24"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If the Supported Point Formats"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dad5d63eacf19f24"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Extension is indeed sent, it MUST contain the value 0 (uncompressed)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dad5d63eacf19f24"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "as one of the items in the list of point formats."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Actions of the receiver:",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cf9d38bdf687314d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "A server that receives a ClientHello containing one or both of these"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cf9d38bdf687314d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "extensions MUST use the client's enumerated capabilities to guide its"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cf9d38bdf687314d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "selection of an appropriate cipher suite."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  One of the proposed ECC"
              }
            ],
            "   cipher suites must be negotiated only if the server can successfully",
            "   complete the handshake while using the curves and point formats",
            "   supported by the client (cf. Sections 5.3 and 5.4).",
            "",
            "   NOTE: A server participating in an ECDHE-ECDSA key exchange may use",
            "   different curves for (i) the ECDSA key in its certificate, and (ii)",
            "   the ephemeral ECDH key in the ServerKeyExchange message.  The server",
            "   must consider the extensions in both cases.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f7761338561ba75d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If a server does not understand the Supported Elliptic Curves"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f7761338561ba75d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Extension, does not understand the Supported Point Formats Extension,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f7761338561ba75d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "or is unable to complete the ECC handshake while restricting itself"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f7761338561ba75d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "to the enumerated curves and point formats, it MUST NOT negotiate the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f7761338561ba75d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "use of an ECC cipher suite."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Depending on what other cipher suites"
              }
            ],
            "   are proposed by the client and supported by the server, this may",
            "   result in a fatal handshake failure alert due to the lack of common",
            "   cipher suites."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "3123d3f8d4a9e58f",
            "3123d3f8d4a9e58f",
            "75051c4cd959c823",
            "75051c4cd959c823",
            "75051c4cd959c823",
            "dad5d63eacf19f24",
            "dad5d63eacf19f24",
            "dad5d63eacf19f24",
            "cf9d38bdf687314d",
            "cf9d38bdf687314d",
            "cf9d38bdf687314d",
            "f7761338561ba75d",
            "f7761338561ba75d",
            "f7761338561ba75d",
            "f7761338561ba75d",
            "f7761338561ba75d"
          ],
          "title": "Client Hello Extensions"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.1.1",
          "lines": [
            "        enum {",
            "            sect163k1 (1), sect163r1 (2), sect163r2 (3),",
            "            sect193r1 (4), sect193r2 (5), sect233k1 (6),",
            "            sect233r1 (7), sect239k1 (8), sect283k1 (9),",
            "            sect283r1 (10), sect409k1 (11), sect409r1 (12),",
            "            sect571k1 (13), sect571r1 (14), secp160k1 (15),",
            "            secp160r1 (16), secp160r2 (17), secp192k1 (18),",
            "            secp192r1 (19), secp224k1 (20), secp224r1 (21),",
            "            secp256k1 (22), secp256r1 (23), secp384r1 (24),",
            "            secp521r1 (25),",
            "            reserved (0xFE00..0xFEFF),",
            "            arbitrary_explicit_prime_curves(0xFF01),",
            "            arbitrary_explicit_char2_curves(0xFF02),",
            "            (0xFFFF)",
            "        } NamedCurve;",
            "",
            "   sect163k1, etc:   Indicates support of the corresponding named curve",
            "      or class of explicitly defined curves.  The named curves defined",
            "      here are those specified in SEC 2 [13].  Note that many of these",
            "      curves are also recommended in ANSI X9.62 [7] and FIPS 186-2 [11].",
            "      Values 0xFE00 through 0xFEFF are reserved for private use.  Values",
            "      0xFF01 and 0xFF02 indicate that the client supports arbitrary",
            "      prime and characteristic-2 curves, respectively (the curve",
            "      parameters must be encoded explicitly in ECParameters).",
            "",
            "   The NamedCurve name space is maintained by IANA.  See Section 8 for",
            "   information on how new value assignments are added.",
            "",
            "        struct {",
            "            NamedCurve elliptic_curve_list<1..2^16-1>",
            "        } EllipticCurveList;",
            "",
            "   Items in elliptic_curve_list are ordered according to the client's",
            "   preferences (favorite choice first).",
            "",
            "   As an example, a client that only supports secp192r1 (aka NIST P-192;",
            "   value 19 = 0x0013) and secp224r1 (aka NIST P-224; value 21 = 0x0015)",
            "   and prefers to use secp192r1 would include a TLS extension consisting",
            "   of the following octets.  Note that the first two octets indicate the",
            "   extension type (Supported Elliptic Curves Extension):",
            "",
            "        00 0A 00 06 00 04 00 13 00 15",
            "",
            "   A client that supports arbitrary explicit characteristic-2 curves",
            "   (value 0xFF02) would include an extension consisting of the following",
            "   octets:",
            "",
            "        00 0A 00 04 00 02 FF 02"
          ],
          "title": "Supported Elliptic Curves Extension"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.1.2",
          "lines": [
            "        enum { uncompressed (0), ansiX962_compressed_prime (1),",
            "               ansiX962_compressed_char2 (2), reserved (248..255)",
            "        } ECPointFormat;",
            "",
            "        struct {",
            "            ECPointFormat ec_point_format_list<1..2^8-1>",
            "        } ECPointFormatList;",
            "",
            "   Three point formats are included in the definition of ECPointFormat",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   above.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b4262cc8e7979b9e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The uncompressed point format is the default format in that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b4262cc8e7979b9e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "implementations of this document MUST support it for all of their"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b4262cc8e7979b9e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "supported curves."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Compressed point formats reduce bandwidth by"
              }
            ],
            "   including only the x-coordinate and a single bit of the y-coordinate",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   of the point.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "75bbe01ca0564d0b"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Implementations of this document MAY support the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "75bbe01ca0564d0b"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "ansiX962_compressed_prime and ansiX962_compressed_char2 formats,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "75bbe01ca0564d0b"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "where the former applies only to prime curves and the latter applies"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "75bbe01ca0564d0b"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "only to characteristic-2 curves."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  (These formats are specified in"
              }
            ],
            "   [7].)  Values 248 through 255 are reserved for private use.",
            "",
            "   The ECPointFormat name space is maintained by IANA.  See Section 8",
            "   for information on how new value assignments are added.",
            "",
            "   Items in ec_point_format_list are ordered according to the client's",
            "   preferences (favorite choice first).",
            "",
            "   A client that can parse only the uncompressed point format (value 0)",
            "   includes an extension consisting of the following octets; note that",
            "   the first two octets indicate the extension type (Supported Point",
            "   Formats Extension):",
            "",
            "        00 0B 00 02 01 00",
            "",
            "   A client that in the case of prime fields prefers the compressed",
            "   format (ansiX962_compressed_prime, value 1) over the uncompressed",
            "   format (value 0), but in the case of characteristic-2 fields prefers",
            "   the uncompressed format (value 0) over the compressed format",
            "   (ansiX962_compressed_char2, value 2), may indicate these preferences",
            "   by including an extension consisting of the following octets:",
            "",
            "        00 0B 00 04 03 01 00 02"
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "b4262cc8e7979b9e",
            "b4262cc8e7979b9e",
            "b4262cc8e7979b9e",
            "75bbe01ca0564d0b",
            "75bbe01ca0564d0b",
            "75bbe01ca0564d0b",
            "75bbe01ca0564d0b"
          ],
          "title": "Supported Point Formats Extension"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.2",
          "lines": [
            "   This section specifies a TLS extension that can be included with the",
            "   ServerHello message as described in [4], the Supported Point Formats",
            "   Extension.",
            "",
            "   When this extension is sent:",
            "",
            "   The Supported Point Formats Extension is included in a ServerHello",
            "   message in response to a ClientHello message containing the Supported",
            "   Point Formats Extension when negotiating an ECC cipher suite.",
            "",
            "   Meaning of this extension:",
            "",
            "   This extension allows a server to enumerate the point formats it can",
            "   parse (for the curve that will appear in its ServerKeyExchange",
            "   message when using the ECDHE_ECDSA, ECDHE_RSA, or ECDH_anon key",
            "   exchange algorithm, or for the curve that is used in the server's",
            "   public key that will appear in its Certificate message when using the",
            "   ECDH_ECDSA or ECDH_RSA key exchange algorithm).",
            "",
            "   Structure of this extension:",
            "",
            "   The server's Supported Point Formats Extension has the same structure",
            "   as the client's Supported Point Formats Extension (see",
            "   Section 5.1.2).  Items in elliptic_curve_list here are ordered",
            "   according to the server's preference (favorite choice first).  Note",
            "   that the server may include items that were not found in the client's",
            "   list (e.g., the server may prefer to receive points in compressed",
            "   format even when a client cannot parse this format: the same client",
            "   may nevertheless be capable of outputting points in compressed",
            "   format).",
            "",
            "   Actions of the sender:",
            "",
            "   A server that selects an ECC cipher suite in response to a",
            "   ClientHello message including a Supported Point Formats Extension",
            "   appends this extension (along with others) to its ServerHello",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   message, enumerating the point formats it can parse.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a95648544ccf7ff4"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The Supported"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a95648544ccf7ff4"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Point Formats Extension, when used, MUST contain the value 0"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a95648544ccf7ff4"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "(uncompressed) as one of the items in the list of point formats."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Actions of the receiver:",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b49ba66fd2462583"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "A client that receives a ServerHello message containing a Supported"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b49ba66fd2462583"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Point Formats Extension MUST respect the server's choice of point"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b49ba66fd2462583"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "formats during the handshake (cf."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " Sections 5.6 and 5.7).  If no"
              }
            ],
            "   Supported Point Formats Extension is received with the ServerHello,",
            "   this is equivalent to an extension allowing only the uncompressed",
            "   point format."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "a95648544ccf7ff4",
            "a95648544ccf7ff4",
            "a95648544ccf7ff4",
            "b49ba66fd2462583",
            "b49ba66fd2462583",
            "b49ba66fd2462583"
          ],
          "title": "Server Hello Extension"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.3",
          "lines": [
            "   When this message is sent:",
            "",
            "   This message is sent in all non-anonymous ECC-based key exchange",
            "   algorithms.",
            "",
            "   Meaning of this message:",
            "",
            "   This message is used to authentically convey the server's static",
            "   public key to the client.  The following table shows the server",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   certificate type appropriate for each key exchange algorithm.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c60a8ca99b64aef6"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "ECC"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c60a8ca99b64aef6"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "public keys MUST be encoded in certificates as described in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c60a8ca99b64aef6"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Section 5.9."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   NOTE: The server's Certificate message is capable of carrying a chain",
            "   of certificates.  The restrictions mentioned in Table 3 apply only to",
            "   the server's certificate (first in the chain).",
            "",
            "          Key Exchange Algorithm  Server Certificate Type",
            "          ----------------------  -----------------------",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e1e07f3ccfdb82ce"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "ECDH_ECDSA              Certificate MUST contain an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "                                  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e1e07f3ccfdb82ce"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "ECDH-capable public key."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "252caeed607f7d30",
                  "5ac3f21017b5172b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "It"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "                                  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "252caeed607f7d30",
                  "5ac3f21017b5172b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "MUST be signed with ECDSA."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0cfdbda7bb007cda"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "ECDHE_ECDSA             Certificate MUST contain an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "                                  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0cfdbda7bb007cda"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "ECDSA-capable public key."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  It"
              }
            ],
            "                                  MUST be signed with ECDSA.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "20d0080c4e9cd3d8"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "ECDH_RSA                Certificate MUST contain an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "                                  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "20d0080c4e9cd3d8"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "ECDH-capable public key."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1a59b27b66394644",
                  "7a82e402be2e4884"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "It"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "                                  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1a59b27b66394644",
                  "7a82e402be2e4884"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "MUST be signed with RSA."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9dd4095f9a9b529c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "ECDHE_RSA               Certificate MUST contain an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "                                  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9dd4095f9a9b529c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "RSA public key authorized for"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "                                  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9dd4095f9a9b529c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "use in digital signatures."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  It"
              }
            ],
            "                                  MUST be signed with RSA.",
            "",
            "                    Table 3: Server Certificate Types",
            "",
            "   Structure of this message:",
            "",
            "   Identical to the TLS Certificate format.",
            "",
            "   Actions of the sender:",
            "",
            "   The server constructs an appropriate certificate chain and conveys it",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   to the client in the Certificate message.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "157308eb444662d0",
                  "97184be452ceda7c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If the client has used a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "157308eb444662d0",
                  "97184be452ceda7c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Supported Elliptic Curves Extension, the public key in the server's"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "157308eb444662d0",
                  "97184be452ceda7c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "certificate MUST respect the client's choice of elliptic curves; in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "157308eb444662d0",
                  "97184be452ceda7c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "particular, the public key MUST employ a named curve (not the same"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "157308eb444662d0",
                  "97184be452ceda7c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "curve as an explicit curve) unless the client has indicated support"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "157308eb444662d0",
                  "97184be452ceda7c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "for explicit curves of the appropriate type."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "71140e180c20852c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If the client has used"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "71140e180c20852c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "a Supported Point Formats Extension, both the server's public key"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "71140e180c20852c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "point and (in the case of an explicit curve) the curve's base point"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "71140e180c20852c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "MUST respect the client's choice of point formats."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5e052b4747a84922"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "(A server that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5e052b4747a84922"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "cannot satisfy these requirements MUST NOT choose an ECC cipher suite"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5e052b4747a84922"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "in its ServerHello message.)"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Actions of the receiver:",
            "",
            "   The client validates the certificate chain, extracts the server's",
            "   public key, and checks that the key type is appropriate for the",
            "   negotiated key exchange algorithm.  (A possible reason for a fatal",
            "   handshake failure is that the client's capabilities for handling",
            "   elliptic curves and point formats are exceeded; cf. Section 5.1.)"
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "c60a8ca99b64aef6",
            "c60a8ca99b64aef6",
            "c60a8ca99b64aef6",
            "e1e07f3ccfdb82ce",
            "e1e07f3ccfdb82ce",
            "252caeed607f7d30",
            "252caeed607f7d30",
            "0cfdbda7bb007cda",
            "0cfdbda7bb007cda",
            "5ac3f21017b5172b",
            "5ac3f21017b5172b",
            "20d0080c4e9cd3d8",
            "20d0080c4e9cd3d8",
            "1a59b27b66394644",
            "1a59b27b66394644",
            "9dd4095f9a9b529c",
            "9dd4095f9a9b529c",
            "9dd4095f9a9b529c",
