            "   Provisions Relating to IETF Documents",
            "   (http://trustee.ietf.org/license-info) in effect on the date of",
            "   publication of this document.  Please review these documents",
            "   carefully, as they describe your rights and restrictions with respect",
            "   to this document.  Code Components extracted from this document must",
            "   include Simplified BSD License text as described in Section 4.e of",
            "   the Trust Legal Provisions and are provided without warranty as",
            "   described in the Simplified BSD License."
          ],
          "title": "Copyright Notice"
        },
        {
          "id": "name-table-of-contents",
          "lines": [
            "   1. Introduction ....................................................3",
            "   2. Conventions Used in This Document ...............................4",
            "   3. Secure Renegotiation Definition .................................4",
            "      3.1. Additional Connection State ................................4",
            "      3.2. Extension Definition .......................................5",
            "      3.3. Renegotiation Protection Request Signaling Cipher",
            "           Suite Value ................................................6",
            "      3.4. Client Behavior: Initial Handshake .........................6",
            "      3.5. Client Behavior: Secure Renegotiation ......................7",
            "      3.6. Server Behavior: Initial Handshake .........................7",
            "      3.7. Server Behavior: Secure Renegotiation ......................8",
            "   4. Backward Compatibility ..........................................9",
            "      4.1. Client Considerations ......................................9",
            "      4.2. Client Behavior: Legacy (Insecure) Renegotiation ..........10",
            "      4.3. Server Considerations .....................................10",
            "      4.4. Server Behavior: Legacy (Insecure) Renegotiation ..........11",
            "      4.5. SSLv3 .....................................................11",
            "   5. Security Considerations ........................................12",
            "   6. IANA Considerations ............................................13",
            "   7. Acknowledgements ...............................................13",
            "   8. References .....................................................13",
            "      8.1. Normative References ......................................13",
            "      8.2. Informative References ....................................13"
          ],
          "title": "Table of Contents"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-1",
          "lines": [
            "   TLS [RFC5246] allows either the client or the server to initiate",
            "   renegotiation -- a new handshake that establishes new cryptographic",
            "   parameters.  Unfortunately, although the new handshake is carried out",
            "   using the cryptographic parameters established by the original",
            "   handshake, there is no cryptographic binding between the two.  This",
            "   creates the opportunity for an attack in which the attacker who can",
            "   intercept a client's transport layer connection can inject traffic of",
            "   his own as a prefix to the client's interaction with the server.  One",
            "   form of this attack [Ray09] proceeds as shown below:",
            "",
            "   Client                        Attacker                        Server",
            "   ------                        -------                         ------",
            "                                     <----------- Handshake ---------->",
            "                                     <======= Initial Traffic ========>",
            "   <--------------------------  Handshake ============================>",
            "   <======================== Client Traffic ==========================>",
            "",
            "   To start the attack, the attacker forms a TLS connection to the",
            "   server (perhaps in response to an initial intercepted connection from",
            "   the client).  He then sends any traffic of his choice to the server.",
            "   This may involve multiple requests and responses at the application",
            "   layer, or may simply be a partial application layer request intended",
            "   to prefix the client's data.  This traffic is shown with == to",
            "   indicate it is encrypted.  He then allows the client's TLS handshake",
            "   to proceed with the server.  The handshake is in the clear to the",
            "   attacker but encrypted over the attacker's TLS connection to the",
            "   server.  Once the handshake has completed, the client communicates",
            "   with the server over the newly established security parameters with",
            "   the server.  The attacker cannot read this traffic, but the server",
            "   believes that the initial traffic to and from the attacker is the",
            "   same as that to and from the client.",
            "",
            "   If certificate-based client authentication is used, the server will",
            "   see a stream of bytes where the initial bytes are protected but",
            "   unauthenticated by TLS and subsequent bytes are authenticated by TLS",
            "   and bound to the client's certificate.  In some protocols (notably",
            "   HTTPS), no distinction is made between pre- and post-authentication",
            "   stages and the bytes are handled uniformly, resulting in the server",
            "   believing that the initial traffic corresponds to the authenticated",
            "   client identity.  Even without certificate-based authentication, a",
            "   variety of attacks may be possible in which the attacker convinces",
            "   the server to accept data from it as data from the client.  For",
            "   instance, if HTTPS [RFC2818] is in use with HTTP cookies [RFC2965],",
            "   the attacker may be able to generate a request of his choice",
            "   validated by the client's cookie.",
            "",
            "   Some protocols -- such as IMAP or SMTP -- have more explicit",
            "   transitions between authenticated and unauthenticated phases and",
            "   require that the protocol state machine be partly or fully reset at",
            "   such transitions.  If strictly followed, these rules may limit the",
            "   effect of attacks.  Unfortunately, there is no requirement for state",
            "   machine resets at TLS renegotiation, and thus there is still a",
            "   potential window of vulnerability, for instance, by prefixing a",
            "   command that writes to an area visible by the attacker with a command",
            "   by the client that includes his password, thus making the client's",
            "   password visible to the attacker (note that this precise attack does",
            "   not work with challenge-response authentication schemes, but other",
            "   attacks may be possible).  Similar attacks are available with SMTP,",
            "   and in fact do not necessarily require the attacker to have an",
            "   account on the target server.",
            "",
            "   It is important to note that in both cases these attacks are possible",
            "   because the client sends unsolicited authentication information",
            "   without requiring any specific data from the server over the TLS",
            "   connection.  Protocols that require a round trip to the server over",
            "   TLS before the client sends sensitive information are likely to be",
            "   less vulnerable.",
            "",
            "   These attacks can be prevented by cryptographically binding",
            "   renegotiation handshakes to the enclosing TLS cryptographic",
            "   parameters, thus allowing the server to differentiate renegotiation",
            "   from initial negotiation, as well as preventing renegotiations from",
            "   being spliced in between connections.  An attempt by an attacker to",
            "   inject himself as described above will result in a mismatch of the",
            "   cryptographic binding and can thus be detected.  The data used in the",
            "   extension is similar to, but not the same as, the data used in the",
            "   tls-unique and/or tls-unique-for-telnet channel bindings described in",
            "   [TLS-CHANNEL-BINDINGS]; however, this extension is not a general-",
            "   purpose RFC 5056 [RFC5056] channel binding facility."
          ],
          "title": "Introduction"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2",
          "lines": [
            "   The key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\",",
            "   \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and \"OPTIONAL\" in this",
            "   document are to be interpreted as described in [RFC2119]."
          ],
          "title": "Conventions Used in This Document"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Secure Renegotiation Definition"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.1",
          "lines": [
            "   Both client and server need to store three additional values for each",
            "   TLS connection state (see RFC 5246, Section 6.1).  Note that these",
            "   values are specific to connection (not a TLS session cache entry).",
            "",
            "   o  a \"secure_renegotiation\" flag, indicating whether secure",
            "      renegotiation is in use for this connection.",
            "",
            "   o  \"client_verify_data\":  the verify_data from the Finished message",
            "      sent by the client on the immediately previous handshake.  For",
            "      currently defined TLS versions and cipher suites, this will be a",
            "      12-byte value; for SSLv3, this will be a 36-byte value.",
            "",
            "   o  \"server_verify_data\":  the verify_data from the Finished message",
            "      sent by the server on the immediately previous handshake."
          ],
          "title": "Additional Connection State"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.2",
          "lines": [
            "   This document defines a new TLS extension, \"renegotiation_info\" (with",
            "   extension type 0xff01), which contains a cryptographic binding to the",
            "   enclosing TLS connection (if any) for which the renegotiation is",
            "   being performed.  The \"extension data\" field of this extension",
            "   contains a \"RenegotiationInfo\" structure:",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          opaque renegotiated_connection<0..255>;",
            "      } RenegotiationInfo;",
            "",
            "   The contents of this extension are specified as follows.",
            "",
            "   o  If this is the initial handshake for a connection, then the",
            "      \"renegotiated_connection\" field is of zero length in both the",
            "      ClientHello and the ServerHello.  Thus, the entire encoding of the",
            "      extension is ff 01 00 01 00.  The first two octets represent the",
            "      extension type, the third and fourth octets the length of the",
            "      extension itself, and the final octet the zero length byte for the",
            "      \"renegotiated_connection\" field.",
            "",
            "   o  For ClientHellos that are renegotiating, this field contains the",
            "      \"client_verify_data\" specified in Section 3.1.",
            "",
            "   o  For ServerHellos that are renegotiating, this field contains the",
            "      concatenation of client_verify_data and server_verify_data.  For",
            "      current versions of TLS, this will be a 24-byte value (for SSLv3,",
            "      it will be a 72-byte value).",
            "",
            "   This extension also can be used with Datagram TLS (DTLS) [RFC4347].",
            "   Although, for editorial simplicity, this document refers to TLS, all",
            "   requirements in this document apply equally to DTLS."
          ],
          "title": "Extension Definition"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.3",
          "lines": [
            "   Both the SSLv3 and TLS 1.0/TLS 1.1 specifications require",
            "   implementations to ignore data following the ClientHello (i.e.,",
            "   extensions) if they do not understand it.  However, some SSLv3 and",
            "   TLS 1.0 implementations incorrectly fail the handshake in such a",
            "   case.  This means that clients that offer the \"renegotiation_info\"",
            "   extension may encounter handshake failures.  In order to enhance",
            "   compatibility with such servers, this document defines a second",
            "   signaling mechanism via a special Signaling Cipher Suite Value (SCSV)",
            "   \"TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV\", with code point {0x00, 0xFF}.",
            "   This SCSV is not a true cipher suite (it does not correspond to any",
            "   valid set of algorithms) and cannot be negotiated.  Instead, it has",
            "   the same semantics as an empty \"renegotiation_info\" extension, as",
            "   described in the following sections.  Because SSLv3 and TLS",
            "   implementations reliably ignore unknown cipher suites, the SCSV may",
            "   be safely sent to any server.  The SCSV can also be included in the",
            "   SSLv2 backward compatible CLIENT-HELLO (see Appendix E.2 of",
            "   [RFC5246]).",
            "",
            "   Note:  a minimal client that does not support renegotiation at all",
            "   can simply use the SCSV in all initial handshakes.  The rules in the",
            "   following sections will cause any compliant server to abort the",
            "   handshake when it sees an apparent attempt at renegotiation by such a",
            "   client."
          ],
          "title": "Renegotiation Protection Request Signaling Cipher Suite Value"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.4",
          "lines": [
            "   Note that this section and Section 3.5 apply to both full handshakes",
            "   and session resumption handshakes.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "64877ede6ba6b5cc",
                  "fa341e598dda598a",
                  "9b81f2954b40d1a0",
                  "b67637c330398b96"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "o  The client MUST include either an empty \"renegotiation_info\""
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "64877ede6ba6b5cc",
                  "fa341e598dda598a",
                  "9b81f2954b40d1a0",
                  "b67637c330398b96"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "extension, or the TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV signaling"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "64877ede6ba6b5cc",
                  "fa341e598dda598a",
                  "9b81f2954b40d1a0",
                  "b67637c330398b96"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "cipher suite value in the ClientHello."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9b81f2954b40d1a0",
                  "b67637c330398b96"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "700ce4717f4f5aab",
                  "9b81f2954b40d1a0",
                  "b67637c330398b96"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Including both is NOT"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "700ce4717f4f5aab",
                  "9b81f2954b40d1a0",
                  "b67637c330398b96"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "RECOMMENDED."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4dd8c3322c6b3dc8",
                  "4ffd49d04997c13d",
                  "0a84dfbaa0314b15"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "o  When a ServerHello is received, the client MUST check if it"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4dd8c3322c6b3dc8",
                  "4ffd49d04997c13d",
                  "0a84dfbaa0314b15"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "includes the \"renegotiation_info\" extension:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3d1b9fc35fcb6e1d",
                  "30c887659afbac0d"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "*  If the extension is not present, the server does not support"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "         "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3d1b9fc35fcb6e1d",
                  "30c887659afbac0d"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "secure renegotiation; set secure_renegotiation flag to FALSE."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "         "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "30c887659afbac0d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "In this case, some clients may want to terminate the handshake"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "         "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "30c887659afbac0d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "instead of continuing; see Section 4.1 for discussion."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4a7c3d702b68da63"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "*  If the extension is present, set the secure_renegotiation flag"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "         "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4a7c3d702b68da63"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "to TRUE"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "96680edb95e16b70",
                  "262cb940284de6ff",
                  "4a7c3d702b68da63"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "96680edb95e16b70",
                  "262cb940284de6ff"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a50342c39ae0aa0",
                  "f17781d662f646c2",
                  "96680edb95e16b70",
                  "262cb940284de6ff"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "The client MUST then verify that the length of the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "         "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a50342c39ae0aa0",
                  "f17781d662f646c2",
                  "96680edb95e16b70",
                  "262cb940284de6ff"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "\"renegotiated_connection\" field is zero, and if it is not, MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "         "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a50342c39ae0aa0",
                  "f17781d662f646c2",
                  "96680edb95e16b70",
                  "262cb940284de6ff"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "abort the handshake (by sending a fatal handshake_failure"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "         "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a50342c39ae0aa0",
                  "f17781d662f646c2",
                  "96680edb95e16b70",
                  "262cb940284de6ff"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "alert)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "         "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a6bcf259c2ab4444"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Note: later in Section 3, \"abort the handshake\" is used as"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "         "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a6bcf259c2ab4444"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "shorthand for \"send a fatal handshake_failure alert and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "         "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a6bcf259c2ab4444"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "terminate the connection\"."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   o  When the handshake has completed, the client needs to save the",
            "      client_verify_data and server_verify_data values for future use."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "64877ede6ba6b5cc",
            "64877ede6ba6b5cc",
            "64877ede6ba6b5cc",
            "700ce4717f4f5aab",
            "700ce4717f4f5aab",
            "4dd8c3322c6b3dc8",
            "4dd8c3322c6b3dc8",
            "0a50342c39ae0aa0",
            "0a50342c39ae0aa0",
            "0a50342c39ae0aa0",
            "0a50342c39ae0aa0",
            "f17781d662f646c2",
            "f17781d662f646c2",
            "f17781d662f646c2",
            "f17781d662f646c2"
          ],
          "title": "Client Behavior: Initial Handshake"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.5",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "85adbeb5e08f996c",
                  "f560be8b8fc4dac3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "This text applies if the connection's \"secure_renegotiation\" flag is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "85adbeb5e08f996c",
                  "f560be8b8fc4dac3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "set to TRUE (if it is set to FALSE, see Section 4.2)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7a8d2bea0effa94f",
                  "71c85741b81eea01",
                  "2c04bb940d7e7b57",
                  "98e12e73d09e38ab",
                  "3370faddc4c7ddb6"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "o  The client MUST include the \"renegotiation_info\" extension in the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7a8d2bea0effa94f",
                  "71c85741b81eea01",
                  "2c04bb940d7e7b57",
                  "98e12e73d09e38ab",
                  "3370faddc4c7ddb6"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "ClientHello"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7a8d2bea0effa94f",
                  "2c04bb940d7e7b57",
                  "3370faddc4c7ddb6"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": ", containing the saved client_verify_data."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e78902a4a524e817",
                  "87ee908ab8941660",
                  "6451a595e7cd6d86"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "The SCSV"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e78902a4a524e817",
                  "87ee908ab8941660",
                  "6451a595e7cd6d86"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "MUST NOT be included."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ec8ea810ad3a6864",
                  "7876356e25610ca3",
                  "e379e0ee9f032739",
                  "52ee1c6edfb7cbba"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "o  When a ServerHello is received, the client MUST verify that the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ec8ea810ad3a6864",
                  "7876356e25610ca3",
                  "e379e0ee9f032739",
                  "52ee1c6edfb7cbba"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "\"renegotiation_info\" extension is present; if it is not, the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ec8ea810ad3a6864",
                  "7876356e25610ca3",
                  "e379e0ee9f032739",
                  "52ee1c6edfb7cbba"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "client MUST abort the handshake."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ca255fa8a9c831f2",
                  "2adeae113bede334",
                  "95ee8c9b7bd1c833"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "o  The client MUST then verify that the first half of the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ca255fa8a9c831f2",
                  "2adeae113bede334",
                  "95ee8c9b7bd1c833"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "\"renegotiated_connection\" field is equal to the saved"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ca255fa8a9c831f2",
                  "2adeae113bede334",
                  "95ee8c9b7bd1c833"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "client_verify_data value, and the second half is equal to the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ca255fa8a9c831f2",
                  "2adeae113bede334",
                  "95ee8c9b7bd1c833"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "saved server_verify_data value."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2adeae113bede334",
                  "95ee8c9b7bd1c833"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "53bc49e341d672aa",
                  "2adeae113bede334",
                  "95ee8c9b7bd1c833"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "If they are not, the client MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "53bc49e341d672aa",
                  "2adeae113bede334",
                  "95ee8c9b7bd1c833"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "abort the handshake."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   o  When the handshake has completed, the client needs to save the new",
            "      client_verify_data and server_verify_data values."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "7a8d2bea0effa94f",
            "7a8d2bea0effa94f",
            "e78902a4a524e817",
            "e78902a4a524e817",
            "ec8ea810ad3a6864",
            "ec8ea810ad3a6864",
            "ec8ea810ad3a6864",
            "7876356e25610ca3",
            "7876356e25610ca3",
            "7876356e25610ca3",
            "ca255fa8a9c831f2",
            "ca255fa8a9c831f2",
            "ca255fa8a9c831f2",
            "ca255fa8a9c831f2",
            "53bc49e341d672aa",
            "53bc49e341d672aa"
          ],
          "title": "Client Behavior: Secure Renegotiation"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.6",
          "lines": [
            "   Note that this section and Section 3.7 apply to both full handshakes",
            "   and session-resumption handshakes.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "42fee3f1bdf70fb9",
                  "bf34ce56e5aa5018",
                  "3bdcc57a5b805b7c"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "o  When a ClientHello is received, the server MUST check if it"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "42fee3f1bdf70fb9",
                  "bf34ce56e5aa5018",
                  "3bdcc57a5b805b7c"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "includes the TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV SCSV."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf34ce56e5aa5018",
                  "3bdcc57a5b805b7c"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "  If it does,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf34ce56e5aa5018",
                  "3bdcc57a5b805b7c"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "set the secure_renegotiation flag to TRUE."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e07d94bf28bf737f",
                  "f7a87cc2f2377a62",
                  "a46ce4748acb0c9d"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "o  The server MUST check if the \"renegotiation_info\" extension is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e07d94bf28bf737f",
                  "f7a87cc2f2377a62",
                  "a46ce4748acb0c9d"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "included in the ClientHello."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ad4216bc2993b40f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the extension is present, set"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ad4216bc2993b40f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "secure_renegotiation flag to TRUE."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cc866b584e8367e1",
                  "c2610fae3743ec59",
                  "f4ebf968d4e47f24",
                  "4c0f334c5aa1a8c5"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "The server MUST then verify"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cc866b584e8367e1",
                  "c2610fae3743ec59",
                  "f4ebf968d4e47f24",
                  "4c0f334c5aa1a8c5"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "that the length of the \"renegotiated_connection\" field is zero,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cc866b584e8367e1",
                  "c2610fae3743ec59",
                  "f4ebf968d4e47f24",
                  "4c0f334c5aa1a8c5"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "and if it is not, MUST abort the handshake."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "61f896de291e5026"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "o  If neither the TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV SCSV nor the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "61f896de291e5026"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "\"renegotiation_info\" extension was included, set the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "61f896de291e5026"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "secure_renegotiation flag to FALSE.  In this case, some servers"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "61f896de291e5026"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "may want to terminate the handshake instead of continuing"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "; see"
              }
            ],
            "      Section 4.3 for discussion.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c9d7a35db68e80e0",
                  "b359b4efd9578506",
                  "85f041e24eb46530",
                  "8f011f4e7c4db444"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "o  If the secure_renegotiation flag is set to TRUE, the server MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c9d7a35db68e80e0",
                  "b359b4efd9578506",
                  "85f041e24eb46530",
                  "8f011f4e7c4db444"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "include an empty \"renegotiation_info\" extension in the ServerHello"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c9d7a35db68e80e0",
                  "b359b4efd9578506",
                  "85f041e24eb46530",
                  "8f011f4e7c4db444"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "message."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   o  When the handshake has completed, the server needs to save the",
            "      client_verify_data and server_verify_data values for future use.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cb6b14e1bd26dec4",
                  "f0c5b2de1baa568f",
                  "04210638809eddd3"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "TLS servers implementing this specification MUST ignore any unknown"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cb6b14e1bd26dec4",
                  "f0c5b2de1baa568f",
                  "04210638809eddd3"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "extensions offered by the client and they MUST accept version numbers"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cb6b14e1bd26dec4",
                  "f0c5b2de1baa568f",
                  "04210638809eddd3"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "higher than their highest version number and negotiate the highest"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cb6b14e1bd26dec4",
                  "f0c5b2de1baa568f",
                  "04210638809eddd3"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "common version."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cb6b14e1bd26dec4"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "  These two requirements reiterate preexisting"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cb6b14e1bd26dec4"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "requirements in RFC 5246 and are merely stated here in the interest"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cb6b14e1bd26dec4"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "of forward compatibility."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "15c6e5901c6a6062"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Note that sending a \"renegotiation_info\" extension in response to a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "15c6e5901c6a6062"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "ClientHello containing only the SCSV is an explicit exception to the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "15c6e5901c6a6062"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "prohibition in RFC 5246, Section 7.4.1.4, on the server sending"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "15c6e5901c6a6062"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "unsolicited extensions and is only allowed because the client is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "15c6e5901c6a6062"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "signaling its willingness to receive the extension via the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "15c6e5901c6a6062"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV SCSV."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8de98128f4c6754a",
                  "9b705028fa53a808"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "TLS implementations MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8de98128f4c6754a",
                  "9b705028fa53a808"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "continue to comply with Section 7.4.1.4 for all other extensions."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "42fee3f1bdf70fb9",
            "42fee3f1bdf70fb9",
            "e07d94bf28bf737f",
            "e07d94bf28bf737f",
            "cc866b584e8367e1",
            "cc866b584e8367e1",
            "cc866b584e8367e1",
            "c2610fae3743ec59",
            "c2610fae3743ec59",
            "c2610fae3743ec59",
            "c9d7a35db68e80e0",
            "c9d7a35db68e80e0",
            "c9d7a35db68e80e0",
            "f0c5b2de1baa568f",
            "f0c5b2de1baa568f",
            "f0c5b2de1baa568f",
            "f0c5b2de1baa568f",
            "04210638809eddd3",
            "04210638809eddd3",
            "04210638809eddd3",
            "04210638809eddd3",
            "9b705028fa53a808",
            "9b705028fa53a808"
          ],
          "title": "Server Behavior: Initial Handshake"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.7",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8b19c17ca36ab8c0",
                  "8e3066315172e7a9",
                  "55fb0dc70059d8cb"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "This text applies if the connection's \"secure_renegotiation\" flag is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8b19c17ca36ab8c0",
                  "8e3066315172e7a9",
                  "55fb0dc70059d8cb"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "set to TRUE (if it is set to FALSE, see Section 4.4)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bbce47850d1bdec3",
                  "8468a20e82adc4cb",
                  "e3cbe3d6b92d0f23"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "o  When a ClientHello is received, the server MUST verify that it"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bbce47850d1bdec3",
                  "8468a20e82adc4cb",
                  "e3cbe3d6b92d0f23"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "does not contain the TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV SCSV."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8468a20e82adc4cb",
                  "e3cbe3d6b92d0f23"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5c5c1594f928cc33",
                  "8468a20e82adc4cb",
                  "e3cbe3d6b92d0f23"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "If"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5c5c1594f928cc33",
                  "8468a20e82adc4cb",
                  "e3cbe3d6b92d0f23"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "the SCSV is present, the server MUST abort the handshake."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4544c93b33d908a3",
                  "e1e5e852bb08728a",
                  "4743f154c3462b94",
                  "115c98a0b6be9555"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "o  The server MUST verify that the \"renegotiation_info\" extension is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4544c93b33d908a3",
                  "e1e5e852bb08728a",
                  "4743f154c3462b94",
                  "115c98a0b6be9555"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "present; if it is not, the server MUST abort the handshake."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b874f2aad6f4ff30",
                  "49417f5b2df1c39c",
                  "9a74350847b41a25",
                  "088d7f20abb21fca"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "o  The server MUST verify that the value of the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b874f2aad6f4ff30",
                  "49417f5b2df1c39c",
                  "9a74350847b41a25",
                  "088d7f20abb21fca"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "\"renegotiated_connection\" field is equal to the saved"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b874f2aad6f4ff30",
                  "49417f5b2df1c39c",
                  "9a74350847b41a25",
                  "088d7f20abb21fca"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "client_verify_data value; if it is not, the server MUST abort the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b874f2aad6f4ff30",
                  "49417f5b2df1c39c",
                  "9a74350847b41a25",
                  "088d7f20abb21fca"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "handshake."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "597fb9df89ac7610",
                  "c2003520e2fb07a7",
                  "3e54c106c9ef3a32"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "o  The server MUST include a \"renegotiation_info\" extension"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "597fb9df89ac7610",
                  "c2003520e2fb07a7",
                  "3e54c106c9ef3a32"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "containing the saved client_verify_data and server_verify_data in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "597fb9df89ac7610",
                  "c2003520e2fb07a7",
                  "3e54c106c9ef3a32"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "the ServerHello."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   o  When the handshake has completed, the server needs to save the new",
            "      client_verify_data and server_verify_data values."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "bbce47850d1bdec3",
            "bbce47850d1bdec3",
            "5c5c1594f928cc33",
            "5c5c1594f928cc33",
            "4544c93b33d908a3",
            "4544c93b33d908a3",
            "e1e5e852bb08728a",
            "e1e5e852bb08728a",
            "b874f2aad6f4ff30",
            "b874f2aad6f4ff30",
            "b874f2aad6f4ff30",
            "b874f2aad6f4ff30",
            "49417f5b2df1c39c",
            "49417f5b2df1c39c",
            "49417f5b2df1c39c",
            "49417f5b2df1c39c",
            "597fb9df89ac7610",
            "597fb9df89ac7610",
            "597fb9df89ac7610"
          ],
          "title": "Server Behavior: Secure Renegotiation"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4",
          "lines": [
            "   Existing implementations that do not support this extension are",
            "   widely deployed and, in general, must interoperate with newer",
            "   implementations that do support it.  This section describes",
            "   considerations for backward compatible interoperation."
          ],
          "title": "Backward Compatibility"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.1",
          "lines": [
            "   If a client offers the \"renegotiation_info\" extension or the",
            "   TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV SCSV and the server does not reply",
            "   with \"renegotiation_info\" in the ServerHello, then this indicates",
            "   that the server does not support secure renegotiation.  Because some",
            "   attacks (see Section 1) look like a single handshake to the client,",
            "   the client cannot determine whether or not the connection is under",
            "   attack.  Note, however, that merely because the server does not",
            "   acknowledge the extension does not mean that it is vulnerable; it",
            "   might choose to reject all renegotiations and simply not signal it.",
            "   However, it is not possible for the client to determine purely via",
            "   TLS mechanisms whether or not this is the case.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dc406c5f5841a5dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "If clients wish to ensure that such attacks are impossible, they need"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dc406c5f5841a5dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "to terminate the connection immediately upon failure to receive the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dc406c5f5841a5dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "extension without completing the handshake.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "44b42fc4b4e7ec86",
                  "dc406c5f5841a5dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "Such clients MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "44b42fc4b4e7ec86",
                  "dc406c5f5841a5dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "generate a fatal \"handshake_failure\" alert prior to terminating the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "44b42fc4b4e7ec86",
                  "dc406c5f5841a5dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "connection."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dc406c5f5841a5dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "  However, it is expected that many TLS servers that do"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dc406c5f5841a5dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "not support renegotiation (and thus are not vulnerable) will not"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dc406c5f5841a5dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "support this extension either, so in general, clients that implement"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dc406c5f5841a5dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "this behavior will encounter interoperability problems."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  There is no"
              }
            ],
            "   set of client behaviors that will guarantee security and achieve",
            "   maximum interoperability during the transition period.  Clients need",
            "   to choose one or the other preference when dealing with potentially",
            "   un-upgraded servers."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "44b42fc4b4e7ec86",
            "44b42fc4b4e7ec86",
            "44b42fc4b4e7ec86"
          ],
          "title": "Client Considerations"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.2",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a1b2dc21da92584",
                  "42b600441d3af609"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "This text applies if the connection's \"secure_renegotiation\" flag is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a1b2dc21da92584",
                  "42b600441d3af609"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "set to FALSE."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a1b2dc21da92584",
                  "42b600441d3af609"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "It is possible that un-upgraded servers will request that the client"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a1b2dc21da92584",
                  "42b600441d3af609"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "renegotiate.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "17a73310425663cd",
                  "0a1b2dc21da92584",
                  "42b600441d3af609"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "It is RECOMMENDED that clients refuse this"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "17a73310425663cd",
                  "0a1b2dc21da92584",
                  "42b600441d3af609"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "renegotiation request."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a1b2dc21da92584",
                  "42b600441d3af609"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3b24b0cc29836241",
                  "0a1b2dc21da92584",
                  "42b600441d3af609"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Clients that do so MUST respond to such"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3b24b0cc29836241",
                  "0a1b2dc21da92584",
                  "42b600441d3af609"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "requests with a \"no_renegotiation\" alert (RFC 5246 requires this"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3b24b0cc29836241",
                  "0a1b2dc21da92584",
                  "42b600441d3af609"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "alert to be at the \"warning\" level)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a1b2dc21da92584",
                  "42b600441d3af609"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "  It is possible that the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a1b2dc21da92584",
                  "42b600441d3af609"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "apparently un-upgraded server is in fact an attacker who is then"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a1b2dc21da92584",
                  "42b600441d3af609"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "allowing the client to renegotiate with a different, legitimate,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a1b2dc21da92584",
                  "42b600441d3af609"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "upgraded server."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e6575c3299446461",
                  "5aada95a636d7762"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "If clients nevertheless choose to renegotiate, they"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e6575c3299446461",
                  "5aada95a636d7762"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "MUST behave as described below."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf0a17b8503a1c70",
                  "ec8b8e8e881118d5"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "Clients that choose to renegotiate MUST provide either the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf0a17b8503a1c70",
                  "ec8b8e8e881118d5"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV SCSV or \"renegotiation_info\" in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf0a17b8503a1c70",
                  "ec8b8e8e881118d5"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "their ClientHello."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf0a17b8503a1c70"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "  In a legitimate renegotiation with an un-upgraded"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf0a17b8503a1c70"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "server, that server should ignore both of these signals.  However, if"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf0a17b8503a1c70"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "the server (incorrectly) fails to ignore extensions, sending the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf0a17b8503a1c70"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "\"renegotiation_info\" extension may cause a handshake failure.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf0a17b8503a1c70",
                  "34a17c9799c71750"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "Thus,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf0a17b8503a1c70",
                  "34a17c9799c71750"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "it is permitted, though NOT RECOMMENDED, for the client to simply"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf0a17b8503a1c70",
                  "34a17c9799c71750"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "send the SCSV."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf0a17b8503a1c70"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "  This is the only situation in which clients are"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf0a17b8503a1c70"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "permitted to not send the \"renegotiation_info\" extension in a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf0a17b8503a1c70"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "ClientHello that is used for renegotiation."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Note that in the case of a downgrade attack, if this is an initial",
            "   handshake from the server's perspective, then use of the SCSV from",
            "   the client precludes detection of this attack by the server (if this",
            "   is a renegotiation from the server's perspective, then it will detect",
            "   the attack).  However, the attack will be detected by the client when",
            "   the server sends an empty \"renegotiation_info\" extension and the",
            "   client is expecting one containing the previous verify_data.  By",
            "   contrast, if the client sends the \"renegotiation_info\" extension,",
            "   then the server will immediately detect the attack.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "044b13b11c48e6cc",
                  "411cb11348fe81d7"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "When the ServerHello is received, the client MUST verify that it does"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "044b13b11c48e6cc",
                  "411cb11348fe81d7"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "not contain the \"renegotiation_info\" extension."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "044b13b11c48e6cc"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "044b13b11c48e6cc",
                  "ae7b7b28ecfff407"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "If it does, the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "044b13b11c48e6cc",
                  "ae7b7b28ecfff407"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "client MUST abort the handshake."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "044b13b11c48e6cc"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "  (Because the server has already"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "044b13b11c48e6cc"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "indicated it does not support secure renegotiation, the only way that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "044b13b11c48e6cc"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "this can happen is if the server is broken or there is an attack.)"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "17a73310425663cd",
            "17a73310425663cd",
            "3b24b0cc29836241",
            "3b24b0cc29836241",
            "3b24b0cc29836241",
            "5aada95a636d7762",
            "5aada95a636d7762",
            "ec8b8e8e881118d5",
            "ec8b8e8e881118d5",
            "ec8b8e8e881118d5",
            "34a17c9799c71750",
            "34a17c9799c71750",
            "34a17c9799c71750",
            "411cb11348fe81d7",
            "411cb11348fe81d7",
            "ae7b7b28ecfff407",
            "ae7b7b28ecfff407"
          ],
          "title": "Client Behavior: Legacy (Insecure) Renegotiation"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.3",
          "lines": [
            "   If the client does not offer the \"renegotiation_info\" extension or",
            "   the TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV SCSV, then this indicates that",
            "   the client does not support secure renegotiation.  Although the",
            "   attack described in Section 1 looks like two handshakes to the",
            "",
            "   server, other attacks may be possible in which the renegotiation is",
            "   seen only by the client.  If servers wish to ensure that such attacks",
            "   are impossible, they need to terminate the connection immediately",
            "   upon failure to negotiate the use of secure renegotiation.  Servers",
            "   that do choose to allow connections from unpatched clients can still",
            "   prevent the attack described in Section 1 by refusing to renegotiate",
            "   over those connections.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7ff29782b4e960d4",
                  "3c6e004713d93f76",
                  "82db7560ff84ec18"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "In order to enable clients to probe, even servers that do not support"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7ff29782b4e960d4",
                  "3c6e004713d93f76",
                  "82db7560ff84ec18"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "renegotiation MUST implement the minimal version of the extension"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7ff29782b4e960d4",
                  "3c6e004713d93f76",
                  "82db7560ff84ec18"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "described in this document for initial handshakes, thus signaling"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7ff29782b4e960d4",
                  "3c6e004713d93f76",
                  "82db7560ff84ec18"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "that they have been upgraded."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "7ff29782b4e960d4",
            "7ff29782b4e960d4",
            "7ff29782b4e960d4",
            "7ff29782b4e960d4"
          ],
          "title": "Server Considerations"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.4",
          "lines": [
            "   This text applies if the connection's \"secure_renegotiation\" flag is",
            "   set to FALSE.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3642c873eee05b43",
                  "8be4faa466a149c8"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "It is RECOMMENDED that servers not permit legacy renegotiation."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3642c873eee05b43"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3642c873eee05b43",
                  "4d26b66474218409"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "If"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3642c873eee05b43",
                  "4d26b66474218409"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "servers nevertheless do permit it, they MUST follow the requirements"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3642c873eee05b43",
                  "4d26b66474218409"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "in this section."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cc65989d0b737e29",
                  "871d73ea7e796244"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "o  When a ClientHello is received, the server MUST verify that it"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cc65989d0b737e29",
                  "871d73ea7e796244"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "does not contain the TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV SCSV."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cc65989d0b737e29"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cc65989d0b737e29",
                  "5c8b9749322b41f2"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "If"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cc65989d0b737e29",
                  "5c8b9749322b41f2"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "the SCSV is present, the server MUST abort the handshake."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4f91cb0c70bf2bd5",
                  "fd600a44fb642b25",
                  "60d93122d1afd831"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "o  The server MUST verify that the \"renegotiation_info\" extension is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4f91cb0c70bf2bd5",
                  "fd600a44fb642b25",
                  "60d93122d1afd831"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "not present; if it is, the server MUST abort the handshake."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "8be4faa466a149c8",
            "4d26b66474218409",
            "4d26b66474218409",
            "4d26b66474218409",
            "871d73ea7e796244",
            "871d73ea7e796244",
            "5c8b9749322b41f2",
            "5c8b9749322b41f2",
            "fd600a44fb642b25",
            "fd600a44fb642b25",
            "60d93122d1afd831",
            "60d93122d1afd831"
          ],
          "title": "Server Behavior: Legacy (Insecure) Renegotiation"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.5",
          "lines": [
            "   While SSLv3 is not a protocol under IETF change control (see",
            "   [SSLv3]), it was the original basis for TLS and most TLS",
            "   implementations also support SSLv3.  The IETF encourages SSLv3",
            "   implementations to adopt the \"renegotiation_info\" extension and SCSV",
            "   as defined in this document.  The semantics of the SCSV and extension",
            "   are identical to TLS stacks except for the size of the verify_data",
            "   values, which are 36 bytes long each.  Note that this will require",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   adding at least minimal extension processing to such stacks.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "22a362ea5074be6b",
                  "dd572bdb15f4c247",
                  "9fe0370090e91461",
                  "b0de584713655056"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Clients"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "22a362ea5074be6b",
                  "dd572bdb15f4c247",
                  "9fe0370090e91461",
                  "b0de584713655056"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "that support SSLv3 and offer secure renegotiation (either via SCSV or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "22a362ea5074be6b",
                  "dd572bdb15f4c247",
                  "9fe0370090e91461",
                  "b0de584713655056"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "\"renegotiation_info\") MUST accept the \"renegotiation_info\" extension"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "22a362ea5074be6b",
                  "dd572bdb15f4c247",
                  "9fe0370090e91461",
                  "b0de584713655056"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "from the server, even if the server version is {0x03, 0x00}, and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "22a362ea5074be6b",
                  "dd572bdb15f4c247",
                  "9fe0370090e91461",
                  "b0de584713655056"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "behave as described in this specification."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9fe0370090e91461"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f0e97622f6918264",
                  "ef174da8123ec9bc",
                  "9fe0370090e91461",
                  "03b67ddd687b28be"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "TLS servers that support"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f0e97622f6918264",
                  "ef174da8123ec9bc",
                  "9fe0370090e91461",
                  "03b67ddd687b28be"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "secure renegotiation and support SSLv3 MUST accept SCSV or the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f0e97622f6918264",
                  "ef174da8123ec9bc",
                  "9fe0370090e91461",
                  "03b67ddd687b28be"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "\"renegotiation_info\" extension and respond as described in this"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f0e97622f6918264",
                  "ef174da8123ec9bc",
                  "9fe0370090e91461",
                  "03b67ddd687b28be"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "specification even if the offered client version is {0x03, 0x00}."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5bcfdae8c4bdeada",
                  "2a8ac6ecb268c005"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "SSLv3 does not define the \"no_renegotiation\" alert (and does"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5bcfdae8c4bdeada",
                  "2a8ac6ecb268c005"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "not offer a way to indicate a refusal to renegotiate at a \"warning\""
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5bcfdae8c4bdeada",
                  "2a8ac6ecb268c005"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "level).  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a5aec8a585e0ab32",
                  "5bcfdae8c4bdeada",
                  "2a8ac6ecb268c005"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "SSLv3 clients that refuse renegotiation SHOULD use a fatal"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a5aec8a585e0ab32",
                  "5bcfdae8c4bdeada",
                  "2a8ac6ecb268c005"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "handshake_failure alert."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "22a362ea5074be6b",
            "22a362ea5074be6b",
            "22a362ea5074be6b",
            "22a362ea5074be6b",
            "22a362ea5074be6b",
            "f0e97622f6918264",
            "f0e97622f6918264",
            "f0e97622f6918264",
            "f0e97622f6918264",
            "a5aec8a585e0ab32",
            "a5aec8a585e0ab32"
          ],
          "title": "SSLv3"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5",
          "lines": [
            "   The extension described in this document prevents an attack on TLS.",
            "   If this extension is not used, TLS renegotiation is subject to an",
            "   attack in which the attacker can inject their own conversation with",
            "   the TLS server as a prefix to the client's conversation.  This attack",
            "   is invisible to the client and looks like an ordinary renegotiation",
            "   to the server.  The extension defined in this document allows",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   renegotiation to be performed safely.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "76a0e3b69343d926",
                  "85453d8fe15fd23b"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "Servers SHOULD NOT allow"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "76a0e3b69343d926",
                  "85453d8fe15fd23b"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "clients to renegotiate without using this extension."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Many servers"
              }
            ],
            "   can mitigate this attack simply by refusing to renegotiate at all.",
            "",
            "   While this extension mitigates the man-in-the-middle attack described",
            "   in the overview, it does not resolve all possible problems an",
            "   application may face if it is unaware of renegotiation.  For example,",
            "   during renegotiation, either the client or the server can present a",
            "   different certificate than was used earlier.  This may come as a",
            "   surprise to application developers (who might have expected, for",
            "   example, that a \"getPeerCertificates()\" API call returns the same",
            "   value if called twice), and might be handled in an insecure way.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f86ef1534b322335",
                  "0616745bf9b58291",
                  "97cbaa711dbdaafb",
                  "c4c1c0b2af8a140d"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "TLS implementations SHOULD provide a mechanism to disable and enable"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f86ef1534b322335",
                  "0616745bf9b58291",
                  "97cbaa711dbdaafb",
                  "c4c1c0b2af8a140d"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "renegotiation."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   TLS implementers are encouraged to clearly document how renegotiation",
            "   interacts with the APIs offered to applications (for example, which",
            "   API calls might return different values on different calls, or which",
            "   callbacks might get called multiple times).",
            "",
            "   To make life simpler for applications that use renegotiation but do",
            "   not expect the certificate to change once it has been authenticated,",
            "   TLS implementations may also wish to offer the applications the",
            "   option to abort the renegotiation if the peer tries to authenticate",
            "   with a different certificate and/or different server name (in the",
            "   server_name extension) than was used earlier.  TLS implementations",
            "   may alternatively offer the option to disable renegotiation once the",
            "   client certificate has been authenticated.  However, enabling these",
            "   options by default for all applications could break existing",
            "   applications that depend on using renegotiation to change from one",
            "   certificate to another.  (For example, long-lived TLS connections",
            "   could change to a renewed certificate; or renegotiation could select",
            "   a different cipher suite that requires using a different",
            "   certificate.)",
            "",
            "   Finally, designers of applications that depend on renegotiation are",
            "   reminded that many TLS APIs represent application data as a simple",
            "   octet stream; applications may not be able to determine exactly which",
            "   application data octets were received before, during, or after",
            "   renegotiation.  Especially if the peer presents a different",
            "   certificate during renegotiation, care is needed when specifying how",
            "   the application should handle the data."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "85453d8fe15fd23b",
            "85453d8fe15fd23b",
            "f86ef1534b322335",
            "f86ef1534b322335"
          ],
          "title": "Security Considerations"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6",
          "lines": [
            "   IANA has added the extension code point 65281 (0xff01), which has",
            "   been used for prototype implementations, for the \"renegotiation_info\"",
            "   extension to the TLS ExtensionType values registry.",
            "",
            "   IANA has added TLS cipher suite number 0x00,0xFF with name",
            "   TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV to the TLS Cipher Suite registry."
          ],
          "title": "IANA Considerations"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7",
          "lines": [
            "   This vulnerability was originally discovered by Marsh Ray and",
            "   independently rediscovered by Martin Rex.  The general concept behind",
            "   the extension described here was independently invented by Steve",
            "   Dispensa, Nasko Oskov, and Eric Rescorla with refinements from Nelson",
            "   Bolyard, Pasi Eronen, Michael D'Errico, Stephen Farrell, Michael",
            "   Gray, David-Sarah Hopwood, Ben Laurie, David Makepeace, Bodo Moeller,",
            "   Martin Rex, Peter Robinson, Jesse Walker, Nico Williams, and other",
            "   members of the Project Mogul team and the TLS WG."
          ],
          "title": "Acknowledgements"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-8",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "References"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-8.1",
          "lines": [
            "   [RFC2119]  Bradner, S., \"Key words for use in RFCs to Indicate",
            "              Requirement Levels\", BCP 14, RFC 2119, March 1997.",
            "",
            "   [RFC5246]  Dierks, T. and E. Rescorla, \"The Transport Layer Security",
            "              (TLS) Protocol Version 1.2\", RFC 5246, August 2008."
          ],
          "title": "Normative References"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-8.2",
          "lines": [
            "   [RFC4347]  Rescorla, E. and N. Modadugu, \"Datagram Transport Layer",
            "              Security\", RFC 4347, April 2006.",
            "",
            "   [RFC5056]  Williams, N., \"On the Use of Channel Bindings to Secure",
            "              Channels\", RFC 5056, November 2007.",
            "",
            "   [TLS-CHANNEL-BINDINGS]",
            "              Altman, J., Williams, N., and L. Zhu, \"Channel Bindings",
            "              for TLS\", Work in Progress, October 2009.",
            "",
            "   [RFC2818]  Rescorla, E., \"HTTP Over TLS\", RFC 2818, May 2000.",
            "",
            "   [RFC2965]  Kristol, D. and L. Montulli, \"HTTP State Management",
            "              Mechanism\", RFC 2965, October 2000.",
            "",
            "   [Ray09]    Ray, M., \"Authentication Gap in TLS Renegotiation\",",
            "              November 2009, <http://extendedsubset.com/?p=8>.",
            "",
            "   [SSLv3]    Freier, A., Karlton, P., and P. Kocher, \"The SSL Protocol",
            "              Version 3.0\", Work in Progress, November 1996."
          ],
          "title": "Informative References"
        },
        {
          "id": "name-authors-addresses",
          "lines": [
            "   Eric Rescorla",
            "   RTFM, Inc.",
            "   2064 Edgewood Drive",
            "   Palo Alto, CA  94303",
            "   USA",
            "",
            "   EMail:  ekr@rtfm.com",
            "",
            "   Marsh Ray",
            "   PhoneFactor",
            "   7301 W 129th Street",
            "   Overland Park, KS  66213",
            "   USA",
            "",
            "   EMail:  marsh@extendedsubset.com",
            "",
            "   Steve Dispensa",
            "   PhoneFactor",
            "   7301 W 129th Street",
            "   Overland Park, KS  66213",
            "   USA",
            "",
            "   EMail:  dispensa@phonefactor.com",
            "",
            "   Nasko Oskov",
            "   Microsoft",
            "   One Microsoft Way",
            "   Redmond, WA  98052",
            "   USA",
            "",
            "   EMail:  nasko.oskov@microsoft.com"
          ],
          "title": "Authors' Addresses"
        }
      ]
    },
    "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5869": {
      "format": "ietf",
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "name-abstract",
          "lines": [
            "   This document specifies a simple Hashed Message Authentication Code",
            "   (HMAC)-based key derivation function (HKDF), which can be used as a",
            "   building block in various protocols and applications.  The key",
            "   derivation function (KDF) is intended to support a wide range of",
            "   applications and requirements, and is conservative in its use of",
            "   cryptographic hash functions."
          ],
          "title": "Abstract"
        },
        {
          "id": "name-status-of-this-memo",
          "lines": [
            "   This document is not an Internet Standards Track specification; it is",
            "   published for informational purposes.",
            "",
            "   This document is a product of the Internet Engineering Task Force",
            "   (IETF).  It represents the consensus of the IETF community.  It has",
            "   received public review and has been approved for publication by the",
            "   Internet Engineering Steering Group (IESG).  Not all documents",
            "   approved by the IESG are a candidate for any level of Internet",
            "   Standard; see Section 2 of RFC 5741.",
            "",
            "   Information about the current status of this document, any errata,",
            "   and how to provide feedback on it may be obtained at",
            "   http://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc5869."
          ],
          "title": "Status of This Memo"
        },
        {
          "id": "name-copyright-notice",
          "lines": [
            "   Copyright (c) 2010 IETF Trust and the persons identified as the",
            "   document authors.  All rights reserved.",
            "",
            "   This document is subject to BCP 78 and the IETF Trust's Legal",
            "   Provisions Relating to IETF Documents",
            "   (http://trustee.ietf.org/license-info) in effect on the date of",
            "   publication of this document.  Please review these documents",
            "   carefully, as they describe your rights and restrictions with respect",
            "   to this document.  Code Components extracted from this document must",
            "   include Simplified BSD License text as described in Section 4.e of",
            "   the Trust Legal Provisions and are provided without warranty as",
            "   described in the Simplified BSD License."
          ],
          "title": "Copyright Notice"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-1",
          "lines": [
            "   A key derivation function (KDF) is a basic and essential component of",
            "   cryptographic systems.  Its goal is to take some source of initial",
            "   keying material and derive from it one or more cryptographically",
            "   strong secret keys.",
            "",
            "   This document specifies a simple HMAC-based [HMAC] KDF, named HKDF,",
            "   which can be used as a building block in various protocols and",
            "   applications, and is already used in several IETF protocols,",
            "   including [IKEv2], [PANA], and [EAP-AKA].  The purpose is to document",
            "   this KDF in a general way to facilitate adoption in future protocols",
            "   and applications, and to discourage the proliferation of multiple KDF",
            "   mechanisms.  It is not intended as a call to change existing",
            "   protocols and does not change or update existing specifications using",
            "   this KDF.",
            "",
            "   HKDF follows the \"extract-then-expand\" paradigm, where the KDF",
            "   logically consists of two modules.  The first stage takes the input",
            "   keying material and \"extracts\" from it a fixed-length pseudorandom",
            "   key K.  The second stage \"expands\" the key K into several additional",
            "   pseudorandom keys (the output of the KDF).",
            "",
            "   In many applications, the input keying material is not necessarily",
            "   distributed uniformly, and the attacker may have some partial",
            "   knowledge about it (for example, a Diffie-Hellman value computed by a",
            "   key exchange protocol) or even partial control of it (as in some",
            "   entropy-gathering applications).  Thus, the goal of the \"extract\"",
            "   stage is to \"concentrate\" the possibly dispersed entropy of the input",
            "   keying material into a short, but cryptographically strong,",
            "   pseudorandom key.  In some applications, the input may already be a",
            "   good pseudorandom key; in these cases, the \"extract\" stage is not",
            "   necessary, and the \"expand\" part can be used alone.",
            "",
            "   The second stage \"expands\" the pseudorandom key to the desired",
            "   length; the number and lengths of the output keys depend on the",
            "   specific cryptographic algorithms for which the keys are needed.",
            "",
            "   Note that some existing KDF specifications, such as NIST Special",
            "   Publication 800-56A [800-56A], NIST Special Publication 800-108",
            "   [800-108] and IEEE Standard 1363a-2004 [1363a], either only consider",
            "   the second stage (expanding a pseudorandom key), or do not explicitly",
            "   differentiate between the \"extract\" and \"expand\" stages, often",
            "   resulting in design shortcomings.  The goal of this specification is",
            "   to accommodate a wide range of KDF requirements while minimizing the",
            "   assumptions about the underlying hash function.  The \"extract-then-",
            "   expand\" paradigm supports well this goal (see [HKDF-paper] for more",
            "   information about the design rationale)."
          ],
          "title": "Introduction"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "HMAC-based Key Derivation Function (HKDF)"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.1",
          "lines": [
            "   HMAC-Hash denotes the HMAC function [HMAC] instantiated with hash",
            "   function 'Hash'.  HMAC always has two arguments: the first is a key",
            "   and the second an input (or message).  (Note that in the extract",
            "   step, 'IKM' is used as the HMAC input, not as the HMAC key.)",
            "",
            "   When the message is composed of several elements we use concatenation",
            "   (denoted |) in the second argument; for example, HMAC(K, elem1 |",
            "   elem2 | elem3).",
            "",
            "   The key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\",",
            "   \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and \"OPTIONAL\" in this",
            "   document are to be interpreted as described in [KEYWORDS]."
          ],
          "title": "Notation"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.2",
          "lines": [
            "   HKDF-Extract(salt, IKM) -> PRK",
            "",
            "   Options:",
            "      Hash     a hash function; HashLen denotes the length of the",
            "               hash function output in octets",
            "",
            "   Inputs:",
            "      salt     optional salt value (a non-secret random value);",
            "               if not provided, it is set to a string of HashLen zeros.",
            "      IKM      input keying material",
            "",
            "   Output:",
            "      PRK      a pseudorandom key (of HashLen octets)",
            "",
            "   The output PRK is calculated as follows:",
            "",
            "   PRK = HMAC-Hash(salt, IKM)"
          ],
          "title": "Step 1: Extract"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.3",
          "lines": [
            "   HKDF-Expand(PRK, info, L) -> OKM",
            "",
            "   Options:",
            "      Hash     a hash function; HashLen denotes the length of the",
            "               hash function output in octets",
            "",
            "   Inputs:",
            "      PRK      a pseudorandom key of at least HashLen octets",
            "               (usually, the output from the extract step)",
            "      info     optional context and application specific information",
            "               (can be a zero-length string)",
            "      L        length of output keying material in octets",
            "               (<= 255*HashLen)",
            "",
            "   Output:",
            "      OKM      output keying material (of L octets)",
            "",
            "   The output OKM is calculated as follows:",
            "",
            "   N = ceil(L/HashLen)",
            "   T = T(1) | T(2) | T(3) | ... | T(N)",
            "   OKM = first L octets of T",
            "",
            "   where:",
            "   T(0) = empty string (zero length)",
            "   T(1) = HMAC-Hash(PRK, T(0) | info | 0x01)",
            "   T(2) = HMAC-Hash(PRK, T(1) | info | 0x02)",
            "   T(3) = HMAC-Hash(PRK, T(2) | info | 0x03)",
            "   ...",
            "",
            "   (where the constant concatenated to the end of each T(n) is a",
            "   single octet.)"
          ],
          "title": "Step 2: Expand"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3",
          "lines": [
            "   This section contains a set of guiding principles regarding the use",
            "   of HKDF.  A much more extensive account of such principles and design",
            "   rationale can be found in [HKDF-paper]."
          ],
          "title": "Notes to HKDF Users"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.1",
          "lines": [
            "   HKDF is defined to operate with and without random salt.  This is",
            "   done to accommodate applications where a salt value is not available.",
            "   We stress, however, that the use of salt adds significantly to the",
            "   strength of HKDF, ensuring independence between different uses of the",
            "   hash function, supporting \"source-independent\" extraction, and",
            "   strengthening the analytical results that back the HKDF design.",
            "",
            "   Random salt differs fundamentally from the initial keying material in",
            "   two ways: it is non-secret and can be re-used.  As such, salt values",
            "   are available to many applications.  For example, a pseudorandom",
            "   number generator (PRNG) that continuously produces outputs by",
            "   applying HKDF to renewable pools of entropy (e.g., sampled system",
            "   events) can fix a salt value and use it for multiple applications of",
            "",
            "   HKDF without having to protect the secrecy of the salt.  In a",
            "   different application domain, a key agreement protocol deriving",
            "   cryptographic keys from a Diffie-Hellman exchange can derive a salt",
            "   value from public nonces exchanged and authenticated between",
            "   communicating parties as part of the key agreement (this is the",
            "   approach taken in [IKEv2]).",
            "",
            "   Ideally, the salt value is a random (or pseudorandom) string of the",
            "   length HashLen.  Yet, even a salt value of less quality (shorter in",
            "   size or with limited entropy) may still make a significant",
            "   contribution to the security of the output keying material; designers",
            "   of applications are therefore encouraged to provide salt values to",
            "   HKDF if such values can be obtained by the application.",
            "",
            "   It is worth noting that, while not the typical case, some",
            "   applications may even have a secret salt value available for use; in",
            "   such a case, HKDF provides an even stronger security guarantee.  An",
            "   example of such application is IKEv1 in its \"public-key encryption",
            "   mode\", where the \"salt\" to the extractor is computed from nonces that",
            "   are secret; similarly, the pre-shared mode of IKEv1 uses a secret",
            "   salt derived from the pre-shared key."
          ],
          "title": "To Salt or not to Salt"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.2",
          "lines": [
            "   While the 'info' value is optional in the definition of HKDF, it is",
            "   often of great importance in applications.  Its main objective is to",
            "   bind the derived key material to application- and context-specific",
            "   information.  For example, 'info' may contain a protocol number,",
            "   algorithm identifiers, user identities, etc.  In particular, it may",
            "   prevent the derivation of the same keying material for different",
            "   contexts (when the same input key material (IKM) is used in such",
            "   different contexts).  It may also accommodate additional inputs to",
            "   the key expansion part, if so desired (e.g., an application may want",
            "   to bind the key material to its length L, thus making L part of the",
            "   'info' field).  There is one technical requirement from 'info': it",
            "   should be independent of the input key material value IKM."
          ],
          "title": "The 'info' Input to HKDF"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.3",
          "lines": [
            "   In some applications, the input key material IKM may already be",
            "   present as a cryptographically strong key (for example, the premaster",
            "   secret in TLS RSA cipher suites would be a pseudorandom string,",
            "   except for the first two octets).  In this case, one can skip the",
            "   extract part and use IKM directly to key HMAC in the expand step.  On",
            "   the other hand, applications may still use the extract part for the",
            "   sake of compatibility with the general case.  In particular, if IKM",
            "   is random (or pseudorandom) but longer than an HMAC key, the extract",
            "   step can serve to output a suitable HMAC key (in the case of HMAC",
            "",
            "   this shortening via the extractor is not strictly necessary since",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   HMAC is defined to work with long keys too).  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b339cb10907936ae"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "Note, however, that if"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b339cb10907936ae"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "the IKM is a Diffie-Hellman value, as in the case of TLS with Diffie-"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b339cb10907936ae"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "Hellman, then the extract part SHOULD NOT be skipped."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Doing so would"
              }
            ],
            "   result in using the Diffie-Hellman value g^{xy} itself (which is NOT",
            "   a uniformly random or pseudorandom string) as the key PRK for HMAC.",
            "   Instead, HKDF should apply the extract step to g^{xy} (preferably",
            "   with a salt value) and use the resultant PRK as a key to HMAC in the",
            "   expansion part.",
            "",
            "   In the case where the amount of required key bits, L, is no more than",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   HashLen, one could use PRK directly as the OKM.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d1d98dd5eaba5a06"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "This, however, is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d1d98dd5eaba5a06"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "NOT RECOMMENDED, especially because it would omit the use of 'info'"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d1d98dd5eaba5a06"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "as part of the derivation process (and adding 'info' as an input to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d1d98dd5eaba5a06"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "the extract step is not advisable -- see [HKDF-paper])."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "b339cb10907936ae",
            "b339cb10907936ae",
            "b339cb10907936ae",
            "d1d98dd5eaba5a06",
            "d1d98dd5eaba5a06",
            "d1d98dd5eaba5a06",
            "d1d98dd5eaba5a06"
          ],
          "title": "To Skip or not to Skip"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.4",
          "lines": [
            "   The analysis of key derivation functions assumes that the input",
            "   keying material (IKM) comes from some source modeled as a probability",
            "   distribution over bit streams of a certain length (e.g., streams",
            "   produced by an entropy pool, values derived from Diffie-Hellman",
            "   exponents chosen at random, etc.); each instance of IKM is a sample",
            "   from that distribution.  A major goal of key derivation functions is",
            "   to ensure that, when applying the KDF to any two values IKM and IKM'",
            "   sampled from the (same) source distribution, the resultant keys OKM",
            "   and OKM' are essentially independent of each other (in a statistical",
            "   or computational sense).  To achieve this goal, it is important that",
            "   inputs to KDF are selected from appropriate input distributions and",
            "   also that inputs are chosen independently of each other (technically,",
            "   it is necessary that each sample will have sufficient entropy, even",
            "   when conditioned on other inputs to KDF).",
            "",
            "   Independence is also an important aspect of the salt value provided",
            "   to a KDF.  While there is no need to keep the salt secret, and the",
            "   same salt value can be used with multiple IKM values, it is assumed",
            "   that salt values are independent of the input keying material.  In",
            "   particular, an application needs to make sure that salt values are",
            "   not chosen or manipulated by an attacker.  As an example, consider",
            "   the case (as in IKE) where the salt is derived from nonces supplied",
            "   by the parties in a key exchange protocol.  Before the protocol can",
            "   use such salt to derive keys, it needs to make sure that these nonces",
            "   are authenticated as coming from the legitimate parties rather than",
            "   selected by the attacker (in IKE, for example this authentication is",
            "   an integral part of the authenticated Diffie-Hellman exchange)."
          ],
          "title": "The Role of Independence"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4",
          "lines": [
            "   HKDF is intended for use in a wide variety of KDF applications.",
            "   These include the building of pseudorandom generators from imperfect",
            "   sources of randomness (such as a physical random number generator",
            "   (RNG)); the generation of pseudorandomness out of weak sources of",
            "   randomness, such as entropy collected from system events, user's",
            "   keystrokes, etc.; the derivation of cryptographic keys from a shared",
            "   Diffie-Hellman value in a key-agreement protocol; derivation of",
            "   symmetric keys from a hybrid public-key encryption scheme; key",
            "   derivation for key-wrapping mechanisms; and more.  All of these",
            "   applications can benefit from the simplicity and multi-purpose nature",
            "   of HKDF, as well as from its analytical foundation.",
            "",
            "   On the other hand, it is anticipated that some applications will not",
            "   be able to use HKDF \"as-is\" due to specific operational requirements,",
            "   or will be able to use it but without the full benefits of the",
            "   scheme.  One significant example is the derivation of cryptographic",
            "   keys from a source of low entropy, such as a user's password.  The",
            "   extract step in HKDF can concentrate existing entropy but cannot",
            "   amplify entropy.  In the case of password-based KDFs, a main goal is",
            "   to slow down dictionary attacks using two ingredients: a salt value,",
            "   and the intentional slowing of the key derivation computation.  HKDF",
            "   naturally accommodates the use of salt; however, a slowing down",
            "   mechanism is not part of this specification.  Applications interested",
            "   in a password-based KDF should consider whether, for example, [PKCS5]",
            "   meets their needs better than HKDF."
          ],
          "title": "Applications of HKDF"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5",
          "lines": [
            "   In spite of the simplicity of HKDF, there are many security",
            "   considerations that have been taken into account in the design and",
            "   analysis of this construction.  An exposition of all of these aspects",
            "   is beyond the scope of this document.  Please refer to [HKDF-paper]",
            "   for detailed information, including rationale for the design and for",
            "   the guidelines presented in Section 3.",
            "",
            "   A major effort has been made in the above paper [HKDF-paper] to",
            "   provide a cryptographic analysis of HKDF as a multi-purpose KDF that",
            "   exercises much care in the way it utilizes cryptographic hash",
            "   functions.  This is particularly important due to the limited",
            "   confidence we have in the strength of current hash functions.  This",
            "   analysis, however, does not imply the absolute security of any",
            "   scheme, and it depends heavily on the strength of the underlying hash",
            "   function and on modeling choices.  Yet, it serves as a strong",
            "   indication of the correct structure of the HKDF design and its",
            "   advantages over other common KDF schemes."
          ],
          "title": "Security Considerations"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6",
          "lines": [
            "   The authors would like to thank members of the CFRG (Crypto Forum",
            "   Research Group) list for their useful comments, and to Dan Harkins",
            "   for providing test vectors."
          ],
          "title": "Acknowledgments"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "References"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.1",
          "lines": [
            "   [HMAC]       Krawczyk, H., Bellare, M., and R. Canetti, \"HMAC: Keyed-",
            "                Hashing for Message Authentication\", RFC 2104,",
            "                February 1997.",
            "",
            "   [KEYWORDS]   Bradner, S., \"Key words for use in RFCs to Indicate",
            "                Requirement Levels\", BCP 14, RFC 2119, March 1997.",
            "",
            "   [SHS]        National Institute of Standards and Technology, \"Secure",
            "                Hash Standard\", FIPS PUB 180-3, October 2008."
          ],
          "title": "Normative References"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.2",
          "lines": [
            "   [1363a]      Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers, \"IEEE",
            "                Standard Specifications for Public-Key Cryptography -",
            "                Amendment 1: Additional Techniques\", IEEE Std",
            "                1363a-2004, 2004.",
            "",
            "   [800-108]    National Institute of Standards and Technology,",
            "                \"Recommendation for Key Derivation Using Pseudorandom",
            "                Functions\", NIST Special Publication 800-108,",
            "                November 2008.",
            "",
            "   [800-56A]    National Institute of Standards and Technology,",
            "                \"Recommendation for Pair-Wise Key Establishment Schemes",
            "                Using Discrete Logarithm Cryptography (Revised)\", NIST",
            "                Special Publication 800-56A, March 2007.",
            "",
            "   [EAP-AKA]    Arkko, J., Lehtovirta, V., and P. Eronen, \"Improved",
            "                Extensible Authentication Protocol Method for 3rd",
            "                Generation Authentication and Key Agreement (EAP-AKA')\",",
            "                RFC 5448, May 2009.",
            "",
            "   [HKDF-paper] Krawczyk, H., \"Cryptographic Extraction and Key",
            "                Derivation: The HKDF Scheme\", Proceedings of CRYPTO 2010",
            "                (to appear), 2010, <http://eprint.iacr.org/2010/264>.",
            "",
            "   [IKEv2]      Kaufman, C., Ed., \"Internet Key Exchange (IKEv2)",
            "                Protocol\", RFC 4306, December 2005.",
            "",
            "   [PANA]       Forsberg, D., Ohba, Y., Ed., Patil, B., Tschofenig, H.,",
            "                and A. Yegin, \"Protocol for Carrying Authentication for",
            "                Network Access (PANA)\", RFC 5191, May 2008.",
            "",
            "   [PKCS5]      Kaliski, B., \"PKCS #5: Password-Based Cryptography",
            "                Specification Version 2.0\", RFC 2898, September 2000."
          ],
          "title": "Informative References"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-A",
          "lines": [
            "   This appendix provides test vectors for SHA-256 and SHA-1 hash",
            "   functions [SHS]."
          ],
          "title": "Test Vectors"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-A.1",
          "lines": [
            "   Basic test case with SHA-256",
            "",
            "   Hash = SHA-256",
            "   IKM  = 0x0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b (22 octets)",
            "   salt = 0x000102030405060708090a0b0c (13 octets)",
            "   info = 0xf0f1f2f3f4f5f6f7f8f9 (10 octets)",
            "   L    = 42",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5995f7198499383f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "PRK  = 0x077709362c2e32df0ddc3f0dc47bba63"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5995f7198499383f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "90b6c73bb50f9c3122ec844ad7c2b3e5 (32 octets)"
              }
            ],
            "   OKM  = 0x3cb25f25faacd57a90434f64d0362f2a",
            "          2d2d0a90cf1a5a4c5db02d56ecc4c5bf",
            "          34007208d5b887185865 (42 octets)"
          ],
          "title": "Test Case 1"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-A.2",
          "lines": [
            "   Test with SHA-256 and longer inputs/outputs",
            "",
            "   Hash = SHA-256",
            "   IKM  = 0x000102030405060708090a0b0c0d0e0f",
            "          101112131415161718191a1b1c1d1e1f",
            "          202122232425262728292a2b2c2d2e2f",
            "          303132333435363738393a3b3c3d3e3f",
            "          404142434445464748494a4b4c4d4e4f (80 octets)",
            "   salt = 0x606162636465666768696a6b6c6d6e6f",
            "          707172737475767778797a7b7c7d7e7f",
            "          808182838485868788898a8b8c8d8e8f",
            "          909192939495969798999a9b9c9d9e9f",
            "          a0a1a2a3a4a5a6a7a8a9aaabacadaeaf (80 octets)",
            "   info = 0xb0b1b2b3b4b5b6b7b8b9babbbcbdbebf",
            "          c0c1c2c3c4c5c6c7c8c9cacbcccdcecf",
            "          d0d1d2d3d4d5d6d7d8d9dadbdcdddedf",
            "          e0e1e2e3e4e5e6e7e8e9eaebecedeeef",
            "          f0f1f2f3f4f5f6f7f8f9fafbfcfdfeff (80 octets)",
            "   L    = 82",
            "",
            "   PRK  = 0x06a6b88c5853361a06104c9ceb35b45c",
            "          ef760014904671014a193f40c15fc244 (32 octets)",
            "   OKM  = 0xb11e398dc80327a1c8e7f78c596a4934",
            "          4f012eda2d4efad8a050cc4c19afa97c",
            "          59045a99cac7827271cb41c65e590e09",
            "          da3275600c2f09b8367793a9aca3db71",
            "          cc30c58179ec3e87c14c01d5c1f3434f",
            "          1d87 (82 octets)"
          ],
          "title": "Test Case 2"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-A.3",
          "lines": [
            "   Test with SHA-256 and zero-length salt/info",
            "",
            "   Hash = SHA-256",
            "   IKM  = 0x0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b (22 octets)",
            "   salt = (0 octets)",
            "   info = (0 octets)",
            "   L    = 42",
            "",
            "   PRK  = 0x19ef24a32c717b167f33a91d6f648bdf",
            "          96596776afdb6377ac434c1c293ccb04 (32 octets)",
            "   OKM  = 0x8da4e775a563c18f715f802a063c5a31",
            "          b8a11f5c5ee1879ec3454e5f3c738d2d",
            "          9d201395faa4b61a96c8 (42 octets)"
          ],
          "title": "Test Case 3"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-A.4",
          "lines": [
            "   Basic test case with SHA-1",
            "",
            "   Hash = SHA-1",
            "   IKM  = 0x0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b (11 octets)",
            "   salt = 0x000102030405060708090a0b0c (13 octets)",
            "   info = 0xf0f1f2f3f4f5f6f7f8f9 (10 octets)",
            "   L    = 42",
            "",
            "   PRK  = 0x9b6c18c432a7bf8f0e71c8eb88f4b30baa2ba243 (20 octets)",
            "   OKM  = 0x085a01ea1b10f36933068b56efa5ad81",
            "          a4f14b822f5b091568a9cdd4f155fda2",
            "          c22e422478d305f3f896 (42 octets)"
          ],
          "title": "Test Case 4"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-A.5",
          "lines": [
            "   Test with SHA-1 and longer inputs/outputs",
            "",
            "   Hash = SHA-1",
            "   IKM  = 0x000102030405060708090a0b0c0d0e0f",
            "          101112131415161718191a1b1c1d1e1f",
            "          202122232425262728292a2b2c2d2e2f",
            "          303132333435363738393a3b3c3d3e3f",
            "          404142434445464748494a4b4c4d4e4f (80 octets)",
            "   salt = 0x606162636465666768696a6b6c6d6e6f",
            "          707172737475767778797a7b7c7d7e7f",
            "          808182838485868788898a8b8c8d8e8f",
            "          909192939495969798999a9b9c9d9e9f",
            "          a0a1a2a3a4a5a6a7a8a9aaabacadaeaf (80 octets)",
            "   info = 0xb0b1b2b3b4b5b6b7b8b9babbbcbdbebf",
            "          c0c1c2c3c4c5c6c7c8c9cacbcccdcecf",
            "          d0d1d2d3d4d5d6d7d8d9dadbdcdddedf",
            "          e0e1e2e3e4e5e6e7e8e9eaebecedeeef",
            "          f0f1f2f3f4f5f6f7f8f9fafbfcfdfeff (80 octets)",
            "   L    = 82",
            "",
            "   PRK  = 0x8adae09a2a307059478d309b26c4115a224cfaf6 (20 octets)",
            "   OKM  = 0x0bd770a74d1160f7c9f12cd5912a06eb",
            "          ff6adcae899d92191fe4305673ba2ffe",
            "          8fa3f1a4e5ad79f3f334b3b202b2173c",
            "          486ea37ce3d397ed034c7f9dfeb15c5e",
            "          927336d0441f4c4300e2cff0d0900b52",
            "          d3b4 (82 octets)"
          ],
          "title": "Test Case 5"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-A.6",
          "lines": [
            "   Test with SHA-1 and zero-length salt/info",
            "",
            "   Hash = SHA-1",
            "   IKM  = 0x0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b (22 octets)",
            "   salt = (0 octets)",
            "   info = (0 octets)",
