        {
          "id": "section-1",
          "lines": [
            "   The primary goal of TLS is to provide a secure channel between two",
            "   communicating peers; the only requirement from the underlying",
            "   transport is a reliable, in-order data stream.  Specifically, the",
            "   secure channel should provide the following properties:",
            "",
            "   -  Authentication: The server side of the channel is always",
            "      authenticated; the client side is optionally authenticated.",
            "      Authentication can happen via asymmetric cryptography (e.g., RSA",
            "      [RSA], the Elliptic Curve Digital Signature Algorithm (ECDSA)",
            "      [ECDSA], or the Edwards-Curve Digital Signature Algorithm (EdDSA)",
            "      [RFC8032]) or a symmetric pre-shared key (PSK).",
            "",
            "   -  Confidentiality: Data sent over the channel after establishment is",
            "      only visible to the endpoints.  TLS does not hide the length of",
            "      the data it transmits, though endpoints are able to pad TLS",
            "      records in order to obscure lengths and improve protection against",
            "      traffic analysis techniques.",
            "",
            "   -  Integrity: Data sent over the channel after establishment cannot",
            "      be modified by attackers without detection.",
            "",
            "   These properties should be true even in the face of an attacker who",
            "   has complete control of the network, as described in [RFC3552].  See",
            "   Appendix E for a more complete statement of the relevant security",
            "   properties.",
            "",
            "   TLS consists of two primary components:",
            "",
            "   -  A handshake protocol (Section 4) that authenticates the",
            "      communicating parties, negotiates cryptographic modes and",
            "      parameters, and establishes shared keying material.  The handshake",
            "      protocol is designed to resist tampering; an active attacker",
            "      should not be able to force the peers to negotiate different",
            "      parameters than they would if the connection were not under",
            "      attack.",
            "",
            "   -  A record protocol (Section 5) that uses the parameters established",
            "      by the handshake protocol to protect traffic between the",
            "      communicating peers.  The record protocol divides traffic up into",
            "      a series of records, each of which is independently protected",
            "      using the traffic keys.",
            "",
            "   TLS is application protocol independent; higher-level protocols can",
            "   layer on top of TLS transparently.  The TLS standard, however, does",
            "   not specify how protocols add security with TLS; how to initiate TLS",
            "   handshaking and how to interpret the authentication certificates",
            "   exchanged are left to the judgment of the designers and implementors",
            "   of protocols that run on top of TLS.",
            "",
            "   This document defines TLS version 1.3.  While TLS 1.3 is not directly",
            "   compatible with previous versions, all versions of TLS incorporate a",
            "   versioning mechanism which allows clients and servers to",
            "   interoperably negotiate a common version if one is supported by both",
            "   peers.",
            "",
            "   This document supersedes and obsoletes previous versions of TLS,",
            "   including version 1.2 [RFC5246].  It also obsoletes the TLS ticket",
            "   mechanism defined in [RFC5077] and replaces it with the mechanism",
            "   defined in Section 2.2.  Because TLS 1.3 changes the way keys are",
            "   derived, it updates [RFC5705] as described in Section 7.5.  It also",
            "   changes how Online Certificate Status Protocol (OCSP) messages are",
            "   carried and therefore updates [RFC6066] and obsoletes [RFC6961] as",
            "   described in Section 4.4.2.1."
          ],
          "title": "Introduction"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-1.1",
          "lines": [
            "   The key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\",",
            "   \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"NOT RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and",
            "   \"OPTIONAL\" in this document are to be interpreted as described in",
            "   BCP 14 [RFC2119] [RFC8174] when, and only when, they appear in all",
            "   capitals, as shown here.",
            "",
            "   The following terms are used:",
            "",
            "   client:  The endpoint initiating the TLS connection.",
            "",
            "   connection:  A transport-layer connection between two endpoints.",
            "",
            "   endpoint:  Either the client or server of the connection.",
            "",
            "   handshake:  An initial negotiation between client and server that",
            "      establishes the parameters of their subsequent interactions",
            "      within TLS.",
            "",
            "   peer:  An endpoint.  When discussing a particular endpoint, \"peer\"",
            "      refers to the endpoint that is not the primary subject of",
            "      discussion.",
            "",
            "   receiver:  An endpoint that is receiving records.",
            "",
            "   sender:  An endpoint that is transmitting records.",
            "",
            "   server:  The endpoint that did not initiate the TLS connection."
          ],
          "title": "Conventions and Terminology"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-1.2",
          "lines": [
            "   The following is a list of the major functional differences between",
            "   TLS 1.2 and TLS 1.3.  It is not intended to be exhaustive, and there",
            "   are many minor differences.",
            "",
            "   -  The list of supported symmetric encryption algorithms has been",
            "      pruned of all algorithms that are considered legacy.  Those that",
            "      remain are all Authenticated Encryption with Associated Data",
            "      (AEAD) algorithms.  The cipher suite concept has been changed to",
            "      separate the authentication and key exchange mechanisms from the",
            "      record protection algorithm (including secret key length) and a",
            "      hash to be used with both the key derivation function and",
            "      handshake message authentication code (MAC).",
            "",
            "   -  A zero round-trip time (0-RTT) mode was added, saving a round trip",
            "      at connection setup for some application data, at the cost of",
            "      certain security properties.",
            "",
            "   -  Static RSA and Diffie-Hellman cipher suites have been removed; all",
            "      public-key based key exchange mechanisms now provide forward",
            "      secrecy.",
            "",
            "   -  All handshake messages after the ServerHello are now encrypted.",
            "      The newly introduced EncryptedExtensions message allows various",
            "      extensions previously sent in the clear in the ServerHello to also",
            "      enjoy confidentiality protection.",
            "",
            "   -  The key derivation functions have been redesigned.  The new design",
            "      allows easier analysis by cryptographers due to their improved key",
            "      separation properties.  The HMAC-based Extract-and-Expand Key",
            "      Derivation Function (HKDF) is used as an underlying primitive.",
            "",
            "   -  The handshake state machine has been significantly restructured to",
            "      be more consistent and to remove superfluous messages such as",
            "      ChangeCipherSpec (except when needed for middlebox compatibility).",
            "",
            "   -  Elliptic curve algorithms are now in the base spec, and new",
            "      signature algorithms, such as EdDSA, are included.  TLS 1.3",
            "      removed point format negotiation in favor of a single point format",
            "      for each curve.",
            "",
            "   -  Other cryptographic improvements were made, including changing the",
            "      RSA padding to use the RSA Probabilistic Signature Scheme",
            "      (RSASSA-PSS), and the removal of compression, the Digital",
            "      Signature Algorithm (DSA), and custom Ephemeral Diffie-Hellman",
            "      (DHE) groups.",
            "",
            "   -  The TLS 1.2 version negotiation mechanism has been deprecated in",
            "      favor of a version list in an extension.  This increases",
            "      compatibility with existing servers that incorrectly implemented",
            "      version negotiation.",
            "",
            "   -  Session resumption with and without server-side state as well as",
            "      the PSK-based cipher suites of earlier TLS versions have been",
            "      replaced by a single new PSK exchange.",
            "",
            "   -  References have been updated to point to the updated versions of",
            "      RFCs, as appropriate (e.g., RFC 5280 rather than RFC 3280)."
          ],
          "title": "Major Differences from TLS 1.2"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-1.3",
          "lines": [
            "   This document defines several changes that optionally affect",
            "   implementations of TLS 1.2, including those which do not also support",
            "   TLS 1.3:",
            "",
            "   -  A version downgrade protection mechanism is described in",
            "      Section 4.1.3.",
            "",
            "   -  RSASSA-PSS signature schemes are defined in Section 4.2.3.",
            "",
            "   -  The \"supported_versions\" ClientHello extension can be used to",
            "      negotiate the version of TLS to use, in preference to the",
            "      legacy_version field of the ClientHello.",
            "",
            "   -  The \"signature_algorithms_cert\" extension allows a client to",
            "      indicate which signature algorithms it can validate in X.509",
            "      certificates.",
            "",
            "   Additionally, this document clarifies some compliance requirements",
            "   for earlier versions of TLS; see Section 9.3."
          ],
          "title": "Updates Affecting TLS 1.2"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2",
          "lines": [
            "   The cryptographic parameters used by the secure channel are produced",
            "   by the TLS handshake protocol.  This sub-protocol of TLS is used by",
            "   the client and server when first communicating with each other.  The",
            "   handshake protocol allows peers to negotiate a protocol version,",
            "   select cryptographic algorithms, optionally authenticate each other,",
            "   and establish shared secret keying material.  Once the handshake is",
            "   complete, the peers use the established keys to protect the",
            "   application-layer traffic.",
            "",
            "   A failure of the handshake or other protocol error triggers the",
            "   termination of the connection, optionally preceded by an alert",
            "   message (Section 6).",
            "",
            "   TLS supports three basic key exchange modes:",
            "",
            "   -  (EC)DHE (Diffie-Hellman over either finite fields or elliptic",
            "      curves)",
            "",
            "   -  PSK-only",
            "",
            "   -  PSK with (EC)DHE",
            "",
            "   Figure 1 below shows the basic full TLS handshake:",
            "",
            "       Client                                           Server",
            "",
            "Key  ^ ClientHello",
            "Exch | + key_share*",
            "     | + signature_algorithms*",
            "     | + psk_key_exchange_modes*",
            "     v + pre_shared_key*       -------->",
            "                                                  ServerHello  ^ Key",
            "                                                 + key_share*  | Exch",
            "                                            + pre_shared_key*  v",
            "                                        {EncryptedExtensions}  ^  Server",
            "                                        {CertificateRequest*}  v  Params",
            "                                               {Certificate*}  ^",
            "                                         {CertificateVerify*}  | Auth",
            "                                                   {Finished}  v",
            "                               <--------  [Application Data*]",
            "     ^ {Certificate*}",
            "Auth | {CertificateVerify*}",
            "     v {Finished}              -------->",
            "       [Application Data]      <------->  [Application Data]",
            "",
            "              +  Indicates noteworthy extensions sent in the",
            "                 previously noted message.",
            "",
            "              *  Indicates optional or situation-dependent",
            "                 messages/extensions that are not always sent.",
            "",
            "              {} Indicates messages protected using keys",
            "                 derived from a [sender]_handshake_traffic_secret.",
            "",
            "              [] Indicates messages protected using keys",
            "                 derived from [sender]_application_traffic_secret_N.",
            "",
            "               Figure 1: Message Flow for Full TLS Handshake",
            "",
            "   The handshake can be thought of as having three phases (indicated in",
            "   the diagram above):",
            "",
            "   -  Key Exchange: Establish shared keying material and select the",
            "      cryptographic parameters.  Everything after this phase is",
            "      encrypted.",
            "",
            "   -  Server Parameters: Establish other handshake parameters",
            "      (whether the client is authenticated, application-layer protocol",
            "      support, etc.).",
            "",
            "   -  Authentication: Authenticate the server (and, optionally, the",
            "      client) and provide key confirmation and handshake integrity.",
            "",
            "   In the Key Exchange phase, the client sends the ClientHello",
            "   (Section 4.1.2) message, which contains a random nonce",
            "   (ClientHello.random); its offered protocol versions; a list of",
            "   symmetric cipher/HKDF hash pairs; either a set of Diffie-Hellman key",
            "   shares (in the \"key_share\" (Section 4.2.8) extension), a set of",
            "   pre-shared key labels (in the \"pre_shared_key\" (Section 4.2.11)",
            "   extension), or both; and potentially additional extensions.",
            "   Additional fields and/or messages may also be present for middlebox",
            "   compatibility.",
            "",
            "   The server processes the ClientHello and determines the appropriate",
            "   cryptographic parameters for the connection.  It then responds with",
            "   its own ServerHello (Section 4.1.3), which indicates the negotiated",
            "   connection parameters.  The combination of the ClientHello and the",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   ServerHello determines the shared keys.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "75d473a313035a90"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If (EC)DHE key establishment"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "75d473a313035a90"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "is in use, then the ServerHello contains a \"key_share\" extension with"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "75d473a313035a90"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "the server's ephemeral Diffie-Hellman share; the server's share MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "75d473a313035a90"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "be in the same group as one of the client's shares."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  If PSK key"
              }
            ],
            "   establishment is in use, then the ServerHello contains a",
            "   \"pre_shared_key\" extension indicating which of the client's offered",
            "   PSKs was selected.  Note that implementations can use (EC)DHE and PSK",
            "   together, in which case both extensions will be supplied.",
            "",
            "   The server then sends two messages to establish the Server",
            "   Parameters:",
            "",
            "   EncryptedExtensions:  responses to ClientHello extensions that are",
            "      not required to determine the cryptographic parameters, other than",
            "      those that are specific to individual certificates.",
            "      [Section 4.3.1]",
            "",
            "   CertificateRequest:  if certificate-based client authentication is",
            "      desired, the desired parameters for that certificate.  This",
            "      message is omitted if client authentication is not desired.",
            "      [Section 4.3.2]",
            "",
            "   Finally, the client and server exchange Authentication messages.  TLS",
            "   uses the same set of messages every time that certificate-based",
            "   authentication is needed.  (PSK-based authentication happens as a",
            "   side effect of key exchange.)  Specifically:",
            "",
            "   Certificate:  The certificate of the endpoint and any per-certificate",
            "      extensions.  This message is omitted by the server if not",
            "      authenticating with a certificate and by the client if the server",
            "      did not send CertificateRequest (thus indicating that the client",
            "      should not authenticate with a certificate).  Note that if raw",
            "      public keys [RFC7250] or the cached information extension",
            "      [RFC7924] are in use, then this message will not contain a",
            "      certificate but rather some other value corresponding to the",
            "      server's long-term key.  [Section 4.4.2]",
            "",
            "   CertificateVerify:  A signature over the entire handshake using the",
            "      private key corresponding to the public key in the Certificate",
            "      message.  This message is omitted if the endpoint is not",
            "      authenticating via a certificate.  [Section 4.4.3]",
            "",
            "   Finished:  A MAC (Message Authentication Code) over the entire",
            "      handshake.  This message provides key confirmation, binds the",
            "      endpoint's identity to the exchanged keys, and in PSK mode also",
            "      authenticates the handshake.  [Section 4.4.4]",
            "",
            "   Upon receiving the server's messages, the client responds with its",
            "   Authentication messages, namely Certificate and CertificateVerify (if",
            "   requested), and Finished.",
            "",
            "   At this point, the handshake is complete, and the client and server",
            "   derive the keying material required by the record layer to exchange",
            "   application-layer data protected through authenticated encryption.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "38850007859c392a"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Application Data MUST NOT be sent prior to sending the Finished"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "38850007859c392a"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "message, except as specified in Section 2.3."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Note that while the"
              }
            ],
            "   server may send Application Data prior to receiving the client's",
            "   Authentication messages, any data sent at that point is, of course,",
            "   being sent to an unauthenticated peer."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "75d473a313035a90",
            "75d473a313035a90",
            "75d473a313035a90",
            "75d473a313035a90",
            "38850007859c392a",
            "38850007859c392a"
          ],
          "title": "Protocol Overview"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.1",
          "lines": [
            "   If the client has not provided a sufficient \"key_share\" extension",
            "   (e.g., it includes only DHE or ECDHE groups unacceptable to or",
            "   unsupported by the server), the server corrects the mismatch with a",
            "   HelloRetryRequest and the client needs to restart the handshake with",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   an appropriate \"key_share\" extension, as shown in Figure 2.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b10dfa8c5b12ee19"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If no"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b10dfa8c5b12ee19"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "common cryptographic parameters can be negotiated, the server MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b10dfa8c5b12ee19"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "abort the handshake with an appropriate alert."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "        Client                                               Server",
            "",
            "        ClientHello",
            "        + key_share             -------->",
            "                                                  HelloRetryRequest",
            "                                <--------               + key_share",
            "        ClientHello",
            "        + key_share             -------->",
            "                                                        ServerHello",
            "                                                        + key_share",
            "                                              {EncryptedExtensions}",
            "                                              {CertificateRequest*}",
            "                                                     {Certificate*}",
            "                                               {CertificateVerify*}",
            "                                                         {Finished}",
            "                                <--------       [Application Data*]",
            "        {Certificate*}",
            "        {CertificateVerify*}",
            "        {Finished}              -------->",
            "        [Application Data]      <------->        [Application Data]",
            "",
            "             Figure 2: Message Flow for a Full Handshake with",
            "                           Mismatched Parameters",
            "",
            "   Note: The handshake transcript incorporates the initial",
            "   ClientHello/HelloRetryRequest exchange; it is not reset with the",
            "   new ClientHello.",
            "",
            "   TLS also allows several optimized variants of the basic handshake, as",
            "   described in the following sections."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "b10dfa8c5b12ee19",
            "b10dfa8c5b12ee19",
            "b10dfa8c5b12ee19"
          ],
          "title": "Incorrect DHE Share"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.2",
          "lines": [
            "   Although TLS PSKs can be established out of band, PSKs can also be",
            "   established in a previous connection and then used to establish a new",
            "   connection (\"session resumption\" or \"resuming\" with a PSK).  Once a",
            "   handshake has completed, the server can send the client a PSK",
            "   identity that corresponds to a unique key derived from the initial",
            "   handshake (see Section 4.6.1).  The client can then use that PSK",
            "   identity in future handshakes to negotiate the use of the associated",
            "   PSK.  If the server accepts the PSK, then the security context of the",
            "   new connection is cryptographically tied to the original connection",
            "   and the key derived from the initial handshake is used to bootstrap",
            "   the cryptographic state instead of a full handshake.  In TLS 1.2 and",
            "   below, this functionality was provided by \"session IDs\" and \"session",
            "   tickets\" [RFC5077].  Both mechanisms are obsoleted in TLS 1.3.",
            "",
            "   PSKs can be used with (EC)DHE key exchange in order to provide",
            "   forward secrecy in combination with shared keys, or can be used",
            "   alone, at the cost of losing forward secrecy for the application",
            "   data.",
            "",
            "   Figure 3 shows a pair of handshakes in which the first handshake",
            "   establishes a PSK and the second handshake uses it:",
            "",
            "          Client                                               Server",
            "",
            "   Initial Handshake:",
            "          ClientHello",
            "          + key_share               -------->",
            "                                                          ServerHello",
            "                                                          + key_share",
            "                                                {EncryptedExtensions}",
            "                                                {CertificateRequest*}",
            "                                                       {Certificate*}",
            "                                                 {CertificateVerify*}",
            "                                                           {Finished}",
            "                                    <--------     [Application Data*]",
            "          {Certificate*}",
            "          {CertificateVerify*}",
            "          {Finished}                -------->",
            "                                    <--------      [NewSessionTicket]",
            "          [Application Data]        <------->      [Application Data]",
            "",
            "   Subsequent Handshake:",
            "          ClientHello",
            "          + key_share*",
            "          + pre_shared_key          -------->",
            "                                                          ServerHello",
            "                                                     + pre_shared_key",
            "                                                         + key_share*",
            "                                                {EncryptedExtensions}",
            "                                                           {Finished}",
            "                                    <--------     [Application Data*]",
            "          {Finished}                -------->",
            "          [Application Data]        <------->      [Application Data]",
            "",
            "               Figure 3: Message Flow for Resumption and PSK",
            "",
            "   As the server is authenticating via a PSK, it does not send a",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   Certificate or a CertificateVerify message.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "97f6e2d3dfd9cd33"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "When a client offers"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "97f6e2d3dfd9cd33"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "resumption via a PSK, it SHOULD also supply a \"key_share\" extension"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "97f6e2d3dfd9cd33"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "to the server to allow the server to decline resumption and fall back"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "97f6e2d3dfd9cd33"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "to a full handshake, if needed."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  The server responds with a"
              }
            ],
            "   \"pre_shared_key\" extension to negotiate the use of PSK key",
            "   establishment and can (as shown here) respond with a \"key_share\"",
            "   extension to do (EC)DHE key establishment, thus providing forward",
            "   secrecy.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cd50d0124ec4eee9"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "When PSKs are provisioned out of band, the PSK identity and the KDF"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cd50d0124ec4eee9"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "hash algorithm to be used with the PSK MUST also be provisioned."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Note:  When using an out-of-band provisioned pre-shared secret, a",
            "      critical consideration is using sufficient entropy during the key",
            "      generation, as discussed in [RFC4086].  Deriving a shared secret",
            "      from a password or other low-entropy sources is not secure.  A",
            "      low-entropy secret, or password, is subject to dictionary attacks",
            "      based on the PSK binder.  The specified PSK authentication is not",
            "      a strong password-based authenticated key exchange even when used",
            "      with Diffie-Hellman key establishment.  Specifically, it does not",
            "      prevent an attacker that can observe the handshake from performing",
            "      a brute-force attack on the password/pre-shared key."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "97f6e2d3dfd9cd33",
            "97f6e2d3dfd9cd33",
            "97f6e2d3dfd9cd33",
            "97f6e2d3dfd9cd33",
            "cd50d0124ec4eee9",
            "cd50d0124ec4eee9"
          ],
          "title": "Resumption and Pre-Shared Key (PSK)"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.3",
          "lines": [
            "   When clients and servers share a PSK (either obtained externally or",
            "   via a previous handshake), TLS 1.3 allows clients to send data on the",
            "   first flight (\"early data\").  The client uses the PSK to authenticate",
            "   the server and to encrypt the early data.",
            "",
            "   As shown in Figure 4, the 0-RTT data is just added to the 1-RTT",
            "   handshake in the first flight.  The rest of the handshake uses the",
            "   same messages as for a 1-RTT handshake with PSK resumption.",
            "",
            "         Client                                               Server",
            "",
            "         ClientHello",
            "         + early_data",
            "         + key_share*",
            "         + psk_key_exchange_modes",
            "         + pre_shared_key",
            "         (Application Data*)     -------->",
            "                                                         ServerHello",
            "                                                    + pre_shared_key",
            "                                                        + key_share*",
            "                                               {EncryptedExtensions}",
            "                                                       + early_data*",
            "                                                          {Finished}",
            "                                 <--------       [Application Data*]",
            "         (EndOfEarlyData)",
            "         {Finished}              -------->",
            "         [Application Data]      <------->        [Application Data]",
            "",
            "               +  Indicates noteworthy extensions sent in the",
            "                  previously noted message.",
            "",
            "               *  Indicates optional or situation-dependent",
            "                  messages/extensions that are not always sent.",
            "",
            "               () Indicates messages protected using keys",
            "                  derived from a client_early_traffic_secret.",
            "",
            "               {} Indicates messages protected using keys",
            "                  derived from a [sender]_handshake_traffic_secret.",
            "",
            "               [] Indicates messages protected using keys",
            "                  derived from [sender]_application_traffic_secret_N.",
            "",
            "               Figure 4: Message Flow for a 0-RTT Handshake",
            "",
            "   IMPORTANT NOTE: The security properties for 0-RTT data are weaker",
            "   than those for other kinds of TLS data.  Specifically:",
            "",
            "   1.  This data is not forward secret, as it is encrypted solely under",
            "       keys derived using the offered PSK.",
            "",
            "   2.  There are no guarantees of non-replay between connections.",
            "       Protection against replay for ordinary TLS 1.3 1-RTT data is",
            "       provided via the server's Random value, but 0-RTT data does not",
            "       depend on the ServerHello and therefore has weaker guarantees.",
            "       This is especially relevant if the data is authenticated either",
            "       with TLS client authentication or inside the application",
            "       protocol.  The same warnings apply to any use of the",
            "       early_exporter_master_secret.",
            "",
            "   0-RTT data cannot be duplicated within a connection (i.e., the server",
            "   will not process the same data twice for the same connection), and an",
            "   attacker will not be able to make 0-RTT data appear to be 1-RTT data",
            "   (because it is protected with different keys).  Appendix E.5 contains",
            "   a description of potential attacks, and Section 8 describes",
            "   mechanisms which the server can use to limit the impact of replay."
          ],
          "title": "0-RTT Data"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3",
          "lines": [
            "   This document deals with the formatting of data in an external",
            "   representation.  The following very basic and somewhat casually",
            "   defined presentation syntax will be used."
          ],
          "title": "Presentation Language"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.1",
          "lines": [
            "   The representation of all data items is explicitly specified.  The",
            "   basic data block size is one byte (i.e., 8 bits).  Multiple-byte data",
            "   items are concatenations of bytes, from left to right, from top to",
            "   bottom.  From the byte stream, a multi-byte item (a numeric in the",
            "   following example) is formed (using C notation) by:",
            "",
            "      value = (byte[0] << 8*(n-1)) | (byte[1] << 8*(n-2)) |",
            "              ... | byte[n-1];",
            "",
            "   This byte ordering for multi-byte values is the commonplace network",
            "   byte order or big-endian format."
          ],
          "title": "Basic Block Size"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.2",
          "lines": [
            "   Comments begin with \"/*\" and end with \"*/\".",
            "",
            "   Optional components are denoted by enclosing them in \"[[ ]]\" (double",
            "   brackets).",
            "",
            "   Single-byte entities containing uninterpreted data are of",
            "   type opaque.",
            "",
            "   A type alias T' for an existing type T is defined by:",
            "",
            "      T T';"
          ],
          "title": "Miscellaneous"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.3",
          "lines": [
            "   The basic numeric data type is an unsigned byte (uint8).  All larger",
            "   numeric data types are constructed from a fixed-length series of",
            "   bytes concatenated as described in Section 3.1 and are also unsigned.",
            "   The following numeric types are predefined.",
            "",
            "      uint8 uint16[2];",
            "      uint8 uint24[3];",
            "      uint8 uint32[4];",
            "      uint8 uint64[8];",
            "",
            "   All values, here and elsewhere in the specification, are transmitted",
            "   in network byte (big-endian) order; the uint32 represented by the hex",
            "   bytes 01 02 03 04 is equivalent to the decimal value 16909060."
          ],
          "title": "Numbers"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.4",
          "lines": [
            "   A vector (single-dimensioned array) is a stream of homogeneous data",
            "   elements.  The size of the vector may be specified at documentation",
            "   time or left unspecified until runtime.  In either case, the length",
            "   declares the number of bytes, not the number of elements, in the",
            "   vector.  The syntax for specifying a new type, T', that is a fixed-",
            "   length vector of type T is",
            "",
            "      T T'[n];",
            "",
            "   Here, T' occupies n bytes in the data stream, where n is a multiple",
            "   of the size of T.  The length of the vector is not included in the",
            "   encoded stream.",
            "",
            "   In the following example, Datum is defined to be three consecutive",
            "   bytes that the protocol does not interpret, while Data is three",
            "   consecutive Datum, consuming a total of nine bytes.",
            "",
            "      opaque Datum[3];      /* three uninterpreted bytes */",
            "      Datum Data[9];        /* three consecutive 3-byte vectors */",
            "",
            "   Variable-length vectors are defined by specifying a subrange of legal",
            "   lengths, inclusively, using the notation <floor..ceiling>.  When",
            "   these are encoded, the actual length precedes the vector's contents",
            "   in the byte stream.  The length will be in the form of a number",
            "   consuming as many bytes as required to hold the vector's specified",
            "   maximum (ceiling) length.  A variable-length vector with an actual",
            "   length field of zero is referred to as an empty vector.",
            "",
            "      T T'<floor..ceiling>;",
            "",
            "   In the following example, \"mandatory\" is a vector that must contain",
            "   between 300 and 400 bytes of type opaque.  It can never be empty.",
            "   The actual length field consumes two bytes, a uint16, which is",
            "   sufficient to represent the value 400 (see Section 3.3).  Similarly,",
            "   \"longer\" can represent up to 800 bytes of data, or 400 uint16",
            "   elements, and it may be empty.  Its encoding will include a two-byte",
            "   actual length field prepended to the vector.  The length of an",
            "   encoded vector must be an exact multiple of the length of a single",
            "   element (e.g., a 17-byte vector of uint16 would be illegal).",
            "",
            "      opaque mandatory<300..400>;",
            "            /* length field is two bytes, cannot be empty */",
            "      uint16 longer<0..800>;",
            "            /* zero to 400 16-bit unsigned integers */"
          ],
          "title": "Vectors"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.5",
          "lines": [
            "   An additional sparse data type, called \"enum\" or \"enumerated\", is",
            "   available.  Each definition is a different type.  Only enumerateds of",
            "   the same type may be assigned or compared.  Every element of an",
            "   enumerated must be assigned a value, as demonstrated in the following",
            "   example.  Since the elements of the enumerated are not ordered, they",
            "   can be assigned any unique value, in any order.",
            "",
            "      enum { e1(v1), e2(v2), ... , en(vn) [[, (n)]] } Te;",
            "",
            "   Future extensions or additions to the protocol may define new values.",
            "   Implementations need to be able to parse and ignore unknown values",
            "   unless the definition of the field states otherwise.",
            "",
            "   An enumerated occupies as much space in the byte stream as would its",
            "   maximal defined ordinal value.  The following definition would cause",
            "   one byte to be used to carry fields of type Color.",
            "",
            "      enum { red(3), blue(5), white(7) } Color;",
            "",
            "   One may optionally specify a value without its associated tag to",
            "   force the width definition without defining a superfluous element.",
            "",
            "   In the following example, Taste will consume two bytes in the data",
            "   stream but can only assume the values 1, 2, or 4 in the current",
            "   version of the protocol.",
            "",
            "      enum { sweet(1), sour(2), bitter(4), (32000) } Taste;",
            "",
            "   The names of the elements of an enumeration are scoped within the",
            "   defined type.  In the first example, a fully qualified reference to",
            "   the second element of the enumeration would be Color.blue.  Such",
            "   qualification is not required if the target of the assignment is well",
            "   specified.",
            "",
            "      Color color = Color.blue;     /* overspecified, legal */",
            "      Color color = blue;           /* correct, type implicit */",
            "",
            "   The names assigned to enumerateds do not need to be unique.  The",
            "   numerical value can describe a range over which the same name",
            "   applies.  The value includes the minimum and maximum inclusive values",
            "   in that range, separated by two period characters.  This is",
            "   principally useful for reserving regions of the space.",
            "",
            "      enum { sad(0), meh(1..254), happy(255) } Mood;"
          ],
          "title": "Enumerateds"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.6",
          "lines": [
            "   Structure types may be constructed from primitive types for",
            "   convenience.  Each specification declares a new, unique type.  The",
            "   syntax used for definitions is much like that of C.",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          T1 f1;",
            "          T2 f2;",
            "          ...",
            "          Tn fn;",
            "      } T;",
            "",
            "   Fixed- and variable-length vector fields are allowed using the",
            "   standard vector syntax.  Structures V1 and V2 in the variants example",
            "   (Section 3.8) demonstrate this.",
            "",
            "   The fields within a structure may be qualified using the type's name,",
            "   with a syntax much like that available for enumerateds.  For example,",
            "   T.f2 refers to the second field of the previous declaration."
          ],
          "title": "Constructed Types"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.7",
          "lines": [
            "   Fields and variables may be assigned a fixed value using \"=\", as in:",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          T1 f1 = 8;  /* T.f1 must always be 8 */",
            "          T2 f2;",
            "      } T;"
          ],
          "title": "Constants"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.8",
          "lines": [
            "   Defined structures may have variants based on some knowledge that is",
            "   available within the environment.  The selector must be an enumerated",
            "   type that defines the possible variants the structure defines.  Each",
            "   arm of the select (below) specifies the type of that variant's field",
            "   and an optional field label.  The mechanism by which the variant is",
            "   selected at runtime is not prescribed by the presentation language.",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          T1 f1;",
            "          T2 f2;",
            "          ....",
            "          Tn fn;",
            "          select (E) {",
            "              case e1: Te1 [[fe1]];",
            "              case e2: Te2 [[fe2]];",
            "              ....",
            "              case en: Ten [[fen]];",
            "          };",
            "      } Tv;",
            "",
            "   For example:",
            "",
            "      enum { apple(0), orange(1) } VariantTag;",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          uint16 number;",
            "          opaque string<0..10>; /* variable length */",
            "      } V1;",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          uint32 number;",
            "          opaque string[10];    /* fixed length */",
            "      } V2;",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          VariantTag type;",
            "          select (VariantRecord.type) {",
            "              case apple:  V1;",
            "              case orange: V2;",
            "          };",
            "      } VariantRecord;"
          ],
          "title": "Variants"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4",
          "lines": [
            "   The handshake protocol is used to negotiate the security parameters",
            "   of a connection.  Handshake messages are supplied to the TLS record",
            "   layer, where they are encapsulated within one or more TLSPlaintext or",
            "   TLSCiphertext structures which are processed and transmitted as",
            "   specified by the current active connection state.",
            "",
            "      enum {",
            "          client_hello(1),",
            "          server_hello(2),",
            "          new_session_ticket(4),",
            "          end_of_early_data(5),",
            "          encrypted_extensions(8),",
            "          certificate(11),",
            "          certificate_request(13),",
            "          certificate_verify(15),",
            "          finished(20),",
            "          key_update(24),",
            "          message_hash(254),",
            "          (255)",
            "      } HandshakeType;",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          HandshakeType msg_type;    /* handshake type */",
            "          uint24 length;             /* remaining bytes in message */",
            "          select (Handshake.msg_type) {",
            "              case client_hello:          ClientHello;",
            "              case server_hello:          ServerHello;",
            "              case end_of_early_data:     EndOfEarlyData;",
            "              case encrypted_extensions:  EncryptedExtensions;",
            "              case certificate_request:   CertificateRequest;",
            "              case certificate:           Certificate;",
            "              case certificate_verify:    CertificateVerify;",
            "              case finished:              Finished;",
            "              case new_session_ticket:    NewSessionTicket;",
            "              case key_update:            KeyUpdate;",
            "          };",
            "      } Handshake;",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "51cc0ba4bb43053e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Protocol messages MUST be sent in the order defined in Section 4.4.1"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "51cc0ba4bb43053e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "and shown in the diagrams in Section 2."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "582063b0b4f85d4f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "A peer which receives a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "582063b0b4f85d4f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "handshake message in an unexpected order MUST abort the handshake"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "582063b0b4f85d4f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "with an \"unexpected_message\" alert."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   New handshake message types are assigned by IANA as described in",
            "   Section 11."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "51cc0ba4bb43053e",
            "51cc0ba4bb43053e",
            "582063b0b4f85d4f",
            "582063b0b4f85d4f",
            "582063b0b4f85d4f"
          ],
          "title": "Handshake Protocol"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.1",
          "lines": [
            "   The key exchange messages are used to determine the security",
            "   capabilities of the client and the server and to establish shared",
            "   secrets, including the traffic keys used to protect the rest of the",
            "   handshake and the data."
          ],
          "title": "Key Exchange Messages"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.1.1",
          "lines": [
            "   In TLS, the cryptographic negotiation proceeds by the client offering",
            "   the following four sets of options in its ClientHello:",
            "",
            "   -  A list of cipher suites which indicates the AEAD algorithm/HKDF",
            "      hash pairs which the client supports.",
            "",
            "   -  A \"supported_groups\" (Section 4.2.7) extension which indicates the",
            "      (EC)DHE groups which the client supports and a \"key_share\"",
            "      (Section 4.2.8) extension which contains (EC)DHE shares for some",
            "      or all of these groups.",
            "",
            "   -  A \"signature_algorithms\" (Section 4.2.3) extension which indicates",
            "      the signature algorithms which the client can accept.  A",
            "      \"signature_algorithms_cert\" extension (Section 4.2.3) may also be",
            "      added to indicate certificate-specific signature algorithms.",
            "",
            "   -  A \"pre_shared_key\" (Section 4.2.11) extension which contains a",
            "      list of symmetric key identities known to the client and a",
            "      \"psk_key_exchange_modes\" (Section 4.2.9) extension which indicates",
            "      the key exchange modes that may be used with PSKs.",
            "",
            "   If the server does not select a PSK, then the first three of these",
            "   options are entirely orthogonal: the server independently selects a",
            "   cipher suite, an (EC)DHE group and key share for key establishment,",
            "   and a signature algorithm/certificate pair to authenticate itself to",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   the client.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e068d06631fb6532"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If there is no overlap between the received"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e068d06631fb6532"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "\"supported_groups\" and the groups supported by the server, then the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e068d06631fb6532"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "server MUST abort the handshake with a \"handshake_failure\" or an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e068d06631fb6532"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "\"insufficient_security\" alert."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd1ae794904f99ea"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If the server selects a PSK, then it MUST also select a key"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd1ae794904f99ea"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "establishment mode from the set indicated by the client's"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd1ae794904f99ea"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "\"psk_key_exchange_modes\" extension (at present, PSK alone or with"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd1ae794904f99ea"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "(EC)DHE)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Note that if the PSK can be used without (EC)DHE, then"
              }
            ],
            "   non-overlap in the \"supported_groups\" parameters need not be fatal,",
            "   as it is in the non-PSK case discussed in the previous paragraph.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9cef03a329d73ad2",
                  "8ac20731e36fb61b",
                  "f0f918fba3b61161"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "If the server selects an (EC)DHE group and the client did not offer a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9cef03a329d73ad2",
                  "8ac20731e36fb61b",
                  "f0f918fba3b61161"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "compatible \"key_share\" extension in the initial ClientHello, the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9cef03a329d73ad2",
                  "8ac20731e36fb61b",
                  "f0f918fba3b61161"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "server MUST respond with a HelloRetryRequest (Section 4.1.4) message."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   If the server successfully selects parameters and does not require a",
            "   HelloRetryRequest, it indicates the selected parameters in the",
            "   ServerHello as follows:",
            "",
            "   -  If PSK is being used, then the server will send a \"pre_shared_key\"",
            "      extension indicating the selected key.",
            "",
            "   -  When (EC)DHE is in use, the server will also provide a \"key_share\"",
            "      extension.  If PSK is not being used, then (EC)DHE and",
            "      certificate-based authentication are always used.",
            "",
            "   -  When authenticating via a certificate, the server will send the",
            "      Certificate (Section 4.4.2) and CertificateVerify (Section 4.4.3)",
            "      messages.  In TLS 1.3 as defined by this document, either a PSK or",
            "      a certificate is always used, but not both.  Future documents may",
            "      define how to use them together.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e7575817257f2d9b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If the server is unable to negotiate a supported set of parameters"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e7575817257f2d9b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "(i.e., there is no overlap between the client and server parameters),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e7575817257f2d9b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "it MUST abort the handshake with either a \"handshake_failure\" or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e7575817257f2d9b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "\"insufficient_security\" fatal alert (see Section 6)."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "e068d06631fb6532",
            "e068d06631fb6532",
            "e068d06631fb6532",
            "e068d06631fb6532",
            "dd1ae794904f99ea",
            "dd1ae794904f99ea",
            "dd1ae794904f99ea",
            "dd1ae794904f99ea",
            "9cef03a329d73ad2",
            "9cef03a329d73ad2",
            "9cef03a329d73ad2",
            "e7575817257f2d9b",
            "e7575817257f2d9b",
            "e7575817257f2d9b",
            "e7575817257f2d9b"
          ],
          "title": "Cryptographic Negotiation"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.1.2",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "005b19d69b5f0606"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "When a client first connects to a server, it is REQUIRED to send the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "005b19d69b5f0606"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "ClientHello as its first TLS message."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "21dc78dd610dc39e",
                  "cf0b8179ef45bead"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "The client will also send a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "21dc78dd610dc39e",
                  "cf0b8179ef45bead"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "ClientHello when the server has responded to its ClientHello with a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "21dc78dd610dc39e",
                  "cf0b8179ef45bead"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "HelloRetryRequest.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "872331e419b16210",
                  "21dc78dd610dc39e",
                  "cf0b8179ef45bead"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "In that case, the client MUST send the same"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "872331e419b16210",
                  "21dc78dd610dc39e",
                  "cf0b8179ef45bead"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "ClientHello without modification"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "872331e419b16210",
                  "cf0b8179ef45bead"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": ", except as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b3712d1dcf1c9a8a",
                  "4d693aade8696fcd"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "-  If a \"key_share\" extension was supplied in the HelloRetryRequest,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b3712d1dcf1c9a8a",
                  "4d693aade8696fcd"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "replacing the list of shares with a list containing a single"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b3712d1dcf1c9a8a",
                  "4d693aade8696fcd"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "KeyShareEntry from the indicated group."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "54df1c7fa9c225c9",
                  "d4a4b19c354f7d22"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "-  Removing the \"early_data\" extension (Section 4.2.10) if one was"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "54df1c7fa9c225c9",
                  "d4a4b19c354f7d22"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "present.  Early data is not permitted after a HelloRetryRequest."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5d114ca55e650c05",
                  "e985629df8b99073"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "-  Including a \"cookie\" extension if one was provided in the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5d114ca55e650c05",
                  "e985629df8b99073"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "HelloRetryRequest."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "71e35d08520feac5",
                  "2c0825122fe6a680"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "-  Updating the \"pre_shared_key\" extension if present by recomputing"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "71e35d08520feac5",
                  "2c0825122fe6a680"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "the \"obfuscated_ticket_age\" and binder values and (optionally)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "71e35d08520feac5",
                  "2c0825122fe6a680"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "removing any PSKs which are incompatible with the server's"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "71e35d08520feac5",
                  "2c0825122fe6a680"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "indicated cipher suite."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   -  Optionally adding, removing, or changing the length of the",
            "      \"padding\" extension [RFC7685].",
            "",
            "   -  Other modifications that may be allowed by an extension defined in",
            "      the future and present in the HelloRetryRequest.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "41a65620371214a9"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Because TLS 1.3 forbids renegotiation, if a server has negotiated"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "41a65620371214a9"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "TLS 1.3 and receives a ClientHello at any other time, it MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "41a65620371214a9"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "terminate the connection with an \"unexpected_message\" alert."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d5176110f47f21ce"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If a server established a TLS connection with a previous version of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d5176110f47f21ce"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "TLS and receives a TLS 1.3 ClientHello in a renegotiation, it MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d5176110f47f21ce"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "retain the previous protocol version."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c96714f548349547"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "In particular, it MUST NOT"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c96714f548349547"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "negotiate TLS 1.3."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Structure of this message:",
            "",
            "      uint16 ProtocolVersion;",
            "      opaque Random[32];",
            "",
            "      uint8 CipherSuite[2];    /* Cryptographic suite selector */",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          ProtocolVersion legacy_version = 0x0303;    /* TLS v1.2 */",
            "          Random random;",
            "          opaque legacy_session_id<0..32>;",
            "          CipherSuite cipher_suites<2..2^16-2>;",
            "          opaque legacy_compression_methods<1..2^8-1>;",
            "          Extension extensions<8..2^16-1>;",
            "      } ClientHello;",
            "",
            "   legacy_version:  In previous versions of TLS, this field was used for",
            "      version negotiation and represented the highest version number",
            "      supported by the client.  Experience has shown that many servers",
            "      do not properly implement version negotiation, leading to \"version",
            "      intolerance\" in which the server rejects an otherwise acceptable",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      ClientHello with a version number higher than it supports.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "73c92d8a7f6bd05f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "In"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "73c92d8a7f6bd05f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "TLS 1.3, the client indicates its version preferences in the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "73c92d8a7f6bd05f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "\"supported_versions\" extension (Section 4.2.1) and the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "73c92d8a7f6bd05f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "legacy_version field MUST be set to 0x0303, which is the version"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "73c92d8a7f6bd05f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "number for TLS 1.2."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  TLS 1.3 ClientHellos are identified as having"
              }
            ],
            "      a legacy_version of 0x0303 and a supported_versions extension",
            "      present with 0x0304 as the highest version indicated therein.",
            "      (See Appendix D for details about backward compatibility.)",
            "",
            "   random:  32 bytes generated by a secure random number generator.  See",
            "      Appendix C for additional information.",
            "",
            "   legacy_session_id:  Versions of TLS before TLS 1.3 supported a",
            "      \"session resumption\" feature which has been merged with pre-shared",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      keys in this version (see Section 2.2).  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4d1e858cb75ea39c"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "A client which has a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4d1e858cb75ea39c"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "cached session ID set by a pre-TLS 1.3 server SHOULD set this"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4d1e858cb75ea39c"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "field to that value."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "afa3e54661eb83a4",
                  "d7a3d4bdf1ac6eea"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "In compatibility mode (see Appendix D.4),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "afa3e54661eb83a4",
                  "d7a3d4bdf1ac6eea"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "this field MUST be non-empty, so a client not offering a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "afa3e54661eb83a4",
                  "d7a3d4bdf1ac6eea"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "pre-TLS 1.3 session MUST generate a new 32-byte value."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "923169c159396cbf"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "This value"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "923169c159396cbf"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "need not be random but SHOULD be unpredictable to avoid"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "923169c159396cbf"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "implementations fixating on a specific value (also known as"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "923169c159396cbf"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "ossification)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ee1a31fbf30cf717"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Otherwise, it MUST be set as a zero-length vector"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ee1a31fbf30cf717"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "(i.e., a zero-valued single byte length field)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   cipher_suites:  A list of the symmetric cipher options supported by",
            "      the client, specifically the record protection algorithm",
            "      (including secret key length) and a hash to be used with HKDF, in",
            "      descending order of client preference.  Values are defined in",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      Appendix B.4.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d5e0951fab56264d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If the list contains cipher suites that the server"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d5e0951fab56264d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "does not recognize, support, or wish to use, the server MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d5e0951fab56264d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "ignore those cipher suites and process the remaining ones as"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d5e0951fab56264d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "usual."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "00c2c5849fdcde05"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "If the client is attempting a PSK key establishment, it"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "00c2c5849fdcde05"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "SHOULD advertise at least one cipher suite indicating a Hash"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "00c2c5849fdcde05"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "associated with the PSK."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   legacy_compression_methods:  Versions of TLS before 1.3 supported",
            "      compression with the list of supported compression methods being",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      sent in this field.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "48f7675934f4aa5d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "For every TLS 1.3 ClientHello, this vector"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "48f7675934f4aa5d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "MUST contain exactly one byte, set to zero, which corresponds to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "48f7675934f4aa5d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "the \"null\" compression method in prior versions of TLS."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3b18e0360f05118c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3b18e0360f05118c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "TLS 1.3 ClientHello is received with any other value in this"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3b18e0360f05118c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "field, the server MUST abort the handshake with an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3b18e0360f05118c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "\"illegal_parameter\" alert."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "67ad389ea2030a1a"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Note that TLS 1.3 servers might"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "67ad389ea2030a1a"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "receive TLS 1.2 or prior ClientHellos which contain other"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "67ad389ea2030a1a"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "compression methods and (if negotiating such a prior version) MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "67ad389ea2030a1a"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "follow the procedures for the appropriate prior version of TLS."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   extensions:  Clients request extended functionality from servers by",
            "      sending data in the extensions field.  The actual \"Extension\"",
            "      format is defined in Section 4.2.  In TLS 1.3, the use of certain",
            "      extensions is mandatory, as functionality has moved into",
            "      extensions to preserve ClientHello compatibility with previous",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      versions of TLS.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4ba5414f74ef5bf4"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Servers MUST ignore unrecognized extensions."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   All versions of TLS allow an extensions field to optionally follow",
            "   the compression_methods field.  TLS 1.3 ClientHello messages always",
            "   contain extensions (minimally \"supported_versions\", otherwise, they",
            "   will be interpreted as TLS 1.2 ClientHello messages).  However,",
            "   TLS 1.3 servers might receive ClientHello messages without an",
            "   extensions field from prior versions of TLS.  The presence of",
            "   extensions can be detected by determining whether there are bytes",
            "   following the compression_methods field at the end of the",
            "   ClientHello.  Note that this method of detecting optional data",
            "   differs from the normal TLS method of having a variable-length field,",
            "   but it is used for compatibility with TLS before extensions were",
            "   defined.  TLS 1.3 servers will need to perform this check first and",
            "   only attempt to negotiate TLS 1.3 if the \"supported_versions\"",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   extension is present.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "60407c4a111ead29"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If negotiating a version of TLS prior to 1.3,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "60407c4a111ead29"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "a server MUST check that the message either contains no data after"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "60407c4a111ead29"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "legacy_compression_methods or that it contains a valid extensions"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "60407c4a111ead29"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "block with no data following."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a5bd580df3bdfa90"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If not, then it MUST abort the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a5bd580df3bdfa90"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "handshake with a \"decode_error\" alert."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a5b1e321d8c36bb8"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "In the event that a client requests additional functionality using"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a5b1e321d8c36bb8"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "extensions and this functionality is not supplied by the server, the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a5b1e321d8c36bb8"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "client MAY abort the handshake."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   After sending the ClientHello message, the client waits for a",
            "   ServerHello or HelloRetryRequest message.  If early data is in use,",
            "   the client may transmit early Application Data (Section 2.3) while",
            "   waiting for the next handshake message."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "005b19d69b5f0606",
            "005b19d69b5f0606",
            "872331e419b16210",
            "872331e419b16210",
            "41a65620371214a9",
            "41a65620371214a9",
            "41a65620371214a9",
            "d5176110f47f21ce",
            "d5176110f47f21ce",
            "d5176110f47f21ce",
            "c96714f548349547",
            "c96714f548349547",
            "73c92d8a7f6bd05f",
            "73c92d8a7f6bd05f",
            "73c92d8a7f6bd05f",
            "73c92d8a7f6bd05f",
            "73c92d8a7f6bd05f",
            "4d1e858cb75ea39c",
            "4d1e858cb75ea39c",
            "4d1e858cb75ea39c",
            "afa3e54661eb83a4",
            "afa3e54661eb83a4",
            "afa3e54661eb83a4",
            "d7a3d4bdf1ac6eea",
            "d7a3d4bdf1ac6eea",
            "d7a3d4bdf1ac6eea",
            "923169c159396cbf",
            "923169c159396cbf",
            "923169c159396cbf",
            "923169c159396cbf",
            "ee1a31fbf30cf717",
            "ee1a31fbf30cf717",
            "d5e0951fab56264d",
            "d5e0951fab56264d",
            "d5e0951fab56264d",
            "d5e0951fab56264d",
            "00c2c5849fdcde05",
            "00c2c5849fdcde05",
            "00c2c5849fdcde05",
            "48f7675934f4aa5d",
            "48f7675934f4aa5d",
            "48f7675934f4aa5d",
            "3b18e0360f05118c",
            "3b18e0360f05118c",
            "3b18e0360f05118c",
            "3b18e0360f05118c",
            "67ad389ea2030a1a",
            "67ad389ea2030a1a",
            "67ad389ea2030a1a",
            "67ad389ea2030a1a",
            "4ba5414f74ef5bf4",
            "60407c4a111ead29",
            "60407c4a111ead29",
            "60407c4a111ead29",
            "60407c4a111ead29",
            "a5bd580df3bdfa90",
            "a5bd580df3bdfa90",
            "a5b1e321d8c36bb8",
            "a5b1e321d8c36bb8",
            "a5b1e321d8c36bb8"
          ],
          "title": "Client Hello"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.1.3",
          "lines": [
            "   The server will send this message in response to a ClientHello",
            "   message to proceed with the handshake if it is able to negotiate an",
            "   acceptable set of handshake parameters based on the ClientHello.",
            "",
            "   Structure of this message:",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          ProtocolVersion legacy_version = 0x0303;    /* TLS v1.2 */",
            "          Random random;",
            "          opaque legacy_session_id_echo<0..32>;",
            "          CipherSuite cipher_suite;",
            "          uint8 legacy_compression_method = 0;",
            "          Extension extensions<6..2^16-1>;",
            "      } ServerHello;",
            "",
            "   legacy_version:  In previous versions of TLS, this field was used for",
            "      version negotiation and represented the selected version number",
            "      for the connection.  Unfortunately, some middleboxes fail when",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      presented with new values.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "45d3759c87b023f9"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "In TLS 1.3, the TLS server indicates"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "45d3759c87b023f9"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "its version using the \"supported_versions\" extension"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "45d3759c87b023f9"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "(Section 4.2.1), and the legacy_version field MUST be set to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "45d3759c87b023f9"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "0x0303, which is the version number for TLS 1.2."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  (See Appendix D"
              }
            ],
            "      for details about backward compatibility.)",
            "",
            "   random:  32 bytes generated by a secure random number generator.  See",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      Appendix C for additional information.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "39bcef49b9ae72d1",
                  "fd53c4afa6e8fd00"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The last 8 bytes MUST be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "39bcef49b9ae72d1",
                  "fd53c4afa6e8fd00"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "overwritten as described below if negotiating TLS 1.2 or TLS 1.1,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "39bcef49b9ae72d1",
                  "fd53c4afa6e8fd00"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "but the remaining bytes MUST be random."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "af6ec61269ebb2d8"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "This structure is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "af6ec61269ebb2d8"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "generated by the server and MUST be generated independently of the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "af6ec61269ebb2d8"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "ClientHello.random."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   legacy_session_id_echo:  The contents of the client's",
            "      legacy_session_id field.  Note that this field is echoed even if",
            "      the client's value corresponded to a cached pre-TLS 1.3 session",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      which the server has chosen not to resume.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d391da7ea2ed3323",
                  "25e71d9f9201c77a"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "A client which"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d391da7ea2ed3323",
                  "25e71d9f9201c77a"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "receives a legacy_session_id_echo field that does not match what"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d391da7ea2ed3323",
                  "25e71d9f9201c77a"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "it sent in the ClientHello MUST abort the handshake with an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d391da7ea2ed3323",
                  "25e71d9f9201c77a"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "\"illegal_parameter\" alert."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   cipher_suite:  The single cipher suite selected by the server from",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      the list in ClientHello.cipher_suites.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "72a82d1141e3171f",
                  "6dfce7eafbecaf5d"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "A client which receives a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "72a82d1141e3171f",
                  "6dfce7eafbecaf5d"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "cipher suite that was not offered MUST abort the handshake with an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "72a82d1141e3171f",
                  "6dfce7eafbecaf5d"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "\"illegal_parameter\" alert."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f72d30fe8f1f3d3c",
                  "b9f459fc14a4cb28"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "legacy_compression_method:  A single byte which MUST have the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f72d30fe8f1f3d3c",
                  "b9f459fc14a4cb28"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "value 0."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   extensions:  A list of extensions.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eab010798f42628c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The ServerHello MUST only include"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eab010798f42628c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "extensions which are required to establish the cryptographic"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eab010798f42628c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "context and negotiate the protocol version."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1b957a008808a714"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "All TLS 1.3"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1b957a008808a714"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "ServerHello messages MUST contain the \"supported_versions\""
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1b957a008808a714"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "extension."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Current ServerHello messages additionally contain"
              }
            ],
            "      either the \"pre_shared_key\" extension or the \"key_share\"",
            "      extension, or both (when using a PSK with (EC)DHE key",
            "      establishment).  Other extensions (see Section 4.2) are sent",
            "      separately in the EncryptedExtensions message.",
            "",
            "   For reasons of backward compatibility with middleboxes (see",
            "   Appendix D.4), the HelloRetryRequest message uses the same structure",
            "   as the ServerHello, but with Random set to the special value of the",
            "   SHA-256 of \"HelloRetryRequest\":",
            "",
            "     CF 21 AD 74 E5 9A 61 11 BE 1D 8C 02 1E 65 B8 91",
            "     C2 A2 11 16 7A BB 8C 5E 07 9E 09 E2 C8 A8 33 9C",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6182228959970007",
                  "baf742f8356dfdfb",
                  "9b5a8e3a9d05f14c"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Upon receiving a message with type server_hello, implementations MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6182228959970007",
                  "baf742f8356dfdfb",
                  "9b5a8e3a9d05f14c"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "first examine the Random value and, if it matches this value, process"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6182228959970007",
                  "baf742f8356dfdfb",
                  "9b5a8e3a9d05f14c"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "it as described in Section 4.1.4)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   TLS 1.3 has a downgrade protection mechanism embedded in the server's",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   random value.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4417392a7fb8abca"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "TLS 1.3 servers which negotiate TLS 1.2 or below in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4417392a7fb8abca"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "response to a ClientHello MUST set the last 8 bytes of their Random"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4417392a7fb8abca"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "value specially in their ServerHello."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dee73fa43fc5774c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If negotiating TLS 1.2, TLS 1.3 servers MUST set the last 8 bytes of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dee73fa43fc5774c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "their Random value to the bytes:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "     44 4F 57 4E 47 52 44 01",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1e0a3de4ec540923"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If negotiating TLS 1.1 or below, TLS 1.3 servers MUST, and TLS 1.2"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1e0a3de4ec540923"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "servers SHOULD, set the last 8 bytes of their ServerHello.Random"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1e0a3de4ec540923"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "value to the bytes:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "     44 4F 57 4E 47 52 44 00",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cd2e51dbcfe07872"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "TLS 1.3 clients receiving a ServerHello indicating TLS 1.2 or below"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cd2e51dbcfe07872"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "MUST check that the last 8 bytes are not equal to either of these"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cd2e51dbcfe07872"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "values."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "76b8d4e5b54a6641"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "TLS 1.2 clients SHOULD also check that the last 8 bytes are"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "76b8d4e5b54a6641"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "not equal to the second value if the ServerHello indicates TLS 1.1 or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "76b8d4e5b54a6641"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "below."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5d01154e70093464"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If a match is found, the client MUST abort the handshake with"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5d01154e70093464"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "an \"illegal_parameter\" alert."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This mechanism provides limited"
              }
            ],
            "   protection against downgrade attacks over and above what is provided",
            "   by the Finished exchange: because the ServerKeyExchange, a message",
            "   present in TLS 1.2 and below, includes a signature over both random",
            "   values, it is not possible for an active attacker to modify the",
            "",
            "   random values without detection as long as ephemeral ciphers are",
            "   used.  It does not provide downgrade protection when static RSA",
            "   is used.",
            "",
            "   Note: This is a change from [RFC5246], so in practice many TLS 1.2",
            "   clients and servers will not behave as specified above.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a9c4d9de9bc869e6"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "A legacy TLS client performing renegotiation with TLS 1.2 or prior"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a9c4d9de9bc869e6"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "and which receives a TLS 1.3 ServerHello during renegotiation MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a9c4d9de9bc869e6"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "abort the handshake with a \"protocol_version\" alert."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Note that"
              }
            ],
            "   renegotiation is not possible when TLS 1.3 has been negotiated."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "45d3759c87b023f9",
            "45d3759c87b023f9",
            "45d3759c87b023f9",
            "45d3759c87b023f9",
            "39bcef49b9ae72d1",
            "39bcef49b9ae72d1",
            "39bcef49b9ae72d1",
            "fd53c4afa6e8fd00",
            "fd53c4afa6e8fd00",
            "fd53c4afa6e8fd00",
            "af6ec61269ebb2d8",
            "af6ec61269ebb2d8",
            "af6ec61269ebb2d8",
            "d391da7ea2ed3323",
            "d391da7ea2ed3323",
            "d391da7ea2ed3323",
            "d391da7ea2ed3323",
            "72a82d1141e3171f",
            "72a82d1141e3171f",
            "72a82d1141e3171f",
            "f72d30fe8f1f3d3c",
            "f72d30fe8f1f3d3c",
            "eab010798f42628c",
            "eab010798f42628c",
            "eab010798f42628c",
            "1b957a008808a714",
            "1b957a008808a714",
            "1b957a008808a714",
            "6182228959970007",
            "6182228959970007",
            "6182228959970007",
            "4417392a7fb8abca",
            "4417392a7fb8abca",
            "4417392a7fb8abca",
            "dee73fa43fc5774c",
            "dee73fa43fc5774c",
            "1e0a3de4ec540923",
            "1e0a3de4ec540923",
            "1e0a3de4ec540923",
            "cd2e51dbcfe07872",
            "cd2e51dbcfe07872",
            "cd2e51dbcfe07872",
            "76b8d4e5b54a6641",
            "76b8d4e5b54a6641",
            "76b8d4e5b54a6641",
            "5d01154e70093464",
            "5d01154e70093464",
            "a9c4d9de9bc869e6",
            "a9c4d9de9bc869e6",
            "a9c4d9de9bc869e6"
          ],
          "title": "Server Hello"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.1.4",
          "lines": [
            "   The server will send this message in response to a ClientHello",
            "   message if it is able to find an acceptable set of parameters but the",
            "   ClientHello does not contain sufficient information to proceed with",
            "   the handshake.  As discussed in Section 4.1.3, the HelloRetryRequest",
            "   has the same format as a ServerHello message, and the legacy_version,",
            "   legacy_session_id_echo, cipher_suite, and legacy_compression_method",
            "   fields have the same meaning.  However, for convenience we discuss",
            "   \"HelloRetryRequest\" throughout this document as if it were a distinct",
            "   message.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "29c848806cacb9e3",
                  "fb204cec65cb67e5",
                  "7329d68f68e012d6"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "The server's extensions MUST contain \"supported_versions\"."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd15bfb69bcdd610"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "Additionally, it SHOULD contain the minimal set of extensions"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd15bfb69bcdd610"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "necessary for the client to generate a correct ClientHello pair."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dbb8e4564a355733",
                  "a1e7a7d4ba07d3c0",
                  "1b03262b18e4b6df",
                  "92762bf0503913be",
                  "20af75f7ff46ba2e"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "As"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dbb8e4564a355733",
                  "a1e7a7d4ba07d3c0",
                  "1b03262b18e4b6df",
                  "92762bf0503913be",
                  "20af75f7ff46ba2e"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "with the ServerHello, a HelloRetryRequest MUST NOT contain any"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dbb8e4564a355733",
                  "a1e7a7d4ba07d3c0",
                  "1b03262b18e4b6df",
                  "92762bf0503913be",
                  "20af75f7ff46ba2e"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "extensions that were not first offered by the client in its"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dbb8e4564a355733",
                  "a1e7a7d4ba07d3c0",
                  "1b03262b18e4b6df",
                  "92762bf0503913be",
                  "20af75f7ff46ba2e"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "ClientHello, with the exception of optionally the \"cookie\" (see"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dbb8e4564a355733",
                  "a1e7a7d4ba07d3c0",
                  "1b03262b18e4b6df",
                  "92762bf0503913be",
                  "20af75f7ff46ba2e"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Section 4.2.2) extension."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "abf9a5b268de4302",
                  "4c4b46a80075d521",
                  "3867219f122d4027",
                  "63cc7d7cdbdccc3b",
                  "ad2af49d87d2a7a1",
                  "a704046c4562f0fc"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Upon receipt of a HelloRetryRequest, the client MUST check the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "abf9a5b268de4302",
                  "4c4b46a80075d521",
                  "3867219f122d4027",
                  "63cc7d7cdbdccc3b",
                  "ad2af49d87d2a7a1",
                  "a704046c4562f0fc"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "legacy_version"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "abf9a5b268de4302",
                  "4c4b46a80075d521",
                  "3867219f122d4027",
                  "ad2af49d87d2a7a1",
                  "a704046c4562f0fc"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": ", legacy_session_id_echo"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "abf9a5b268de4302",
                  "4c4b46a80075d521",
                  "3867219f122d4027",
                  "ad2af49d87d2a7a1"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": ", cipher_suite"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "abf9a5b268de4302",
                  "4c4b46a80075d521",
                  "ad2af49d87d2a7a1"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": ", and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "abf9a5b268de4302",
                  "4c4b46a80075d521",
                  "ad2af49d87d2a7a1"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "legacy_compression_method"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "abf9a5b268de4302",
                  "4c4b46a80075d521"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": " as specified in Section 4.1.3 and then"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "abf9a5b268de4302",
                  "4c4b46a80075d521"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "process the extensions, starting with determining the version using"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "abf9a5b268de4302",
                  "4c4b46a80075d521"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "\"supported_versions\"."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f3026b04b3878269",
                  "17eee8a6df166de2",
                  "8ca72b5c20a52a85"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Clients MUST abort the handshake with an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f3026b04b3878269",
                  "17eee8a6df166de2",
                  "8ca72b5c20a52a85"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "\"illegal_parameter\" alert if the HelloRetryRequest would not result"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f3026b04b3878269",
                  "17eee8a6df166de2",
                  "8ca72b5c20a52a85"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "in any change in the ClientHello."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bdae2e12f7b1d4f9",
                  "a0d055b6d9c39627",
                  "4fa511a47213fcaa"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "If a client receives a second"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bdae2e12f7b1d4f9",
                  "a0d055b6d9c39627",
                  "4fa511a47213fcaa"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "HelloRetryRequest in the same connection (i.e., where the ClientHello"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bdae2e12f7b1d4f9",
                  "a0d055b6d9c39627",
                  "4fa511a47213fcaa"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "was itself in response to a HelloRetryRequest), it MUST abort the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bdae2e12f7b1d4f9",
                  "a0d055b6d9c39627",
                  "4fa511a47213fcaa"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "handshake with an \"unexpected_message\" alert."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1862fd868a428757",
                  "860b63c0f64f096c",
                  "7c5b0042523d5214"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Otherwise, the client MUST process all extensions in the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1862fd868a428757",
                  "860b63c0f64f096c",
                  "7c5b0042523d5214"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "HelloRetryRequest"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1862fd868a428757",
                  "860b63c0f64f096c"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": " and send a second updated ClientHello."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a351680ab895ce91"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a351680ab895ce91"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "HelloRetryRequest extensions defined in this specification are:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a351680ab895ce91"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "-  supported_versions (see Section 4.2.1)"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a351680ab895ce91"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "-  cookie (see Section 4.2.2)"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a351680ab895ce91"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "-  key_share (see Section 4.2.8)"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6cb0ef45c8699ad3",
                  "18ff6491d4079e1e",
                  "0afb153c9ad2fcbb"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "A client which receives a cipher suite that was not offered MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6cb0ef45c8699ad3",
                  "18ff6491d4079e1e",
                  "0afb153c9ad2fcbb"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "abort the handshake."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fa90a6ebf67b5372",
                  "3508fa55b70932fd",
                  "d06c6c5bd8f548f9",
                  "683f6972634e6954"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Servers MUST ensure that they negotiate the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fa90a6ebf67b5372",
                  "3508fa55b70932fd",
                  "d06c6c5bd8f548f9",
                  "683f6972634e6954"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "same cipher suite when receiving a conformant updated ClientHello (if"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fa90a6ebf67b5372",
                  "3508fa55b70932fd",
                  "d06c6c5bd8f548f9",
                  "683f6972634e6954"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "the server selects the cipher suite as the first step in the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fa90a6ebf67b5372",
                  "3508fa55b70932fd",
                  "d06c6c5bd8f548f9",
                  "683f6972634e6954"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "negotiation, then this will happen automatically)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "75443a4e3d4c052a",
                  "9995896098fcf65b",
                  "57df50bf762de5f5"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Upon receiving"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "75443a4e3d4c052a",
                  "9995896098fcf65b",
                  "57df50bf762de5f5"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "the ServerHello, clients MUST check that the cipher suite supplied in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "75443a4e3d4c052a",
                  "9995896098fcf65b",
                  "57df50bf762de5f5"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "the ServerHello is the same as that in the HelloRetryRequest and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "75443a4e3d4c052a",
                  "9995896098fcf65b",
                  "57df50bf762de5f5"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "otherwise abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "29f45c7e3f29acaa",
                  "9f8ff17762c81a2b",
                  "1535c7a286df59d1",
                  "2a8a9692cd54325c",
                  "753d152e32e5fb29",
                  "7f987f8f24219b7b"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "In addition, in its updated ClientHello, the client SHOULD NOT offer"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "29f45c7e3f29acaa",
                  "9f8ff17762c81a2b",
                  "1535c7a286df59d1",
                  "2a8a9692cd54325c",
                  "753d152e32e5fb29",
                  "7f987f8f24219b7b"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "any pre-shared keys associated with a hash other than that of the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "29f45c7e3f29acaa",
                  "9f8ff17762c81a2b",
                  "1535c7a286df59d1",
                  "2a8a9692cd54325c",
                  "753d152e32e5fb29",
                  "7f987f8f24219b7b"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "selected cipher suite."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2a8a9692cd54325c",
                  "7f987f8f24219b7b"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "  This allows the client to avoid having to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2a8a9692cd54325c",
                  "7f987f8f24219b7b"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "compute partial hash transcripts for multiple hashes in the second"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2a8a9692cd54325c",
                  "7f987f8f24219b7b"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "ClientHello."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "65e6f4b97af84f33",
                  "c4928a980c0f9cd9",
                  "acc35cc6c3c008d6",
                  "170136f2148e6adf"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "The value of selected_version in the HelloRetryRequest"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "65e6f4b97af84f33",
                  "c4928a980c0f9cd9",
                  "acc35cc6c3c008d6",
                  "170136f2148e6adf"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "\"supported_versions\" extension MUST be retained in the ServerHello,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "65e6f4b97af84f33",
                  "c4928a980c0f9cd9",
                  "acc35cc6c3c008d6",
                  "170136f2148e6adf"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "and a client MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\""
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "65e6f4b97af84f33",
                  "c4928a980c0f9cd9",
                  "acc35cc6c3c008d6",
                  "170136f2148e6adf"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "alert if the value changes."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "29c848806cacb9e3",
            "dd15bfb69bcdd610",
            "dd15bfb69bcdd610",
            "dbb8e4564a355733",
            "dbb8e4564a355733",
            "dbb8e4564a355733",
            "dbb8e4564a355733",
            "dbb8e4564a355733",
            "abf9a5b268de4302",
            "abf9a5b268de4302",
            "abf9a5b268de4302",
            "abf9a5b268de4302",
            "abf9a5b268de4302",
            "f3026b04b3878269",
            "f3026b04b3878269",
            "f3026b04b3878269",
            "bdae2e12f7b1d4f9",
            "bdae2e12f7b1d4f9",
            "bdae2e12f7b1d4f9",
            "bdae2e12f7b1d4f9",
            "1862fd868a428757",
            "1862fd868a428757",
            "6cb0ef45c8699ad3",
            "6cb0ef45c8699ad3",
            "fa90a6ebf67b5372",
            "fa90a6ebf67b5372",
            "fa90a6ebf67b5372",
            "fa90a6ebf67b5372",
            "75443a4e3d4c052a",
            "75443a4e3d4c052a",
            "75443a4e3d4c052a",
            "75443a4e3d4c052a",
            "29f45c7e3f29acaa",
            "29f45c7e3f29acaa",
            "29f45c7e3f29acaa",
            "65e6f4b97af84f33",
            "65e6f4b97af84f33",
            "65e6f4b97af84f33",
            "65e6f4b97af84f33",
            "c4928a980c0f9cd9",
            "c4928a980c0f9cd9",
            "c4928a980c0f9cd9",
            "c4928a980c0f9cd9"
          ],
          "title": "Hello Retry Request"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.2",
          "lines": [
            "   A number of TLS messages contain tag-length-value encoded extensions",
            "   structures.",
            "",
            "    struct {",
            "        ExtensionType extension_type;",
            "        opaque extension_data<0..2^16-1>;",
            "    } Extension;",
            "",
            "    enum {",
            "        server_name(0),                             /* RFC 6066 */",
            "        max_fragment_length(1),                     /* RFC 6066 */",
            "        status_request(5),                          /* RFC 6066 */",
            "        supported_groups(10),                       /* RFC 8422, 7919 */",
            "        signature_algorithms(13),                   /* RFC 8446 */",
            "        use_srtp(14),                               /* RFC 5764 */",
            "        heartbeat(15),                              /* RFC 6520 */",
            "        application_layer_protocol_negotiation(16), /* RFC 7301 */",
            "        signed_certificate_timestamp(18),           /* RFC 6962 */",
            "        client_certificate_type(19),                /* RFC 7250 */",
            "        server_certificate_type(20),                /* RFC 7250 */",
            "        padding(21),                                /* RFC 7685 */",
            "        pre_shared_key(41),                         /* RFC 8446 */",
            "        early_data(42),                             /* RFC 8446 */",
            "        supported_versions(43),                     /* RFC 8446 */",
            "        cookie(44),                                 /* RFC 8446 */",
            "        psk_key_exchange_modes(45),                 /* RFC 8446 */",
            "        certificate_authorities(47),                /* RFC 8446 */",
            "        oid_filters(48),                            /* RFC 8446 */",
            "        post_handshake_auth(49),                    /* RFC 8446 */",
            "        signature_algorithms_cert(50),              /* RFC 8446 */",
            "        key_share(51),                              /* RFC 8446 */",
            "        (65535)",
            "    } ExtensionType;",
            "",
            "   Here:",
            "",
            "   -  \"extension_type\" identifies the particular extension type.",
            "",
            "   -  \"extension_data\" contains information specific to the particular",
            "      extension type.",
            "",
            "   The list of extension types is maintained by IANA as described in",
            "   Section 11.",
            "",
            "   Extensions are generally structured in a request/response fashion,",
            "   though some extensions are just indications with no corresponding",
            "   response.  The client sends its extension requests in the ClientHello",
            "   message, and the server sends its extension responses in the",
            "   ServerHello, EncryptedExtensions, HelloRetryRequest, and Certificate",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   messages.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a037a5758b71e9ad"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "The server sends extension requests in the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a037a5758b71e9ad"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "CertificateRequest message which a client MAY respond to with a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a037a5758b71e9ad"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Certificate message."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "498cfeb6682ed352"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "The server MAY also send unsolicited extensions"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "498cfeb6682ed352"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "in the NewSessionTicket, though the client does not respond directly"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "498cfeb6682ed352"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "to these."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "10c68cc726525727",
                  "2a7b9dc49a99108c",
                  "5532cacbe0753ea4"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Implementations MUST NOT send extension responses if the remote"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "10c68cc726525727",
                  "2a7b9dc49a99108c",
                  "5532cacbe0753ea4"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "endpoint did not send the corresponding extension requests, with the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "10c68cc726525727",
                  "2a7b9dc49a99108c",
                  "5532cacbe0753ea4"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "exception of the \"cookie\" extension in the HelloRetryRequest."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5532cacbe0753ea4"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a39513dea09440d0",
                  "508500918dae4f3b",
                  "5532cacbe0753ea4"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Upon"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a39513dea09440d0",
                  "508500918dae4f3b",
                  "5532cacbe0753ea4"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "receiving such an extension, an endpoint MUST abort the handshake"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a39513dea09440d0",
                  "508500918dae4f3b",
                  "5532cacbe0753ea4"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "with an \"unsupported_extension\" alert."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The table below indicates the messages where a given extension may",
            "   appear, using the following notation: CH (ClientHello),",
            "   SH (ServerHello), EE (EncryptedExtensions), CT (Certificate),",
            "   CR (CertificateRequest), NST (NewSessionTicket), and",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   HRR (HelloRetryRequest).  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "63b9edf8e4f04e81",
                  "375c6eb7390322b7"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "If an implementation receives an extension"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "63b9edf8e4f04e81",
                  "375c6eb7390322b7"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "which it recognizes and which is not specified for the message in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "63b9edf8e4f04e81",
                  "375c6eb7390322b7"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "which it appears, it MUST abort the handshake with an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "63b9edf8e4f04e81",
                  "375c6eb7390322b7"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "\"illegal_parameter\" alert."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   +--------------------------------------------------+-------------+",
            "   | Extension                                        |     TLS 1.3 |",
            "   +--------------------------------------------------+-------------+",
            "   | server_name [RFC6066]                            |      CH, EE |",
            "   |                                                  |             |",
            "   | max_fragment_length [RFC6066]                    |      CH, EE |",
            "   |                                                  |             |",
            "   | status_request [RFC6066]                         |  CH, CR, CT |",
            "   |                                                  |             |",
            "   | supported_groups [RFC7919]                       |      CH, EE |",
            "   |                                                  |             |",
            "   | signature_algorithms (RFC 8446)                  |      CH, CR |",
            "   |                                                  |             |",
            "   | use_srtp [RFC5764]                               |      CH, EE |",
            "   |                                                  |             |",
            "   | heartbeat [RFC6520]                              |      CH, EE |",
            "   |                                                  |             |",
            "   | application_layer_protocol_negotiation [RFC7301] |      CH, EE |",
            "   |                                                  |             |",
            "   | signed_certificate_timestamp [RFC6962]           |  CH, CR, CT |",
            "   |                                                  |             |",
            "   | client_certificate_type [RFC7250]                |      CH, EE |",
            "   |                                                  |             |",
            "   | server_certificate_type [RFC7250]                |      CH, EE |",
            "   |                                                  |             |",
            "   | padding [RFC7685]                                |          CH |",
            "   |                                                  |             |",
            "   | key_share (RFC 8446)                             | CH, SH, HRR |",
            "   |                                                  |             |",
            "   | pre_shared_key (RFC 8446)                        |      CH, SH |",
            "   |                                                  |             |",
            "   | psk_key_exchange_modes (RFC 8446)                |          CH |",
            "   |                                                  |             |",
            "   | early_data (RFC 8446)                            | CH, EE, NST |",
            "   |                                                  |             |",
            "   | cookie (RFC 8446)                                |     CH, HRR |",
            "   |                                                  |             |",
            "   | supported_versions (RFC 8446)                    | CH, SH, HRR |",
            "   |                                                  |             |",
            "   | certificate_authorities (RFC 8446)               |      CH, CR |",
            "   |                                                  |             |",
            "   | oid_filters (RFC 8446)                           |          CR |",
            "   |                                                  |             |",
            "   | post_handshake_auth (RFC 8446)                   |          CH |",
            "   |                                                  |             |",
            "   | signature_algorithms_cert (RFC 8446)             |      CH, CR |",
            "   +--------------------------------------------------+-------------+",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "197ed0bf4ed3ac80"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "When multiple extensions of different types are present, the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "197ed0bf4ed3ac80"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "extensions MAY appear in any order, with the exception of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "197ed0bf4ed3ac80"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "\"pre_shared_key\" (Section 4.2.11) which MUST be the last extension in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "197ed0bf4ed3ac80"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "the ClientHello (but can appear anywhere in the ServerHello"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "197ed0bf4ed3ac80"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "extensions block)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4c0c81955d98f4ff"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "There MUST NOT be more than one extension of the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4c0c81955d98f4ff"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "same type in a given extension block."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   In TLS 1.3, unlike TLS 1.2, extensions are negotiated for each",
            "   handshake even when in resumption-PSK mode.  However, 0-RTT",
            "   parameters are those negotiated in the previous handshake; mismatches",
            "   may require rejecting 0-RTT (see Section 4.2.10).",
            "",
            "   There are subtle (and not so subtle) interactions that may occur in",
            "   this protocol between new features and existing features which may",
            "   result in a significant reduction in overall security.  The following",
            "   considerations should be taken into account when designing new",
            "   extensions:",
            "",
            "   -  Some cases where a server does not agree to an extension are error",
            "      conditions (e.g., the handshake cannot continue), and some are",
            "      simply refusals to support particular features.  In general, error",
            "      alerts should be used for the former and a field in the server",
            "      extension response for the latter.",
            "",
            "   -  Extensions should, as far as possible, be designed to prevent any",
            "      attack that forces use (or non-use) of a particular feature by",
            "      manipulation of handshake messages.  This principle should be",
            "      followed regardless of whether the feature is believed to cause a",
            "      security problem.  Often the fact that the extension fields are",
            "      included in the inputs to the Finished message hashes will be",
            "      sufficient, but extreme care is needed when the extension changes",
            "      the meaning of messages sent in the handshake phase.  Designers",
            "      and implementors should be aware of the fact that until the",
            "      handshake has been authenticated, active attackers can modify",
            "      messages and insert, remove, or replace extensions."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "a037a5758b71e9ad",
            "a037a5758b71e9ad",
            "a037a5758b71e9ad",
            "498cfeb6682ed352",
            "498cfeb6682ed352",
            "498cfeb6682ed352",
            "10c68cc726525727",
            "10c68cc726525727",
            "10c68cc726525727",
            "a39513dea09440d0",
            "a39513dea09440d0",
            "a39513dea09440d0",
            "63b9edf8e4f04e81",
            "63b9edf8e4f04e81",
            "63b9edf8e4f04e81",
            "63b9edf8e4f04e81",
            "197ed0bf4ed3ac80",
            "197ed0bf4ed3ac80",
            "197ed0bf4ed3ac80",
            "197ed0bf4ed3ac80",
            "197ed0bf4ed3ac80",
            "4c0c81955d98f4ff",
            "4c0c81955d98f4ff"
          ],
          "title": "Extensions"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.2.1",
          "lines": [
            "      struct {",
            "          select (Handshake.msg_type) {",
            "              case client_hello:",
            "                   ProtocolVersion versions<2..254>;",
            "",
            "              case server_hello: /* and HelloRetryRequest */",
            "                   ProtocolVersion selected_version;",
            "          };",
            "      } SupportedVersions;",
            "",
            "   The \"supported_versions\" extension is used by the client to indicate",
            "   which versions of TLS it supports and by the server to indicate which",
            "   version it is using.  The extension contains a list of supported",
            "   versions in preference order, with the most preferred version first.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "76ee01ab38ae49ec",
                  "90297231957bd8ef"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Implementations of this specification MUST send this extension in the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "76ee01ab38ae49ec",
                  "90297231957bd8ef"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "ClientHello containing all versions of TLS which they are prepared to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "76ee01ab38ae49ec",
                  "90297231957bd8ef"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "negotiate (for this specification, that means minimally 0x0304, but"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "76ee01ab38ae49ec",
                  "90297231957bd8ef"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "if previous versions of TLS are allowed to be negotiated, they MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "76ee01ab38ae49ec",
                  "90297231957bd8ef"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "be present as well)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6bd8bc474596d812"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If this extension is not present, servers which are compliant with"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6bd8bc474596d812"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "this specification and which also support TLS 1.2 MUST negotiate"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6bd8bc474596d812"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "TLS 1.2 or prior as specified in [RFC5246], even if"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6bd8bc474596d812"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "ClientHello.legacy_version is 0x0304 or later."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2b9e23db3a8bf16c"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Servers MAY abort the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2b9e23db3a8bf16c"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "handshake upon receiving a ClientHello with legacy_version 0x0304 or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2b9e23db3a8bf16c"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "later."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "30b97efb1204a874",
                  "117b8e4cf38485f1",
                  "942990c83d4c8342"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "If this extension is present in the ClientHello, servers MUST NOT use"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "30b97efb1204a874",
                  "117b8e4cf38485f1",
                  "942990c83d4c8342"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "the ClientHello.legacy_version value for version negotiation and MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "30b97efb1204a874",
                  "117b8e4cf38485f1",
                  "942990c83d4c8342"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "use only the \"supported_versions\" extension to determine client"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "30b97efb1204a874",
                  "117b8e4cf38485f1",
                  "942990c83d4c8342"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "preferences."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9bb38757ec23daa3",
                  "8ba00072029cd718"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Servers MUST only select a version of TLS present in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9bb38757ec23daa3",
                  "8ba00072029cd718"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "that extension and MUST ignore any unknown versions that are present"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9bb38757ec23daa3",
                  "8ba00072029cd718"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "in that extension."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Note that this mechanism makes it possible to"
              }
            ],
            "   negotiate a version prior to TLS 1.2 if one side supports a sparse",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   range.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eeedb52a4b15ed1e"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "Implementations of TLS 1.3 which choose to support prior"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eeedb52a4b15ed1e"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "versions of TLS SHOULD support TLS 1.2."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c0b04475fe68a2dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Servers MUST be prepared to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c0b04475fe68a2dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "receive ClientHellos that include this extension but do not include"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c0b04475fe68a2dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "0x0304 in the list of versions."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "688dd95fa5fc7d0d",
                  "b488c0e18b2fce50"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "A server which negotiates a version of TLS prior to TLS 1.3 MUST set"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "688dd95fa5fc7d0d",
                  "b488c0e18b2fce50"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "ServerHello.version and MUST NOT send the \"supported_versions\""
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "688dd95fa5fc7d0d",
                  "b488c0e18b2fce50"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "extension."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "046ad44ca04a3e8f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "A server which negotiates TLS 1.3 MUST respond by sending"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "046ad44ca04a3e8f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "a \"supported_versions\" extension containing the selected version"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "046ad44ca04a3e8f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "value (0x0304)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e90ff39c0d4d11d6"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "It MUST set the ServerHello.legacy_version field to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e90ff39c0d4d11d6"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "0x0303 (TLS 1.2)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ea526891e6481a37"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Clients MUST check for this extension prior to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ea526891e6481a37"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "processing the rest of the ServerHello (although they will have to"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   parse the ServerHello in order to read the extension).  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "74f3ad32a0f00007",
                  "57500015faad53dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If this"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "74f3ad32a0f00007",
                  "57500015faad53dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "extension is present, clients MUST ignore the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "74f3ad32a0f00007",
                  "57500015faad53dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "ServerHello.legacy_version value and MUST use only the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "74f3ad32a0f00007",
                  "57500015faad53dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "\"supported_versions\" extension to determine the selected version."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fbe002703a61e612"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fbe002703a61e612"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "the \"supported_versions\" extension in the ServerHello contains a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fbe002703a61e612"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "version not offered by the client or contains a version prior to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fbe002703a61e612"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "TLS 1.3, the client MUST abort the handshake with an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fbe002703a61e612"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "\"illegal_parameter\" alert."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "76ee01ab38ae49ec",
            "76ee01ab38ae49ec",
            "76ee01ab38ae49ec",
            "76ee01ab38ae49ec",
            "76ee01ab38ae49ec",
            "90297231957bd8ef",
            "90297231957bd8ef",
            "90297231957bd8ef",
            "90297231957bd8ef",
            "90297231957bd8ef",
            "6bd8bc474596d812",
            "6bd8bc474596d812",
            "6bd8bc474596d812",
            "6bd8bc474596d812",
            "2b9e23db3a8bf16c",
            "2b9e23db3a8bf16c",
            "2b9e23db3a8bf16c",
            "30b97efb1204a874",
            "30b97efb1204a874",
            "30b97efb1204a874",
            "30b97efb1204a874",
            "117b8e4cf38485f1",
            "117b8e4cf38485f1",
            "117b8e4cf38485f1",
            "117b8e4cf38485f1",
            "9bb38757ec23daa3",
            "9bb38757ec23daa3",
            "9bb38757ec23daa3",
            "8ba00072029cd718",
            "8ba00072029cd718",
            "8ba00072029cd718",
            "c0b04475fe68a2dd",
            "c0b04475fe68a2dd",
            "c0b04475fe68a2dd",
            "eeedb52a4b15ed1e",
            "eeedb52a4b15ed1e",
            "688dd95fa5fc7d0d",
            "688dd95fa5fc7d0d",
            "688dd95fa5fc7d0d",
            "b488c0e18b2fce50",
            "b488c0e18b2fce50",
            "b488c0e18b2fce50",
            "046ad44ca04a3e8f",
            "046ad44ca04a3e8f",
            "046ad44ca04a3e8f",
            "e90ff39c0d4d11d6",
            "e90ff39c0d4d11d6",
            "ea526891e6481a37",
            "ea526891e6481a37",
            "74f3ad32a0f00007",
            "74f3ad32a0f00007",
            "74f3ad32a0f00007",
            "74f3ad32a0f00007",
            "57500015faad53dd",
            "57500015faad53dd",
            "57500015faad53dd",
            "57500015faad53dd",
            "fbe002703a61e612",
            "fbe002703a61e612",
            "fbe002703a61e612",
            "fbe002703a61e612",
            "fbe002703a61e612"
          ],
          "title": "Supported Versions"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.2.2",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1063b342126a4e03"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "struct {"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1063b342126a4e03"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "opaque cookie<1..2^16-1>;"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1063b342126a4e03"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "} Cookie;"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9650e4559b097dfd"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Cookies serve two primary purposes:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9650e4559b097dfd"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "-  Allowing the server to force the client to demonstrate"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9650e4559b097dfd"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "reachability at their apparent network address (thus providing a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9650e4559b097dfd"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "measure of DoS protection).  This is primarily useful for"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9650e4559b097dfd"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "non-connection-oriented transports (see [RFC6347] for an example"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9650e4559b097dfd"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "of this)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9650e4559b097dfd"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "-  Allowing the server to offload state to the client, thus allowing"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9650e4559b097dfd"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "it to send a HelloRetryRequest without storing any state.  The"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9650e4559b097dfd"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "server can do this by storing the hash of the ClientHello in the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9650e4559b097dfd"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "HelloRetryRequest cookie (protected with some suitable integrity"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9650e4559b097dfd"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "protection algorithm)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "79824a7b4eb20072",
                  "ae4597c12cf9dcdf",
                  "9650e4559b097dfd"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "When sending a HelloRetryRequest, the server MAY provide a \"cookie\""
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "79824a7b4eb20072",
                  "ae4597c12cf9dcdf",
                  "9650e4559b097dfd"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "extension to the client (this is an exception to the usual rule that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "79824a7b4eb20072",
                  "ae4597c12cf9dcdf",
                  "9650e4559b097dfd"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "the only extensions that may be sent are those that appear in the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "79824a7b4eb20072",
                  "ae4597c12cf9dcdf",
                  "9650e4559b097dfd"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "ClientHello)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ae4597c12cf9dcdf"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2e326cab508fa7f2",
                  "ae4597c12cf9dcdf",
                  "5db26ee75711b9d1",
                  "eb7e3a3357f34fc3"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "When sending the new ClientHello, the client MUST copy"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2e326cab508fa7f2",
                  "ae4597c12cf9dcdf",
                  "5db26ee75711b9d1",
                  "eb7e3a3357f34fc3"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "the contents of the extension received in the HelloRetryRequest into"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2e326cab508fa7f2",
                  "ae4597c12cf9dcdf",
                  "5db26ee75711b9d1",
                  "eb7e3a3357f34fc3"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "a \"cookie\" extension in the new ClientHello."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bd0d6be60129293b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Clients MUST NOT use"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bd0d6be60129293b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "cookies in their initial ClientHello in subsequent connections."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   When a server is operating statelessly, it may receive an unprotected",
            "   record of type change_cipher_spec between the first and second",
            "   ClientHello (see Section 5).  Since the server is not storing any",
            "   state, this will appear as if it were the first message to be",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   received.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cbcf7b78e9caf6cf"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Servers operating statelessly MUST ignore these records."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "79824a7b4eb20072",
            "79824a7b4eb20072",
            "79824a7b4eb20072",
            "79824a7b4eb20072",
            "2e326cab508fa7f2",
            "2e326cab508fa7f2",
            "2e326cab508fa7f2",
            "bd0d6be60129293b",
            "bd0d6be60129293b",
            "cbcf7b78e9caf6cf"
          ],
          "title": "Cookie"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.2.3",
          "lines": [
            "   TLS 1.3 provides two extensions for indicating which signature",
            "   algorithms may be used in digital signatures.  The",
            "   \"signature_algorithms_cert\" extension applies to signatures in",
            "   certificates, and the \"signature_algorithms\" extension, which",
            "   originally appeared in TLS 1.2, applies to signatures in",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   CertificateVerify messages.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f6840a998bc64b3b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The keys found in certificates MUST also"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f6840a998bc64b3b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "be of appropriate type for the signature algorithms they are used"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f6840a998bc64b3b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "with."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This is a particular issue for RSA keys and PSS signatures, as"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   described below.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9ecd3cbc0fd28b91"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "If no \"signature_algorithms_cert\" extension is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9ecd3cbc0fd28b91"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "present, then the \"signature_algorithms\" extension also applies to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9ecd3cbc0fd28b91"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "signatures appearing in certificates."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a0ef6ed6de0e1ac"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Clients which desire the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a0ef6ed6de0e1ac"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "server to authenticate itself via a certificate MUST send the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a0ef6ed6de0e1ac"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "\"signature_algorithms\" extension."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dadffba726b05db4"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If a server is authenticating via"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dadffba726b05db4"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "a certificate and the client has not sent a \"signature_algorithms\""
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dadffba726b05db4"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "extension, then the server MUST abort the handshake with a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dadffba726b05db4"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "\"missing_extension\" alert (see Section 9.2)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The \"signature_algorithms_cert\" extension was added to allow",
            "   implementations which supported different sets of algorithms for",
            "   certificates and in TLS itself to clearly signal their capabilities.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4cabe718c48e4a28"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "TLS 1.2 implementations SHOULD also process this extension."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a1ead1d2188a0c2c"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Implementations which have the same policy in both cases MAY omit the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a1ead1d2188a0c2c"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "\"signature_algorithms_cert\" extension."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The \"extension_data\" field of these extensions contains a",
            "   SignatureSchemeList value:",
            "",
            "      enum {",
            "          /* RSASSA-PKCS1-v1_5 algorithms */",
            "          rsa_pkcs1_sha256(0x0401),",
            "          rsa_pkcs1_sha384(0x0501),",
            "          rsa_pkcs1_sha512(0x0601),",
            "",
            "          /* ECDSA algorithms */",
            "          ecdsa_secp256r1_sha256(0x0403),",
            "          ecdsa_secp384r1_sha384(0x0503),",
            "          ecdsa_secp521r1_sha512(0x0603),",
            "",
            "          /* RSASSA-PSS algorithms with public key OID rsaEncryption */",
            "          rsa_pss_rsae_sha256(0x0804),",
            "          rsa_pss_rsae_sha384(0x0805),",
            "          rsa_pss_rsae_sha512(0x0806),",
            "",
            "          /* EdDSA algorithms */",
            "          ed25519(0x0807),",
            "          ed448(0x0808),",
            "",
            "          /* RSASSA-PSS algorithms with public key OID RSASSA-PSS */",
            "          rsa_pss_pss_sha256(0x0809),",
            "          rsa_pss_pss_sha384(0x080a),",
            "          rsa_pss_pss_sha512(0x080b),",
            "",
            "          /* Legacy algorithms */",
            "          rsa_pkcs1_sha1(0x0201),",
            "          ecdsa_sha1(0x0203),",
            "",
            "          /* Reserved Code Points */",
            "          private_use(0xFE00..0xFFFF),",
            "          (0xFFFF)",
            "      } SignatureScheme;",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          SignatureScheme supported_signature_algorithms<2..2^16-2>;",
            "      } SignatureSchemeList;",
            "",
            "   Note: This enum is named \"SignatureScheme\" because there is already a",
            "   \"SignatureAlgorithm\" type in TLS 1.2, which this replaces.  We use",
            "   the term \"signature algorithm\" throughout the text.",
            "",
            "   Each SignatureScheme value lists a single signature algorithm that",
            "   the client is willing to verify.  The values are indicated in",
            "   descending order of preference.  Note that a signature algorithm",
            "   takes as input an arbitrary-length message, rather than a digest.",
            "   Algorithms which traditionally act on a digest should be defined in",
            "   TLS to first hash the input with a specified hash algorithm and then",
            "   proceed as usual.  The code point groups listed above have the",
            "   following meanings:",
            "",
            "   RSASSA-PKCS1-v1_5 algorithms:  Indicates a signature algorithm using",
            "      RSASSA-PKCS1-v1_5 [RFC8017] with the corresponding hash algorithm",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      as defined in [SHS].  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3af7b0cda3b0e97c",
                  "e20adffb9dd4f740"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "These values refer solely to signatures"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3af7b0cda3b0e97c",
                  "e20adffb9dd4f740"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "which appear in certificates (see Section 4.4.2.2) and are not"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3af7b0cda3b0e97c",
                  "e20adffb9dd4f740"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "defined for use in signed TLS handshake messages, although they"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3af7b0cda3b0e97c",
                  "e20adffb9dd4f740"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "MAY appear in \"signature_algorithms\" and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3af7b0cda3b0e97c",
                  "e20adffb9dd4f740"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "\"signature_algorithms_cert\" for backward compatibility with"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3af7b0cda3b0e97c",
                  "e20adffb9dd4f740"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "TLS 1.2."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   ECDSA algorithms:  Indicates a signature algorithm using ECDSA",
            "      [ECDSA], the corresponding curve as defined in ANSI X9.62 [ECDSA]",
            "      and FIPS 186-4 [DSS], and the corresponding hash algorithm as",
            "      defined in [SHS].  The signature is represented as a DER-encoded",
            "      [X690] ECDSA-Sig-Value structure.",
            "",
            "   RSASSA-PSS RSAE algorithms:  Indicates a signature algorithm using",
            "      RSASSA-PSS [RFC8017] with mask generation function 1.  The digest",
            "      used in the mask generation function and the digest being signed",
            "      are both the corresponding hash algorithm as defined in [SHS].",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "80555d519c6f2370"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The length of the Salt MUST be equal to the length of the output"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "80555d519c6f2370"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "of the digest algorithm."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2152825c8167f789"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If the public key is carried in an X.509"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2152825c8167f789"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "certificate, it MUST use the rsaEncryption OID [RFC5280]."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   EdDSA algorithms:  Indicates a signature algorithm using EdDSA as",
            "      defined in [RFC8032] or its successors.  Note that these",
            "      correspond to the \"PureEdDSA\" algorithms and not the \"prehash\"",
            "      variants.",
            "",
            "   RSASSA-PSS PSS algorithms:  Indicates a signature algorithm using",
            "      RSASSA-PSS [RFC8017] with mask generation function 1.  The digest",
            "      used in the mask generation function and the digest being signed",
            "      are both the corresponding hash algorithm as defined in [SHS].",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "51d2174120eeeacf"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The length of the Salt MUST be equal to the length of the digest"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "51d2174120eeeacf"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "algorithm."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5a0f30e26a8a0901"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If the public key is carried in an X.509 certificate,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5a0f30e26a8a0901"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "it MUST use the RSASSA-PSS OID [RFC5756]."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d44f4b10e6141a1e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "When used in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d44f4b10e6141a1e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "certificate signatures, the algorithm parameters MUST be DER"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d44f4b10e6141a1e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "encoded."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8edde5af99d0f493"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If the corresponding public key's parameters are"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8edde5af99d0f493"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "present, then the parameters in the signature MUST be identical to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8edde5af99d0f493"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "those in the public key."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Legacy algorithms:  Indicates algorithms which are being deprecated",
            "      because they use algorithms with known weaknesses, specifically",
            "      SHA-1 which is used in this context with either (1) RSA using",
            "      RSASSA-PKCS1-v1_5 or (2) ECDSA.  These values refer solely to",
            "      signatures which appear in certificates (see Section 4.4.2.2) and",
            "      are not defined for use in signed TLS handshake messages, although",
            "      they MAY appear in \"signature_algorithms\" and",
            "      \"signature_algorithms_cert\" for backward compatibility with",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      TLS 1.2.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "420ec11afd4d43dc"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "Endpoints SHOULD NOT negotiate these algorithms but are"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "420ec11afd4d43dc"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "permitted to do so solely for backward compatibility."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5fb8786068822c94"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Clients"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5fb8786068822c94"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "offering these values MUST list them as the lowest priority"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5fb8786068822c94"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "(listed after all other algorithms in SignatureSchemeList)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bd27d653b32bb7a5"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "TLS 1.3 servers MUST NOT offer a SHA-1 signed certificate unless"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bd27d653b32bb7a5"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "no valid certificate chain can be produced without it (see"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bd27d653b32bb7a5"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Section 4.4.2.2)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The signatures on certificates that are self-signed or certificates",
            "   that are trust anchors are not validated, since they begin a",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   certification path (see [RFC5280], Section 3.2).  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1e225cfcb93bee7d"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "A certificate that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1e225cfcb93bee7d"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "begins a certification path MAY use a signature algorithm that is not"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1e225cfcb93bee7d"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "advertised as being supported in the \"signature_algorithms\""
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1e225cfcb93bee7d"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "extension."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   Note that TLS 1.2 defines this extension differently.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e1419856d5601312"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "TLS 1.3"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e1419856d5601312"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "implementations willing to negotiate TLS 1.2 MUST behave in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e1419856d5601312"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "accordance with the requirements of [RFC5246] when negotiating that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e1419856d5601312"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "version."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  In particular:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "585d67023015314a"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "-  TLS 1.2 ClientHellos MAY omit this extension."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   -  In TLS 1.2, the extension contained hash/signature pairs.  The",
            "      pairs are encoded in two octets, so SignatureScheme values have",
            "      been allocated to align with TLS 1.2's encoding.  Some legacy",
            "      pairs are left unallocated.  These algorithms are deprecated as of",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      TLS 1.3.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a5bda35bb775d91b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "They MUST NOT be offered or negotiated by any"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a5bda35bb775d91b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "implementation."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bcab6d6ee60587cb"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "In particular, MD5 [SLOTH], SHA-224, and DSA"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bcab6d6ee60587cb"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "MUST NOT be used."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   -  ECDSA signature schemes align with TLS 1.2's ECDSA hash/signature",
            "      pairs.  However, the old semantics did not constrain the signing",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      curve.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "54bc1a1342dc0c08"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If TLS 1.2 is negotiated, implementations MUST be prepared"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "54bc1a1342dc0c08"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "to accept a signature that uses any curve that they advertised in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "54bc1a1342dc0c08"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "the \"supported_groups\" extension."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b61c99b381030efb"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "-  Implementations that advertise support for RSASSA-PSS (which is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b61c99b381030efb"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "mandatory in TLS 1.3) MUST be prepared to accept a signature using"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b61c99b381030efb"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "that scheme even when TLS 1.2 is negotiated."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  In TLS 1.2,"
              }
            ],
            "      RSASSA-PSS is used with RSA cipher suites."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "f6840a998bc64b3b",
            "f6840a998bc64b3b",
            "f6840a998bc64b3b",
            "0a0ef6ed6de0e1ac",
            "0a0ef6ed6de0e1ac",
            "0a0ef6ed6de0e1ac",
            "dadffba726b05db4",
            "dadffba726b05db4",
            "dadffba726b05db4",
            "dadffba726b05db4",
            "4cabe718c48e4a28",
            "a1ead1d2188a0c2c",
            "a1ead1d2188a0c2c",
            "3af7b0cda3b0e97c",
            "3af7b0cda3b0e97c",
            "3af7b0cda3b0e97c",
            "3af7b0cda3b0e97c",
            "3af7b0cda3b0e97c",
            "3af7b0cda3b0e97c",
            "80555d519c6f2370",
            "80555d519c6f2370",
            "2152825c8167f789",
            "2152825c8167f789",
            "51d2174120eeeacf",
            "51d2174120eeeacf",
            "5a0f30e26a8a0901",
            "5a0f30e26a8a0901",
            "d44f4b10e6141a1e",
            "d44f4b10e6141a1e",
            "d44f4b10e6141a1e",
            "8edde5af99d0f493",
            "8edde5af99d0f493",
            "8edde5af99d0f493",
            "e20adffb9dd4f740",
            "e20adffb9dd4f740",
            "e20adffb9dd4f740",
            "e20adffb9dd4f740",
            "e20adffb9dd4f740",
            "e20adffb9dd4f740",
            "420ec11afd4d43dc",
            "420ec11afd4d43dc",
            "5fb8786068822c94",
            "5fb8786068822c94",
            "5fb8786068822c94",
            "bd27d653b32bb7a5",
            "bd27d653b32bb7a5",
            "bd27d653b32bb7a5",
            "1e225cfcb93bee7d",
            "1e225cfcb93bee7d",
            "1e225cfcb93bee7d",
            "1e225cfcb93bee7d",
            "e1419856d5601312",
            "e1419856d5601312",
            "e1419856d5601312",
            "e1419856d5601312",
            "585d67023015314a",
            "a5bda35bb775d91b",
            "a5bda35bb775d91b",
            "bcab6d6ee60587cb",
            "bcab6d6ee60587cb",
            "54bc1a1342dc0c08",
            "54bc1a1342dc0c08",
            "54bc1a1342dc0c08",
            "b61c99b381030efb",
            "b61c99b381030efb",
            "b61c99b381030efb"
          ],
          "title": "Signature Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.2.4",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e648ff193a53d846",
                  "5cfe1b95c33ab976"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "The \"certificate_authorities\" extension is used to indicate the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e648ff193a53d846",
                  "5cfe1b95c33ab976"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "certificate authorities (CAs) which an endpoint supports and which"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e648ff193a53d846",
                  "5cfe1b95c33ab976"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "SHOULD be used by the receiving endpoint to guide certificate"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e648ff193a53d846",
                  "5cfe1b95c33ab976"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "selection."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The body of the \"certificate_authorities\" extension consists of a",
            "   CertificateAuthoritiesExtension structure.",
            "",
            "      opaque DistinguishedName<1..2^16-1>;",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          DistinguishedName authorities<3..2^16-1>;",
            "      } CertificateAuthoritiesExtension;",
            "",
            "   authorities:  A list of the distinguished names [X501] of acceptable",
            "      certificate authorities, represented in DER-encoded [X690] format.",
            "      These distinguished names specify a desired distinguished name for",
            "      a trust anchor or subordinate CA; thus, this message can be used",
            "      to describe known trust anchors as well as a desired authorization",
            "      space.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3cd98aedfa14d59a",
                  "02a16cec81965f7d",
                  "a1942acdd494e9ac"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "The client MAY send the \"certificate_authorities\" extension in the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3cd98aedfa14d59a",
                  "02a16cec81965f7d",
                  "a1942acdd494e9ac"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "ClientHello message."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6ed0c296f2ca915c",
                  "d5d81ff4d4d50258",
                  "d2f5765f40a6e11d"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "The server MAY send it in the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6ed0c296f2ca915c",
                  "d5d81ff4d4d50258",
                  "d2f5765f40a6e11d"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "CertificateRequest message."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The \"trusted_ca_keys\" extension [RFC6066], which serves a similar",
            "   purpose but is more complicated, is not used in TLS 1.3 (although it",
            "   may appear in ClientHello messages from clients which are offering",
            "   prior versions of TLS)."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "e648ff193a53d846",
            "e648ff193a53d846",
            "e648ff193a53d846",
            "e648ff193a53d846",
            "3cd98aedfa14d59a",
            "3cd98aedfa14d59a",
            "6ed0c296f2ca915c",
            "6ed0c296f2ca915c"
          ],
          "title": "Certificate Authorities"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.2.5",
          "lines": [
            "   The \"oid_filters\" extension allows servers to provide a set of",
            "   OID/value pairs which it would like the client's certificate to",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   match.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7805c955ccca5cef"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "This extension, if provided by the server, MUST only be sent"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7805c955ccca5cef"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "in the CertificateRequest message."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          opaque certificate_extension_oid<1..2^8-1>;",
            "          opaque certificate_extension_values<0..2^16-1>;",
            "      } OIDFilter;",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          OIDFilter filters<0..2^16-1>;",
            "      } OIDFilterExtension;",
            "",
            "   filters:  A list of certificate extension OIDs [RFC5280] with their",
            "      allowed value(s) and represented in DER-encoded [X690] format.",
            "      Some certificate extension OIDs allow multiple values (e.g.,",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      Extended Key Usage).  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a7645c1d5aae21d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If the server has included a non-empty"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a7645c1d5aae21d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "filters list, the client certificate included in the response MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a7645c1d5aae21d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "contain all of the specified extension OIDs that the client"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a7645c1d5aae21d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "recognizes."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b7a12abb9462706d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "For each extension OID recognized by the client, all"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b7a12abb9462706d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "of the specified values MUST be present in the client certificate"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b7a12abb9462706d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "(but the certificate MAY have other values as well)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6baf2ddd3b3f8316"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "However, the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6baf2ddd3b3f8316"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "client MUST ignore and skip any unrecognized certificate extension"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6baf2ddd3b3f8316"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "OIDs."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b1f1a5ea963868ee"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "If the client ignored some of the required certificate"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b1f1a5ea963868ee"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "extension OIDs and supplied a certificate that does not satisfy"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b1f1a5ea963868ee"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "the request, the server MAY at its discretion either continue the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b1f1a5ea963868ee"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "connection without client authentication or abort the handshake"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b1f1a5ea963868ee"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "with an \"unsupported_certificate\" alert."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aed4e48326840399"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Any given OID MUST NOT"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aed4e48326840399"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "appear more than once in the filters list."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   PKIX RFCs define a variety of certificate extension OIDs and their",
            "   corresponding value types.  Depending on the type, matching",
            "   certificate extension values are not necessarily bitwise-equal.  It",
            "   is expected that TLS implementations will rely on their PKI libraries",
            "   to perform certificate selection using certificate extension OIDs.",
            "",
            "   This document defines matching rules for two standard certificate",
            "   extensions defined in [RFC5280]:",
            "",
            "   -  The Key Usage extension in a certificate matches the request when",
            "      all key usage bits asserted in the request are also asserted in",
            "      the Key Usage certificate extension.",
            "",
            "   -  The Extended Key Usage extension in a certificate matches the",
            "      request when all key purpose OIDs present in the request are also",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      found in the Extended Key Usage certificate extension.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b0ed093de5c6b444"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b0ed093de5c6b444"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "special anyExtendedKeyUsage OID MUST NOT be used in the request."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Separate specifications may define matching rules for other",
            "   certificate extensions."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "7805c955ccca5cef",
            "7805c955ccca5cef",
            "0a7645c1d5aae21d",
            "0a7645c1d5aae21d",
            "0a7645c1d5aae21d",
            "0a7645c1d5aae21d",
            "b7a12abb9462706d",
            "b7a12abb9462706d",
            "b7a12abb9462706d",
            "6baf2ddd3b3f8316",
            "6baf2ddd3b3f8316",
            "6baf2ddd3b3f8316",
            "b1f1a5ea963868ee",
            "b1f1a5ea963868ee",
            "b1f1a5ea963868ee",
            "b1f1a5ea963868ee",
            "b1f1a5ea963868ee",
            "aed4e48326840399",
            "aed4e48326840399",
            "b0ed093de5c6b444",
            "b0ed093de5c6b444"
          ],
          "title": "OID Filters"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.2.6",
          "lines": [
            "   The \"post_handshake_auth\" extension is used to indicate that a client",
            "   is willing to perform post-handshake authentication (Section 4.6.2).",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c6909abf7bf8febd"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Servers MUST NOT send a post-handshake CertificateRequest to clients"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c6909abf7bf8febd"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "which do not offer this extension."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "25f3792191b278d1"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Servers MUST NOT send this"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "25f3792191b278d1"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "extension."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "      struct {} PostHandshakeAuth;",
            "",
            "   The \"extension_data\" field of the \"post_handshake_auth\" extension is",
            "   zero length."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "c6909abf7bf8febd",
            "c6909abf7bf8febd",
            "25f3792191b278d1",
            "25f3792191b278d1"
          ],
          "title": "Post-Handshake Client Authentication"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.2.7",
          "lines": [
            "   When sent by the client, the \"supported_groups\" extension indicates",
            "   the named groups which the client supports for key exchange, ordered",
            "   from most preferred to least preferred.",
            "",
            "   Note: In versions of TLS prior to TLS 1.3, this extension was named",
            "   \"elliptic_curves\" and only contained elliptic curve groups.  See",
            "   [RFC8422] and [RFC7919].  This extension was also used to negotiate",
            "   ECDSA curves.  Signature algorithms are now negotiated independently",
            "   (see Section 4.2.3).",
            "",
            "   The \"extension_data\" field of this extension contains a",
            "   \"NamedGroupList\" value:",
            "",
            "      enum {",
            "",
            "          /* Elliptic Curve Groups (ECDHE) */",
            "          secp256r1(0x0017), secp384r1(0x0018), secp521r1(0x0019),",
            "          x25519(0x001D), x448(0x001E),",
            "",
            "          /* Finite Field Groups (DHE) */",
            "          ffdhe2048(0x0100), ffdhe3072(0x0101), ffdhe4096(0x0102),",
            "          ffdhe6144(0x0103), ffdhe8192(0x0104),",
            "",
            "          /* Reserved Code Points */",
            "          ffdhe_private_use(0x01FC..0x01FF),",
            "          ecdhe_private_use(0xFE00..0xFEFF),",
            "          (0xFFFF)",
            "      } NamedGroup;",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          NamedGroup named_group_list<2..2^16-1>;",
            "      } NamedGroupList;",
            "",
            "   Elliptic Curve Groups (ECDHE):  Indicates support for the",
            "      corresponding named curve, defined in either FIPS 186-4 [DSS] or",
            "      [RFC7748].  Values 0xFE00 through 0xFEFF are reserved for",
            "      Private Use [RFC8126].",
            "",
            "   Finite Field Groups (DHE):  Indicates support for the corresponding",
            "      finite field group, defined in [RFC7919].  Values 0x01FC through",
            "      0x01FF are reserved for Private Use.",
            "",
            "   Items in named_group_list are ordered according to the sender's",
            "   preferences (most preferred choice first).",
            "",
            "   As of TLS 1.3, servers are permitted to send the \"supported_groups\"",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   extension to the client.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d4c70d2c2c9de825"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Clients MUST NOT act upon any information"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d4c70d2c2c9de825"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "found in \"supported_groups\" prior to successful completion of the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d4c70d2c2c9de825"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "handshake but MAY use the information learned from a successfully"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d4c70d2c2c9de825"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "completed handshake to change what groups they use in their"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d4c70d2c2c9de825"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "\"key_share\" extension in subsequent connections."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd278e4e443b2f2a",
                  "c1b493bba3b178da"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "If the server has a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd278e4e443b2f2a",
                  "c1b493bba3b178da"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "group it prefers to the ones in the \"key_share\" extension but is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd278e4e443b2f2a",
                  "c1b493bba3b178da"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "still willing to accept the ClientHello, it SHOULD send"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd278e4e443b2f2a",
                  "c1b493bba3b178da"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "\"supported_groups\" to update the client's view of its preferences;"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd278e4e443b2f2a",
                  "c1b493bba3b178da"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "this extension SHOULD contain all groups the server supports,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd278e4e443b2f2a",
                  "c1b493bba3b178da"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "regardless of whether they are currently supported by the client."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "d4c70d2c2c9de825",
            "d4c70d2c2c9de825",
            "d4c70d2c2c9de825",
            "d4c70d2c2c9de825",
            "d4c70d2c2c9de825",
            "dd278e4e443b2f2a",
            "dd278e4e443b2f2a",
            "dd278e4e443b2f2a",
            "dd278e4e443b2f2a",
            "dd278e4e443b2f2a",
            "dd278e4e443b2f2a",
            "c1b493bba3b178da",
            "c1b493bba3b178da",
            "c1b493bba3b178da",
            "c1b493bba3b178da",
            "c1b493bba3b178da",
            "c1b493bba3b178da"
          ],
          "title": "Supported Groups"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.2.8",
          "lines": [
            "   The \"key_share\" extension contains the endpoint's cryptographic",
            "   parameters.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8ad40ad8bc81a988"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Clients MAY send an empty client_shares vector in order to request"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8ad40ad8bc81a988"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "group selection from the server, at the cost of an additional round"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8ad40ad8bc81a988"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "trip (see Section 4.1.4)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          NamedGroup group;",
            "          opaque key_exchange<1..2^16-1>;",
            "      } KeyShareEntry;",
            "",
            "   group:  The named group for the key being exchanged.",
            "",
            "   key_exchange:  Key exchange information.  The contents of this field",
            "      are determined by the specified group and its corresponding",
            "      definition.  Finite Field Diffie-Hellman [DH76] parameters are",
            "      described in Section 4.2.8.1; Elliptic Curve Diffie-Hellman",
            "      parameters are described in Section 4.2.8.2.",
            "",
            "   In the ClientHello message, the \"extension_data\" field of this",
            "   extension contains a \"KeyShareClientHello\" value:",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          KeyShareEntry client_shares<0..2^16-1>;",
            "      } KeyShareClientHello;",
            "",
            "   client_shares:  A list of offered KeyShareEntry values in descending",
            "      order of client preference.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1d30392ee23c71f0"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "This vector MAY be empty if the client is requesting a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1d30392ee23c71f0"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "HelloRetryRequest."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "592c5005e18aab18",
                  "bd064bae6be53a1f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Each KeyShareEntry value MUST correspond to a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "592c5005e18aab18",
                  "bd064bae6be53a1f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "group offered in the \"supported_groups\" extension and MUST appear in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "592c5005e18aab18",
                  "bd064bae6be53a1f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "the same order."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d199239e9bebe2ea",
                  "9cc8089c5a9441ad"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "However, the values MAY be a non-contiguous subset"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d199239e9bebe2ea",
                  "9cc8089c5a9441ad"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "of the \"supported_groups\" extension and MAY omit the most preferred"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d199239e9bebe2ea",
                  "9cc8089c5a9441ad"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "groups."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Such a situation could arise if the most preferred groups"
              }
            ],
            "   are new and unlikely to be supported in enough places to make",
            "   pregenerating key shares for them efficient.",
            "",
            "   Clients can offer as many KeyShareEntry values as the number of",
            "   supported groups it is offering, each representing a single set of",
            "   key exchange parameters.  For instance, a client might offer shares",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   for several elliptic curves or multiple FFDHE groups.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8d4143c57d9c0f95"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8d4143c57d9c0f95"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "key_exchange values for each KeyShareEntry MUST be generated"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8d4143c57d9c0f95"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "independently."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d07524c1b0d9b4d4"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Clients MUST NOT offer multiple KeyShareEntry values"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d07524c1b0d9b4d4"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "for the same group."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5a759d7ae2a8ccf8"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Clients MUST NOT offer any KeyShareEntry values"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5a759d7ae2a8ccf8"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "for groups not listed in the client's \"supported_groups\" extension."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3f842d08be5f5108"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Servers MAY check for violations of these rules and abort the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3f842d08be5f5108"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert if one is violated."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   In a HelloRetryRequest message, the \"extension_data\" field of this",
            "   extension contains a KeyShareHelloRetryRequest value:",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          NamedGroup selected_group;",
            "      } KeyShareHelloRetryRequest;",
            "",
            "   selected_group:  The mutually supported group the server intends to",
            "      negotiate and is requesting a retried ClientHello/KeyShare for.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a77380646188cccb",
                  "ec9c4b08ed2ea019",
                  "c70971b044228b08"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Upon receipt of this extension in a HelloRetryRequest, the client"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a77380646188cccb",
                  "ec9c4b08ed2ea019",
                  "c70971b044228b08"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "MUST verify that (1) the selected_group field corresponds to a group"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a77380646188cccb",
                  "ec9c4b08ed2ea019",
                  "c70971b044228b08"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "which was provided in the \"supported_groups\" extension in the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a77380646188cccb",
                  "ec9c4b08ed2ea019",
                  "c70971b044228b08"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "original ClientHello"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a77380646188cccb"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a77380646188cccb",
                  "c745ab8ce13d2b6e",
                  "abe2c1e18887c5fd"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "and (2) the selected_group field does not"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a77380646188cccb",
                  "c745ab8ce13d2b6e",
                  "abe2c1e18887c5fd"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "correspond to a group which was provided in the \"key_share\" extension"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a77380646188cccb",
                  "c745ab8ce13d2b6e",
                  "abe2c1e18887c5fd"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "in the original ClientHello."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9715f0bec6100ed9",
                  "736e583531dbd4f5"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If either of these checks fails, then"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9715f0bec6100ed9",
                  "736e583531dbd4f5"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "the client MUST abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\""
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9715f0bec6100ed9",
                  "736e583531dbd4f5"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "alert."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "36c532a56bfb49d0",
                  "3aaed3b8d5b80d25",
                  "b2e8aaad57056ae3",
                  "666d61c9917d37c1"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Otherwise, when sending the new ClientHello, the client MUST"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3aaed3b8d5b80d25",
                  "b2e8aaad57056ae3",
                  "666d61c9917d37c1"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "replace the original \"key_share\" extension with one containing only a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3aaed3b8d5b80d25",
                  "b2e8aaad57056ae3",
                  "666d61c9917d37c1"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "new KeyShareEntry for the group indicated in the selected_group field"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3aaed3b8d5b80d25",
                  "b2e8aaad57056ae3",
                  "666d61c9917d37c1"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "of the triggering HelloRetryRequest."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   In a ServerHello message, the \"extension_data\" field of this",
            "   extension contains a KeyShareServerHello value:",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          KeyShareEntry server_share;",
            "      } KeyShareServerHello;",
            "",
            "   server_share:  A single KeyShareEntry value that is in the same group",
            "      as one of the client's shares.",
            "",
            "   If using (EC)DHE key establishment, servers offer exactly one",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   KeyShareEntry in the ServerHello.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6b1d704717f26870"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "This value MUST be in the same"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6b1d704717f26870"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "group as the KeyShareEntry value offered by the client that the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6b1d704717f26870"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "server has selected for the negotiated key exchange."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "be143059001f489d",
                  "e23bde55d4a98e04"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Servers"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "be143059001f489d",
                  "e23bde55d4a98e04"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "MUST NOT send a KeyShareEntry for any group not indicated in the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "be143059001f489d",
                  "e23bde55d4a98e04"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "client's \"supported_groups\" extension and MUST NOT send a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "be143059001f489d",
                  "e23bde55d4a98e04"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "KeyShareEntry when using the \"psk_ke\" PskKeyExchangeMode."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d4dc4fb9c6c474e0",
                  "b17f4f0602661715",
                  "38b766fc7ea56fde"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "If using"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d4dc4fb9c6c474e0",
                  "b17f4f0602661715",
                  "38b766fc7ea56fde"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "(EC)DHE key establishment and a HelloRetryRequest containing a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d4dc4fb9c6c474e0",
                  "b17f4f0602661715",
                  "38b766fc7ea56fde"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "\"key_share\" extension was received by the client, the client MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d4dc4fb9c6c474e0",
                  "b17f4f0602661715",
                  "38b766fc7ea56fde"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "verify that the selected NamedGroup in the ServerHello is the same as"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d4dc4fb9c6c474e0",
                  "b17f4f0602661715",
                  "38b766fc7ea56fde"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "that in the HelloRetryRequest."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b17f4f0602661715",
                  "38b766fc7ea56fde"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f856403d3f06c9df",
                  "b17f4f0602661715",
                  "38b766fc7ea56fde"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "If this check fails, the client MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f856403d3f06c9df",
                  "b17f4f0602661715",
                  "38b766fc7ea56fde"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "abort the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "8ad40ad8bc81a988",
            "8ad40ad8bc81a988",
            "8ad40ad8bc81a988",
            "1d30392ee23c71f0",
            "1d30392ee23c71f0",
            "592c5005e18aab18",
            "592c5005e18aab18",
            "592c5005e18aab18",
            "bd064bae6be53a1f",
            "bd064bae6be53a1f",
            "bd064bae6be53a1f",
            "d199239e9bebe2ea",
            "d199239e9bebe2ea",
            "d199239e9bebe2ea",
            "9cc8089c5a9441ad",
            "9cc8089c5a9441ad",
            "9cc8089c5a9441ad",
            "8d4143c57d9c0f95",
            "8d4143c57d9c0f95",
            "8d4143c57d9c0f95",
            "d07524c1b0d9b4d4",
            "d07524c1b0d9b4d4",
            "5a759d7ae2a8ccf8",
            "5a759d7ae2a8ccf8",
            "3f842d08be5f5108",
            "3f842d08be5f5108",
            "a77380646188cccb",
            "a77380646188cccb",
            "a77380646188cccb",
            "a77380646188cccb",
            "a77380646188cccb",
            "a77380646188cccb",
            "9715f0bec6100ed9",
            "9715f0bec6100ed9",
            "9715f0bec6100ed9",
            "36c532a56bfb49d0",
            "6b1d704717f26870",
            "6b1d704717f26870",
            "6b1d704717f26870",
            "be143059001f489d",
            "be143059001f489d",
            "be143059001f489d",
            "be143059001f489d",
            "e23bde55d4a98e04",
            "e23bde55d4a98e04",
            "e23bde55d4a98e04",
            "e23bde55d4a98e04",
            "d4dc4fb9c6c474e0",
            "d4dc4fb9c6c474e0",
            "d4dc4fb9c6c474e0",
            "d4dc4fb9c6c474e0",
            "d4dc4fb9c6c474e0",
            "f856403d3f06c9df",
            "f856403d3f06c9df"
          ],
          "title": "Key Share"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.2.8.1",
          "lines": [
            "   Diffie-Hellman [DH76] parameters for both clients and servers are",
            "   encoded in the opaque key_exchange field of a KeyShareEntry in a",
            "   KeyShare structure.  The opaque value contains the Diffie-Hellman",
            "   public value (Y = g^X mod p) for the specified group (see [RFC7919]",
            "   for group definitions) encoded as a big-endian integer and padded to",
            "   the left with zeros to the size of p in bytes.",
            "",
            "   Note: For a given Diffie-Hellman group, the padding results in all",
            "   public keys having the same length.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "95b6307e3854a0ff"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Peers MUST validate each other's public key Y by ensuring that 1 < Y"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "95b6307e3854a0ff"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "< p-1."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This check ensures that the remote peer is properly behaved"
              }
            ],
            "   and isn't forcing the local system into a small subgroup."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "95b6307e3854a0ff",
            "95b6307e3854a0ff"
          ],
          "title": "Diffie-Hellman Parameters"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.2.8.2",
          "lines": [
            "   ECDHE parameters for both clients and servers are encoded in the",
            "   opaque key_exchange field of a KeyShareEntry in a KeyShare structure.",
            "",
            "   For secp256r1, secp384r1, and secp521r1, the contents are the",
            "   serialized value of the following struct:",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          uint8 legacy_form = 4;",
            "          opaque X[coordinate_length];",
            "          opaque Y[coordinate_length];",
            "      } UncompressedPointRepresentation;",
            "",
            "   X and Y, respectively, are the binary representations of the x and y",
            "   values in network byte order.  There are no internal length markers,",
            "   so each number representation occupies as many octets as implied by",
            "   the curve parameters.  For P-256, this means that each of X and Y use",
            "   32 octets, padded on the left by zeros if necessary.  For P-384, they",
            "   take 48 octets each.  For P-521, they take 66 octets each.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "863aeebe2d32fa79",
                  "baf971f52ae287f7",
                  "62655efaa879ccad"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "For the curves secp256r1, secp384r1, and secp521r1, peers MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "863aeebe2d32fa79",
                  "baf971f52ae287f7",
                  "62655efaa879ccad"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "validate each other's public value Q by ensuring that the point is a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "863aeebe2d32fa79",
                  "baf971f52ae287f7",
                  "62655efaa879ccad"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "valid point on the elliptic curve."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "62655efaa879ccad"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "  The appropriate validation"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "62655efaa879ccad"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "procedures are defined in Section 4.3.7 of [ECDSA] and alternatively"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "62655efaa879ccad"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "in Section 5.6.2.3 of [KEYAGREEMENT].  This process consists of three"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "62655efaa879ccad"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "steps: (1) verify that Q is not the point at infinity (O), (2) verify"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "62655efaa879ccad"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "that for Q = (x, y) both integers x and y are in the correct"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "62655efaa879ccad"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "interval, and (3) ensure that (x, y) is a correct solution to the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "62655efaa879ccad"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "elliptic curve equation.  For these curves, implementors do not need"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "62655efaa879ccad"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "to verify membership in the correct subgroup."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   For X25519 and X448, the contents of the public value are the byte",
            "   string inputs and outputs of the corresponding functions defined in",
            "   [RFC7748]: 32 bytes for X25519 and 56 bytes for X448.",
            "",
            "   Note: Versions of TLS prior to 1.3 permitted point format",
            "   negotiation; TLS 1.3 removes this feature in favor of a single point",
            "   format for each curve."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "863aeebe2d32fa79",
            "863aeebe2d32fa79",
            "863aeebe2d32fa79"
          ],
          "title": "ECDHE Parameters"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.2.9",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e67a8d8ea44d5276"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "In order to use PSKs, clients MUST also send a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e67a8d8ea44d5276"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "\"psk_key_exchange_modes\" extension."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  The semantics of this extension"
              }
            ],
            "   are that the client only supports the use of PSKs with these modes,",
            "   which restricts both the use of PSKs offered in this ClientHello and",
            "   those which the server might supply via NewSessionTicket.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cedafc4dba6de757"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "A client MUST provide a \"psk_key_exchange_modes\" extension if it"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cedafc4dba6de757"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "offers a \"pre_shared_key\" extension."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c573d9ded17dea75",
                  "20f54c35022a3caf"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If clients offer"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c573d9ded17dea75",
                  "20f54c35022a3caf"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "\"pre_shared_key\" without a \"psk_key_exchange_modes\" extension,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c573d9ded17dea75",
                  "20f54c35022a3caf"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "servers MUST abort the handshake."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "af42cbb374401cba",
                  "e19b9a842772ba17"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "Servers MUST NOT select a key"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "af42cbb374401cba",
                  "e19b9a842772ba17"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "exchange mode that is not listed by the client."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e19b9a842772ba17"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "  This extension also"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e19b9a842772ba17"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "restricts the modes for use with PSK resumption."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "80fd55e2e50f76be"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "Servers SHOULD NOT"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "80fd55e2e50f76be"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "send NewSessionTicket with tickets that are not compatible with the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "80fd55e2e50f76be"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "advertised modes; however, if a server does so, the impact will just"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "80fd55e2e50f76be"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "be that the client's attempts at resumption fail."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8751adeedec4cecf"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The server MUST NOT send a \"psk_key_exchange_modes\" extension."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "      enum { psk_ke(0), psk_dhe_ke(1), (255) } PskKeyExchangeMode;",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          PskKeyExchangeMode ke_modes<1..255>;",
            "      } PskKeyExchangeModes;",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   psk_ke:  PSK-only key establishment.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e293f13c9eb24316"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "In this mode, the server"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e293f13c9eb24316"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "MUST NOT supply a \"key_share\" value."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   psk_dhe_ke:  PSK with (EC)DHE key establishment.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6b9a4366888818a"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "In this mode, the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6b9a4366888818a"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "client and server MUST supply \"key_share\" values as described in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6b9a4366888818a"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Section 4.2.8."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Any future values that are allocated must ensure that the transmitted",
            "   protocol messages unambiguously identify which mode was selected by",
            "   the server; at present, this is indicated by the presence of the",
            "   \"key_share\" in the ServerHello."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "e67a8d8ea44d5276",
            "e67a8d8ea44d5276",
            "cedafc4dba6de757",
            "cedafc4dba6de757",
            "c573d9ded17dea75",
            "c573d9ded17dea75",
            "c573d9ded17dea75",
            "af42cbb374401cba",
            "af42cbb374401cba",
            "80fd55e2e50f76be",
            "80fd55e2e50f76be",
            "80fd55e2e50f76be",
            "80fd55e2e50f76be",
            "8751adeedec4cecf",
            "e293f13c9eb24316",
            "e293f13c9eb24316",
            "b6b9a4366888818a",
            "b6b9a4366888818a",
            "b6b9a4366888818a"
          ],
          "title": "Pre-Shared Key Exchange Modes"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.2.10",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "09909db927a4fc04",
                  "f40d8d82aae98cec",
                  "dda48e86ba8cccf9",
                  "003ce408b054b0aa"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "When a PSK is used and early data is allowed for that PSK, the client"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "09909db927a4fc04",
                  "f40d8d82aae98cec",
                  "dda48e86ba8cccf9",
                  "003ce408b054b0aa"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "can send Application Data in its first flight of messages.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "23025bbd378fa98e",
                  "09909db927a4fc04",
                  "f40d8d82aae98cec",
                  "dda48e86ba8cccf9",
                  "003ce408b054b0aa"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "If the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "23025bbd378fa98e",
                  "09909db927a4fc04",
                  "f40d8d82aae98cec",
                  "dda48e86ba8cccf9",
                  "003ce408b054b0aa"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "client opts to do so, it MUST supply both the \"pre_shared_key\" and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "23025bbd378fa98e",
                  "09909db927a4fc04",
                  "f40d8d82aae98cec",
                  "dda48e86ba8cccf9",
                  "003ce408b054b0aa"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "\"early_data\" extensions."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d41a405d89f0400f",
                  "f1f9c78beb600deb",
                  "6d498e8a5425d9e8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The \"extension_data\" field of this extension contains an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d41a405d89f0400f",
                  "f1f9c78beb600deb",
                  "6d498e8a5425d9e8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "\"EarlyDataIndication\" value."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d41a405d89f0400f",
                  "f1f9c78beb600deb",
                  "6d498e8a5425d9e8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "struct {} Empty;"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d41a405d89f0400f",
                  "f1f9c78beb600deb",
                  "6d498e8a5425d9e8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "struct {"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d41a405d89f0400f",
                  "f1f9c78beb600deb",
                  "6d498e8a5425d9e8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "select (Handshake.msg_type) {"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "              "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f1f9c78beb600deb"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "case new_session_ticket:   uint32 max_early_data_size;"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "              "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d18e0833ec8b1bd1"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "case client_hello:         Empty;"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "              "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b040a0ab047d751e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "case encrypted_extensions: Empty;"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cf37298fbb33f2f2",
                  "18b3600491b5f0ea",
                  "b040a0ab047d751e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "};"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cf37298fbb33f2f2",
                  "18b3600491b5f0ea",
                  "b040a0ab047d751e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "} EarlyDataIndication;"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   See Section 4.6.1 for details regarding the use of the",
            "   max_early_data_size field.",
            "",
            "   The parameters for the 0-RTT data (version, symmetric cipher suite,",
            "   Application-Layer Protocol Negotiation (ALPN) [RFC7301] protocol,",
            "   etc.) are those associated with the PSK in use.  For externally",
            "   provisioned PSKs, the associated values are those provisioned along",
            "   with the key.  For PSKs established via a NewSessionTicket message,",
            "   the associated values are those which were negotiated in the",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   connection which established the PSK.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d6262dcc5a65eeb6"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The PSK used to encrypt the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d6262dcc5a65eeb6"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "early data MUST be the first PSK listed in the client's"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d6262dcc5a65eeb6"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "\"pre_shared_key\" extension."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "844f87075683da49",
                  "a598f3de17ec2f4b"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "For PSKs provisioned via NewSessionTicket, a server MUST validate"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "844f87075683da49",
                  "a598f3de17ec2f4b"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "that the ticket age for the selected PSK identity (computed by"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "844f87075683da49",
                  "a598f3de17ec2f4b"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "subtracting ticket_age_add from PskIdentity.obfuscated_ticket_age"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "844f87075683da49",
                  "a598f3de17ec2f4b"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "modulo 2^32) is within a small tolerance of the time since the ticket"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "844f87075683da49",
                  "a598f3de17ec2f4b"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "was issued (see Section 8)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "710e2c7e2536e962",
                  "77fe6b7805044ab1"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "If it is not, the server SHOULD proceed"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "710e2c7e2536e962",
                  "77fe6b7805044ab1"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "with the handshake but reject 0-RTT, and SHOULD NOT take any other"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "710e2c7e2536e962",
                  "77fe6b7805044ab1"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "action that assumes that this ClientHello is fresh."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   0-RTT messages sent in the first flight have the same (encrypted)",
            "   content types as messages of the same type sent in other flights",
            "   (handshake and application_data) but are protected under different",
            "   keys.  After receiving the server's Finished message, if the server",
            "   has accepted early data, an EndOfEarlyData message will be sent to",
            "   indicate the key change.  This message will be encrypted with the",
            "   0-RTT traffic keys.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d81672f8522ce714",
                  "401896ecbaa7202a",
                  "5cc49a157e83595c",
                  "98be7f7531d73cc1",
                  "e89eecfd6f29f577",
                  "479d5159a6f2c6fc",
                  "3d6575bfdefd4906",
                  "d4328fc5f9e64fe9"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "A server which receives an \"early_data\" extension MUST behave in one"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d81672f8522ce714",
                  "401896ecbaa7202a",
                  "5cc49a157e83595c",
                  "98be7f7531d73cc1",
                  "e89eecfd6f29f577",
                  "479d5159a6f2c6fc",
                  "3d6575bfdefd4906",
                  "d4328fc5f9e64fe9"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "of three ways:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "98be7f7531d73cc1",
                  "479d5159a6f2c6fc"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "-  Ignore the extension and return a regular 1-RTT response."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  The"
              }
            ],
            "      server then skips past early data by attempting to deprotect",
            "      received records using the handshake traffic key, discarding",
            "      records which fail deprotection (up to the configured",
            "      max_early_data_size).  Once a record is deprotected successfully,",
            "      it is treated as the start of the client's second flight and the",
            "      server proceeds as with an ordinary 1-RTT handshake.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "81ac0f279bca3327",
                  "583a184c20dbda8d",
                  "8b26772c23f988bd"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "-  Request that the client send another ClientHello by responding"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "81ac0f279bca3327",
                  "583a184c20dbda8d",
                  "8b26772c23f988bd"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "with a HelloRetryRequest."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d7b27ded396d510e",
                  "93c25423c0e152f2",
                  "320102222914a9b7",
                  "ee57a6f60560d9fb",
                  "01e5a6662ef6af1c"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "A client MUST NOT include the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d7b27ded396d510e",
                  "93c25423c0e152f2",
                  "320102222914a9b7",
                  "ee57a6f60560d9fb",
                  "01e5a6662ef6af1c"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "\"early_data\" extension in its followup ClientHello."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  The server"
              }
            ],
            "      then ignores early data by skipping all records with an external",
            "      content type of \"application_data\" (indicating that they are",
            "      encrypted), up to the configured max_early_data_size.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "41710ca7fa823729",
                  "86de1a31cfe883aa"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "-  Return its own \"early_data\" extension in EncryptedExtensions,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "41710ca7fa823729",
                  "86de1a31cfe883aa"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "indicating that it intends to process the early data."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  It is not"
              }
            ],
            "      possible for the server to accept only a subset of the early data",
            "      messages.  Even though the server sends a message accepting early",
            "      data, the actual early data itself may already be in flight by the",
            "      time the server generates this message.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ffe09bf4a6a1f7fd",
                  "45da849a09c80518",
                  "eb63de8a0b50e570"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "In order to accept early data, the server MUST have accepted a PSK"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ffe09bf4a6a1f7fd",
                  "45da849a09c80518",
                  "eb63de8a0b50e570"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "cipher suite and selected the first key offered in the client's"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ffe09bf4a6a1f7fd",
                  "45da849a09c80518",
                  "eb63de8a0b50e570"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "\"pre_shared_key\" extension."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5a68da93877fb1c0",
                  "bea55874a7756c8f",
                  "b64b8bc781cb0dad"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "In addition, it MUST verify that the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5a68da93877fb1c0",
                  "bea55874a7756c8f",
                  "b64b8bc781cb0dad"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "following values are the same as those associated with the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5a68da93877fb1c0",
                  "bea55874a7756c8f",
                  "b64b8bc781cb0dad"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "selected PSK:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ff590985d9967e47",
                  "b64b8bc781cb0dad"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "-  The TLS version number"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6ad4ee0bff0ce97",
                  "c5d07dc50a26395d"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "-  The selected cipher suite"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd3f7e9e8182050f",
                  "2e091b2d42793f99"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "-  The selected ALPN [RFC7301] protocol, if any"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   These requirements are a superset of those needed to perform a 1-RTT",
            "   handshake using the PSK in question.  For externally established",
            "   PSKs, the associated values are those provisioned along with the key.",
            "   For PSKs established via a NewSessionTicket message, the associated",
            "   values are those negotiated in the connection during which the ticket",
            "   was established.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d277b84bf1a7b06e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Future extensions MUST define their interaction with 0-RTT."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f615fea14e863ff0",
                  "51c14eae89f530c7",
                  "41702b44e5aea298"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If any of these checks fail, the server MUST NOT respond with the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f615fea14e863ff0",
                  "51c14eae89f530c7",
                  "41702b44e5aea298"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "extension"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f615fea14e863ff0"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": " and must discard all the first-flight data using one of the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f615fea14e863ff0"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "first two mechanisms listed above (thus falling back to 1-RTT or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f615fea14e863ff0"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "2-RTT)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d45aaa763fb57017",
                  "61a7188690056ad4",
                  "e656d577ace20d4b"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "If the client attempts a 0-RTT handshake but the server"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d45aaa763fb57017",
                  "61a7188690056ad4",
                  "e656d577ace20d4b"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "rejects it, the server will generally not have the 0-RTT record"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d45aaa763fb57017",
                  "61a7188690056ad4",
                  "e656d577ace20d4b"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "protection keys and must instead use trial decryption (either with"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d45aaa763fb57017",
                  "61a7188690056ad4",
                  "e656d577ace20d4b"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "the 1-RTT handshake keys or by looking for a cleartext ClientHello in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d45aaa763fb57017",
                  "61a7188690056ad4",
                  "e656d577ace20d4b"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "the case of a HelloRetryRequest) to find the first non-0-RTT message."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "605af3386085090a",
                  "d45aaa763fb57017",
                  "e656d577ace20d4b"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "If the server chooses to accept the \"early_data\" extension, then it"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "605af3386085090a",
                  "d45aaa763fb57017",
                  "e656d577ace20d4b"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "MUST comply with the same error-handling requirements specified for"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "605af3386085090a",
                  "d45aaa763fb57017",
                  "e656d577ace20d4b"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "all records when processing early data records."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d45aaa763fb57017",
                  "e656d577ace20d4b"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6c9dc5834099cf71",
                  "d45aaa763fb57017",
                  "e656d577ace20d4b"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Specifically, if the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6c9dc5834099cf71",
                  "d45aaa763fb57017",
                  "e656d577ace20d4b"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "server fails to decrypt a 0-RTT record following an accepted"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6c9dc5834099cf71",
                  "d45aaa763fb57017",
                  "e656d577ace20d4b"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "\"early_data\" extension, it MUST terminate the connection with a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6c9dc5834099cf71",
                  "d45aaa763fb57017",
                  "e656d577ace20d4b"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "\"bad_record_mac\" alert as per Section 5.2."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1b1fb0021ac37e01"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "If the server rejects the \"early_data\" extension, the client"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1b1fb0021ac37e01"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "application MAY opt to retransmit the Application Data previously"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1b1fb0021ac37e01"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "sent in early data once the handshake has been completed."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Note that"
              }
            ],
            "   automatic retransmission of early data could result in incorrect",
            "   assumptions regarding the status of the connection.  For instance,",
            "   when the negotiated connection selects a different ALPN protocol from",
            "   what was used for the early data, an application might need to",
            "   construct different messages.  Similarly, if early data assumes",
            "   anything about the connection state, it might be sent in error after",
            "   the handshake completes.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aa53e90df0a806c2"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "A TLS implementation SHOULD NOT automatically resend early data;"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aa53e90df0a806c2"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "applications are in a better position to decide when retransmission"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aa53e90df0a806c2"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "is appropriate."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aadce952eb81e08f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "A TLS implementation MUST NOT automatically resend"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aadce952eb81e08f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "early data unless the negotiated connection selects the same ALPN"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aadce952eb81e08f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "protocol."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "23025bbd378fa98e",
            "23025bbd378fa98e",
            "23025bbd378fa98e",
            "d6262dcc5a65eeb6",
            "d6262dcc5a65eeb6",
            "d6262dcc5a65eeb6",
            "844f87075683da49",
            "844f87075683da49",
            "844f87075683da49",
            "844f87075683da49",
            "844f87075683da49",
            "710e2c7e2536e962",
            "710e2c7e2536e962",
            "710e2c7e2536e962",
            "77fe6b7805044ab1",
            "77fe6b7805044ab1",
            "77fe6b7805044ab1",
            "d81672f8522ce714",
            "d81672f8522ce714",
            "d7b27ded396d510e",
            "d7b27ded396d510e",
            "ffe09bf4a6a1f7fd",
            "ffe09bf4a6a1f7fd",
            "ffe09bf4a6a1f7fd",
            "5a68da93877fb1c0",
            "5a68da93877fb1c0",
            "5a68da93877fb1c0",
            "d277b84bf1a7b06e",
            "f615fea14e863ff0",
            "f615fea14e863ff0",
            "f615fea14e863ff0",
            "f615fea14e863ff0",
            "605af3386085090a",
            "605af3386085090a",
            "605af3386085090a",
            "6c9dc5834099cf71",
            "6c9dc5834099cf71",
            "6c9dc5834099cf71",
            "6c9dc5834099cf71",
            "1b1fb0021ac37e01",
            "1b1fb0021ac37e01",
            "1b1fb0021ac37e01",
            "aa53e90df0a806c2",
            "aa53e90df0a806c2",
            "aa53e90df0a806c2",
            "aadce952eb81e08f",
            "aadce952eb81e08f",
            "aadce952eb81e08f"
          ],
          "title": "Early Data Indication"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.2.11",
          "lines": [
            "   The \"pre_shared_key\" extension is used to negotiate the identity of",
            "   the pre-shared key to be used with a given handshake in association",
            "   with PSK key establishment.",
            "",
            "   The \"extension_data\" field of this extension contains a",
            "   \"PreSharedKeyExtension\" value:",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          opaque identity<1..2^16-1>;",
            "          uint32 obfuscated_ticket_age;",
            "      } PskIdentity;",
            "",
            "      opaque PskBinderEntry<32..255>;",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          PskIdentity identities<7..2^16-1>;",
            "          PskBinderEntry binders<33..2^16-1>;",
            "      } OfferedPsks;",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          select (Handshake.msg_type) {",
            "              case client_hello: OfferedPsks;",
            "              case server_hello: uint16 selected_identity;",
            "          };",
            "      } PreSharedKeyExtension;",
            "",
            "   identity:  A label for a key.  For instance, a ticket (as defined in",
            "      Appendix B.3.4) or a label for a pre-shared key established",
            "      externally.",
            "",
            "   obfuscated_ticket_age:  An obfuscated version of the age of the key.",
            "      Section 4.2.11.1 describes how to form this value for identities",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      established via the NewSessionTicket message.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7429abf3835d4721",
                  "52a57bf8d8863393",
                  "6fd463dd3b01d109",
                  "7256e0586fd2c0b5"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "For identities"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7429abf3835d4721",
                  "52a57bf8d8863393",
                  "6fd463dd3b01d109",
                  "7256e0586fd2c0b5"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "established externally, an obfuscated_ticket_age of 0 SHOULD be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7429abf3835d4721",
                  "52a57bf8d8863393",
                  "6fd463dd3b01d109",
                  "7256e0586fd2c0b5"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "used,"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7429abf3835d4721",
                  "52a57bf8d8863393",
                  "7256e0586fd2c0b5"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": " and servers MUST ignore the value."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   identities:  A list of the identities that the client is willing to",
            "      negotiate with the server.  If sent alongside the \"early_data\"",
            "      extension (see Section 4.2.10), the first identity is the one used",
            "      for 0-RTT data.",
            "",
            "   binders:  A series of HMAC values, one for each value in the",
            "      identities list and in the same order, computed as described",
            "      below.",
            "",
            "   selected_identity:  The server's chosen identity expressed as a",
            "      (0-based) index into the identities in the client's list.",
            "",
            "   Each PSK is associated with a single Hash algorithm.  For PSKs",
            "   established via the ticket mechanism (Section 4.6.1), this is the KDF",
            "   Hash algorithm on the connection where the ticket was established.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6ea23c49a492d05e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "For externally established PSKs, the Hash algorithm MUST be set when"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   the PSK is established or default to SHA-256 if no such algorithm is",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   defined.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f3064356bb5fa9ac",
                  "de51bb753f5ff8ed",
                  "1d6d6c925f4b3a77"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "The server MUST ensure that it selects a compatible PSK"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f3064356bb5fa9ac",
                  "de51bb753f5ff8ed",
                  "1d6d6c925f4b3a77"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "(if any) and cipher suite."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   In TLS versions prior to TLS 1.3, the Server Name Identification",
            "   (SNI) value was intended to be associated with the session (Section 3",
            "   of [RFC6066]), with the server being required to enforce that the SNI",
            "   value associated with the session matches the one specified in the",
            "   resumption handshake.  However, in reality the implementations were",
            "   not consistent on which of two supplied SNI values they would use,",
            "   leading to the consistency requirement being de facto enforced by the",
            "   clients.  In TLS 1.3, the SNI value is always explicitly specified in",
            "   the resumption handshake, and there is no need for the server to",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   associate an SNI value with the ticket.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8c132252468686fc"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "Clients, however, SHOULD"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8c132252468686fc"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "store the SNI with the PSK to fulfill the requirements of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8c132252468686fc"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "Section 4.6.1."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Implementor's note: When session resumption is the primary use case",
            "   of PSKs, the most straightforward way to implement the PSK/cipher",
            "   suite matching requirements is to negotiate the cipher suite first",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   and then exclude any incompatible PSKs.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3b6b02db3d65bab7"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "Any unknown PSKs (e.g., ones"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3b6b02db3d65bab7"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "not in the PSK database or encrypted with an unknown key) SHOULD"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3b6b02db3d65bab7"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "simply be ignored."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "40e78921cdaf2102",
                  "1dc5526115a9d6f2"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "If no acceptable PSKs are found, the server"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "40e78921cdaf2102",
                  "1dc5526115a9d6f2"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "SHOULD perform a non-PSK handshake if possible."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "65f219443c6233d9"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "If backward"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "65f219443c6233d9"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "compatibility is important, client-provided, externally established"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "65f219443c6233d9"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "PSKs SHOULD influence cipher suite selection."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aee3a4b91390d1b6",
                  "cba0c033cd3db8e2"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "Prior to accepting PSK key establishment, the server MUST validate"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aee3a4b91390d1b6",
                  "cba0c033cd3db8e2"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "the corresponding binder value (see Section 4.2.11.2 below)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cba0c033cd3db8e2"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cb53eb2a6f7c43aa",
                  "cba0c033cd3db8e2"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If this"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cb53eb2a6f7c43aa",
                  "cba0c033cd3db8e2"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "value is not present or does not validate, the server MUST abort the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cb53eb2a6f7c43aa",
                  "cba0c033cd3db8e2"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "handshake."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2c53ae685b9a4ba5",
                  "8d4e351161aa827d"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "Servers SHOULD NOT attempt to validate multiple binders;"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2c53ae685b9a4ba5",
                  "8d4e351161aa827d"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "rather, they SHOULD select a single PSK and validate solely the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2c53ae685b9a4ba5",
                  "8d4e351161aa827d"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "binder that corresponds to that PSK."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  See Section 8.2 and"
              }
            ],
            "   Appendix E.6 for the security rationale for this requirement.  In",
            "   order to accept PSK key establishment, the server sends a",
            "   \"pre_shared_key\" extension indicating the selected identity.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a7b66586bd3d512c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Clients MUST verify that the server's selected_identity is within the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a7b66586bd3d512c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "range supplied by the client, "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a7b66586bd3d512c",
                  "519fb8bbdc7af9ca",
                  "de5fac7d471d8d96"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "that the server selected a cipher suite"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a7b66586bd3d512c",
                  "519fb8bbdc7af9ca",
                  "de5fac7d471d8d96"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "indicating a Hash associated with the PSK"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a7b66586bd3d512c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": ", and that a server"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a7b66586bd3d512c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "\"key_share\" extension is present if required by the ClientHello"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a7b66586bd3d512c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "\"psk_key_exchange_modes\" extension."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "192b651a7ed0e300"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If these values are not"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "192b651a7ed0e300"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "consistent, the client MUST abort the handshake with an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "192b651a7ed0e300"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "\"illegal_parameter\" alert."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c0179567d3dbf745"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If the server supplies an \"early_data\" extension, the client MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c0179567d3dbf745"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "verify that the server's selected_identity is 0."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c9165a378ef788dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If any other value"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c9165a378ef788dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "is returned, the client MUST abort the handshake with an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c9165a378ef788dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "\"illegal_parameter\" alert."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "80e1b862f9dfbc85",
                  "7daab9e552dd6150"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The \"pre_shared_key\" extension MUST be the last extension in the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "80e1b862f9dfbc85",
                  "7daab9e552dd6150"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "ClientHello (this facilitates implementation as described below)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "165b38376175b179",
                  "7daab9e552dd6150"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "Servers MUST check that it is the last extension and otherwise fail"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "165b38376175b179",
                  "7daab9e552dd6150"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "7429abf3835d4721",
            "7429abf3835d4721",
            "7429abf3835d4721",
            "6ea23c49a492d05e",
            "f3064356bb5fa9ac",
            "f3064356bb5fa9ac",
            "8c132252468686fc",
            "8c132252468686fc",
            "8c132252468686fc",
            "3b6b02db3d65bab7",
            "3b6b02db3d65bab7",
            "3b6b02db3d65bab7",
            "40e78921cdaf2102",
            "40e78921cdaf2102",
            "65f219443c6233d9",
            "65f219443c6233d9",
            "65f219443c6233d9",
            "aee3a4b91390d1b6",
            "aee3a4b91390d1b6",
            "cb53eb2a6f7c43aa",
            "cb53eb2a6f7c43aa",
            "cb53eb2a6f7c43aa",
            "2c53ae685b9a4ba5",
            "2c53ae685b9a4ba5",
            "2c53ae685b9a4ba5",
            "8d4e351161aa827d",
            "8d4e351161aa827d",
            "8d4e351161aa827d",
            "a7b66586bd3d512c",
            "a7b66586bd3d512c",
            "a7b66586bd3d512c",
            "a7b66586bd3d512c",
            "a7b66586bd3d512c",
            "192b651a7ed0e300",
            "192b651a7ed0e300",
            "192b651a7ed0e300",
            "c0179567d3dbf745",
            "c0179567d3dbf745",
            "c9165a378ef788dd",
            "c9165a378ef788dd",
            "c9165a378ef788dd",
            "80e1b862f9dfbc85",
            "80e1b862f9dfbc85",
            "165b38376175b179",
            "165b38376175b179"
          ],
          "title": "Pre-Shared Key Extension"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.2.11.1",
          "lines": [
            "   The client's view of the age of a ticket is the time since the",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   receipt of the NewSessionTicket message.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "70a7626e603a4383"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Clients MUST NOT attempt to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "70a7626e603a4383"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "use tickets which have ages greater than the \"ticket_lifetime\" value"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "70a7626e603a4383"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "which was provided with the ticket."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5e3abede99d35ef8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The \"obfuscated_ticket_age\""
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5e3abede99d35ef8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "field of each PskIdentity contains an obfuscated version of the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5e3abede99d35ef8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "ticket age formed by taking the age in milliseconds and adding the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5e3abede99d35ef8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "\"ticket_age_add\" value that was included with the ticket (see"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5e3abede99d35ef8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Section 4.6.1), modulo 2^32."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This addition prevents passive"
              }
            ],
            "   observers from correlating connections unless tickets are reused.",
            "   Note that the \"ticket_lifetime\" field in the NewSessionTicket message",
            "   is in seconds but the \"obfuscated_ticket_age\" is in milliseconds.",
            "   Because ticket lifetimes are restricted to a week, 32 bits is enough",
            "   to represent any plausible age, even in milliseconds."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "70a7626e603a4383",
            "70a7626e603a4383",
            "70a7626e603a4383"
          ],
          "title": "Ticket Age"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.2.11.2",
          "lines": [
            "   The PSK binder value forms a binding between a PSK and the current",
            "   handshake, as well as a binding between the handshake in which the",
            "   PSK was generated (if via a NewSessionTicket message) and the current",
            "   handshake.  Each entry in the binders list is computed as an HMAC",
            "   over a transcript hash (see Section 4.4.1) containing a partial",
            "   ClientHello up to and including the PreSharedKeyExtension.identities",
            "   field.  That is, it includes all of the ClientHello but not the",
            "   binders list itself.  The length fields for the message (including",
            "   the overall length, the length of the extensions block, and the",
            "   length of the \"pre_shared_key\" extension) are all set as if binders",
            "   of the correct lengths were present.",
            "",
            "   The PskBinderEntry is computed in the same way as the Finished",
            "   message (Section 4.4.4) but with the BaseKey being the binder_key",
            "   derived via the key schedule from the corresponding PSK which is",
            "   being offered (see Section 7.1).",
            "",
            "   If the handshake includes a HelloRetryRequest, the initial",
            "   ClientHello and HelloRetryRequest are included in the transcript",
            "   along with the new ClientHello.  For instance, if the client sends",
            "   ClientHello1, its binder will be computed over:",
            "",
            "      Transcript-Hash(Truncate(ClientHello1))",
            "",
            "   Where Truncate() removes the binders list from the ClientHello.",
            "",
            "   If the server responds with a HelloRetryRequest and the client then",
            "   sends ClientHello2, its binder will be computed over:",
            "",
            "      Transcript-Hash(ClientHello1,",
            "                      HelloRetryRequest,",
            "                      Truncate(ClientHello2))",
            "",
            "   The full ClientHello1/ClientHello2 is included in all other handshake",
            "   hash computations.  Note that in the first flight,",
            "   Truncate(ClientHello1) is hashed directly, but in the second flight,",
            "   ClientHello1 is hashed and then reinjected as a \"message_hash\"",
            "   message, as described in Section 4.4.1."
          ],
          "title": "PSK Binder"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.2.11.3",
          "lines": [
            "   Clients are permitted to \"stream\" 0-RTT data until they receive the",
            "   server's Finished, only then sending the EndOfEarlyData message,",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   followed by the rest of the handshake.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "231a4f40282f02e3"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "In order to avoid deadlocks,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "231a4f40282f02e3"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "when accepting \"early_data\", servers MUST process the client's"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "231a4f40282f02e3"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "ClientHello and then immediately send their flight of messages,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "231a4f40282f02e3"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "rather than waiting for the client's EndOfEarlyData message before"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "231a4f40282f02e3"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "sending its ServerHello."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "231a4f40282f02e3",
            "231a4f40282f02e3",
            "231a4f40282f02e3",
            "231a4f40282f02e3",
            "231a4f40282f02e3"
          ],
          "title": "Processing Order"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.3",
          "lines": [
            "   The next two messages from the server, EncryptedExtensions and",
            "   CertificateRequest, contain information from the server that",
            "   determines the rest of the handshake.  These messages are encrypted",
            "   with keys derived from the server_handshake_traffic_secret."
          ],
          "title": "Server Parameters"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.3.1",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "88c30e1bfb734cce"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "In all handshakes, the server MUST send the EncryptedExtensions"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "88c30e1bfb734cce"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "message immediately after the ServerHello message."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This is the first"
              }
            ],
            "   message that is encrypted under keys derived from the",
            "   server_handshake_traffic_secret.",
            "",
            "   The EncryptedExtensions message contains extensions that can be",
            "   protected, i.e., any which are not needed to establish the",
            "   cryptographic context but which are not associated with individual",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   certificates.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4934e7e9be30604c",
                  "2246a53463058a37"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The client MUST check EncryptedExtensions for the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4934e7e9be30604c",
                  "2246a53463058a37"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "presence of any forbidden extensions and if any are found MUST abort"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4934e7e9be30604c",
                  "2246a53463058a37"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Structure of this message:",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          Extension extensions<0..2^16-1>;",
            "      } EncryptedExtensions;",
            "",
            "   extensions:  A list of extensions.  For more information, see the",
            "      table in Section 4.2."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "88c30e1bfb734cce",
            "88c30e1bfb734cce",
            "4934e7e9be30604c",
            "4934e7e9be30604c",
            "4934e7e9be30604c",
            "2246a53463058a37",
            "2246a53463058a37",
            "2246a53463058a37"
          ],
          "title": "Encrypted Extensions"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.3.2",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f2804bd9a42479aa"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "A server which is authenticating with a certificate MAY optionally"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f2804bd9a42479aa"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "request a certificate from the client."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6154ee949912e856"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "This message, if sent, MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6154ee949912e856"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "follow EncryptedExtensions."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Structure of this message:",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          opaque certificate_request_context<0..2^8-1>;",
            "          Extension extensions<2..2^16-1>;",
            "      } CertificateRequest;",
            "",
            "   certificate_request_context:  An opaque string which identifies the",
            "      certificate request and which will be echoed in the client's",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      Certificate message.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2b7278e0ff990212"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The certificate_request_context MUST be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2b7278e0ff990212"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "unique within the scope of this connection (thus preventing replay"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2b7278e0ff990212"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "of client CertificateVerify messages)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0c5b32e3f91a809a"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "This field SHALL be zero"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0c5b32e3f91a809a"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "length unless used for the post-handshake authentication exchanges"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0c5b32e3f91a809a"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "described in Section 4.6.2."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a8b224a5a55478e7"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "When requesting post-handshake"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a8b224a5a55478e7"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "authentication, the server SHOULD make the context unpredictable"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a8b224a5a55478e7"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "to the client (e.g., by randomly generating it) in order to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a8b224a5a55478e7"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "prevent an attacker who has temporary access to the client's"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a8b224a5a55478e7"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "private key from pre-computing valid CertificateVerify messages."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   extensions:  A set of extensions describing the parameters of the",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      certificate being requested.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6732b022d6dbc39e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The \"signature_algorithms\" extension"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6732b022d6dbc39e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "MUST be specified, and other extensions may optionally be included"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6732b022d6dbc39e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "if defined for this message."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7824b9464825dd83"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Clients MUST ignore unrecognized"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7824b9464825dd83"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "extensions."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   In prior versions of TLS, the CertificateRequest message carried a",
            "   list of signature algorithms and certificate authorities which the",
            "   server would accept.  In TLS 1.3, the former is expressed by sending",
            "   the \"signature_algorithms\" and optionally \"signature_algorithms_cert\"",
            "   extensions.  The latter is expressed by sending the",
            "   \"certificate_authorities\" extension (see Section 4.2.4).",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d59e29730d8701ee"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Servers which are authenticating with a PSK MUST NOT send the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d59e29730d8701ee"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "CertificateRequest message in the main handshake, though they MAY"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d59e29730d8701ee"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "send it in post-handshake authentication (see Section 4.6.2) provided"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d59e29730d8701ee"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "that the client has sent the \"post_handshake_auth\" extension (see"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d59e29730d8701ee"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Section 4.2.6)."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "f2804bd9a42479aa",
            "f2804bd9a42479aa",
            "6154ee949912e856",
            "6154ee949912e856",
            "2b7278e0ff990212",
            "2b7278e0ff990212",
            "2b7278e0ff990212",
            "0c5b32e3f91a809a",
            "0c5b32e3f91a809a",
            "0c5b32e3f91a809a",
            "a8b224a5a55478e7",
            "a8b224a5a55478e7",
            "a8b224a5a55478e7",
            "a8b224a5a55478e7",
            "a8b224a5a55478e7",
            "6732b022d6dbc39e",
            "6732b022d6dbc39e",
            "6732b022d6dbc39e",
            "7824b9464825dd83",
            "7824b9464825dd83",
            "d59e29730d8701ee",
            "d59e29730d8701ee",
            "d59e29730d8701ee",
            "d59e29730d8701ee",
            "d59e29730d8701ee"
          ],
          "title": "Certificate Request"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.4",
          "lines": [
            "   As discussed in Section 2, TLS generally uses a common set of",
            "   messages for authentication, key confirmation, and handshake",
            "   integrity: Certificate, CertificateVerify, and Finished.  (The PSK",
            "   binders also perform key confirmation, in a similar fashion.)  These",
            "   three messages are always sent as the last messages in their",
            "   handshake flight.  The Certificate and CertificateVerify messages are",
            "   only sent under certain circumstances, as defined below.  The",
            "   Finished message is always sent as part of the Authentication Block.",
            "   These messages are encrypted under keys derived from the",
            "   [sender]_handshake_traffic_secret.",
            "",
            "   The computations for the Authentication messages all uniformly take",
            "   the following inputs:",
            "",
            "   -  The certificate and signing key to be used.",
            "",
            "   -  A Handshake Context consisting of the set of messages to be",
            "      included in the transcript hash.",
            "",
            "   -  A Base Key to be used to compute a MAC key.",
            "",
            "   Based on these inputs, the messages then contain:",
            "",
            "   Certificate:  The certificate to be used for authentication, and any",
            "      supporting certificates in the chain.  Note that certificate-based",
            "      client authentication is not available in PSK handshake flows",
            "      (including 0-RTT).",
            "",
            "   CertificateVerify:  A signature over the value",
            "      Transcript-Hash(Handshake Context, Certificate).",
            "",
            "   Finished:  A MAC over the value Transcript-Hash(Handshake Context,",
            "      Certificate, CertificateVerify) using a MAC key derived from the",
            "      Base Key.",
            "",
            "   The following table defines the Handshake Context and MAC Base Key",
            "   for each scenario:",
            "",
            "   +-----------+-------------------------+-----------------------------+",
            "   | Mode      | Handshake Context       | Base Key                    |",
            "   +-----------+-------------------------+-----------------------------+",
            "   | Server    | ClientHello ... later   | server_handshake_traffic_   |",
            "   |           | of EncryptedExtensions/ | secret                      |",
            "   |           | CertificateRequest      |                             |",
            "   |           |                         |                             |",
            "   | Client    | ClientHello ... later   | client_handshake_traffic_   |",
            "   |           | of server               | secret                      |",
            "   |           | Finished/EndOfEarlyData |                             |",
            "   |           |                         |                             |",
            "   | Post-     | ClientHello ... client  | client_application_traffic_ |",
            "   | Handshake | Finished +              | secret_N                    |",
            "   |           | CertificateRequest      |                             |",
            "   +-----------+-------------------------+-----------------------------+"
          ],
          "title": "Authentication Messages"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.4.1",
          "lines": [
            "   Many of the cryptographic computations in TLS make use of a",
            "   transcript hash.  This value is computed by hashing the concatenation",
            "   of each included handshake message, including the handshake message",
            "   header carrying the handshake message type and length fields, but not",
            "   including record layer headers.  I.e.,",
            "",
            "    Transcript-Hash(M1, M2, ... Mn) = Hash(M1 || M2 || ... || Mn)",
            "",
            "   As an exception to this general rule, when the server responds to a",
            "   ClientHello with a HelloRetryRequest, the value of ClientHello1 is",
            "   replaced with a special synthetic handshake message of handshake type",
            "   \"message_hash\" containing Hash(ClientHello1).  I.e.,",
            "",
            "  Transcript-Hash(ClientHello1, HelloRetryRequest, ... Mn) =",
            "      Hash(message_hash ||        /* Handshake type */",
            "           00 00 Hash.length  ||  /* Handshake message length (bytes) */",
            "           Hash(ClientHello1) ||  /* Hash of ClientHello1 */",
            "           HelloRetryRequest  || ... || Mn)",
            "",
            "   The reason for this construction is to allow the server to do a",
            "   stateless HelloRetryRequest by storing just the hash of ClientHello1",
            "   in the cookie, rather than requiring it to export the entire",
            "   intermediate hash state (see Section 4.2.2).",
            "",
            "   For concreteness, the transcript hash is always taken from the",
            "   following sequence of handshake messages, starting at the first",
            "   ClientHello and including only those messages that were sent:",
            "   ClientHello, HelloRetryRequest, ClientHello, ServerHello,",
            "   EncryptedExtensions, server CertificateRequest, server Certificate,",
            "   server CertificateVerify, server Finished, EndOfEarlyData, client",
            "   Certificate, client CertificateVerify, client Finished.",
            "",
            "   In general, implementations can implement the transcript by keeping a",
            "   running transcript hash value based on the negotiated hash.  Note,",
            "   however, that subsequent post-handshake authentications do not",
            "   include each other, just the messages through the end of the main",
            "   handshake."
          ],
          "title": "The Transcript Hash"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.4.2",
          "lines": [
            "   This message conveys the endpoint's certificate chain to the peer.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4abd77d3223ab59d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The server MUST send a Certificate message whenever the agreed-upon"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4abd77d3223ab59d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "key exchange method uses certificates for authentication (this"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4abd77d3223ab59d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "includes all key exchange methods defined in this document"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4abd77d3223ab59d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "except PSK)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6ee525cff6c4fb04"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The client MUST send a Certificate message if and only if the server"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6ee525cff6c4fb04"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "has requested client authentication via a CertificateRequest message"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6ee525cff6c4fb04"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "(Section 4.3.2)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "209e70c7a0100e05"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If the server requests client authentication but no"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "209e70c7a0100e05"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "suitable certificate is available, the client MUST send a Certificate"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "209e70c7a0100e05"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "message containing no certificates (i.e., with the \"certificate_list\""
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "209e70c7a0100e05"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "field having length 0)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fef3fbcc5a95ef7d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "A Finished message MUST be sent regardless"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fef3fbcc5a95ef7d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "of whether the Certificate message is empty."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Structure of this message:",
            "",
            "      enum {",
            "          X509(0),",
            "          RawPublicKey(2),",
            "          (255)",
            "      } CertificateType;",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          select (certificate_type) {",
            "              case RawPublicKey:",
            "                /* From RFC 7250 ASN.1_subjectPublicKeyInfo */",
            "                opaque ASN1_subjectPublicKeyInfo<1..2^24-1>;",
            "",
            "              case X509:",
            "                opaque cert_data<1..2^24-1>;",
            "          };",
            "          Extension extensions<0..2^16-1>;",
            "      } CertificateEntry;",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          opaque certificate_request_context<0..2^8-1>;",
            "          CertificateEntry certificate_list<0..2^24-1>;",
            "      } Certificate;",
            "",
            "   certificate_request_context:  If this message is in response to a",
            "      CertificateRequest, the value of certificate_request_context in",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      that message.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e7ed6e804d4612a7"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Otherwise (in the case of server authentication),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e7ed6e804d4612a7"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "this field SHALL be zero length."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   certificate_list:  A sequence (chain) of CertificateEntry structures,",
            "      each containing a single certificate and set of extensions.",
            "",
            "   extensions:  A set of extension values for the CertificateEntry.  The",
            "      \"Extension\" format is defined in Section 4.2.  Valid extensions",
            "      for server certificates at present include the OCSP Status",
            "      extension [RFC6066] and the SignedCertificateTimestamp extension",
            "      [RFC6962]; future extensions may be defined for this message as",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      well.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4d236a60cfe3e9b9"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Extensions in the Certificate message from the server MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4d236a60cfe3e9b9"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "correspond to ones from the ClientHello message."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "24d1ae85db088862"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Extensions in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "24d1ae85db088862"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "the Certificate message from the client MUST correspond to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "24d1ae85db088862"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "extensions in the CertificateRequest message from the server."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "61c0ebc6382ecf37",
                  "4405939a02ed8f3e"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "If"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "61c0ebc6382ecf37",
                  "4405939a02ed8f3e"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "an extension applies to the entire chain, it SHOULD be included in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "61c0ebc6382ecf37",
                  "4405939a02ed8f3e"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "the first CertificateEntry."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   If the corresponding certificate type extension",
            "   (\"server_certificate_type\" or \"client_certificate_type\") was not",
            "   negotiated in EncryptedExtensions, or the X.509 certificate type was",
            "   negotiated, then each CertificateEntry contains a DER-encoded X.509",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   certificate.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8bd9f50007fe8614"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The sender's certificate MUST come in the first"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8bd9f50007fe8614"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "CertificateEntry in the list."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "06c90425c39d6264"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "Each following certificate SHOULD"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "06c90425c39d6264"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "directly certify the one immediately preceding it."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d04f65875f448f5f"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Because"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d04f65875f448f5f"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "certificate validation requires that trust anchors be distributed"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d04f65875f448f5f"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "independently, a certificate that specifies a trust anchor MAY be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d04f65875f448f5f"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "omitted from the chain, provided that supported peers are known to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d04f65875f448f5f"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "possess any omitted certificates."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Note: Prior to TLS 1.3, \"certificate_list\" ordering required each",
            "   certificate to certify the one immediately preceding it; however,",
            "   some implementations allowed some flexibility.  Servers sometimes",
            "   send both a current and deprecated intermediate for transitional",
            "   purposes, and others are simply configured incorrectly, but these",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   cases can nonetheless be validated properly.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bced0d15f317e6e6"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "For maximum"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bced0d15f317e6e6"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "compatibility, all implementations SHOULD be prepared to handle"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bced0d15f317e6e6"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "potentially extraneous certificates and arbitrary orderings from any"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bced0d15f317e6e6"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "TLS version, with the exception of the end-entity certificate which"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bced0d15f317e6e6"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "MUST be first."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b3a41dfc5c7396fd"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If the RawPublicKey certificate type was negotiated, then the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b3a41dfc5c7396fd"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "certificate_list MUST contain no more than one CertificateEntry,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b3a41dfc5c7396fd"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "which contains an ASN1_subjectPublicKeyInfo value as defined in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b3a41dfc5c7396fd"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "[RFC7250], Section 3."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "06daca84ed05e630"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The OpenPGP certificate type [RFC6091] MUST NOT be used with TLS 1.3."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "063a327f4f1026ef"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The server's certificate_list MUST always be non-empty."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  A client"
              }
            ],
            "   will send an empty certificate_list if it does not have an",
            "   appropriate certificate to send in response to the server's",
            "   authentication request."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "4abd77d3223ab59d",
            "4abd77d3223ab59d",
            "4abd77d3223ab59d",
            "4abd77d3223ab59d",
            "6ee525cff6c4fb04",
            "6ee525cff6c4fb04",
            "6ee525cff6c4fb04",
            "209e70c7a0100e05",
            "209e70c7a0100e05",
            "209e70c7a0100e05",
            "209e70c7a0100e05",
            "fef3fbcc5a95ef7d",
            "fef3fbcc5a95ef7d",
            "e7ed6e804d4612a7",
            "e7ed6e804d4612a7",
            "4d236a60cfe3e9b9",
            "4d236a60cfe3e9b9",
            "24d1ae85db088862",
            "24d1ae85db088862",
            "24d1ae85db088862",
            "61c0ebc6382ecf37",
            "61c0ebc6382ecf37",
            "61c0ebc6382ecf37",
            "8bd9f50007fe8614",
            "8bd9f50007fe8614",
            "06c90425c39d6264",
            "06c90425c39d6264",
            "d04f65875f448f5f",
            "d04f65875f448f5f",
            "d04f65875f448f5f",
            "d04f65875f448f5f",
            "d04f65875f448f5f",
            "bced0d15f317e6e6",
            "bced0d15f317e6e6",
            "bced0d15f317e6e6",
            "bced0d15f317e6e6",
            "bced0d15f317e6e6",
            "b3a41dfc5c7396fd",
            "b3a41dfc5c7396fd",
            "b3a41dfc5c7396fd",
            "b3a41dfc5c7396fd",
            "06daca84ed05e630",
            "063a327f4f1026ef"
          ],
          "title": "Certificate"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.4.2.1",
          "lines": [
            "   [RFC6066] and [RFC6961] provide extensions to negotiate the server",
            "   sending OCSP responses to the client.  In TLS 1.2 and below, the",
            "   server replies with an empty extension to indicate negotiation of",
            "   this extension and the OCSP information is carried in a",
            "   CertificateStatus message.  In TLS 1.3, the server's OCSP information",
            "   is carried in an extension in the CertificateEntry containing the",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   associated certificate.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "99e9813b5474e471"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Specifically, the body of the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "99e9813b5474e471"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "\"status_request\" extension from the server MUST be a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "99e9813b5474e471"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "CertificateStatus structure as defined in [RFC6066], which is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "99e9813b5474e471"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "interpreted as defined in [RFC6960]."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Note: The status_request_v2 extension [RFC6961] is deprecated.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "790f01944937d089",
                  "d59c6ce161f7d151"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "TLS 1.3 servers MUST NOT act upon its presence or information in it"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "790f01944937d089",
                  "d59c6ce161f7d151"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "when processing ClientHello messages; in particular, they MUST NOT"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "790f01944937d089",
                  "d59c6ce161f7d151"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "send the status_request_v2 extension in the EncryptedExtensions,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "790f01944937d089",
                  "d59c6ce161f7d151"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "CertificateRequest, or Certificate messages."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf45a719222b1e69"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "TLS 1.3 servers MUST be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf45a719222b1e69"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "able to process ClientHello messages that include it, as it MAY be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf45a719222b1e69"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "sent by clients that wish to use it in earlier protocol versions."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "60a71ea562cdaff8",
                  "8c30e83563ff74ff"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "A server MAY request that a client present an OCSP response with its"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "60a71ea562cdaff8",
                  "8c30e83563ff74ff"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "certificate by sending an empty \"status_request\" extension in its"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "60a71ea562cdaff8",
                  "8c30e83563ff74ff"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "CertificateRequest message."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e99e9695dc6392a0"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If the client opts to send an OCSP"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e99e9695dc6392a0"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "response, the body of its \"status_request\" extension MUST be a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e99e9695dc6392a0"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "CertificateStatus structure as defined in [RFC6066]."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Similarly, [RFC6962] provides a mechanism for a server to send a",
            "   Signed Certificate Timestamp (SCT) as an extension in the ServerHello",
            "   in TLS 1.2 and below.  In TLS 1.3, the server's SCT information is",
            "   carried in an extension in the CertificateEntry."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "99e9813b5474e471",
            "99e9813b5474e471",
            "99e9813b5474e471",
            "99e9813b5474e471",
            "790f01944937d089",
            "790f01944937d089",
            "790f01944937d089",
            "790f01944937d089",
            "d59c6ce161f7d151",
            "d59c6ce161f7d151",
            "d59c6ce161f7d151",
            "d59c6ce161f7d151",
            "bf45a719222b1e69",
            "bf45a719222b1e69",
            "bf45a719222b1e69",
            "60a71ea562cdaff8",
            "60a71ea562cdaff8",
            "60a71ea562cdaff8",
            "e99e9695dc6392a0",
            "e99e9695dc6392a0",
            "e99e9695dc6392a0"
          ],
          "title": "OCSP Status and SCT Extensions"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.4.2.2",
          "lines": [
            "   The following rules apply to the certificates sent by the server:",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "33a8ef11c32c54a1"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "-  The certificate type MUST be X.509v3 [RFC5280], unless explicitly"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "33a8ef11c32c54a1"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "negotiated otherwise (e.g., [RFC7250])."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fb35068b9112978a"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "-  The server's end-entity certificate's public key (and associated"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fb35068b9112978a"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "restrictions) MUST be compatible with the selected authentication"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fb35068b9112978a"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "algorithm from the client's \"signature_algorithms\" extension"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fb35068b9112978a"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "(currently RSA, ECDSA, or EdDSA)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c18374c7eda655fe",
                  "85ec8572533919c9"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "-  The certificate MUST allow the key to be used for signing (i.e.,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c18374c7eda655fe",
                  "85ec8572533919c9"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "the digitalSignature bit MUST be set if the Key Usage extension is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c18374c7eda655fe",
                  "85ec8572533919c9"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "present) with a signature scheme indicated in the client's"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c18374c7eda655fe",
                  "85ec8572533919c9"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "\"signature_algorithms\"/\"signature_algorithms_cert\" extensions (see"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c18374c7eda655fe",
                  "85ec8572533919c9"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Section 4.2.3)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   -  The \"server_name\" [RFC6066] and \"certificate_authorities\"",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      extensions are used to guide certificate selection.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "70532d034b26d794"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "As servers"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "70532d034b26d794"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "MAY require the presence of the \"server_name\" extension, clients"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "70532d034b26d794"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "SHOULD send this extension, when applicable."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "25715c627c314159"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "All certificates provided by the server MUST be signed by a signature"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "25715c627c314159"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "algorithm advertised by the client if it is able to provide such a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "25715c627c314159"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "chain (see Section 4.2.3)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2c9c9fdc91b7b29f"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Certificates that are self-signed or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2c9c9fdc91b7b29f"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "certificates that are expected to be trust anchors are not validated"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2c9c9fdc91b7b29f"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "as part of the chain and therefore MAY be signed with any algorithm."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "412f77ccc1be5b6a"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "If the server cannot produce a certificate chain that is signed only"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "412f77ccc1be5b6a"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "via the indicated supported algorithms, then it SHOULD continue the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "412f77ccc1be5b6a"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "handshake by sending the client a certificate chain of its choice"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "412f77ccc1be5b6a"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "that may include algorithms that are not known to be supported by the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "412f77ccc1be5b6a"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "client."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "001c0a7f58cb969b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "This fallback chain SHOULD NOT use the deprecated SHA-1 hash"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "001c0a7f58cb969b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "algorithm in general, but MAY do so if the client's advertisement"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "001c0a7f58cb969b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "permits it, and MUST NOT do so otherwise."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c55bc846986a19e3"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If the client cannot construct an acceptable chain using the provided"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c55bc846986a19e3"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "certificates and decides to abort the handshake, then it MUST abort"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c55bc846986a19e3"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "the handshake with an appropriate certificate-related alert (by"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c55bc846986a19e3"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "default, \"unsupported_certificate\"; see Section 6.2 for more"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c55bc846986a19e3"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "information)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   If the server has multiple certificates, it chooses one of them based",
            "   on the above-mentioned criteria (in addition to other criteria, such",
            "   as transport-layer endpoint, local configuration, and preferences)."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "33a8ef11c32c54a1",
            "33a8ef11c32c54a1",
            "fb35068b9112978a",
            "fb35068b9112978a",
            "fb35068b9112978a",
            "fb35068b9112978a",
            "c18374c7eda655fe",
            "c18374c7eda655fe",
            "c18374c7eda655fe",
            "c18374c7eda655fe",
            "c18374c7eda655fe",
            "85ec8572533919c9",
            "85ec8572533919c9",
            "85ec8572533919c9",
            "85ec8572533919c9",
            "85ec8572533919c9",
            "70532d034b26d794",
            "70532d034b26d794",
            "70532d034b26d794",
            "25715c627c314159",
            "25715c627c314159",
            "25715c627c314159",
            "2c9c9fdc91b7b29f",
            "2c9c9fdc91b7b29f",
            "2c9c9fdc91b7b29f",
            "412f77ccc1be5b6a",
            "412f77ccc1be5b6a",
            "412f77ccc1be5b6a",
            "412f77ccc1be5b6a",
            "412f77ccc1be5b6a",
            "001c0a7f58cb969b",
            "001c0a7f58cb969b",
            "001c0a7f58cb969b",
            "c55bc846986a19e3",
            "c55bc846986a19e3",
            "c55bc846986a19e3",
            "c55bc846986a19e3",
            "c55bc846986a19e3"
          ],
          "title": "Server Certificate Selection"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.4.2.3",
          "lines": [
            "   The following rules apply to certificates sent by the client:",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f9dd2494d87fc7ac"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "-  The certificate type MUST be X.509v3 [RFC5280], unless explicitly"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f9dd2494d87fc7ac"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "negotiated otherwise (e.g., [RFC7250])."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "92ea039063a6a4fc"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "-  If the \"certificate_authorities\" extension in the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "92ea039063a6a4fc"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "CertificateRequest message was present, at least one of the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "92ea039063a6a4fc"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "certificates in the certificate chain SHOULD be issued by one of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "92ea039063a6a4fc"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "the listed CAs."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6bf6f8481195f98e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "-  The certificates MUST be signed using an acceptable signature"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6bf6f8481195f98e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "algorithm, as described in Section 4.3.2."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Note that this relaxes"
              }
            ],
            "      the constraints on certificate-signing algorithms found in prior",
            "      versions of TLS.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1a30a23a8556e7df"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "-  If the CertificateRequest message contained a non-empty"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1a30a23a8556e7df"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "\"oid_filters\" extension, the end-entity certificate MUST match the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1a30a23a8556e7df"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "extension OIDs that are recognized by the client, as described in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1a30a23a8556e7df"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Section 4.2.5."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "f9dd2494d87fc7ac",
            "f9dd2494d87fc7ac",
            "92ea039063a6a4fc",
            "92ea039063a6a4fc",
            "92ea039063a6a4fc",
            "92ea039063a6a4fc",
            "6bf6f8481195f98e",
            "6bf6f8481195f98e",
            "1a30a23a8556e7df",
            "1a30a23a8556e7df",
            "1a30a23a8556e7df",
            "1a30a23a8556e7df"
          ],
          "title": "Client Certificate Selection"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.4.2.4",
          "lines": [
            "   In general, detailed certificate validation procedures are out of",
            "   scope for TLS (see [RFC5280]).  This section provides TLS-specific",
            "   requirements.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b813fbbef032d115"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If the server supplies an empty Certificate message, the client MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b813fbbef032d115"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "abort the handshake with a \"decode_error\" alert."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6d0ca28921107181"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "If the client does not send any certificates (i.e., it sends an empty"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6d0ca28921107181"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Certificate message), the server MAY at its discretion either"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6d0ca28921107181"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "continue the handshake without client authentication or abort the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6d0ca28921107181"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "handshake with a \"certificate_required\" alert."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e7d903a7de7bfb9f"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Also, if some aspect"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e7d903a7de7bfb9f"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "of the certificate chain was unacceptable (e.g., it was not signed by"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e7d903a7de7bfb9f"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "a known, trusted CA), the server MAY at its discretion either"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e7d903a7de7bfb9f"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "continue the handshake (considering the client unauthenticated) or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e7d903a7de7bfb9f"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "abort the handshake."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "132b530bdf9da2be"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Any endpoint receiving any certificate which it would need to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "132b530bdf9da2be"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "validate using any signature algorithm using an MD5 hash MUST abort"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "132b530bdf9da2be"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "the handshake with a \"bad_certificate\" alert."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f151b59e45cf2d77"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "SHA-1 is deprecated,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f151b59e45cf2d77"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "and it is RECOMMENDED that any endpoint receiving any certificate"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f151b59e45cf2d77"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "which it would need to validate using any signature algorithm using a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f151b59e45cf2d77"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "SHA-1 hash abort the handshake with a \"bad_certificate\" alert."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  For"
              }
            ],
            "   clarity, this means that endpoints can accept these algorithms for",
            "   certificates that are self-signed or are trust anchors.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "19cbf074f6884de1"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "All endpoints are RECOMMENDED to transition to SHA-256 or better as"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "19cbf074f6884de1"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "soon as possible to maintain interoperability with implementations"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "19cbf074f6884de1"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "currently in the process of phasing out SHA-1 support."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7698cae83a8477d9"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Note that a certificate containing a key for one signature algorithm"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7698cae83a8477d9"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "MAY be signed using a different signature algorithm (for instance, an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7698cae83a8477d9"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "RSA key signed with an ECDSA key)."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "b813fbbef032d115",
            "b813fbbef032d115",
            "6d0ca28921107181",
            "6d0ca28921107181",
            "6d0ca28921107181",
            "6d0ca28921107181",
            "e7d903a7de7bfb9f",
            "e7d903a7de7bfb9f",
            "e7d903a7de7bfb9f",
            "e7d903a7de7bfb9f",
            "e7d903a7de7bfb9f",
            "132b530bdf9da2be",
            "132b530bdf9da2be",
            "132b530bdf9da2be",
            "f151b59e45cf2d77",
            "f151b59e45cf2d77",
            "f151b59e45cf2d77",
            "f151b59e45cf2d77",
            "19cbf074f6884de1",
            "19cbf074f6884de1",
            "19cbf074f6884de1",
            "7698cae83a8477d9",
            "7698cae83a8477d9",
            "7698cae83a8477d9"
          ],
          "title": "Receiving a Certificate Message"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.4.3",
          "lines": [
            "   This message is used to provide explicit proof that an endpoint",
            "   possesses the private key corresponding to its certificate.  The",
            "   CertificateVerify message also provides integrity for the handshake",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   up to this point.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3c4506799a955fc3"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Servers MUST send this message when authenticating"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3c4506799a955fc3"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "via a certificate."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5755391d5adf153b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Clients MUST send this message whenever"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5755391d5adf153b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "authenticating via a certificate (i.e., when the Certificate message"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5755391d5adf153b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "is non-empty)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f8ccf36c91c96ca8"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "When sent, this message MUST appear immediately after"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f8ccf36c91c96ca8"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "the Certificate message and immediately prior to the Finished"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f8ccf36c91c96ca8"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "message."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Structure of this message:",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          SignatureScheme algorithm;",
            "          opaque signature<0..2^16-1>;",
            "      } CertificateVerify;",
            "",
            "   The algorithm field specifies the signature algorithm used (see",
            "   Section 4.2.3 for the definition of this type).  The signature is a",
            "   digital signature using that algorithm.  The content that is covered",
            "   under the signature is the hash output as described in Section 4.4.1,",
            "   namely:",
            "",
            "      Transcript-Hash(Handshake Context, Certificate)",
            "",
            "   The digital signature is then computed over the concatenation of:",
            "",
            "   -  A string that consists of octet 32 (0x20) repeated 64 times",
            "",
            "   -  The context string",
            "",
            "   -  A single 0 byte which serves as the separator",
            "",
            "   -  The content to be signed",
            "",
            "   This structure is intended to prevent an attack on previous versions",
            "   of TLS in which the ServerKeyExchange format meant that attackers",
            "   could obtain a signature of a message with a chosen 32-byte prefix",
            "   (ClientHello.random).  The initial 64-byte pad clears that prefix",
            "   along with the server-controlled ServerHello.random.",
            "",
            "   The context string for a server signature is",
            "   \"TLS 1.3, server CertificateVerify\".  The context string for a",
            "   client signature is \"TLS 1.3, client CertificateVerify\".  It is",
            "   used to provide separation between signatures made in different",
            "   contexts, helping against potential cross-protocol attacks.",
            "",
            "   For example, if the transcript hash was 32 bytes of 01 (this length",
            "   would make sense for SHA-256), the content covered by the digital",
            "   signature for a server CertificateVerify would be:",
            "",
            "      2020202020202020202020202020202020202020202020202020202020202020",
            "      2020202020202020202020202020202020202020202020202020202020202020",
            "      544c5320312e332c207365727665722043657274696669636174655665726966",
            "      79",
            "      00",
            "      0101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101",
            "",
            "   On the sender side, the process for computing the signature field of",
            "   the CertificateVerify message takes as input:",
            "",
            "   -  The content covered by the digital signature",
            "",
            "   -  The private signing key corresponding to the certificate sent in",
            "      the previous message",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "807d40e07e7d6710",
                  "96ac80c6102e48c0"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If the CertificateVerify message is sent by a server, the signature"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "807d40e07e7d6710",
                  "96ac80c6102e48c0"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "algorithm MUST be one offered in the client's \"signature_algorithms\""
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "807d40e07e7d6710",
                  "96ac80c6102e48c0"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "extension unless no valid certificate chain can be produced without"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "807d40e07e7d6710",
                  "96ac80c6102e48c0"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "unsupported algorithms"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "807d40e07e7d6710"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": " (see Section 4.2.3)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac7884a896092f0c",
                  "c2ec188f44132799"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "If sent by a client, the signature algorithm used in the signature"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac7884a896092f0c",
                  "c2ec188f44132799"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "MUST be one of those present in the supported_signature_algorithms"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac7884a896092f0c",
                  "c2ec188f44132799"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "field of the \"signature_algorithms\" extension in the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac7884a896092f0c",
                  "c2ec188f44132799"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "CertificateRequest message."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cbc1a9c461a530b8"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "In addition, the signature algorithm MUST be compatible with the key"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cbc1a9c461a530b8"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "in the sender's end-entity certificate."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bee992947076e70e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "RSA signatures MUST use an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bee992947076e70e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "RSASSA-PSS algorithm, regardless of whether RSASSA-PKCS1-v1_5"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bee992947076e70e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "algorithms appear in \"signature_algorithms\"."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4ffb772758831195"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The SHA-1 algorithm"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4ffb772758831195"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "MUST NOT be used in any signatures of CertificateVerify messages."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   All SHA-1 signature algorithms in this specification are defined",
            "   solely for use in legacy certificates and are not valid for",
            "   CertificateVerify signatures.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f7c86278942b878c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The receiver of a CertificateVerify message MUST verify the signature"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f7c86278942b878c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "field."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  The verification process takes as input:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   -  The content covered by the digital signature",
            "",
            "   -  The public key contained in the end-entity certificate found in",
            "      the associated Certificate message",
            "",
            "   -  The digital signature received in the signature field of the",
            "      CertificateVerify message",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2ab9d05e0729a616"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If the verification fails, the receiver MUST terminate the handshake"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2ab9d05e0729a616"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "with a \"decrypt_error\" alert."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "3c4506799a955fc3",
            "3c4506799a955fc3",
            "5755391d5adf153b",
            "5755391d5adf153b",
            "5755391d5adf153b",
            "f8ccf36c91c96ca8",
            "f8ccf36c91c96ca8",
            "f8ccf36c91c96ca8",
            "807d40e07e7d6710",
            "807d40e07e7d6710",
            "807d40e07e7d6710",
            "807d40e07e7d6710",
            "ac7884a896092f0c",
            "ac7884a896092f0c",
            "ac7884a896092f0c",
            "ac7884a896092f0c",
            "cbc1a9c461a530b8",
            "cbc1a9c461a530b8",
            "bee992947076e70e",
            "bee992947076e70e",
            "bee992947076e70e",
            "4ffb772758831195",
            "4ffb772758831195",
            "f7c86278942b878c",
            "f7c86278942b878c",
            "2ab9d05e0729a616",
            "2ab9d05e0729a616"
          ],
          "title": "Certificate Verify"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.4.4",
          "lines": [
            "   The Finished message is the final message in the Authentication",
            "   Block.  It is essential for providing authentication of the handshake",
            "   and of the computed keys.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c4ccb40458fdb6ba",
                  "3a3f2cb092a5db0b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Recipients of Finished messages MUST verify that the contents are"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c4ccb40458fdb6ba",
                  "3a3f2cb092a5db0b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "correct and if incorrect MUST terminate the connection with a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c4ccb40458fdb6ba",
                  "3a3f2cb092a5db0b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "\"decrypt_error\" alert."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Once a side has sent its Finished message and has received and",
            "   validated the Finished message from its peer, it may begin to send",
            "   and receive Application Data over the connection.  There are two",
            "   settings in which it is permitted to send data prior to receiving the",
            "   peer's Finished:",
            "",
            "   1.  Clients sending 0-RTT data as described in Section 4.2.10.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   2.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3ab151fc48220efc"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Servers MAY send data after sending their first flight, but"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "       "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3ab151fc48220efc"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "because the handshake is not yet complete, they have no assurance"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "       "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3ab151fc48220efc"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "of either the peer's identity or its liveness (i.e., the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "       "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3ab151fc48220efc"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "ClientHello might have been replayed)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a3b889b1f08552b3",
                  "998c4f3f86b8ee9c",
                  "5521b07b2cb639bd"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The key used to compute the Finished message is computed from the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a3b889b1f08552b3",
                  "998c4f3f86b8ee9c",
                  "5521b07b2cb639bd"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Base Key defined in Section 4.4 using HKDF (see Section 7.1)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a3b889b1f08552b3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Specifically:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a3b889b1f08552b3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "finished_key ="
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "       "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a3b889b1f08552b3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "HKDF-Expand-Label(BaseKey, \"finished\", \"\", Hash.length)"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Structure of this message:",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          opaque verify_data[Hash.length];",
            "      } Finished;",
            "",
            "   The verify_data value is computed as follows:",
            "",
            "      verify_data =",
            "          HMAC(finished_key,",
            "               Transcript-Hash(Handshake Context,",
            "                               Certificate*, CertificateVerify*))",
            "",
            "      * Only included if present.",
            "",
            "   HMAC [RFC2104] uses the Hash algorithm for the handshake.  As noted",
            "   above, the HMAC input can generally be implemented by a running hash,",
            "   i.e., just the handshake hash at this point.",
            "",
            "   In previous versions of TLS, the verify_data was always 12 octets",
            "   long.  In TLS 1.3, it is the size of the HMAC output for the Hash",
            "   used for the handshake.",
            "",
            "   Note: Alerts and any other non-handshake record types are not",
            "   handshake messages and are not included in the hash computations.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "20c88df99fc188c5"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Any records following a Finished message MUST be encrypted under the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "20c88df99fc188c5"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "appropriate application traffic key as described in Section 7.2."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  In"
              }
            ],
            "   particular, this includes any alerts sent by the server in response",
            "   to client Certificate and CertificateVerify messages."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "c4ccb40458fdb6ba",
            "c4ccb40458fdb6ba",
            "c4ccb40458fdb6ba",
            "3a3f2cb092a5db0b",
            "3a3f2cb092a5db0b",
            "3a3f2cb092a5db0b",
            "3ab151fc48220efc",
            "3ab151fc48220efc",
            "3ab151fc48220efc",
            "3ab151fc48220efc",
            "20c88df99fc188c5",
            "20c88df99fc188c5"
          ],
          "title": "Finished"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.5",
          "lines": [
            "      struct {} EndOfEarlyData;",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8d86c83b6ba1e239"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If the server sent an \"early_data\" extension in EncryptedExtensions,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8d86c83b6ba1e239"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "the client MUST send an EndOfEarlyData message after receiving the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8d86c83b6ba1e239"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "server Finished."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "60e42197a49c8cc1"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If the server does not send an \"early_data\""
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "60e42197a49c8cc1"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "extension in EncryptedExtensions, then the client MUST NOT send an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "60e42197a49c8cc1"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "EndOfEarlyData message."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This message indicates that all 0-RTT"
              }
            ],
            "   application_data messages, if any, have been transmitted and that the",
            "",
            "   following records are protected under handshake traffic keys.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "33f9be56ce97aa48",
                  "9c5c7a47a8941f28"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Servers MUST NOT send this message, and clients receiving it MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "33f9be56ce97aa48",
                  "9c5c7a47a8941f28"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "terminate the connection with an \"unexpected_message\" alert."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This"
              }
            ],
            "   message is encrypted under keys derived from the",
            "   client_early_traffic_secret."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "8d86c83b6ba1e239",
            "8d86c83b6ba1e239",
            "8d86c83b6ba1e239",
            "60e42197a49c8cc1",
            "60e42197a49c8cc1",
            "60e42197a49c8cc1",
            "33f9be56ce97aa48",
            "33f9be56ce97aa48",
            "9c5c7a47a8941f28",
            "9c5c7a47a8941f28"
          ],
          "title": "End of Early Data"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.6",
          "lines": [
            "   TLS also allows other messages to be sent after the main handshake.",
            "   These messages use a handshake content type and are encrypted under",
            "   the appropriate application traffic key."
          ],
          "title": "Post-Handshake Messages"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.6.1",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b47112b06121bd19"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "At any time after the server has received the client Finished"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b47112b06121bd19"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "message, it MAY send a NewSessionTicket message."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This message"
              }
            ],
            "   creates a unique association between the ticket value and a secret",
            "   PSK derived from the resumption master secret (see Section 7).",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "88317ae72d3cde40"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "The client MAY use this PSK for future handshakes by including the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "88317ae72d3cde40"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "ticket value in the \"pre_shared_key\" extension in its ClientHello"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "88317ae72d3cde40"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "(Section 4.2.11)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4c38754828ceb6dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Servers MAY send multiple tickets on a single"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4c38754828ceb6dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "connection, either immediately after each other or after specific"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4c38754828ceb6dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "events (see Appendix C.4)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  For instance, the server might send a new"
              }
            ],
            "   ticket after post-handshake authentication in order to encapsulate",
            "   the additional client authentication state.  Multiple tickets are",
            "   useful for clients for a variety of purposes, including:",
            "",
            "   -  Opening multiple parallel HTTP connections.",
            "",
            "   -  Performing connection racing across interfaces and address",
            "      families via (for example) Happy Eyeballs [RFC8305] or related",
            "      techniques.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "50cafc10dd4cd60e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Any ticket MUST only be resumed with a cipher suite that has the same"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "50cafc10dd4cd60e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "KDF hash algorithm as that used to establish the original connection."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "62780f142b254398"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Clients MUST only resume if the new SNI value is valid for the server"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "62780f142b254398"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "certificate presented in the original session and SHOULD only resume"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "62780f142b254398"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "if the SNI value matches the one used in the original session."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  The"
              }
            ],
            "   latter is a performance optimization: normally, there is no reason to",
            "   expect that different servers covered by a single certificate would",
            "   be able to accept each other's tickets; hence, attempting resumption",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   in that case would waste a single-use ticket.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d38158b72b5f36c0"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "If such an indication"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d38158b72b5f36c0"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "is provided (externally or by any other means), clients MAY resume"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d38158b72b5f36c0"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "with a different SNI value."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "957277b04d13793f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "On resumption, if reporting an SNI value to the calling application,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "957277b04d13793f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "implementations MUST use the value sent in the resumption ClientHello"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "957277b04d13793f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "rather than the value sent in the previous session."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Note that if a"
              }
            ],
            "   server implementation declines all PSK identities with different SNI",
            "   values, these two values are always the same.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5fad9888d43e71c6"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Note: Although the resumption master secret depends on the client's"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5fad9888d43e71c6"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "second flight, a server which does not request client authentication"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5fad9888d43e71c6"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "MAY compute the remainder of the transcript independently and then"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5fad9888d43e71c6"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "send a NewSessionTicket immediately upon sending its Finished rather"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5fad9888d43e71c6"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "than waiting for the client Finished."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This might be appropriate in"
              }
            ],
            "   cases where the client is expected to open multiple TLS connections",
            "   in parallel and would benefit from the reduced overhead of a",
            "   resumption handshake, for example.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "31c3e709a81552f3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "struct {"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "31c3e709a81552f3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "uint32 ticket_lifetime;"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "31c3e709a81552f3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "uint32 ticket_age_add;"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "31c3e709a81552f3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "opaque ticket_nonce<0..255>;"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "31c3e709a81552f3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "opaque ticket<1..2^16-1>;"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "31c3e709a81552f3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Extension extensions<0..2^16-2>;"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "31c3e709a81552f3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "} NewSessionTicket;"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   ticket_lifetime:  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "222a4f6d57c36608"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Indicates the lifetime in seconds as a 32-bit"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "222a4f6d57c36608"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "unsigned integer in network byte order from the time of ticket"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "222a4f6d57c36608"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "issuance."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "656f61a2ad010ccb",
                  "ef70f7add62f3037",
                  "0bf9651f174e9745",
                  "4c6258a8282758f0",
                  "7b7c9d531190c1e5"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Servers MUST NOT use any value greater than"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "656f61a2ad010ccb",
                  "ef70f7add62f3037",
                  "0bf9651f174e9745",
                  "4c6258a8282758f0",
                  "7b7c9d531190c1e5"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "604800 seconds (7 days)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f1ca51e161bfa844",
                  "0b7e63295171db5c"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "The value of zero indicates that the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f1ca51e161bfa844",
                  "0b7e63295171db5c"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "ticket should be discarded immediately."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3786b4560b269dc3",
                  "1b74529887b5d528",
                  "deadbcc98c57841c"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Clients MUST NOT cache"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3786b4560b269dc3",
                  "1b74529887b5d528",
                  "deadbcc98c57841c"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "tickets for longer than 7 days, regardless of the ticket_lifetime,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3786b4560b269dc3",
                  "1b74529887b5d528",
                  "deadbcc98c57841c"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "and MAY delete tickets earlier based on local policy."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e0fa0b26c5ad6c69"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "A server"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e0fa0b26c5ad6c69"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "MAY treat a ticket as valid for a shorter period of time than what"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e0fa0b26c5ad6c69"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "is stated in the ticket_lifetime."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   ticket_age_add:  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "596b9a418727d1dc"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "A securely generated, random 32-bit value that is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "596b9a418727d1dc"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "used to obscure the age of the ticket that the client includes in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "596b9a418727d1dc"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the \"pre_shared_key\" extension."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  The client-side ticket age is"
              }
            ],
            "      added to this value modulo 2^32 to obtain the value that is",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      transmitted by the client.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "704e0778f9d4d9f1",
                  "7ee7a9f11dec1428",
                  "d7fe87c5f8915549"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "The server MUST generate a fresh value"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "704e0778f9d4d9f1",
                  "7ee7a9f11dec1428",
                  "d7fe87c5f8915549"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "for each ticket it sends."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   ticket_nonce:  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1ddf1297aca7204f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "A per-ticket value that is unique across all tickets"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1ddf1297aca7204f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "issued on this connection."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   ticket:  The value of the ticket to be used as the PSK identity.  The",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      ticket itself is an opaque label.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "25df5e791c23a767"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "It MAY be either a database"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "25df5e791c23a767"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "lookup key or a self-encrypted and self-authenticated value."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   extensions:  A set of extension values for the ticket.  The",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      \"Extension\" format is defined in Section 4.2.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1683f8d2499d6545"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Clients MUST ignore"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1683f8d2499d6545"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "unrecognized extensions."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The sole extension currently defined for NewSessionTicket is",
            "   \"early_data\", indicating that the ticket may be used to send 0-RTT",
            "   data (Section 4.2.10).  It contains the following value:",
            "",
            "   max_early_data_size:  The maximum amount of 0-RTT data that the",
            "      client is allowed to send when using this ticket, in bytes.  Only",
            "      Application Data payload (i.e., plaintext but not padding or the",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      inner content type byte) is counted.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a9aa147ad6009df2"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "A server receiving more than"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a9aa147ad6009df2"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "max_early_data_size bytes of 0-RTT data SHOULD terminate the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a9aa147ad6009df2"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "connection with an \"unexpected_message\" alert."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ae8d2b48a4bceb0f"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "Note that servers"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ae8d2b48a4bceb0f"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "that reject early data due to lack of cryptographic material will"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ae8d2b48a4bceb0f"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "be unable to differentiate padding from content, so clients"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ae8d2b48a4bceb0f"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "SHOULD NOT depend on being able to send large quantities of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ae8d2b48a4bceb0f"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "padding in early data records."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3db229f3e37c7153"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The PSK associated with the ticket is computed as:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "       "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3db229f3e37c7153"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "HKDF-Expand-Label(resumption_master_secret,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "                        "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3db229f3e37c7153"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "\"resumption\", ticket_nonce, Hash.length)"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Because the ticket_nonce value is distinct for each NewSessionTicket",
            "   message, a different PSK will be derived for each ticket.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aeae97bfaa9c8913",
                  "068721ca1344d595"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "Note that in principle it is possible to continue issuing new tickets"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aeae97bfaa9c8913",
                  "068721ca1344d595"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "which indefinitely extend the lifetime of the keying material"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aeae97bfaa9c8913",
                  "068721ca1344d595"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "originally derived from an initial non-PSK handshake (which was most"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aeae97bfaa9c8913",
                  "068721ca1344d595"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "likely tied to the peer's certificate).  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4dc02e565166411e",
                  "aeae97bfaa9c8913",
                  "068721ca1344d595"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "It is RECOMMENDED that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4dc02e565166411e",
                  "aeae97bfaa9c8913",
                  "068721ca1344d595"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "implementations place limits on the total lifetime of such keying"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4dc02e565166411e",
                  "aeae97bfaa9c8913",
                  "068721ca1344d595"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "material; these limits should take into account the lifetime of the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4dc02e565166411e",
                  "aeae97bfaa9c8913",
                  "068721ca1344d595"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "peer's certificate, the likelihood of intervening revocation, and the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4dc02e565166411e",
                  "aeae97bfaa9c8913",
                  "068721ca1344d595"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "time since the peer's online CertificateVerify signature."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "b47112b06121bd19",
            "b47112b06121bd19",
            "88317ae72d3cde40",
            "88317ae72d3cde40",
            "88317ae72d3cde40",
            "4c38754828ceb6dd",
            "4c38754828ceb6dd",
            "4c38754828ceb6dd",
            "50cafc10dd4cd60e",
            "50cafc10dd4cd60e",
            "62780f142b254398",
            "62780f142b254398",
            "62780f142b254398",
            "d38158b72b5f36c0",
            "d38158b72b5f36c0",
            "d38158b72b5f36c0",
            "957277b04d13793f",
            "957277b04d13793f",
            "957277b04d13793f",
            "5fad9888d43e71c6",
            "5fad9888d43e71c6",
            "5fad9888d43e71c6",
            "5fad9888d43e71c6",
            "5fad9888d43e71c6",
            "656f61a2ad010ccb",
            "656f61a2ad010ccb",
            "3786b4560b269dc3",
            "3786b4560b269dc3",
            "3786b4560b269dc3",
            "e0fa0b26c5ad6c69",
            "e0fa0b26c5ad6c69",
            "e0fa0b26c5ad6c69",
            "704e0778f9d4d9f1",
            "704e0778f9d4d9f1",
            "25df5e791c23a767",
            "25df5e791c23a767",
            "1683f8d2499d6545",
            "1683f8d2499d6545",
            "a9aa147ad6009df2",
            "a9aa147ad6009df2",
            "a9aa147ad6009df2",
            "ae8d2b48a4bceb0f",
            "ae8d2b48a4bceb0f",
            "ae8d2b48a4bceb0f",
            "ae8d2b48a4bceb0f",
            "ae8d2b48a4bceb0f",
            "4dc02e565166411e",
            "4dc02e565166411e",
            "4dc02e565166411e",
            "4dc02e565166411e",
            "4dc02e565166411e"
          ],
          "title": "New Session Ticket Message"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.6.2",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "438dbd2bea4b8abd"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "When the client has sent the \"post_handshake_auth\" extension (see"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "438dbd2bea4b8abd"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Section 4.2.6), a server MAY request client authentication at any"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "438dbd2bea4b8abd"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "time after the handshake has completed by sending a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "438dbd2bea4b8abd"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "CertificateRequest message."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "35cd9979ecfd7824"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The client MUST respond with the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "35cd9979ecfd7824"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "appropriate Authentication messages (see Section 4.4)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8a21f3070a6cfc56"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If the client"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8a21f3070a6cfc56"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "chooses to authenticate, it MUST send Certificate, CertificateVerify,"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   and Finished.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5f208b021853c834"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If it declines, it MUST send a Certificate message"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5f208b021853c834"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "containing no certificates followed by Finished."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9f8f5b236f156e92"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "All of the client's"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9f8f5b236f156e92"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "messages for a given response MUST appear consecutively on the wire"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9f8f5b236f156e92"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "with no intervening messages of other types."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "807815266896ed1a",
                  "e0d5be612f4055ef"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "A client that receives a CertificateRequest message without having"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "807815266896ed1a",
                  "e0d5be612f4055ef"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "sent the \"post_handshake_auth\" extension MUST send an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "807815266896ed1a",
                  "e0d5be612f4055ef"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "\"unexpected_message\" fatal alert."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9e5880b87c69bb5b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Note: Because client authentication could involve prompting the user,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9e5880b87c69bb5b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "servers MUST be prepared for some delay, including receiving an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9e5880b87c69bb5b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "arbitrary number of other messages between sending the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9e5880b87c69bb5b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "CertificateRequest and receiving a response."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7c4d138a019c95a5"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "In addition, clients"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7c4d138a019c95a5"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "which receive multiple CertificateRequests in close succession MAY"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7c4d138a019c95a5"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "respond to them in a different order than they were received (the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7c4d138a019c95a5"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "certificate_request_context value allows the server to disambiguate"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7c4d138a019c95a5"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "the responses)."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "438dbd2bea4b8abd",
            "438dbd2bea4b8abd",
            "438dbd2bea4b8abd",
            "438dbd2bea4b8abd",
            "35cd9979ecfd7824",
            "35cd9979ecfd7824",
            "8a21f3070a6cfc56",
            "8a21f3070a6cfc56",
            "5f208b021853c834",
            "5f208b021853c834",
            "9f8f5b236f156e92",
            "9f8f5b236f156e92",
            "9f8f5b236f156e92",
            "807815266896ed1a",
            "807815266896ed1a",
            "807815266896ed1a",
            "9e5880b87c69bb5b",
            "9e5880b87c69bb5b",
            "9e5880b87c69bb5b",
            "9e5880b87c69bb5b",
            "7c4d138a019c95a5",
            "7c4d138a019c95a5",
            "7c4d138a019c95a5",
            "7c4d138a019c95a5",
            "7c4d138a019c95a5"
          ],
          "title": "Post-Handshake Authentication"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.6.3",
          "lines": [
            "   The KeyUpdate handshake message is used to indicate that the sender",
            "   is updating its sending cryptographic keys.  This message can be sent",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   by either peer after it has sent a Finished message.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "92e3477eaaadd25e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Implementations"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "92e3477eaaadd25e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "that receive a KeyUpdate message prior to receiving a Finished"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "92e3477eaaadd25e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "message MUST terminate the connection with an \"unexpected_message\""
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "92e3477eaaadd25e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "alert."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f8407f08d1aceec4"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "After sending a KeyUpdate message, the sender SHALL send all"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f8407f08d1aceec4"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "its traffic using the next generation of keys, computed as described"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f8407f08d1aceec4"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "in Section 7.2."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "65c2e4a1e0bf6095"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Upon receiving a KeyUpdate, the receiver MUST update"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "65c2e4a1e0bf6095"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "its receiving keys."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "      enum {",
            "          update_not_requested(0), update_requested(1), (255)",
            "      } KeyUpdateRequest;",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          KeyUpdateRequest request_update;",
            "      } KeyUpdate;",
            "",
            "   request_update:  Indicates whether the recipient of the KeyUpdate",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      should respond with its own KeyUpdate.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0d8fcff31c67d68c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If an implementation"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0d8fcff31c67d68c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "receives any other value, it MUST terminate the connection with an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0d8fcff31c67d68c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "\"illegal_parameter\" alert."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "82b8c00e6c35283f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If the request_update field is set to \"update_requested\", then the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "82b8c00e6c35283f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "receiver MUST send a KeyUpdate of its own with request_update set to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "82b8c00e6c35283f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "\"update_not_requested\" prior to sending its next Application Data"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "82b8c00e6c35283f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "record."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This mechanism allows either side to force an update to the"
              }
            ],
            "   entire connection, but causes an implementation which receives",
            "",
            "   multiple KeyUpdates while it is silent to respond with a single",
            "   update.  Note that implementations may receive an arbitrary number of",
            "   messages between sending a KeyUpdate with request_update set to",
            "   \"update_requested\" and receiving the peer's KeyUpdate, because those",
            "   messages may already be in flight.  However, because send and receive",
            "   keys are derived from independent traffic secrets, retaining the",
            "   receive traffic secret does not threaten the forward secrecy of data",
            "   sent before the sender changed keys.",
            "",
            "   If implementations independently send their own KeyUpdates with",
            "   request_update set to \"update_requested\" and they cross in flight,",
            "   then each side will also send a response, with the result that each",
            "   side increments by two generations.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d2679b8d99d7be1b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Both sender and receiver MUST encrypt their KeyUpdate messages with"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d2679b8d99d7be1b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "the old keys."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b4f728e261adcfc6"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Additionally, both sides MUST enforce that a KeyUpdate"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b4f728e261adcfc6"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "with the old key is received before accepting any messages encrypted"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b4f728e261adcfc6"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "with the new key."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Failure to do so may allow message truncation"
              }
            ],
            "   attacks."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "92e3477eaaadd25e",
            "92e3477eaaadd25e",
            "92e3477eaaadd25e",
            "92e3477eaaadd25e",
            "f8407f08d1aceec4",
            "f8407f08d1aceec4",
            "f8407f08d1aceec4",
            "65c2e4a1e0bf6095",
            "65c2e4a1e0bf6095",
            "0d8fcff31c67d68c",
            "0d8fcff31c67d68c",
            "0d8fcff31c67d68c",
            "82b8c00e6c35283f",
            "82b8c00e6c35283f",
            "82b8c00e6c35283f",
            "82b8c00e6c35283f",
            "d2679b8d99d7be1b",
            "d2679b8d99d7be1b",
            "b4f728e261adcfc6",
            "b4f728e261adcfc6",
            "b4f728e261adcfc6"
          ],
          "title": "Key and Initialization Vector Update"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5",
          "lines": [
            "   The TLS record protocol takes messages to be transmitted, fragments",
            "   the data into manageable blocks, protects the records, and transmits",
            "   the result.  Received data is verified, decrypted, reassembled, and",
            "   then delivered to higher-level clients.",
            "",
            "   TLS records are typed, which allows multiple higher-level protocols",
            "   to be multiplexed over the same record layer.  This document",
            "   specifies four content types: handshake, application_data, alert, and",
            "   change_cipher_spec.  The change_cipher_spec record is used only for",
            "   compatibility purposes (see Appendix D.4).",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4fc3eb763e6c43cd"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "An implementation may receive an unencrypted record of type"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4fc3eb763e6c43cd"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "change_cipher_spec consisting of the single byte value 0x01 at any"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4fc3eb763e6c43cd"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "time after the first ClientHello message has been sent or received"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4fc3eb763e6c43cd"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "and before the peer's Finished message has been received and MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4fc3eb763e6c43cd"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "simply drop it without further processing."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Note that this record may"
              }
            ],
            "   appear at a point at the handshake where the implementation is",
            "   expecting protected records, and so it is necessary to detect this",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   condition prior to attempting to deprotect the record.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "890f25a5b8932ad4"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "An"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "890f25a5b8932ad4"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "implementation which receives any other change_cipher_spec value or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "890f25a5b8932ad4"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "which receives a protected change_cipher_spec record MUST abort the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "890f25a5b8932ad4"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "handshake with an \"unexpected_message\" alert."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1cf6c4b857bb323e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If an implementation"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1cf6c4b857bb323e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "detects a change_cipher_spec record received before the first"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1cf6c4b857bb323e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "ClientHello message or after the peer's Finished message, it MUST be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1cf6c4b857bb323e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "treated as an unexpected record type (though stateless servers may"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1cf6c4b857bb323e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "not be able to distinguish these cases from allowed cases)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1254a67aac3d1def"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Implementations MUST NOT send record types not defined in this"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1254a67aac3d1def"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "document unless negotiated by some extension."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a4c522e6b51da31d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If a TLS"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a4c522e6b51da31d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "implementation receives an unexpected record type, it MUST terminate"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a4c522e6b51da31d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "the connection with an \"unexpected_message\" alert."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  New record"
              }
            ],
            "   content type values are assigned by IANA in the TLS ContentType",
            "   registry as described in Section 11."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "4fc3eb763e6c43cd",
            "4fc3eb763e6c43cd",
            "4fc3eb763e6c43cd",
            "4fc3eb763e6c43cd",
            "4fc3eb763e6c43cd",
            "890f25a5b8932ad4",
            "890f25a5b8932ad4",
            "890f25a5b8932ad4",
            "890f25a5b8932ad4",
            "1cf6c4b857bb323e",
            "1cf6c4b857bb323e",
            "1cf6c4b857bb323e",
            "1cf6c4b857bb323e",
            "1cf6c4b857bb323e",
            "1254a67aac3d1def",
            "1254a67aac3d1def",
            "a4c522e6b51da31d",
            "a4c522e6b51da31d",
            "a4c522e6b51da31d"
          ],
          "title": "Record Protocol"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.1",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "25b6a89a97799601"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The record layer fragments information blocks into TLSPlaintext"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "25b6a89a97799601"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "records carrying data in chunks of 2^14 bytes or less."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Message"
              }
            ],
            "   boundaries are handled differently depending on the underlying",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   ContentType.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "afece72bbf74f839"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Any future content types MUST specify appropriate"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "afece72bbf74f839"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "rules."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Note that these rules are stricter than what was enforced in"
              }
            ],
            "   TLS 1.2.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5b47fcbfb934d2b0"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Handshake messages MAY be coalesced into a single TLSPlaintext record"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5b47fcbfb934d2b0"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "or fragmented across several records, provided that:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8f1d9492101803c9",
                  "4d4ddad783843ba7",
                  "72c90e53d7970bd8"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "-  Handshake messages MUST NOT be interleaved with other record"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8f1d9492101803c9",
                  "4d4ddad783843ba7",
                  "72c90e53d7970bd8"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "types."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4d4ddad783843ba7",
                  "72c90e53d7970bd8"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d2e3e303f5f37e0f",
                  "4d4ddad783843ba7",
                  "72c90e53d7970bd8"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "That is, if a handshake message is split over two or more"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d2e3e303f5f37e0f",
                  "4d4ddad783843ba7",
                  "72c90e53d7970bd8"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "records, there MUST NOT be any other records between them."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ebb70a46fd83640d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "-  Handshake messages MUST NOT span key changes."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7a77923b3669c943",
                  "7c1bdef84bd17ef7"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Implementations"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7a77923b3669c943",
                  "7c1bdef84bd17ef7"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "MUST verify that all messages immediately preceding a key change"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7a77923b3669c943",
                  "7c1bdef84bd17ef7"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "align with a record boundary; if not, then they MUST terminate the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7a77923b3669c943",
                  "7c1bdef84bd17ef7"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "connection with an \"unexpected_message\" alert."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "87940533f7d1258f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Because the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "87940533f7d1258f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "ClientHello, EndOfEarlyData, ServerHello, Finished, and KeyUpdate"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "87940533f7d1258f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "messages can immediately precede a key change, implementations"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "87940533f7d1258f"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "MUST send these messages in alignment with a record boundary."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5ab1d4af34771a2b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Implementations MUST NOT send zero-length fragments of Handshake"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5ab1d4af34771a2b"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "types, even if those fragments contain padding."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2c3b71700e7ec641",
                  "0ff81eefbb127a30"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Alert messages (Section 6) MUST NOT be fragmented across records, and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2c3b71700e7ec641",
                  "0ff81eefbb127a30"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "multiple alert messages MUST NOT be coalesced into a single"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2c3b71700e7ec641",
                  "0ff81eefbb127a30"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "TLSPlaintext record."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ff510e2f3879e3c8"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "In other words, a record with an Alert type"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ff510e2f3879e3c8"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "MUST contain exactly one message."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Application Data messages contain data that is opaque to TLS.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   Application Data messages are always protected.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d80bafd3bab6356c"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Zero-length"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d80bafd3bab6356c"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "fragments of Application Data MAY be sent, as they are potentially"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d80bafd3bab6356c"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "useful as a traffic analysis countermeasure."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "da7930fd52343add"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Application Data"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "da7930fd52343add"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "fragments MAY be split across multiple records or coalesced into a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "da7930fd52343add"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "single record."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "      enum {",
            "          invalid(0),",
            "          change_cipher_spec(20),",
            "          alert(21),",
            "          handshake(22),",
            "          application_data(23),",
            "          (255)",
            "      } ContentType;",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          ContentType type;",
            "          ProtocolVersion legacy_record_version;",
            "          uint16 length;",
            "          opaque fragment[TLSPlaintext.length];",
            "      } TLSPlaintext;",
            "",
            "   type:  The higher-level protocol used to process the enclosed",
            "      fragment.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "af6a599231e82c87",
                  "122aab061b35a69a"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "legacy_record_version:  MUST be set to 0x0303 for all records"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "af6a599231e82c87",
                  "122aab061b35a69a"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "generated by a TLS 1.3 implementation other than an initial"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "af6a599231e82c87",
                  "122aab061b35a69a"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "ClientHello (i.e., one not generated after a HelloRetryRequest),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "af6a599231e82c87",
                  "122aab061b35a69a"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "where it MAY also be 0x0301 for compatibility purposes."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "49920aa0f68db405"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "This"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "49920aa0f68db405"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "field is deprecated and MUST be ignored for all purposes."
              }
            ],
            "      Previous versions of TLS would use other values in this field",
            "      under some circumstances.",
            "",
            "   length:  The length (in bytes) of the following",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      TLSPlaintext.fragment.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6d99337d8b40616",
                  "ebda44f328ee9120"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "The length MUST NOT exceed 2^14 bytes."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ebda44f328ee9120"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "28e9bb30c7b9872f",
                  "ebda44f328ee9120"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "An"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "28e9bb30c7b9872f",
                  "ebda44f328ee9120"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "endpoint that receives a record that exceeds this length MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "28e9bb30c7b9872f",
                  "ebda44f328ee9120"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "terminate the connection with a \"record_overflow\" alert."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   fragment:  The data being transmitted.  This value is transparent and",
            "      is treated as an independent block to be dealt with by the higher-",
            "      level protocol specified by the type field.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   This document describes TLS 1.3, which uses the version 0x0304.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd57429528687d75"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "This"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd57429528687d75"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "version value is historical, deriving from the use of 0x0301 for"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd57429528687d75"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "TLS 1.0 and 0x0300 for SSL 3.0.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "515feb29da93c676",
                  "dd57429528687d75"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "In order to maximize backward"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "515feb29da93c676",
                  "dd57429528687d75"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "compatibility, a record containing an initial ClientHello SHOULD have"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "515feb29da93c676",
                  "dd57429528687d75"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "version 0x0301 (reflecting TLS 1.0)"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "515feb29da93c676"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": " and a record containing a second"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "515feb29da93c676"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "ClientHello or a ServerHello MUST have version 0x0303 (reflecting"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "515feb29da93c676"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "TLS 1.2)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  When negotiating prior versions of TLS, endpoints follow"
              }
            ],
            "   the procedure and requirements provided in Appendix D.",
            "",
            "   When record protection has not yet been engaged, TLSPlaintext",
            "   structures are written directly onto the wire.  Once record",
            "   protection has started, TLSPlaintext records are protected and sent",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   as described in the following section.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c5e295988a31fd93"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Note that Application Data"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c5e295988a31fd93"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "records MUST NOT be written to the wire unprotected (see Section 2"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c5e295988a31fd93"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "for details)."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "afece72bbf74f839",
            "afece72bbf74f839",
            "5b47fcbfb934d2b0",
            "5b47fcbfb934d2b0",
            "8f1d9492101803c9",
            "8f1d9492101803c9",
            "d2e3e303f5f37e0f",
            "d2e3e303f5f37e0f",
            "ebb70a46fd83640d",
            "7a77923b3669c943",
            "7a77923b3669c943",
            "7a77923b3669c943",
            "7a77923b3669c943",
            "7c1bdef84bd17ef7",
            "7c1bdef84bd17ef7",
            "7c1bdef84bd17ef7",
            "7c1bdef84bd17ef7",
            "87940533f7d1258f",
            "87940533f7d1258f",
            "87940533f7d1258f",
            "87940533f7d1258f",
            "5ab1d4af34771a2b",
            "5ab1d4af34771a2b",
            "2c3b71700e7ec641",
            "2c3b71700e7ec641",
            "2c3b71700e7ec641",
            "0ff81eefbb127a30",
            "0ff81eefbb127a30",
            "0ff81eefbb127a30",
            "ff510e2f3879e3c8",
            "ff510e2f3879e3c8",
            "d80bafd3bab6356c",
            "d80bafd3bab6356c",
            "d80bafd3bab6356c",
            "da7930fd52343add",
            "da7930fd52343add",
            "da7930fd52343add",
            "af6a599231e82c87",
            "af6a599231e82c87",
            "af6a599231e82c87",
            "af6a599231e82c87",
            "49920aa0f68db405",
            "49920aa0f68db405",
            "b6d99337d8b40616",
            "28e9bb30c7b9872f",
            "28e9bb30c7b9872f",
            "28e9bb30c7b9872f",
            "515feb29da93c676",
            "515feb29da93c676",
            "515feb29da93c676",
            "515feb29da93c676",
            "515feb29da93c676",
            "c5e295988a31fd93",
            "c5e295988a31fd93",
            "c5e295988a31fd93"
          ],
          "title": "Record Layer"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.2",
          "lines": [
            "   The record protection functions translate a TLSPlaintext structure",
            "   into a TLSCiphertext structure.  The deprotection functions reverse",
            "   the process.  In TLS 1.3, as opposed to previous versions of TLS, all",
            "   ciphers are modeled as \"Authenticated Encryption with Associated",
            "   Data\" (AEAD) [RFC5116].  AEAD functions provide a unified encryption",
            "   and authentication operation which turns plaintext into authenticated",
            "   ciphertext and back again.  Each encrypted record consists of a",
            "   plaintext header followed by an encrypted body, which itself contains",
            "   a type and optional padding.",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          opaque content[TLSPlaintext.length];",
            "          ContentType type;",
            "          uint8 zeros[length_of_padding];",
            "      } TLSInnerPlaintext;",
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          ContentType opaque_type = application_data; /* 23 */",
            "          ProtocolVersion legacy_record_version = 0x0303; /* TLS v1.2 */",
            "          uint16 length;",
            "          opaque encrypted_record[TLSCiphertext.length];",
            "      } TLSCiphertext;",
            "",
            "   content:  The TLSPlaintext.fragment value, containing the byte",
            "      encoding of a handshake or an alert message, or the raw bytes of",
            "      the application's data to send.",
            "",
            "   type:  The TLSPlaintext.type value containing the content type of the",
            "      record.",
            "",
            "   zeros:  An arbitrary-length run of zero-valued bytes may appear in",
            "      the cleartext after the type field.  This provides an opportunity",
            "      for senders to pad any TLS record by a chosen amount as long as",
            "      the total stays within record size limits.  See Section 5.4 for",
            "      more details.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aa184e06e785fb4f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "opaque_type:  The outer opaque_type field of a TLSCiphertext record"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aa184e06e785fb4f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "is always set to the value 23 (application_data) for outward"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aa184e06e785fb4f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "compatibility with middleboxes accustomed to parsing previous"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aa184e06e785fb4f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "versions of TLS.  The actual content type of the record is found"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aa184e06e785fb4f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "in TLSInnerPlaintext.type after decryption."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d89b9417630633f0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "legacy_record_version:  The legacy_record_version field is always"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d89b9417630633f0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "0x0303.  TLS 1.3 TLSCiphertexts are not generated until after"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d89b9417630633f0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "TLS 1.3 has been negotiated, so there are no historical"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d89b9417630633f0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "compatibility concerns where other values might be received.  Note"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d89b9417630633f0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "that the handshake protocol, including the ClientHello and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d89b9417630633f0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "ServerHello messages, authenticates the protocol version, so this"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d89b9417630633f0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "value is redundant."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "66738e162a461ed8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "length:  The length (in bytes) of the following"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "66738e162a461ed8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "TLSCiphertext.encrypted_record, which is the sum of the lengths of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "66738e162a461ed8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the content and the padding, plus one for the inner content type,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "66738e162a461ed8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "plus any expansion added by the AEAD algorithm.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "454d9fb43b281160",
                  "66738e162a461ed8"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The length"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "454d9fb43b281160",
                  "66738e162a461ed8"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "MUST NOT exceed 2^14 + 256 bytes."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "66738e162a461ed8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "60b57f5e24c268ce",
                  "66738e162a461ed8"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "An endpoint that receives a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "60b57f5e24c268ce",
                  "66738e162a461ed8"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "record that exceeds this length MUST terminate the connection with"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "60b57f5e24c268ce",
                  "66738e162a461ed8"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "a \"record_overflow\" alert."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   encrypted_record:  The AEAD-encrypted form of the serialized",
            "      TLSInnerPlaintext structure.",
            "",
            "   AEAD algorithms take as input a single key, a nonce, a plaintext, and",
            "   \"additional data\" to be included in the authentication check, as",
            "   described in Section 2.1 of [RFC5116].  The key is either the",
            "   client_write_key or the server_write_key, the nonce is derived from",
            "   the sequence number and the client_write_iv or server_write_iv (see",
            "   Section 5.3), and the additional data input is the record header.",
            "",
            "   I.e.,",
            "",
            "      additional_data = TLSCiphertext.opaque_type ||",
            "                        TLSCiphertext.legacy_record_version ||",
            "                        TLSCiphertext.length",
            "",
            "   The plaintext input to the AEAD algorithm is the encoded",
            "   TLSInnerPlaintext structure.  Derivation of traffic keys is defined",
            "   in Section 7.3.",
            "",
            "   The AEAD output consists of the ciphertext output from the AEAD",
            "   encryption operation.  The length of the plaintext is greater than",
            "   the corresponding TLSPlaintext.length due to the inclusion of",
            "   TLSInnerPlaintext.type and any padding supplied by the sender.  The",
            "   length of the AEAD output will generally be larger than the",
            "   plaintext, but by an amount that varies with the AEAD algorithm.",
            "",
            "   Since the ciphers might incorporate padding, the amount of overhead",
            "   could vary with different lengths of plaintext.  Symbolically,",
            "",
            "      AEADEncrypted =",
            "          AEAD-Encrypt(write_key, nonce, additional_data, plaintext)",
            "",
            "   The encrypted_record field of TLSCiphertext is set to AEADEncrypted.",
            "",
            "   In order to decrypt and verify, the cipher takes as input the key,",
            "   nonce, additional data, and the AEADEncrypted value.  The output is",
            "   either the plaintext or an error indicating that the decryption",
            "   failed.  There is no separate integrity check.  Symbolically,",
            "",
            "      plaintext of encrypted_record =",
            "          AEAD-Decrypt(peer_write_key, nonce,",
            "                       additional_data, AEADEncrypted)",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "550533427877dc47"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If the decryption fails, the receiver MUST terminate the connection"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "550533427877dc47"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "with a \"bad_record_mac\" alert."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d55c1f6d962c3080",
                  "00acf739cb3c57f0"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "An AEAD algorithm used in TLS 1.3 MUST NOT produce an expansion"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d55c1f6d962c3080",
                  "00acf739cb3c57f0"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "greater than 255 octets."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b465beed1e7bb402"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "An endpoint that receives a record from its"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b465beed1e7bb402"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "peer with TLSCiphertext.length larger than 2^14 + 256 octets MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b465beed1e7bb402"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "terminate the connection with a \"record_overflow\" alert."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This limit"
              }
            ],
            "   is derived from the maximum TLSInnerPlaintext length of 2^14 octets +",
            "   1 octet for ContentType + the maximum AEAD expansion of 255 octets."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "454d9fb43b281160",
            "454d9fb43b281160",
            "60b57f5e24c268ce",
            "60b57f5e24c268ce",
            "60b57f5e24c268ce",
            "550533427877dc47",
            "550533427877dc47",
            "d55c1f6d962c3080",
            "d55c1f6d962c3080",
            "b465beed1e7bb402",
            "b465beed1e7bb402",
            "b465beed1e7bb402"
          ],
          "title": "Record Payload Protection"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.3",
          "lines": [
            "   A 64-bit sequence number is maintained separately for reading and",
            "   writing records.  The appropriate sequence number is incremented by",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   one after reading or writing each record.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "717d6a17974a6dfb",
                  "1f23306a2c3fe383"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "Each sequence number is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "717d6a17974a6dfb",
                  "1f23306a2c3fe383"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "set to zero at the beginning of a connection and whenever the key is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "717d6a17974a6dfb",
                  "1f23306a2c3fe383"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "changed; the first record transmitted under a particular traffic key"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "717d6a17974a6dfb",
                  "1f23306a2c3fe383"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "MUST use sequence number 0."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Because the size of sequence numbers is 64-bit, they should not wrap.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "70132ac22369ba0d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If a TLS implementation would need to wrap a sequence number, it MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "70132ac22369ba0d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "either rekey (Section 4.6.3) or terminate the connection."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Each AEAD algorithm will specify a range of possible lengths for the",
            "   per-record nonce, from N_MIN bytes to N_MAX bytes of input [RFC5116].",
            "   The length of the TLS per-record nonce (iv_length) is set to the",
            "   larger of 8 bytes and N_MIN for the AEAD algorithm (see [RFC5116],",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   Section 4).  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3e5d058d3ea7fce9"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "An AEAD algorithm where N_MAX is less than 8 bytes"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3e5d058d3ea7fce9"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "MUST NOT be used with TLS."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  The per-record nonce for the AEAD"
              }
            ],
            "   construction is formed as follows:",
            "",
            "   1.  The 64-bit record sequence number is encoded in network byte",
            "       order and padded to the left with zeros to iv_length.",
            "",
            "   2.  The padded sequence number is XORed with either the static",
            "       client_write_iv or server_write_iv (depending on the role).",
            "",
            "   The resulting quantity (of length iv_length) is used as the",
            "   per-record nonce.",
            "",
            "   Note: This is a different construction from that in TLS 1.2, which",
            "   specified a partially explicit nonce."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "717d6a17974a6dfb",
            "717d6a17974a6dfb",
            "717d6a17974a6dfb",
            "717d6a17974a6dfb",
            "70132ac22369ba0d",
            "70132ac22369ba0d",
            "3e5d058d3ea7fce9",
            "3e5d058d3ea7fce9"
          ],
          "title": "Per-Record Nonce"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.4",
          "lines": [
            "   All encrypted TLS records can be padded to inflate the size of the",
            "   TLSCiphertext.  This allows the sender to hide the size of the",
            "   traffic from an observer.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0cfbe485b0eddf36"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "When generating a TLSCiphertext record, implementations MAY choose to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0cfbe485b0eddf36"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "pad."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  An unpadded record is just a record with a padding length of"
              }
            ],
            "   zero.  Padding is a string of zero-valued bytes appended to the",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   ContentType field before encryption.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "180a59e64012365e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Implementations MUST set the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "180a59e64012365e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "padding octets to all zeros before encrypting."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d9b30735f086c089"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "Application Data records may contain a zero-length"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d9b30735f086c089"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "TLSInnerPlaintext.content if the sender desires."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This permits"
              }
            ],
            "   generation of plausibly sized cover traffic in contexts where the",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   presence or absence of activity may be sensitive.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aeb89794c6089f72",
                  "a118bc99178b292f",
                  "2d548470faac3ef7",
                  "0d87f53fd42a2025"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "Implementations"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aeb89794c6089f72",
                  "a118bc99178b292f",
                  "2d548470faac3ef7",
                  "0d87f53fd42a2025"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "MUST NOT send Handshake and Alert records that have a zero-length"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aeb89794c6089f72",
                  "a118bc99178b292f",
                  "2d548470faac3ef7",
                  "0d87f53fd42a2025"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "TLSInnerPlaintext.content; if such a message is received, the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aeb89794c6089f72",
                  "a118bc99178b292f",
                  "2d548470faac3ef7",
                  "0d87f53fd42a2025"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "receiving implementation MUST terminate the connection with an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aeb89794c6089f72",
                  "a118bc99178b292f",
                  "2d548470faac3ef7",
                  "0d87f53fd42a2025"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "\"unexpected_message\" alert."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The padding sent is automatically verified by the record protection",
            "   mechanism; upon successful decryption of a",
            "   TLSCiphertext.encrypted_record, the receiving implementation scans",
            "   the field from the end toward the beginning until it finds a non-zero",
            "   octet.  This non-zero octet is the content type of the message.  This",
            "   padding scheme was selected because it allows padding of any",
            "   encrypted TLS record by an arbitrary size (from zero up to TLS record",
            "   size limits) without introducing new content types.  The design also",
            "   enforces all-zero padding octets, which allows for quick detection of",
            "   padding errors.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "98e95302e05d1d70"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Implementations MUST limit their scanning to the cleartext returned"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "98e95302e05d1d70"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "from the AEAD decryption."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f2c1b930dbe14713",
                  "886758dcc0dc3840"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "If a receiving implementation does not"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f2c1b930dbe14713",
                  "886758dcc0dc3840"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "find a non-zero octet in the cleartext, it MUST terminate the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f2c1b930dbe14713",
                  "886758dcc0dc3840"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "connection with an \"unexpected_message\" alert."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1c4206b295549383"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The presence of padding does not change the overall record size"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1c4206b295549383"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "limitations: the full encoded TLSInnerPlaintext MUST NOT exceed 2^14"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1c4206b295549383"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "+ 1 octets."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  If the maximum fragment length is reduced -- as, for"
              }
            ],
            "   example, by the record_size_limit extension from [RFC8449] -- then",
            "   the reduced limit applies to the full plaintext, including the",
            "   content type and padding.",
            "",
            "   Selecting a padding policy that suggests when and how much to pad is",
            "   a complex topic and is beyond the scope of this specification.  If",
            "   the application-layer protocol on top of TLS has its own padding, it",
            "   may be preferable to pad Application Data TLS records within the",
            "   application layer.  Padding for encrypted Handshake or Alert records",
            "   must still be handled at the TLS layer, though.  Later documents may",
            "   define padding selection algorithms or define a padding policy",
            "   request mechanism through TLS extensions or some other means."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "0cfbe485b0eddf36",
            "0cfbe485b0eddf36",
            "180a59e64012365e",
            "180a59e64012365e",
            "aeb89794c6089f72",
            "aeb89794c6089f72",
            "aeb89794c6089f72",
            "aeb89794c6089f72",
            "aeb89794c6089f72",
            "a118bc99178b292f",
            "a118bc99178b292f",
            "a118bc99178b292f",
            "a118bc99178b292f",
            "a118bc99178b292f",
            "98e95302e05d1d70",
            "98e95302e05d1d70",
            "f2c1b930dbe14713",
            "f2c1b930dbe14713",
            "f2c1b930dbe14713",
            "1c4206b295549383",
            "1c4206b295549383",
            "1c4206b295549383"
          ],
          "title": "Record Padding"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.5",
          "lines": [
            "   There are cryptographic limits on the amount of plaintext which can",
            "   be safely encrypted under a given set of keys.  [AEAD-LIMITS]",
            "   provides an analysis of these limits under the assumption that the",
            "   underlying primitive (AES or ChaCha20) has no weaknesses.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7890db0808608291"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "Implementations SHOULD do a key update as described in Section 4.6.3"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7890db0808608291"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "prior to reaching these limits."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   For AES-GCM, up to 2^24.5 full-size records (about 24 million) may be",
            "   encrypted on a given connection while keeping a safety margin of",
            "   approximately 2^-57 for Authenticated Encryption (AE) security.  For",
            "   ChaCha20/Poly1305, the record sequence number would wrap before the",
            "   safety limit is reached."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "7890db0808608291",
            "7890db0808608291"
          ],
          "title": "Limits on Key Usage"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6",
          "lines": [
            "   TLS provides an Alert content type to indicate closure information",
            "   and errors.  Like other messages, alert messages are encrypted as",
            "   specified by the current connection state.",
            "",
            "   Alert messages convey a description of the alert and a legacy field",
            "   that conveyed the severity level of the message in previous versions",
            "   of TLS.  Alerts are divided into two classes: closure alerts and",
            "   error alerts.  In TLS 1.3, the severity is implicit in the type of",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   alert being sent, and the \"level\" field can safely be ignored.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a3a6405540804fd"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "The"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a3a6405540804fd"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "\"close_notify\" alert is used to indicate orderly closure of one"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a3a6405540804fd"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "direction of the connection.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb061ccb4fda51e3",
                  "0a3a6405540804fd"
                ],
                "status_id": 19,
                "text": "Upon receiving such an alert, the TLS"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb061ccb4fda51e3",
                  "0a3a6405540804fd"
                ],
                "status_id": 19,
                "text": "implementation SHOULD indicate end-of-data to the application."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Error alerts indicate abortive closure of the connection (see",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   Section 6.2).  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "310f852b73456b73",
                  "0e56140e79982039"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "Upon receiving an error alert, the TLS implementation"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "310f852b73456b73",
                  "0e56140e79982039"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "SHOULD indicate an error to the application and MUST NOT allow any"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "310f852b73456b73",
                  "0e56140e79982039"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "further data to be sent or received on the connection."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "26ade86012b63452"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Servers and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "26ade86012b63452"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "clients MUST forget the secret values and keys established in failed"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "26ade86012b63452"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "connections, with the exception of the PSKs associated with session"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "26ade86012b63452"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "tickets, which SHOULD be discarded if possible."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a73ea16e71e6132f",
                  "987d0f8c54b31cba",
                  "9e7179294667d054"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "All the alerts listed in Section 6.2 MUST be sent with"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a73ea16e71e6132f",
                  "987d0f8c54b31cba",
                  "9e7179294667d054"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "AlertLevel=fatal and "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a73ea16e71e6132f",
                  "987d0f8c54b31cba",
                  "9e7179294667d054",
                  "89238f15801c4117"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "MUST be treated as error alerts when received"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a73ea16e71e6132f",
                  "987d0f8c54b31cba",
                  "9e7179294667d054",
                  "89238f15801c4117"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "regardless of the AlertLevel in the message."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "56c60b19961343b2",
                  "58d05f40520fc508",
                  "12c3305363cb9cde"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Unknown Alert types"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "56c60b19961343b2",
                  "58d05f40520fc508",
                  "12c3305363cb9cde"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "MUST be treated as error alerts."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Note: TLS defines two generic alerts (see Section 6) to use upon",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   failure to parse a message.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7e0e5ddbee0b7a8e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Peers which receive a message which"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7e0e5ddbee0b7a8e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "cannot be parsed according to the syntax (e.g., have a length"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7e0e5ddbee0b7a8e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "extending beyond the message boundary or contain an out-of-range"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7e0e5ddbee0b7a8e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "length) MUST terminate the connection with a \"decode_error\" alert."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8ae6750bdf39c438"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Peers which receive a message which is syntactically correct but"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8ae6750bdf39c438"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "semantically invalid (e.g., a DHE share of p - 1, or an invalid enum)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8ae6750bdf39c438"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "MUST terminate the connection with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "      enum { warning(1), fatal(2), (255) } AlertLevel;",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9165055a648ca402"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "enum {"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9165055a648ca402"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "close_notify(0),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9165055a648ca402"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "unexpected_message(10),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9165055a648ca402"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "bad_record_mac(20),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9165055a648ca402"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "record_overflow(22),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9165055a648ca402"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "handshake_failure(40),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "01ce5bbcfcaa2cae"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "bad_certificate(42),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "01ce5bbcfcaa2cae"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "unsupported_certificate(43),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "01ce5bbcfcaa2cae"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "certificate_revoked(44),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "01ce5bbcfcaa2cae"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "certificate_expired(45),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "01ce5bbcfcaa2cae"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "certificate_unknown(46),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6786e3f9314bbb4c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "illegal_parameter(47),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6786e3f9314bbb4c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "unknown_ca(48),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6786e3f9314bbb4c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "access_denied(49),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6786e3f9314bbb4c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "decode_error(50),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6786e3f9314bbb4c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "decrypt_error(51),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a7150a2b6e8ea7ce"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "protocol_version(70),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a7150a2b6e8ea7ce"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "insufficient_security(71),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a7150a2b6e8ea7ce"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "internal_error(80),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a7150a2b6e8ea7ce"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "inappropriate_fallback(86),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a7150a2b6e8ea7ce"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "user_canceled(90),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0731d012469272fe"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "missing_extension(109),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0731d012469272fe"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "unsupported_extension(110),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0731d012469272fe"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "unrecognized_name(112),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0731d012469272fe"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "bad_certificate_status_response(113),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0731d012469272fe"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "unknown_psk_identity(115),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb01d2c0dfb658a4"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "certificate_required(116),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb01d2c0dfb658a4"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "no_application_protocol(120),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "          "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb01d2c0dfb658a4"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "(255)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb01d2c0dfb658a4"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "} AlertDescription;"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "      struct {",
            "          AlertLevel level;",
            "          AlertDescription description;",
            "      } Alert;"
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "eb061ccb4fda51e3",
            "eb061ccb4fda51e3",
            "310f852b73456b73",
            "310f852b73456b73",
            "310f852b73456b73",
            "26ade86012b63452",
            "26ade86012b63452",
            "26ade86012b63452",
            "26ade86012b63452",
            "a73ea16e71e6132f",
            "a73ea16e71e6132f",
            "a73ea16e71e6132f",
            "987d0f8c54b31cba",
            "987d0f8c54b31cba",
            "987d0f8c54b31cba",
            "56c60b19961343b2",
            "56c60b19961343b2",
            "7e0e5ddbee0b7a8e",
            "7e0e5ddbee0b7a8e",
            "7e0e5ddbee0b7a8e",
            "7e0e5ddbee0b7a8e",
            "8ae6750bdf39c438",
            "8ae6750bdf39c438",
            "8ae6750bdf39c438"
          ],
          "title": "Alert Protocol"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6.1",
          "lines": [
            "   The client and the server must share knowledge that the connection is",
            "   ending in order to avoid a truncation attack.",
            "",
            "   close_notify:  This alert notifies the recipient that the sender will",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      not send any more messages on this connection.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "427c0622337c3cf1",
                  "7bd813240fa800f2",
                  "d78bd80ce93c474f"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "Any data received"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "427c0622337c3cf1",
                  "7bd813240fa800f2",
                  "d78bd80ce93c474f"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "after a closure alert has been received MUST be ignored."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   user_canceled:  This alert notifies the recipient that the sender is",
            "      canceling the handshake for some reason unrelated to a protocol",
            "      failure.  If a user cancels an operation after the handshake is",
            "      complete, just closing the connection by sending a \"close_notify\"",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      is more appropriate.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f80d5d2255cb0a67"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "This alert SHOULD be followed by a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f80d5d2255cb0a67"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "\"close_notify\"."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This alert generally has AlertLevel=warning."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e8b1f77b8344c845",
                  "b48ccfa53809448c"
                ],
                "status_id": 20,
                "text": "Either party MAY initiate a close of its write side of the connection"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e8b1f77b8344c845",
                  "b48ccfa53809448c"
                ],
                "status_id": 20,
                "text": "by sending a \"close_notify\" alert."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b48ccfa53809448c"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "  Any data received after a closure"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b48ccfa53809448c"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "alert has been received MUST be ignored."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "633de2c619a2b13a",
                  "10c7a804f11b2ae4"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "If a transport-level close"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "633de2c619a2b13a",
                  "10c7a804f11b2ae4"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "is received prior to a \"close_notify\", the receiver cannot know that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "633de2c619a2b13a",
                  "10c7a804f11b2ae4"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "all the data that was sent has been received."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d6c260c7e5198c26",
                  "a3947f5dd9df4f38",
                  "385fa6d7f4ba5549"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Each party MUST send a \"close_notify\" alert before closing its write"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d6c260c7e5198c26",
                  "a3947f5dd9df4f38",
                  "385fa6d7f4ba5549"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "side of the connection, unless it has already sent some error alert."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a3947f5dd9df4f38"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "This does not have any effect on its read side of the connection."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4bd07f69034e4314",
                  "64999a6af667a906"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "Note that this is a change from versions of TLS prior to TLS 1.3 in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4bd07f69034e4314",
                  "64999a6af667a906"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "which implementations were required to react to a \"close_notify\" by"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4bd07f69034e4314",
                  "64999a6af667a906"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "discarding pending writes and sending an immediate \"close_notify\""
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4bd07f69034e4314",
                  "64999a6af667a906"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "alert of their own."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  That previous requirement could cause truncation"
              }
            ],
            "   in the read side.  Both parties need not wait to receive a",
            "   \"close_notify\" alert before closing their read side of the",
            "   connection, though doing so would introduce the possibility of",
            "   truncation.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eade19117bff73fa",
                  "82b9fad6a2557b0d",
                  "35c0915ee853b231"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "If the application protocol using TLS provides that any data may be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eade19117bff73fa",
                  "82b9fad6a2557b0d",
                  "35c0915ee853b231"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "carried over the underlying transport after the TLS connection is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eade19117bff73fa",
                  "82b9fad6a2557b0d",
                  "35c0915ee853b231"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "closed, the TLS implementation MUST receive a \"close_notify\" alert"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eade19117bff73fa",
                  "82b9fad6a2557b0d",
                  "35c0915ee853b231"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "before indicating end-of-data to the application layer."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  No part of"
              }
            ],
            "   this standard should be taken to dictate the manner in which a usage",
            "   profile for TLS manages its data transport, including when",
            "   connections are opened or closed.",
            "",
            "   Note: It is assumed that closing the write side of a connection",
            "   reliably delivers pending data before destroying the transport."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "427c0622337c3cf1",
            "427c0622337c3cf1",
            "f80d5d2255cb0a67",
            "f80d5d2255cb0a67",
            "e8b1f77b8344c845",
            "e8b1f77b8344c845",
            "7bd813240fa800f2",
            "7bd813240fa800f2",
            "d6c260c7e5198c26",
            "d6c260c7e5198c26",
            "eade19117bff73fa",
            "eade19117bff73fa",
            "eade19117bff73fa",
            "eade19117bff73fa"
          ],
          "title": "Closure Alerts"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6.2",
          "lines": [
            "   Error handling in TLS is very simple.  When an error is detected, the",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   detecting party sends a message to its peer.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "73707b6f47c2cb1c",
                  "733fbeb20320d33f",
                  "ae3b93c9d925c720"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "Upon transmission or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "73707b6f47c2cb1c",
                  "733fbeb20320d33f",
                  "ae3b93c9d925c720"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "receipt of a fatal alert message, both parties MUST immediately close"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "73707b6f47c2cb1c",
                  "733fbeb20320d33f",
                  "ae3b93c9d925c720"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "the connection."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a9e4330365e99b57",
                  "be444e3ddd1c19ac"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "Whenever an implementation encounters a fatal error condition, it"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a9e4330365e99b57",
                  "be444e3ddd1c19ac"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "SHOULD send an appropriate fatal alert"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a9e4330365e99b57"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a9e4330365e99b57",
                  "5e683d86c1df515c"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "and MUST close the connection"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a9e4330365e99b57",
                  "5e683d86c1df515c"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "without sending or receiving any additional data."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "af4c3f2cf7fa98a2"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "In the rest of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "af4c3f2cf7fa98a2"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "this specification, when the phrases \"terminate the connection\" and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "af4c3f2cf7fa98a2"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "\"abort the handshake\" are used without a specific alert it means that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "af4c3f2cf7fa98a2"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "the implementation SHOULD send the alert indicated by the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "af4c3f2cf7fa98a2"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "descriptions below."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b2e246f2a5ee5653",
                  "167f228069a4e37b"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "The phrases \"terminate the connection with an X"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b2e246f2a5ee5653",
                  "167f228069a4e37b"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "alert\" and \"abort the handshake with an X alert\" mean that the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b2e246f2a5ee5653",
                  "167f228069a4e37b"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "implementation MUST send alert X if it sends any alert."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  All alerts"
              }
            ],
            "   defined below in this section, as well as all unknown alerts, are",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   universally considered fatal as of TLS 1.3 (see Section 6).  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7bc2a3d73c5ed00b",
                  "59a5f1de77ba78b9"
                ],
                "status_id": 19,
                "text": "The"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7bc2a3d73c5ed00b",
                  "59a5f1de77ba78b9"
                ],
                "status_id": 19,
                "text": "implementation SHOULD provide a way to facilitate logging the sending"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7bc2a3d73c5ed00b",
                  "59a5f1de77ba78b9"
                ],
                "status_id": 19,
                "text": "and receiving of alerts."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The following error alerts are defined:",
            "",
            "   unexpected_message:  An inappropriate message (e.g., the wrong",
            "      handshake message, premature Application Data, etc.) was received.",
            "      This alert should never be observed in communication between",
            "      proper implementations.",
            "",
            "   bad_record_mac:  This alert is returned if a record is received which",
            "      cannot be deprotected.  Because AEAD algorithms combine decryption",
            "      and verification, and also to avoid side-channel attacks, this",
            "      alert is used for all deprotection failures.  This alert should",
            "      never be observed in communication between proper implementations,",
            "      except when messages were corrupted in the network.",
            "",
            "   record_overflow:  A TLSCiphertext record was received that had a",
            "      length more than 2^14 + 256 bytes, or a record decrypted to a",
            "      TLSPlaintext record with more than 2^14 bytes (or some other",
            "      negotiated limit).  This alert should never be observed in",
            "      communication between proper implementations, except when messages",
            "      were corrupted in the network.",
            "",
            "   handshake_failure:  Receipt of a \"handshake_failure\" alert message",
            "      indicates that the sender was unable to negotiate an acceptable",
            "      set of security parameters given the options available.",
            "",
            "   bad_certificate:  A certificate was corrupt, contained signatures",
            "      that did not verify correctly, etc.",
            "",
            "   unsupported_certificate:  A certificate was of an unsupported type.",
            "",
            "   certificate_revoked:  A certificate was revoked by its signer.",
            "",
            "   certificate_expired:  A certificate has expired or is not currently",
            "      valid.",
            "",
            "   certificate_unknown:  Some other (unspecified) issue arose in",
            "      processing the certificate, rendering it unacceptable.",
            "",
            "   illegal_parameter:  A field in the handshake was incorrect or",
            "      inconsistent with other fields.  This alert is used for errors",
            "      which conform to the formal protocol syntax but are otherwise",
            "      incorrect.",
            "",
            "   unknown_ca:  A valid certificate chain or partial chain was received,",
            "      but the certificate was not accepted because the CA certificate",
            "      could not be located or could not be matched with a known trust",
            "      anchor.",
            "",
            "   access_denied:  A valid certificate or PSK was received, but when",
            "      access control was applied, the sender decided not to proceed with",
            "      negotiation.",
            "",
            "   decode_error:  A message could not be decoded because some field was",
            "      out of the specified range or the length of the message was",
            "      incorrect.  This alert is used for errors where the message does",
            "      not conform to the formal protocol syntax.  This alert should",
            "      never be observed in communication between proper implementations,",
            "      except when messages were corrupted in the network.",
            "",
            "   decrypt_error:  A handshake (not record layer) cryptographic",
            "      operation failed, including being unable to correctly verify a",
            "      signature or validate a Finished message or a PSK binder.",
            "",
            "   protocol_version:  The protocol version the peer has attempted to",
            "      negotiate is recognized but not supported (see Appendix D).",
            "",
            "   insufficient_security:  Returned instead of \"handshake_failure\" when",
            "      a negotiation has failed specifically because the server requires",
            "      parameters more secure than those supported by the client.",
            "",
            "   internal_error:  An internal error unrelated to the peer or the",
            "      correctness of the protocol (such as a memory allocation failure)",
            "      makes it impossible to continue.",
            "",
            "   inappropriate_fallback:  Sent by a server in response to an invalid",
            "      connection retry attempt from a client (see [RFC7507]).",
            "",
            "   missing_extension:  Sent by endpoints that receive a handshake",
            "      message not containing an extension that is mandatory to send for",
            "      the offered TLS version or other negotiated parameters.",
            "",
            "   unsupported_extension:  Sent by endpoints receiving any handshake",
            "      message containing an extension known to be prohibited for",
            "      inclusion in the given handshake message, or including any",
            "      extensions in a ServerHello or Certificate not first offered in",
            "      the corresponding ClientHello or CertificateRequest.",
            "",
            "   unrecognized_name:  Sent by servers when no server exists identified",
            "      by the name provided by the client via the \"server_name\" extension",
            "      (see [RFC6066]).",
            "",
            "   bad_certificate_status_response:  Sent by clients when an invalid or",
            "      unacceptable OCSP response is provided by the server via the",
            "      \"status_request\" extension (see [RFC6066]).",
            "",
            "   unknown_psk_identity:  Sent by servers when PSK key establishment is",
            "      desired but no acceptable PSK identity is provided by the client.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9bac4c3ca9719a26",
                  "ac79219d091286d1"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Sending this alert is OPTIONAL; servers MAY instead choose to send"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9bac4c3ca9719a26",
                  "ac79219d091286d1"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "a \"decrypt_error\" alert to merely indicate an invalid PSK"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9bac4c3ca9719a26",
                  "ac79219d091286d1"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "identity."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   certificate_required:  Sent by servers when a client certificate is",
            "      desired but none was provided by the client.",
            "",
            "   no_application_protocol:  Sent by servers when a client",
            "      \"application_layer_protocol_negotiation\" extension advertises only",
            "      protocols that the server does not support (see [RFC7301]).",
            "",
            "   New Alert values are assigned by IANA as described in Section 11."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "73707b6f47c2cb1c",
            "73707b6f47c2cb1c",
            "73707b6f47c2cb1c",
            "a9e4330365e99b57",
            "a9e4330365e99b57",
            "a9e4330365e99b57",
            "af4c3f2cf7fa98a2",
            "af4c3f2cf7fa98a2",
            "af4c3f2cf7fa98a2",
            "af4c3f2cf7fa98a2",
            "af4c3f2cf7fa98a2",
            "b2e246f2a5ee5653",
            "b2e246f2a5ee5653",
            "b2e246f2a5ee5653",
            "7bc2a3d73c5ed00b",
            "7bc2a3d73c5ed00b",
            "7bc2a3d73c5ed00b",
            "9bac4c3ca9719a26",
            "9bac4c3ca9719a26",
            "9bac4c3ca9719a26",
            "ac79219d091286d1",
            "ac79219d091286d1",
            "ac79219d091286d1"
          ],
          "title": "Error Alerts"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7",
          "lines": [
            "   The TLS handshake establishes one or more input secrets which are",
            "   combined to create the actual working keying material, as detailed",
            "   below.  The key derivation process incorporates both the input",
            "   secrets and the handshake transcript.  Note that because the",
            "   handshake transcript includes the random values from the Hello",
            "   messages, any given handshake will have different traffic secrets,",
            "   even if the same input secrets are used, as is the case when the same",
            "   PSK is used for multiple connections."
          ],
          "title": "Cryptographic Computations"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.1",
          "lines": [
            "   The key derivation process makes use of the HKDF-Extract and",
            "   HKDF-Expand functions as defined for HKDF [RFC5869], as well as the",
            "   functions defined below:",
            "",
            "       HKDF-Expand-Label(Secret, Label, Context, Length) =",
            "            HKDF-Expand(Secret, HkdfLabel, Length)",
            "",
            "       Where HkdfLabel is specified as:",
            "",
            "       struct {",
            "           uint16 length = Length;",
            "           opaque label<7..255> = \"tls13 \" + Label;",
            "           opaque context<0..255> = Context;",
            "       } HkdfLabel;",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "       "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fc4ccae35477ba81"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Derive-Secret(Secret, Label, Messages) ="
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "            "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fc4ccae35477ba81"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "HKDF-Expand-Label(Secret, Label,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "                              "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fc4ccae35477ba81"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Transcript-Hash(Messages), Hash.length)"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The Hash function used by Transcript-Hash and HKDF is the cipher",
            "   suite hash algorithm.  Hash.length is its output length in bytes.",
            "   Messages is the concatenation of the indicated handshake messages,",
            "   including the handshake message type and length fields, but not",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   including record layer headers.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4f57f2f6261451f1"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Note that in some cases a zero-"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4f57f2f6261451f1"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "length Context (indicated by \"\") is passed to HKDF-Expand-Label"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": ".  The"
              }
            ],
            "   labels specified in this document are all ASCII strings and do not",
            "   include a trailing NUL byte.",
            "",
            "   Note: With common hash functions, any label longer than 12 characters",
            "   requires an additional iteration of the hash function to compute.",
            "   The labels in this specification have all been chosen to fit within",
            "   this limit.",
            "",
            "   Keys are derived from two input secrets using the HKDF-Extract and",
            "   Derive-Secret functions.  The general pattern for adding a new secret",
            "   is to use HKDF-Extract with the Salt being the current secret state",
            "   and the Input Keying Material (IKM) being the new secret to be added.",
            "   In this version of TLS 1.3, the two input secrets are:",
            "",
            "   -  PSK (a pre-shared key established externally or derived from the",
            "      resumption_master_secret value from a previous connection)",
            "",
            "   -  (EC)DHE shared secret (Section 7.4)",
            "",
            "   This produces a full key derivation schedule shown in the diagram",
            "   below.  In this diagram, the following formatting conventions apply:",
            "",
            "   -  HKDF-Extract is drawn as taking the Salt argument from the top and",
            "      the IKM argument from the left, with its output to the bottom and",
            "      the name of the output on the right.",
            "",
            "   -  Derive-Secret's Secret argument is indicated by the incoming",
            "      arrow.  For instance, the Early Secret is the Secret for",
            "      generating the client_early_traffic_secret.",
            "",
            "   -  \"0\" indicates a string of Hash.length bytes set to zero.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "0"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "|"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "v"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "495c77602a92af1b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "PSK ->  HKDF-Extract = Early Secret"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "|"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e29cc2922473abae"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "+-----> Derive-Secret(., \"ext binder\" | \"res binder\", \"\")"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e29cc2922473abae"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "|                     = binder_key"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "|"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "93a5289e573792cc"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "+-----> Derive-Secret(., \"c e traffic\", ClientHello)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "93a5289e573792cc"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "|                     = client_early_traffic_secret"
              }
            ],
            "             |",
            "             +-----> Derive-Secret(., \"e exp master\", ClientHello)",
            "             |                     = early_exporter_master_secret",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "v"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "       "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fc9fce382e2345aa"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Derive-Secret(., \"derived\", \"\")"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "|"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "v"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fc9fce382e2345aa"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "(EC)DHE -> HKDF-Extract = Handshake Secret"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "|"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "974ce4c22651532e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "+-----> Derive-Secret(., \"c hs traffic\","
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "974ce4c22651532e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "|                     ClientHello...ServerHello)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "974ce4c22651532e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "|                     = client_handshake_traffic_secret"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "|"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1841ac4a9821e8fe"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "+-----> Derive-Secret(., \"s hs traffic\","
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1841ac4a9821e8fe"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "|                     ClientHello...ServerHello)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1841ac4a9821e8fe"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "|                     = server_handshake_traffic_secret"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "v"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "       "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "331fcc52ce96286d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Derive-Secret(., \"derived\", \"\")"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "|"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "v"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "331fcc52ce96286d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "0 -> HKDF-Extract = Master Secret"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "|"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f5b8d1a3c38fb3bb"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "+-----> Derive-Secret(., \"c ap traffic\","
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f5b8d1a3c38fb3bb"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "|                     ClientHello...server Finished)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f5b8d1a3c38fb3bb"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "|                     = client_application_traffic_secret_0"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "|"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "061d4b19da3f1560"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "+-----> Derive-Secret(., \"s ap traffic\","
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "061d4b19da3f1560"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "|                     ClientHello...server Finished)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "061d4b19da3f1560"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "|                     = server_application_traffic_secret_0"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "|"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2adc766643c8d9ca"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "+-----> Derive-Secret(., \"exp master\","
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2adc766643c8d9ca"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "|                     ClientHello...server Finished)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2adc766643c8d9ca"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "|                     = exporter_master_secret"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "|"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "95f911781f6bed6e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "+-----> Derive-Secret(., \"res master\","
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "                                   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "95f911781f6bed6e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "ClientHello...client Finished)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "                                   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "95f911781f6bed6e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "= resumption_master_secret"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The general pattern here is that the secrets shown down the left side",
            "   of the diagram are just raw entropy without context, whereas the",
            "   secrets down the right side include Handshake Context and therefore",
            "   can be used to derive working keys without additional context.  Note",
            "   that the different calls to Derive-Secret may take different Messages",
            "   arguments, even with the same secret.  In a 0-RTT exchange,",
            "   Derive-Secret is called with four distinct transcripts; in a",
            "   1-RTT-only exchange, it is called with three distinct transcripts.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d2f97c01a0ca0112"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If a given secret is not available, then the 0-value consisting of a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d2f97c01a0ca0112"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "string of Hash.length bytes set to zeros is used."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Note that this"
              }
            ],
            "   does not mean skipping rounds, so if PSK is not in use, Early Secret",
            "   will still be HKDF-Extract(0, 0).  For the computation of the",
            "   binder_key, the label is \"ext binder\" for external PSKs (those",
            "   provisioned outside of TLS) and \"res binder\" for resumption PSKs",
            "   (those provisioned as the resumption master secret of a previous",
            "   handshake).  The different labels prevent the substitution of one",
            "   type of PSK for the other.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0f389a89823d6a46"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "There are multiple potential Early Secret values, depending on which"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0f389a89823d6a46"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "PSK the server ultimately selects.  The client will need to compute"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0f389a89823d6a46"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "one for each potential PSK"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "; "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "753cf32d49977733"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "if no PSK is selected, it will then need"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "753cf32d49977733"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "to compute the Early Secret corresponding to the zero PSK."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6bc759f7b9849141"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "Once all the values which are to be derived from a given secret have"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6bc759f7b9849141"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "been computed, that secret SHOULD be erased."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "6bc759f7b9849141",
            "6bc759f7b9849141"
          ],
          "title": "Key Schedule"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.2",
          "lines": [
            "   Once the handshake is complete, it is possible for either side to",
            "   update its sending traffic keys using the KeyUpdate handshake message",
            "   defined in Section 4.6.3.  The next generation of traffic keys is",
            "   computed by generating client_/server_application_traffic_secret_N+1",
            "   from client_/server_application_traffic_secret_N as described in this",
            "   section and then re-deriving the traffic keys as described in",
            "   Section 7.3.",
            "",
            "   The next-generation application_traffic_secret is computed as:",
            "",
            "       application_traffic_secret_N+1 =",
            "           HKDF-Expand-Label(application_traffic_secret_N,",
            "                             \"traffic upd\", \"\", Hash.length)",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cfe8bdaea826337d"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "Once client_/server_application_traffic_secret_N+1 and its associated"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cfe8bdaea826337d"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "traffic keys have been computed, implementations SHOULD delete"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cfe8bdaea826337d"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "client_/server_application_traffic_secret_N and its associated"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cfe8bdaea826337d"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "traffic keys."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "cfe8bdaea826337d",
            "cfe8bdaea826337d",
            "cfe8bdaea826337d",
            "cfe8bdaea826337d"
          ],
          "title": "Updating Traffic Secrets"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.3",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a69c788b7dd5351e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The traffic keying material is generated from the following input"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a69c788b7dd5351e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "values:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a69c788b7dd5351e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "-  A secret value"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8f3767290faf7b2b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "-  A purpose value indicating the specific value being generated"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ba97988f04ab28d4"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "-  The length of the key being generated"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "33d6a0a913b244c8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The traffic keying material is generated from an input traffic secret"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "33d6a0a913b244c8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "value using:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "33d6a0a913b244c8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "[sender]_write_key = HKDF-Expand-Label(Secret, \"key\", \"\", key_length)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f31aee0f8d57612f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "[sender]_write_iv  = HKDF-Expand-Label(Secret, \"iv\", \"\", iv_length)"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   [sender] denotes the sending side.  The value of Secret for each",
            "   record type is shown in the table below.",
            "",
            "       +-------------------+---------------------------------------+",
            "       | Record Type       | Secret                                |",
            "       +-------------------+---------------------------------------+",
            "       | 0-RTT Application | client_early_traffic_secret           |",
            "       |                   |                                       |",
            "       | Handshake         | [sender]_handshake_traffic_secret     |",
            "       |                   |                                       |",
            "       | Application Data  | [sender]_application_traffic_secret_N |",
            "       +-------------------+---------------------------------------+",
            "",
            "   All the traffic keying material is recomputed whenever the underlying",
            "   Secret changes (e.g., when changing from the handshake to Application",
            "   Data keys or upon a key update)."
          ],
          "title": "Traffic Key Calculation"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.4",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "(EC)DHE Shared Secret Calculation"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.4.1",
          "lines": [
            "   For finite field groups, a conventional Diffie-Hellman [DH76]",
            "   computation is performed.  The negotiated key (Z) is converted to a",
            "   byte string by encoding in big-endian form and left-padded with zeros",
            "   up to the size of the prime.  This byte string is used as the shared",
            "   secret in the key schedule as specified above.",
            "",
            "   Note that this construction differs from previous versions of TLS",
            "   which removed leading zeros."
          ],
          "title": "Finite Field Diffie-Hellman"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.4.2",
          "lines": [
            "   For secp256r1, secp384r1, and secp521r1, ECDH calculations (including",
            "   parameter and key generation as well as the shared secret",
            "   calculation) are performed according to [IEEE1363] using the",
            "   ECKAS-DH1 scheme with the identity map as the key derivation function",
            "   (KDF), so that the shared secret is the x-coordinate of the ECDH",
            "   shared secret elliptic curve point represented as an octet string.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cae85e0066ec3ebf"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Note that this octet string (\"Z\" in IEEE 1363 terminology) as output"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cae85e0066ec3ebf"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "by FE2OSP (the Field Element to Octet String Conversion Primitive)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cae85e0066ec3ebf"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "has constant length for any given field; leading zeros found in this"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cae85e0066ec3ebf"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "octet string MUST NOT be truncated."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   (Note that this use of the identity KDF is a technicality.  The",
            "   complete picture is that ECDH is employed with a non-trivial KDF",
            "   because TLS does not directly use this secret for anything other than",
            "   for computing other secrets.)",
            "",
            "   For X25519 and X448, the ECDH calculations are as follows:",
            "",
            "   -  The public key to put into the KeyShareEntry.key_exchange",
            "      structure is the result of applying the ECDH scalar multiplication",
            "      function to the secret key of appropriate length (into scalar",
            "      input) and the standard public basepoint (into u-coordinate point",
            "      input).",
            "",
            "   -  The ECDH shared secret is the result of applying the ECDH scalar",
            "      multiplication function to the secret key (into scalar input) and",
            "      the peer's public key (into u-coordinate point input).  The output",
            "      is used raw, with no processing.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dfd6f746d42d57e3"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "For these curves, implementations SHOULD use the approach specified"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dfd6f746d42d57e3"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "in [RFC7748] to calculate the Diffie-Hellman shared secret."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5b7fa6c9e5f3ef42"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Implementations MUST check whether the computed Diffie-Hellman shared"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5b7fa6c9e5f3ef42"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "secret is the all-zero value and abort if so, as described in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5b7fa6c9e5f3ef42"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Section 6 of [RFC7748]."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "65feb35cdd638bb9"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "If implementors use an alternative"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "65feb35cdd638bb9"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "implementation of these elliptic curves, they SHOULD perform the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "65feb35cdd638bb9"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "additional checks specified in Section 7 of [RFC7748]."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "cae85e0066ec3ebf",
            "cae85e0066ec3ebf",
            "cae85e0066ec3ebf",
            "cae85e0066ec3ebf",
            "dfd6f746d42d57e3",
            "dfd6f746d42d57e3",
            "5b7fa6c9e5f3ef42",
            "5b7fa6c9e5f3ef42",
            "5b7fa6c9e5f3ef42",
            "65feb35cdd638bb9",
            "65feb35cdd638bb9",
            "65feb35cdd638bb9"
          ],
          "title": "Elliptic Curve Diffie-Hellman"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.5",
          "lines": [
            "   [RFC5705] defines keying material exporters for TLS in terms of the",
            "   TLS pseudorandom function (PRF).  This document replaces the PRF with",
            "   HKDF, thus requiring a new construction.  The exporter interface",
            "   remains the same.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "105544709b4fb5b9"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The exporter value is computed as:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "105544709b4fb5b9"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "TLS-Exporter(label, context_value, key_length) ="
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "       "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "105544709b4fb5b9"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "HKDF-Expand-Label(Derive-Secret(Secret, label, \"\"),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "                         "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "105544709b4fb5b9"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "\"exporter\", Hash(context_value), key_length)"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Where Secret is either the early_exporter_master_secret or the",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   exporter_master_secret.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c2c215862a5cc104"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Implementations MUST use the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c2c215862a5cc104"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "exporter_master_secret unless explicitly specified by the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c2c215862a5cc104"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "application."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  The early_exporter_master_secret is defined for use in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   settings where an exporter is needed for 0-RTT data.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "242c553d92dc555f"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "A separate"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "242c553d92dc555f"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "interface for the early exporter is RECOMMENDED; this avoids the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "242c553d92dc555f"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "exporter user accidentally using an early exporter when a regular one"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "242c553d92dc555f"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "is desired or vice versa."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   If no context is provided, the context_value is zero length.",
            "   Consequently, providing no context computes the same value as",
            "   providing an empty context.  This is a change from previous versions",
            "   of TLS where an empty context produced a different output than an",
            "   absent context.  As of this document's publication, no allocated",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   exporter label is used both with and without a context.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ee5c8494b1be21a1"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Future"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ee5c8494b1be21a1"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "specifications MUST NOT define a use of exporters that permit both an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ee5c8494b1be21a1"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "empty context and no context with the same label."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "76d395f5924fdcae"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "New uses of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "76d395f5924fdcae"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "exporters SHOULD provide a context in all exporter computations,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "76d395f5924fdcae"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "though the value could be empty."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Requirements for the format of exporter labels are defined in",
            "   Section 4 of [RFC5705]."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "c2c215862a5cc104",
            "c2c215862a5cc104",
            "c2c215862a5cc104",
            "242c553d92dc555f",
            "242c553d92dc555f",
            "242c553d92dc555f",
            "242c553d92dc555f",
            "ee5c8494b1be21a1",
            "ee5c8494b1be21a1",
            "ee5c8494b1be21a1",
            "76d395f5924fdcae",
            "76d395f5924fdcae",
            "76d395f5924fdcae"
          ],
          "title": "Exporters"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-8",
          "lines": [
            "   As noted in Section 2.3 and Appendix E.5, TLS does not provide",
            "   inherent replay protections for 0-RTT data.  There are two potential",
            "   threats to be concerned with:",
            "",
            "   -  Network attackers who mount a replay attack by simply duplicating",
            "      a flight of 0-RTT data.",
            "",
            "   -  Network attackers who take advantage of client retry behavior to",
            "      arrange for the server to receive multiple copies of an",
            "      application message.  This threat already exists to some extent",
            "      because clients that value robustness respond to network errors by",
            "      attempting to retry requests.  However, 0-RTT adds an additional",
            "      dimension for any server system which does not maintain globally",
            "      consistent server state.  Specifically, if a server system has",
            "      multiple zones where tickets from zone A will not be accepted in",
            "      zone B, then an attacker can duplicate a ClientHello and early",
            "      data intended for A to both A and B.  At A, the data will be",
            "      accepted in 0-RTT, but at B the server will reject 0-RTT data and",
            "      instead force a full handshake.  If the attacker blocks the",
            "      ServerHello from A, then the client will complete the handshake",
            "      with B and probably retry the request, leading to duplication on",
            "      the server system as a whole.",
            "",
            "   The first class of attack can be prevented by sharing state to",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   guarantee that the 0-RTT data is accepted at most once.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "198216a05282200a"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "Servers"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "198216a05282200a"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "SHOULD provide that level of replay safety by implementing one of the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "198216a05282200a"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "methods described in this section or by equivalent means."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  It is"
              }
            ],
            "   understood, however, that due to operational concerns not all",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   deployments will maintain state at that level.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aecaea45e0c77642"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Therefore, in normal"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aecaea45e0c77642"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "operation, clients will not know which, if any, of these mechanisms"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aecaea45e0c77642"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "servers actually implement and hence MUST only send early data which"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aecaea45e0c77642"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "they deem safe to be replayed."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   In addition to the direct effects of replays, there is a class of",
            "   attacks where even operations normally considered idempotent could be",
            "   exploited by a large number of replays (timing attacks, resource",
            "   limit exhaustion and others, as described in Appendix E.5).  Those",
            "   can be mitigated by ensuring that every 0-RTT payload can be replayed",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   only a limited number of times.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a8aaf9bd5a7e6c3a"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The server MUST ensure that any"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a8aaf9bd5a7e6c3a"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "instance of it (be it a machine, a thread, or any other entity within"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a8aaf9bd5a7e6c3a"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "the relevant serving infrastructure) would accept 0-RTT for the same"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a8aaf9bd5a7e6c3a"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "0-RTT handshake at most once; this limits the number of replays to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a8aaf9bd5a7e6c3a"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "the number of server instances in the deployment."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Such a guarantee"
              }
            ],
            "   can be accomplished by locally recording data from recently received",
            "   ClientHellos and rejecting repeats, or by any other method that",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   provides the same or a stronger guarantee.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bd47aa35da83a93b"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "The \"at most once per"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bd47aa35da83a93b"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "server instance\" guarantee is a minimum requirement; servers SHOULD"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bd47aa35da83a93b"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "limit 0-RTT replays further when feasible."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "237a288793ba68d2"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The second class of attack cannot be prevented at the TLS layer and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "237a288793ba68d2"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "MUST be dealt with by any application."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Note that any application"
              }
            ],
            "   whose clients implement any kind of retry behavior already needs to",
            "   implement some sort of anti-replay defense."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "198216a05282200a",
            "198216a05282200a",
            "198216a05282200a",
            "aecaea45e0c77642",
            "aecaea45e0c77642",
            "aecaea45e0c77642",
            "aecaea45e0c77642",
            "a8aaf9bd5a7e6c3a",
            "a8aaf9bd5a7e6c3a",
            "a8aaf9bd5a7e6c3a",
            "a8aaf9bd5a7e6c3a",
            "a8aaf9bd5a7e6c3a",
            "bd47aa35da83a93b",
            "bd47aa35da83a93b",
            "bd47aa35da83a93b",
            "237a288793ba68d2",
            "237a288793ba68d2"
          ],
          "title": "0-RTT and Anti-Replay"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-8.1",
          "lines": [
            "   The simplest form of anti-replay defense is for the server to only",
            "   allow each session ticket to be used once.  For instance, the server",
            "   can maintain a database of all outstanding valid tickets, deleting",
            "   each ticket from the database as it is used.  If an unknown ticket is",
            "   provided, the server would then fall back to a full handshake.",
            "",
            "   If the tickets are not self-contained but rather are database keys,",
            "   and the corresponding PSKs are deleted upon use, then connections",
            "   established using PSKs enjoy forward secrecy.  This improves security",
            "   for all 0-RTT data and PSK usage when PSK is used without (EC)DHE.",
            "",
            "   Because this mechanism requires sharing the session database between",
            "   server nodes in environments with multiple distributed servers, it",
            "   may be hard to achieve high rates of successful PSK 0-RTT connections",
            "   when compared to self-encrypted tickets.  Unlike session databases,",
            "   session tickets can successfully do PSK-based session establishment",
            "   even without consistent storage, though when 0-RTT is allowed they",
            "   still require consistent storage for anti-replay of 0-RTT data, as",
            "   detailed in the following section."
          ],
          "title": "Single-Use Tickets"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-8.2",
          "lines": [
            "   An alternative form of anti-replay is to record a unique value",
            "   derived from the ClientHello (generally either the random value or",
            "   the PSK binder) and reject duplicates.  Recording all ClientHellos",
            "   causes state to grow without bound, but a server can instead record",
            "   ClientHellos within a given time window and use the",
            "   \"obfuscated_ticket_age\" to ensure that tickets aren't reused outside",
            "   that window.",
            "",
            "   In order to implement this, when a ClientHello is received, the",
            "   server first verifies the PSK binder as described in Section 4.2.11.",
            "   It then computes the expected_arrival_time as described in the next",
            "   section and rejects 0-RTT if it is outside the recording window,",
            "   falling back to the 1-RTT handshake.",
            "",
            "   If the expected_arrival_time is in the window, then the server checks",
            "   to see if it has recorded a matching ClientHello.  If one is found,",
            "   it either aborts the handshake with an \"illegal_parameter\" alert or",
            "   accepts the PSK but rejects 0-RTT.  If no matching ClientHello is",
            "   found, then it accepts 0-RTT and then stores the ClientHello for as",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   long as the expected_arrival_time is inside the window.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "badf6aa73ca08365",
                  "b709fb3e5bc7e49c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Servers MAY"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "badf6aa73ca08365",
                  "b709fb3e5bc7e49c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "also implement data stores with false positives, such as Bloom"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "badf6aa73ca08365",
                  "b709fb3e5bc7e49c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "filters, in which case they MUST respond to apparent replay by"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "badf6aa73ca08365",
                  "b709fb3e5bc7e49c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "rejecting 0-RTT but MUST NOT abort the handshake."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8e6662057b842cec"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "The server MUST derive the storage key only from validated sections"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8e6662057b842cec"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "of the ClientHello."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  If the ClientHello contains multiple PSK"
              }
            ],
            "   identities, then an attacker can create multiple ClientHellos with",
            "   different binder values for the less-preferred identity on the",
            "   assumption that the server will not verify it (as recommended by",
            "   Section 4.2.11).  I.e., if the client sends PSKs A and B but the",
            "   server prefers A, then the attacker can change the binder for B",
            "   without affecting the binder for A.  If the binder for B is part of",
            "   the storage key, then this ClientHello will not appear as a",
            "   duplicate, which will cause the ClientHello to be accepted, and may",
            "   cause side effects such as replay cache pollution, although any 0-RTT",
            "   data will not be decryptable because it will use different keys.  If",
            "   the validated binder or the ClientHello.random is used as the storage",
            "   key, then this attack is not possible.",
            "",
            "   Because this mechanism does not require storing all outstanding",
            "   tickets, it may be easier to implement in distributed systems with",
            "   high rates of resumption and 0-RTT, at the cost of potentially weaker",
            "   anti-replay defense because of the difficulty of reliably storing and",
            "   retrieving the received ClientHello messages.  In many such systems,",
            "   it is impractical to have globally consistent storage of all the",
            "   received ClientHellos.  In this case, the best anti-replay protection",
            "   is provided by having a single storage zone be authoritative for a",
            "   given ticket and refusing 0-RTT for that ticket in any other zone.",
            "   This approach prevents simple replay by the attacker because only one",
            "   zone will accept 0-RTT data.  A weaker design is to implement",
            "   separate storage for each zone but allow 0-RTT in any zone.  This",
            "   approach limits the number of replays to once per zone.  Application",
            "   message duplication of course remains possible with either design.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "506d21e361f07876"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "When implementations are freshly started, they SHOULD reject 0-RTT as"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "506d21e361f07876"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "long as any portion of their recording window overlaps the startup"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "506d21e361f07876"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "time."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Otherwise, they run the risk of accepting replays which were"
              }
            ],
            "   originally sent during that period.",
            "",
            "   Note: If the client's clock is running much faster than the server's,",
            "   then a ClientHello may be received that is outside the window in the",
            "   future, in which case it might be accepted for 1-RTT, causing a",
            "   client retry, and then acceptable later for 0-RTT.  This is another",
            "   variant of the second form of attack described in Section 8."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "badf6aa73ca08365",
            "badf6aa73ca08365",
            "badf6aa73ca08365",
            "badf6aa73ca08365",
            "b709fb3e5bc7e49c",
            "b709fb3e5bc7e49c",
            "b709fb3e5bc7e49c",
            "b709fb3e5bc7e49c",
            "8e6662057b842cec",
            "8e6662057b842cec",
            "506d21e361f07876",
            "506d21e361f07876",
            "506d21e361f07876"
          ],
          "title": "Client Hello Recording"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-8.3",
          "lines": [
            "   Because the ClientHello indicates the time at which the client sent",
            "   it, it is possible to efficiently determine whether a ClientHello was",
            "   likely sent reasonably recently and only accept 0-RTT for such a",
            "   ClientHello, otherwise falling back to a 1-RTT handshake.  This is",
            "   necessary for the ClientHello storage mechanism described in",
            "   Section 8.2 because otherwise the server needs to store an unlimited",
            "   number of ClientHellos, and is a useful optimization for self-",
            "   contained single-use tickets because it allows efficient rejection of",
            "   ClientHellos which cannot be used for 0-RTT.",
            "",
            "   In order to implement this mechanism, a server needs to store the",
            "   time that the server generated the session ticket, offset by an",
            "   estimate of the round-trip time between client and server.  I.e.,",
            "",
            "       adjusted_creation_time = creation_time + estimated_RTT",
            "",
            "   This value can be encoded in the ticket, thus avoiding the need to",
            "   keep state for each outstanding ticket.  The server can determine the",
            "   client's view of the age of the ticket by subtracting the ticket's",
            "   \"ticket_age_add\" value from the \"obfuscated_ticket_age\" parameter in",
            "   the client's \"pre_shared_key\" extension.  The server can determine",
            "   the expected_arrival_time of the ClientHello as:",
            "",
            "     expected_arrival_time = adjusted_creation_time + clients_ticket_age",
            "",
            "   When a new ClientHello is received, the expected_arrival_time is then",
            "   compared against the current server wall clock time and if they",
            "   differ by more than a certain amount, 0-RTT is rejected, though the",
            "   1-RTT handshake can be allowed to complete.",
            "",
            "   There are several potential sources of error that might cause",
            "   mismatches between the expected_arrival_time and the measured time.",
            "   Variations in client and server clock rates are likely to be minimal,",
            "   though potentially the absolute times may be off by large values.",
            "   Network propagation delays are the most likely causes of a mismatch",
            "   in legitimate values for elapsed time.  Both the NewSessionTicket and",
            "   ClientHello messages might be retransmitted and therefore delayed,",
            "   which might be hidden by TCP.  For clients on the Internet, this",
            "   implies windows on the order of ten seconds to account for errors in",
            "   clocks and variations in measurements; other deployment scenarios may",
            "   have different needs.  Clock skew distributions are not symmetric, so",
            "   the optimal tradeoff may involve an asymmetric range of permissible",
            "   mismatch values.",
            "",
            "   Note that freshness checking alone is not sufficient to prevent",
            "   replays because it does not detect them during the error window,",
            "   which -- depending on bandwidth and system capacity -- could include",
            "   billions of replays in real-world settings.  In addition, this",
            "   freshness checking is only done at the time the ClientHello is",
            "   received and not when subsequent early Application Data records are",
            "   received.  After early data is accepted, records may continue to be",
            "   streamed to the server over a longer time period."
          ],
          "title": "Freshness Checks"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-9",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Compliance Requirements"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-9.1",
          "lines": [
            "   In the absence of an application profile standard specifying",
            "   otherwise:",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c7fcc6080fa679b0"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "A TLS-compliant application MUST implement the TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c7fcc6080fa679b0"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "[GCM] cipher suite and SHOULD implement the TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c7fcc6080fa679b0"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "[GCM] and TLS_CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256 [RFC8439] cipher suites (see"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c7fcc6080fa679b0"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Appendix B.4)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "286b5edd0e7f482c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "A TLS-compliant application MUST support digital signatures with"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "286b5edd0e7f482c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "rsa_pkcs1_sha256 (for certificates), rsa_pss_rsae_sha256 (for"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "286b5edd0e7f482c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "CertificateVerify and certificates), and ecdsa_secp256r1_sha256."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "A"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ef81424b150a1b31"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "TLS-compliant application MUST support key exchange with secp256r1"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ef81424b150a1b31"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "(NIST P-256) and SHOULD support key exchange with X25519 [RFC7748]."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "c7fcc6080fa679b0",
            "c7fcc6080fa679b0",
            "c7fcc6080fa679b0",
            "c7fcc6080fa679b0",
            "286b5edd0e7f482c",
            "286b5edd0e7f482c",
            "286b5edd0e7f482c",
            "ef81424b150a1b31",
            "ef81424b150a1b31",
            "ef81424b150a1b31"
          ],
          "title": "Mandatory-to-Implement Cipher Suites"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-9.2",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9c4532a440392a66"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "In the absence of an application profile standard specifying"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9c4532a440392a66"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "otherwise, a TLS-compliant application MUST implement the following"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9c4532a440392a66"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "TLS extensions:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   -  Supported Versions (\"supported_versions\"; Section 4.2.1)",
            "",
            "   -  Cookie (\"cookie\"; Section 4.2.2)",
            "",
            "   -  Signature Algorithms (\"signature_algorithms\"; Section 4.2.3)",
            "",
            "   -  Signature Algorithms Certificate (\"signature_algorithms_cert\";",
            "      Section 4.2.3)",
            "",
            "   -  Negotiated Groups (\"supported_groups\"; Section 4.2.7)",
            "",
            "   -  Key Share (\"key_share\"; Section 4.2.8)",
            "",
            "   -  Server Name Indication (\"server_name\"; Section 3 of [RFC6066])",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7654d63ef6f08d33"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "All implementations MUST send and use these extensions when offering"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7654d63ef6f08d33"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "applicable features:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "65404e762827ad15"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "-  \"supported_versions\" is REQUIRED for all ClientHello, ServerHello,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "65404e762827ad15"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "and HelloRetryRequest messages."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "05a5770443f47966"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "-  \"signature_algorithms\" is REQUIRED for certificate authentication."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9b951a3b69a50da9"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "-  \"supported_groups\" is REQUIRED for ClientHello messages using DHE"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9b951a3b69a50da9"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "or ECDHE key exchange."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2b877a7ae2c027b0"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "-  \"key_share\" is REQUIRED for DHE or ECDHE key exchange."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a3e60b7eb95ea9fa"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "-  \"pre_shared_key\" is REQUIRED for PSK key agreement."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "47caccfb362c73c1"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "-  \"psk_key_exchange_modes\" is REQUIRED for PSK key agreement."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   A client is considered to be attempting to negotiate using this",
            "   specification if the ClientHello contains a \"supported_versions\"",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   extension with 0x0304 contained in its body.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5a87558e78b64aa7"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Such a ClientHello"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5a87558e78b64aa7"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "message MUST meet the following requirements:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7641303a5c24c7ab"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "-  If not containing a \"pre_shared_key\" extension, it MUST contain"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7641303a5c24c7ab"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "both a \"signature_algorithms\" extension and a \"supported_groups\""
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7641303a5c24c7ab"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "extension."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1451b6d64bdf36ca"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "-  If containing a \"supported_groups\" extension, it MUST also contain"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1451b6d64bdf36ca"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "a \"key_share\" extension, and vice versa."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  An empty"
              }
            ],
            "      KeyShare.client_shares vector is permitted.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5e076a4a578a793c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Servers receiving a ClientHello which does not conform to these"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5e076a4a578a793c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "requirements MUST abort the handshake with a \"missing_extension\""
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5e076a4a578a793c"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "alert."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3c3af8db0cf2b6c4"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Additionally, all implementations MUST support the use of the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3c3af8db0cf2b6c4"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "\"server_name\" extension with applications capable of using it."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8da6419cca4a819e"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Servers MAY require clients to send a valid \"server_name\" extension."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3a6c13ca6b586f23"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "Servers requiring this extension SHOULD respond to a ClientHello"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3a6c13ca6b586f23"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "lacking a \"server_name\" extension by terminating the connection with"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3a6c13ca6b586f23"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "a \"missing_extension\" alert."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "9c4532a440392a66",
            "9c4532a440392a66",
            "9c4532a440392a66",
            "7654d63ef6f08d33",
            "7654d63ef6f08d33",
            "65404e762827ad15",
            "65404e762827ad15",
            "05a5770443f47966",
            "9b951a3b69a50da9",
            "9b951a3b69a50da9",
            "2b877a7ae2c027b0",
            "a3e60b7eb95ea9fa",
            "47caccfb362c73c1",
            "5a87558e78b64aa7",
            "5a87558e78b64aa7",
            "7641303a5c24c7ab",
            "7641303a5c24c7ab",
            "7641303a5c24c7ab",
            "1451b6d64bdf36ca",
            "1451b6d64bdf36ca",
            "5e076a4a578a793c",
            "5e076a4a578a793c",
            "5e076a4a578a793c",
            "3c3af8db0cf2b6c4",
            "3c3af8db0cf2b6c4",
            "8da6419cca4a819e",
            "3a6c13ca6b586f23",
            "3a6c13ca6b586f23",
            "3a6c13ca6b586f23"
          ],
          "title": "Mandatory-to-Implement Extensions"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-9.3",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ea1aaa22ae38e4cd"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "This section describes invariants that TLS endpoints and middleboxes"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ea1aaa22ae38e4cd"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "MUST follow."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  It also applies to earlier versions of TLS."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   TLS is designed to be securely and compatibly extensible.  Newer",
            "   clients or servers, when communicating with newer peers, should",
            "   negotiate the most preferred common parameters.  The TLS handshake",
            "   provides downgrade protection: Middleboxes passing traffic between a",
            "   newer client and newer server without terminating TLS should be",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   unable to influence the handshake (see Appendix E.1).  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dddad5ad17bcbaa9"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "At the same"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dddad5ad17bcbaa9"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "time, deployments update at different rates, so a newer client or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dddad5ad17bcbaa9"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "server MAY continue to support older parameters, which would allow it"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dddad5ad17bcbaa9"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "to interoperate with older endpoints."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2357b170fa5c0810"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "For this to work, implementations MUST correctly handle extensible"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2357b170fa5c0810"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "fields:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "09ee5050fa2823ea"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "-  A client sending a ClientHello MUST support all parameters"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "09ee5050fa2823ea"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "advertised in it."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Otherwise, the server may fail to interoperate"
              }
            ],
            "      by selecting one of those parameters.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ba6a3d27c859e350"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "-  A server receiving a ClientHello MUST correctly ignore all"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ba6a3d27c859e350"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "unrecognized cipher suites, extensions, and other parameters."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      Otherwise, it may fail to interoperate with newer clients.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bae9452a96487f27"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "In"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bae9452a96487f27"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "TLS 1.3, a client receiving a CertificateRequest or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bae9452a96487f27"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "NewSessionTicket MUST also ignore all unrecognized extensions."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8b48d211625c9cef"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "-  A middlebox which terminates a TLS connection MUST behave as a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8b48d211625c9cef"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "compliant TLS server (to the original client), including having a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8b48d211625c9cef"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "certificate which the client is willing to accept, and also as a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8b48d211625c9cef"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "compliant TLS client (to the original server), including verifying"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8b48d211625c9cef"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "the original server's certificate."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8be96a1700525c30",
                  "fb55f13ef1a2c97e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "In particular, it MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8be96a1700525c30",
                  "fb55f13ef1a2c97e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "generate its own ClientHello containing only parameters it"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8be96a1700525c30",
                  "fb55f13ef1a2c97e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "understands, and it MUST generate a fresh ServerHello random"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8be96a1700525c30",
                  "fb55f13ef1a2c97e"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "value, rather than forwarding the endpoint's value."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "      Note that TLS's protocol requirements and security analysis only",
            "      apply to the two connections separately.  Safely deploying a TLS",
            "      terminator requires additional security considerations which are",
            "      beyond the scope of this document.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5ed5cbaa5100f294"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "-  A middlebox which forwards ClientHello parameters it does not"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5ed5cbaa5100f294"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "understand MUST NOT process any messages beyond that ClientHello."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d9c4dad00c9fcee4"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "It MUST forward all subsequent traffic unmodified."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Otherwise, it"
              }
            ],
            "      may fail to interoperate with newer clients and servers.",
            "",
            "      Forwarded ClientHellos may contain advertisements for features not",
            "      supported by the middlebox, so the response may include future TLS",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      additions the middlebox does not recognize.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3eff94e9d64753d2"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "These additions MAY"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3eff94e9d64753d2"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "change any message beyond the ClientHello arbitrarily."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  In"
              }
            ],
            "      particular, the values sent in the ServerHello might change, the",
            "      ServerHello format might change, and the TLSCiphertext format",
            "      might change.",
            "",
            "   The design of TLS 1.3 was constrained by widely deployed",
            "   non-compliant TLS middleboxes (see Appendix D.4); however, it does",
            "   not relax the invariants.  Those middleboxes continue to be",
            "   non-compliant."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "ea1aaa22ae38e4cd",
            "ea1aaa22ae38e4cd",
            "dddad5ad17bcbaa9",
            "dddad5ad17bcbaa9",
            "dddad5ad17bcbaa9",
            "dddad5ad17bcbaa9",
            "2357b170fa5c0810",
            "2357b170fa5c0810",
            "09ee5050fa2823ea",
            "09ee5050fa2823ea",
            "ba6a3d27c859e350",
            "ba6a3d27c859e350",
            "bae9452a96487f27",
            "bae9452a96487f27",
            "bae9452a96487f27",
            "8b48d211625c9cef",
            "8b48d211625c9cef",
            "8b48d211625c9cef",
            "8b48d211625c9cef",
            "8b48d211625c9cef",
            "8be96a1700525c30",
            "8be96a1700525c30",
            "8be96a1700525c30",
            "8be96a1700525c30",
            "fb55f13ef1a2c97e",
            "fb55f13ef1a2c97e",
            "fb55f13ef1a2c97e",
            "fb55f13ef1a2c97e",
            "5ed5cbaa5100f294",
            "5ed5cbaa5100f294",
            "d9c4dad00c9fcee4",
            "3eff94e9d64753d2",
            "3eff94e9d64753d2"
          ],
          "title": "Protocol Invariants"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-10",
          "lines": [
            "   Security issues are discussed throughout this memo, especially in",
            "   Appendices C, D, and E."
          ],
          "title": "Security Considerations"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-11",
          "lines": [
            "   This document uses several registries that were originally created in",
            "   [RFC4346] and updated in [RFC8447].  IANA has updated these to",
            "   reference this document.  The registries and their allocation",
            "   policies are below:",
            "",
            "   -  TLS Cipher Suites registry: values with the first byte in the",
            "      range 0-254 (decimal) are assigned via Specification Required",
            "      [RFC8126].  Values with the first byte 255 (decimal) are reserved",
            "      for Private Use [RFC8126].",
            "",
            "      IANA has added the cipher suites listed in Appendix B.4 to the",
            "      registry.  The \"Value\" and \"Description\" columns are taken from",
            "      the table.  The \"DTLS-OK\" and \"Recommended\" columns are both",
            "      marked as \"Y\" for each new cipher suite.",
            "",
            "   -  TLS ContentType registry: Future values are allocated via",
            "      Standards Action [RFC8126].",
            "",
            "   -  TLS Alerts registry: Future values are allocated via Standards",
            "      Action [RFC8126].  IANA has populated this registry with the",
            "      values from Appendix B.2.  The \"DTLS-OK\" column is marked as \"Y\"",
            "      for all such values.  Values marked as \"_RESERVED\" have comments",
            "      describing their previous usage.",
            "",
            "   -  TLS HandshakeType registry: Future values are allocated via",
            "      Standards Action [RFC8126].  IANA has updated this registry to",
            "      rename item 4 from \"NewSessionTicket\" to \"new_session_ticket\" and",
            "      populated this registry with the values from Appendix B.3.  The",
            "      \"DTLS-OK\" column is marked as \"Y\" for all such values.  Values",
            "      marked \"_RESERVED\" have comments describing their previous or",
            "      temporary usage.",
            "",
            "   This document also uses the TLS ExtensionType Values registry",
            "   originally created in [RFC4366].  IANA has updated it to reference",
            "   this document.  Changes to the registry follow:",
            "",
            "   -  IANA has updated the registration policy as follows:",
            "",
            "      Values with the first byte in the range 0-254 (decimal) are",
            "      assigned via Specification Required [RFC8126].  Values with the",
            "      first byte 255 (decimal) are reserved for Private Use [RFC8126].",
            "",
            "   -  IANA has updated this registry to include the \"key_share\",",
            "      \"pre_shared_key\", \"psk_key_exchange_modes\", \"early_data\",",
            "      \"cookie\", \"supported_versions\", \"certificate_authorities\",",
            "      \"oid_filters\", \"post_handshake_auth\", and",
            "      \"signature_algorithms_cert\" extensions with the values defined in",
            "      this document and the \"Recommended\" value of \"Y\".",
            "",
            "   -  IANA has updated this registry to include a \"TLS 1.3\" column which",
            "      lists the messages in which the extension may appear.  This column",
            "      has been initially populated from the table in Section 4.2, with",
            "      any extension not listed there marked as \"-\" to indicate that it",
            "      is not used by TLS 1.3.",
            "",
            "   This document updates an entry in the TLS Certificate Types registry",
            "   originally created in [RFC6091] and updated in [RFC8447].  IANA has",
            "   updated the entry for value 1 to have the name \"OpenPGP_RESERVED\",",
            "   \"Recommended\" value \"N\", and comment \"Used in TLS versions prior",
            "   to 1.3.\"",
            "",
            "   This document updates an entry in the TLS Certificate Status Types",
            "   registry originally created in [RFC6961].  IANA has updated the entry",
            "   for value 2 to have the name \"ocsp_multi_RESERVED\" and comment \"Used",
            "   in TLS versions prior to 1.3\".",
            "",
            "   This document updates two entries in the TLS Supported Groups",
            "   registry (created under a different name by [RFC4492]; now maintained",
            "   by [RFC8422]) and updated by [RFC7919] and [RFC8447].  The entries",
            "   for values 29 and 30 (x25519 and x448) have been updated to also",
            "   refer to this document.",
            "",
            "   In addition, this document defines two new registries that are",
            "   maintained by IANA:",
            "",
            "   -  TLS SignatureScheme registry: Values with the first byte in the",
            "      range 0-253 (decimal) are assigned via Specification Required",
            "      [RFC8126].  Values with the first byte 254 or 255 (decimal) are",
            "      reserved for Private Use [RFC8126].  Values with the first byte in",
            "      the range 0-6 or with the second byte in the range 0-3 that are",
            "      not currently allocated are reserved for backward compatibility.",
            "      This registry has a \"Recommended\" column.  The registry has been",
            "      initially populated with the values described in Section 4.2.3.",
            "      The following values are marked as \"Recommended\":",
            "      ecdsa_secp256r1_sha256, ecdsa_secp384r1_sha384,",
            "      rsa_pss_rsae_sha256, rsa_pss_rsae_sha384, rsa_pss_rsae_sha512,",
            "      rsa_pss_pss_sha256, rsa_pss_pss_sha384, rsa_pss_pss_sha512, and",
            "      ed25519.  The \"Recommended\" column is assigned a value of \"N\"",
            "      unless explicitly requested, and adding a value with a",
            "      \"Recommended\" value of \"Y\" requires Standards Action [RFC8126].",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2a949f7ea5bda2af",
                  "92102a254396ddbc"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "IESG Approval is REQUIRED for a Y->N transition."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   -  TLS PskKeyExchangeMode registry: Values in the range 0-253",
            "      (decimal) are assigned via Specification Required [RFC8126].",
            "      The values 254 and 255 (decimal) are reserved for Private Use",
            "      [RFC8126].  This registry has a \"Recommended\" column.  The",
            "      registry has been initially populated with psk_ke (0) and",
            "      psk_dhe_ke (1).  Both are marked as \"Recommended\".  The",
            "      \"Recommended\" column is assigned a value of \"N\" unless explicitly",
            "      requested, and adding a value with a \"Recommended\" value of \"Y\"",
            "      requires Standards Action [RFC8126].  IESG Approval is REQUIRED",
            "      for a Y->N transition."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "2a949f7ea5bda2af",
            "92102a254396ddbc"
          ],
          "title": "IANA Considerations"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-12",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "References"
        },
